{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd","id":349384,"title":"Think of fictional characters and say what they would be in CofD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-24T16:31:57-08:00","id":349384,"title":"Think of fictional characters and say what they would be in CofD","content":"As the title says. You may include an explanation behind your choice and some stats if you want. It does not have to be a perfect match.<br /> <br /> Ghost Rider (Marvel Comics): a Sin-Eater. His Threshold is Torn and his Archetype is Reaper all the way. He has Rage 5, Shroud 5 and Hearse 5. He has the Pyre-Flame and Industrial Keys. He has a Memento motorcycle. He has a Reaper Merit that gives him +1 on attacks for each 2 points of Morality stat the target has below 7. He has a Flaw that only lets him use his powers when innocent blood is spilled, and once that happens, it's hard for him to stop. He can't harm anyone who he perceives as innocent (usually someone with Morality stat at 8 and higher, or who fulfills their Virtue often). Psyche is 7. Strength, Dexterity, Presence, Firearms, Weaponry and Drive are all at 5 or more. The Penance Stare is a quick Ceremony that requires a grapple and the target to be truly wicked. Its dice pool is Psyche + Presence vs Composure + Powerstat and it temporarily removes all willpower points, the ability to regain willpower and inflicts the Broken Condition.<br /> <br /> The Doctor (Doctor Who): either a True Fae or a Genius. If he is the former, he is a Fairest (Telluric/Oracle/Artist). If he is the later, he is a Staunen and a member of the Navigators. Explanation for the former can be found here: <a href=\"http://www.giantitp.com/forums/showthread.php?281628-The-Doctor-is-a-True-Fae\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.giantitp.com/forums/showt...-is-a-True-Fae</a>.<br /> <br /> Aang (Avatar: The Last Air Bender): a Mage. While his powers would suggest aptitude for Forces and thus the Obrimos Path, his connection with major Fate related events and his carefree personality suggest Acanthus. He would be a member of the Adamantine Arrow. If you are using Papa Bear's homebrew 25 Paths, Aang is a Magi (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/41641-alternate-watchtowers-supernal-realms?p=41818#post41818\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...1818#post41818</a>).<br /> <br /> Finn (Adventure Time): a Changeling. He would be a Fairest and his kiths would be Apollonian/Soldier (the Apollonian kith can be found here: <a href=\"http://1d4chan.org/wiki/Changeling_Homebrew_Kiths#Apollonian\" target=\"_blank\">http://1d4chan.org/wiki/Changeling_H...ths#Apollonian</a>). The Land Of Ooo was where he spent his Durance, and his Court is Summer. He does have Court Goodwill with Autumn due to his fearlessness, as well as his penchant for investigating mysteries and uncovering secrets.<br /> <br /> The Joker (DC Comics): a Slasher, natch. His Undertaking is Maniac. Alternatively, he is a Changeling or even a True Fae that really likes spreading chaos on the Ironside. His Seeming is Darkling and his Kiths are Razorhand/Moonborn/Lurker. If he is a True Fae, his Titles would be himself (Actor), a special gun (Prop) and a group of ogrish thugs (Wisp). Either way, his Morality stat is zero or absent altogether. I suggest using my reworked version of the Lurker kith: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/348164-some-reworked-contracts-optional-guidelines-for-building-hollows?p=349431#post349431\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...431#post349431</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-24-2014, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T18:23:09-08:00","id":349438,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't Dr. Who be one of those Reincarnating Immortals?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T18:27:51-08:00","id":349440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=349438#post349438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't Dr. Who be one of those Reincarnating Immortals?</div> </div> </div> </div>I always thought of The Doctor as an Acanthus.<br /> <br /> Or for an alternate take he could be a Keeper and the companions are changelings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T18:41:11-08:00","id":349445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=349440#post349440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I always thought of The Doctor as an Acanthus.<br /> <br /> Or for an alternate take he could be a Keeper and the companions are changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div>If he is an Acanthus, he'd need to be an Archmaster of Time to actually time travel, or have a really badass Artifact from Supernal Arcadia to imitate the TARDIS. He would also have the Vital Balance rote from Grimmoire Of Grimmoires (page 33) to extend his lifespan. If he is still a member of an Order, it would probably be Free Council or Adamantine Arrow. Throw in some dots in the Matter, Mind and Prime Arcana to represent his affinity for creating/dealing with machinery, artificial intelligences and magic items. The Sonic Screwdriver would be both an Imbued and Enhanced Item rather than an Artifact, since non Mages can use it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: is there a Legacy of time travellers dedicated to protecting the stability of Time? That would be cool, and the Doctor could be a member.<br /> <br /> EDIT 2: maybe he could have summoned and made a pact with a very powerful entity from the Supernal Arcadia or The Primal Wild to get his regeneration powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-24-2014, 10:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T18:58:01-08:00","id":349450,"title":"","content":"The Initiative from Buffy always made me think of Task Force Valkyrie meets the Cherion Group, and Adam was obviously a Promethean. That whole show was just one of those kitchen sink crossover games where the ST goes way overboard throwing as much as possible in from every line, with more than a healthy dose of homebrew to keep the players guessing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T19:30:08-08:00","id":349461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=349438#post349438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't Dr. Who be one of those Reincarnating Immortals?</div> </div> </div> </div>After reading &quot;Immortals&quot;, I agree, but how would you explain his TARDIS, Sonic Screwdriver and other items/abilities? Would the TARDIS and the Sonic Screwdriver be those objects that gain supernatural qualities for unexplainable/mysterious reasons that appear the God Machine book? I forget their name, I think they're called Leftovers or Castaways.<br /> <br /> EDIT: sorry, I was thinking of Bygones. They are in page 243 of the God Machine book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-24-2014, 10:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T19:32:26-08:00","id":349463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd#post349384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ghost Rider (Marvel Comics): a Sin-Eater. His Threshold is Torn and his Archetype is Reaper all the way. He has Rage 5, Shroud 5 and Hearse 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is Hearse 5?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T19:44:42-08:00","id":349467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=349463#post349463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What is Hearse 5?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hearse is a fan made Manifestation for &quot;Geist: The Sin-Eaters&quot;. This Manifestation is linked with transportation and movement. You can find it here: <a href=\"http://www.giantitp.com/forums/showthread.php?287815-The-Hearse-(A-Geist-The-Sin-Eaters-Manifestation\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.giantitp.com/forums/showt...-Manifestation</a>).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T20:23:08-08:00","id":349489,"title":"","content":"Kratos (God Of War): probably way too Exalted-like to fit, but maybe he could be an Astral personification of Indignation Against The Divine, or a Mage that was trapped in the Astral Realms and turned into such a personification. Maybe he was an changeling of the Ogre Seeming who reached Wyrd 10 and decided that it was time to bring the fight to the Gentry by harnessing their powers. If he is a True Fae, his Titles would be himself (Actor), the Blades Of Exile (Prop) and the Head Of Medusa (Prop), while the other items are Tokens or Hedgespun. If you want to play as a character in a more mythical NWoD that simply has Kratos' powers, a Thyrsus or Mastigos Mage can work. His Blades Of Exile would be a Pandemonium Artifact with the Ranged Blow spell (Space 3), Mind spells for subduing lesser/median life forms and a Forces spell for ignoring gravity while climbing. Put dots in Life and Matter for physical prowess, super endurance, regeneration and improving/breaking objects. Also put dots in Forces, Death and Prime for imitating his magical abilities from the games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-24-2014, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T20:23:47-08:00","id":349490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=349461#post349461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> After reading &quot;Immortals&quot;, I agree, but how would you explain his TARDIS, Sonic Screwdriver and other items/abilities? Would the TARDIS and the Sonic Screwdriver be those objects that gain supernatural qualities for unexplainable/mysterious reasons that appear the God Machine book? I forget their name, I think they're called Leftovers or Castaways.<br /> <br /> EDIT: sorry, I was thinking of Bygones. They are in page 243 of the God Machine book.</div> </div> </div> </div>They could be Bygones, or they could be Relics from Reliquary, or they could just be uniquely supernatural items, since we're not really limited in nWoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T04:06:59-08:00","id":349761,"title":"","content":"Spider-Man (Marvel Comics): either a Changeling Beast or Klagen Genius. Yes, I gave him 3 kiths at Wyrd 7 instead of Wyrd 9.<br /> <br /> If he is a changeling, he has these stats:<br /> <br /> Name: Spider-Man (Peter Parker)<br /> Virtue: Charity/Justice<br /> Vice: Wrath <br /> Concept: Genius Superhero<br /> <br /> Seeming: Beast<br /> Kith: Skitterskulk/Cyclopean/Inventor<br /> Court: Summer<br /> <br /> Mental Attributes: Intelligence 4, Wits 6, Resolve 4<br /> Physical Attributes: Strength 6, Dexterity 4, Stamina 5<br /> Social Attributes: Presence 4, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <br /> Mental Skills: Academics 3, Crafts (Hedgespinning) 3, Computer 3, Medicine 3, Occult 2, Politics 2, Investigation 3, Science (Genetics) 4<br /> Physical Skills: Athletics (Climbing, Web-Slinging) 6, Brawl 5, Drive 1, Firearms 2, Larceny 1, Stealth 3, Survival (Hedge) 2, Weaponry 3<br /> Social Skills: Animal Ken 1, Empathy 3, Expression (Jokes) 4, Intimidation 3, Persuasion (Wisecracking) 3, Streetwise 2, Subterfuge (Protect Identity) 4<br /> <br /> Merits: Virtuous, Ambidextrous, Inspiring, Encyclopedic Knowledge, Area Of Expertise (Genetics, Hedgespinning), Resources 1, Disarm, Quick Draw, Mantle (Summer) 4, Allies 2/Status 1/Contacts (Daily Bugle), Striking Looks +1, Perfect Stillness, Danger Sense, Direction Sense, Iron Stamina 3, Fleet Of Foot 3, Fast Reflexes 2, Hedge Gate Sense, Charmed Life, Faerie Healing, Hedge Duelist 5, Harvest (Emotions 5, Pledges 5), Hollow 8 (Size 2, Amenities 3, Doors 1, Garden 2), Archive 4 (Summer Court History, True Fae, Tokens, Hobgoblins), Workshop 2 (Machines 2), Brownie's Boon, Token 5 (Web Shooters), Hedgespun Raiment 5 (Athletics +2, Initiative +3), Token Maker 5*<br /> <br /> *The target number of successes is decreased to 15 per token dot, but requires Wyrd 6. Also, Spider-Man rolls Wyrd + Science + Workshop bonus (17 dice total) instead of Wyrd + Crafts when building tokens, as long as the token is scientific and/or technological in nature. Lastly, he automatically rerolls the failed dice on each roll without spending glamour, as per the Wyrd 7 bonus for the Inventor kith.<br /> <br /> Health: 10<br /> Willpower: 7<br /> Defense: 4 (10 if you are using GMC)<br /> Initiative Mod: 9<br /> Speed: 19<br /> Wyrd: 7<br /> Contracts: Artifice 5, Smoke 3, Darkness 4, Separation 4, Fleeting Summer 4, Oath And Punishment 4, Vainglory 2, Stone 5, Goblin (Delayed Harm, Shooter\u2019s Bargain, Burden Of Life, Trading Luck For Fate, Good And Bad Luck, Lost And Found)<br /> Clarity: 8 <br /> <br /> Maximum Glamour/Per Turn: 20/7<br /> Frailties: must not harm those he perceives as innocent (minor taboo), must make a wisecrack when he thinks something is silly or absurd (minor taboo)<br /> <br /> If he is a Genius, he has the same stats as the changeling version, but with the following changes:<br /> <br /> Catalyst: Klagen<br /> Foundation: Navigators<br /> Inspiration: 7<br /> Max Mania/Per Turn: 40/7<br /> Obligation: 8<br /> Axioms: Exelixi 4, Katastrofi 3, Apkalypsi 3, Protasia 3, Epikrato 2, Automata 1, Skafoi 2, Metaptropi 1<br /> <br /> Replace the fae Merits with these Genius Merits: Calculus Vampire, Technomancer, Dumpster Diver. Kitbasher, Science Hero, Status (Navigators) 4, Universalist 3, Laboratory 4 (Size 2, Equipment 2), Energy Channeler 1, Attuned Construction (use the highest of two or more Skills when creating wonders that require them)<br /> <br /> Web Shooters:<br /> Construction: Crafts<br /> Requires: Epikrato 2, Katastrofi 3, Skafoi 2<br /> Bound Mania: 6<br /> Size: 1<br /> Roll: For attacking and immobilizing, use Dexterity + Athletics + 4 (Bashing, 8 Again). For pulling objects and doing meat puppetry, use Wits + Athletics + 3. For swinging around, use Wits + Athletics + 3.<br /> Variables: Autofire, Skafoi Ray, Epikrato Ray, Immobilizing Attack, Attribute Damage (Strength), Variable Damage, Explosive Weapon (Blast Area = 20 yards)<br /> Faults: none<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T06:18:12-08:00","id":352602,"title":"","content":"The Slender Man: he shows up in woods, his mind is alien to us, shows up using different forms in the stories of different cultures spanning wide temporal gaps, he kidnaps people (often children) and has strange powers. Sounds like a True Fae to me. He would have the following stats:<br /> <br /> Virtue and Vice: See below, under Fae Aspects<br /> Concept: Mysterious Boogey Man<br /> <br /> Seeming: Darkling<br /> Kith: Mirrorskin<br /> <br /> Mental Attributes: Intelligence 5, Wits 4, Resolve 4<br /> Physical Attributes: Strength 4, Dexterity 3, Stamina 4<br /> Social Attributes: Presence 6, Manipulation 4, Composure 5<br /> <br /> If you are using Second Edition rules: Power 7, Finesse 8, Resistance 6<br /> <br /> Mental Skills: Academics 2, Computer 1, Crafts 1, Investigation 3, Medicine 1, Occult 3, Science 1<br /> Physical Skills: Athletics (Using Tentacles) 3, Brawl (Claws, Tentacles) 3, Larceny 3, Stealth (Forests) 6, Survival (Hedge) 2<br /> Social Skills: Animal Ken 1, Empathy (Children) 1, Expression 1, Intimidation (Appearing Out Of Nowhere) 5, Persuasion 3, Streetwise 1, Subterfuge 4<br /> <br /> Merits: Encyclopedic Knowledge, Eidetic Memory, Disarm (done via tentacles and with Brawl instead of Weaponry), Danger Sense, Direction Sense, Ambidextrous, Fast Reflexes 2, Iron Stamina 3, Harvest (Emotions 5, Dreams 5), Dream Combat 5, Rigid Mask 2, Heavy Weapons (Tentacles) 5, Lethal Mien, Charmed Life<br /> <br /> Health: 11 (Size 7)<br /> Willpower: 9<br /> Defense: 4 (7 if you're using GMC)<br /> Initiative Mod: 10<br /> Speed: 13 (Species Factor 6)<br /> Wyrd: 8<br /> <br /> Contracts: Forge 5, Mirror 6, Smoke 5, Darkness 6, Moon 6, Illusion 5, Stone 3, Vainglory 3, Control The Elements (Fire) 4, Dream 4, Wild 2, Fleeting Autumn 1, Goblin (Fair Entrance, Fool's Gold, Delayed Harm, The Blessing Of Forgetfulness, Mirror Mirror, Diviner's Madness)<br /> <br /> Maximum Glamour/per Turn: 30/8<br /> <br /> Frailties: cannot activate Contracts or Slender Walk while within someone's direct line of sight (major taboo), cannot speak (major taboo), must frighten anyone who catches him on a picture or video (minor taboo), if meeting a child he wants to kidnap, must present himself as friendly (minor taboo)<br /> <br /> Mien Blessings: The Mercurial Visage (Mirrorskin), Spurious Stature (Gargantuan), Fade Into The Foliage (Woodblood)<br /> <br /> Fae Aspects:<br /> <br /> <b>Immortal Flesh:</b> True Fae are fantastic beings made of the fabric of dreams and madness. When manifested in the mortal world, they can shrug off the attempts of the mundane to damage them, and even the most destructive of harms will not be as severe to them. Any physical damage that does not come from Cold Iron will deal only bashing to the True Fae. Certain supernatural sources of damage can deal lethal to the Gentry, but only Hand-Forged Iron will deliver aggravated damage. Additionally, they are not affected by Combat Tilts unless they were caused by cold iron, hand-forged iron, or supernatural powers. Their flesh is also immune to natural infirmities. They do suffer wound penalties, but they can't be knocked unconscious by Bashing damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Alien Mind:</b> Slender Man regains one point of Willpower during every scene in which he stalks and/or frightens someone. He regains all Willpower points when his actions drive someone mad (using Contracts does not count). He also regains one willpower point every time midnight strikes.<br /> <br /> <b>Tentacles:</b> spend 2 Glamour + 1 Willpower point. Gain +2 automatic lethal damage to Brawl, +2 to Defense, +2 to Athletics and +2 to initiate/maintain a grapple. May carry twice as much weight. Once per turn, he may attack with his claws and then spend 1 glamour to also attack with tentacles. Mundane Stealth rolls are halved round down and can't be boosted with willpower. May end this effect at will.<br /> <br /> <b>Sickness Aura:</b> remaining within a varying radius of the Slender Man for more than a period decided by the ST requires a reflexive Stamina + Resolve roll. If the roll fails, you take one lethal damage immediately, plus one bashing damage every following day unless you receive medical attention. Other symptoms may include coughing with blood, fever, hallucinations and compulsive behavior. This aura also makes electronic equipment malfunction according to the ST.<br /> <br /> <b>Slender Walking:</b> the Slender Man may reflexively teleport to any location within Wyrd x 25 yards by spending 1 glamour and rolling Wyrd + Stealth. To teleport toward a victim he can't perceive, he must spend 2 Glamour and sense the target\u2019s fear by rolling Investigation + Wyrd vs Resolve + Composure + equipment (maximum distance is determined by the ST). If the victim gets as many successes as Slender Man or more, he cannot Slender Walk toward that person for a period decided by the ST. Doing research on the Slender Man or thinking too much about him imposes penalties on this roll. If using either type of teleportation for a surprise attack, a -1 penalty is imposed to Perception rolls to detect him, and an Exceptional Success increases the penalty to -3.<br /> <br /> Titles: Slender Man (Actor), Garden Of Shadows (Realm) and Master Proxies (Wisp)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-28-2014, 10:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T14:11:56-08:00","id":354088,"title":"","content":"Doctor who is a demon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T15:54:09-08:00","id":354142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=354088#post354088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doctor who is a demon</div> </div> </div> </div>How so? What would his Incarnation and Agenda be? What are his Embeds and Exploits? What would his demonic form be like? Would his different bodies be different Covers? Would the sonic screwdriver and TARDIS be Embeded/Exploited Gadgets?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-29-2014, 07:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T06:59:36-08:00","id":354705,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Mask\" target=\"_blank\">The Mask/Big Head:</a> someone wearing a Fae Title in Prop form. The Prop belongs to a True Fae with Wyrd 9 who can see what people are doing with it (and loves it). Treat someone who is wearing the Mask as a True Fae Actor, with all the powers and weaknesses that come with that, such as spending glamour to heal wounds, dream warping and invoking new Contract clauses dynamically (you are encouraged to use new clauses of Forge to represent most of the cartoonish powers). You can create Hedgespun items, unlike other True Fae. The Computer, Expression and Empathy Skills do not suffer limitations, and your creativity is unaffected. This Prop only works during the night. <span style=\"color:#2c3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Contracts Of Music can be found on Kismet's World Of Darkness. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2c3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Apply the following characteristics, which overwrite supernatural templates as long as the Mask is being worn. The &quot;built in&quot; Hedgespun items, Seeming and Mien Blessings may vary.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2c3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Seeming: Ogre<br /> <br /> Attributes: Power 9, Finesse 4, Resistance 8</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2c3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Bonus Merits: Ambidextrous, Gunslinger, Quick Draw, Stunt Driver, Disarm, Danger Sense, Direction Sense, Striking Looks +2, Barfly, Inspiring, Fast Reflexes 3, Fleet of Foot 3, Iron Stamina 3, Heavy Weapons 5, Two Weapons 4, Weaponry Dodge, Brawling Dodge, Harvest (Emotions 5, Dreams 5), Enchanting Performance, Charmed Life, Lethal Mien, Hedgespun Shoes 5 (+10 Speed), Hedgespun Suit 5 (2/4 GMC Armor), Hedgespun Hat 5 (+3 Expression, +2 Subterfuge)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2c3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Wyrd: 9</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2c3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Contracts: Vainglory 5, Mirror 7, Forge 7 or more, Stone 5, Separation 5, Music 2, Darkness 3, Goblin (Fair Entrance, Lost And Found, Shooter's Bargain, Delayed Harm)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2c3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Max Glamour/Per Turn: 50/10</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2c3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Frailties: determined by the Storyteller</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Mien Blessings: The Mercurial Visage (Mirrorskin), Lyrical Voice, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/163507-walking-shadows-seemings-and-kiths\"> Weapons </a> (Soldier)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2c3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Fae Aspects: Immortal Flesh and Ruled By Passion</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 01-02-2015, 06:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T14:17:50-08:00","id":355110,"title":"","content":"Let's see if i can label my favorite Vampires in Wod<br /> <br /> Bill Compton From True Blood<br /> <br /> Clan:Mehket<br /> Bloodline:None<br /> <br /> Virtue:Bravery<br /> Vice:Greed.<br /> <br /> Disciplines<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />ominate 3,Auspex 1,Vigor 2<br /> <br /> <br /> Damon Salvatore from the Vampire Diaries:<br /> <br /> Clan<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />aeva<br /> Bloodline:none<br /> <br /> Virtue:hope<br /> Vice:Wrath<br /> <br /> Disciplines<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />ominate 4,Auspex 3,Protean 4,Vigor 4<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T16:04:02-08:00","id":355197,"title":"","content":"Desmond Miles (Assassin's Creed): Acanthus Guardian of the Veil, Subtle Ones Legacy. Desmond is the latest of more than one comingling lines of Sleepwalker and Proximus Dynasties going back more than a thousand years. He Awakened when Abstergo (corporate front for a Seers of the Throne conspiracy) forced him into a powerful artifact which used temporal sympathy to cast his perceptions back into the lives of his Awakened ancestors for extended periods, in an effort to uncover ancient secrets of the Diamond Orders. Unknown to his captors he used the experiences of those ancestors to train himself in the use of his Arcana as well as learning useful spell rotes and skills before escaping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T06:00:04-08:00","id":355695,"title":"","content":"I made some stats for the Doctor.<br /> <br /> Virtue and Vice: Varies. See below under Fae Aspects.<br /> Concept: Eccentric Space-time Traveler<br /> <br /> Seeming: Fairest<br /> Kith: Telluric<br /> <br /> Mental Attributes: Intelligence 6, Wits 4, Resolve 5<br /> Physical Attributes: Strength 3, Dexterity 4, Stamina 4<br /> Social Attributes: Presence 5, Manipulation 4, Composure 4<br /> <br /> If you are using Second Edition rules: Power 8, Finesse 7, Resistance 6<br /> <br /> Mental Skills: Academics (History) 5, Crafts (Hedgespinning) 5, Computer 4, Medicine 3, Occult (Astrology) 3, Politics 3, Investigation 3, Science (Time Travel, Astronomy) 6<br /> Physical Skills: Athletics (Running) 3, Brawl 2, Drive 2, Firearms 3, Larceny 2, Stealth 3, Survival (Hedge) 2, Weaponry (Swords) 6<br /> Social Skills: Animal Ken 2, Empathy 3, Expression 3, Intimidation 3, Persuasion (Invite To Adventures) 4, Socialize 2, Streetwise 3, Subterfuge 3<br /> <br /> Merits: Ambidextrous, Area Of Expertise (History, Hedgespinning, Time Travel), Quick Draw, Disarm, Encyclopedic Knowledge, Common Sense, Danger Sense, Direction Sense, Fighting Finesse (Swords), Striking Looks +1, Inspiring, Well-Traveled, Fast Reflexes 3, Fleet of Foot 3, Iron Stamina 3, Heavy Weapons 5, Hedgespun Weapon 5 (Time Lord Sword: +5L, +3 Piercing), Hedgespun Raiment 5 (Time Lord Clothes: Empathy +2, Athletics +3), Harvest (Emotions 5, Pledges 5), Token 2 (Psychic Paper), Pledgesmith 3, Token Maker 5*, Hollow 10 (Size 5, Amenities 3, Wards 2; located inside the TARDIS), Workshop 5 (Machines 5)<br /> <br /> *The target number of successes is decreased to 15 per dot of the token, but requires Wyrd 6. He rolls Wyrd + Crafts + Machines Specialty w/ Area Of Expertise + Workshop bonus + Sonic Screwdriver bonus = 38 dice. Also, he automatically rerolls the failed dice without spending glamour, as per the Wyrd 7 blessing of the Artist kith.<br /> <br /> Health: 9<br /> Willpower: 9<br /> Defense: 7<br /> Initiative Mod: 10<br /> Speed: 15<br /> Wyrd: 8<br /> Contracts: Artifice 7, Stone 3, Hours 4, Verdant Spring 4, Spellbound Autumn 3, Vainglory 3, Four Directions 2, Goblin (Trading Luck For Fate, Diviner\u2019s Madness, Delayed Harm, Good And Bad Luck)<br /> <br /> Max Glamour/Per Turn: 30/8<br /> Frailties: skin contact or ingestion of ginger (major bane), skin contact or ingestion of Aspirin (major bane), must not interfere with the stability of Time (minor taboo), must not harm his companions (minor taboo)<br /> <br /> Mien Blessings: Music Of The Spheres (Telluric), Panomancy (Oracle), Impeccable Craftsmanship (Artist)<br /> <br /> Fae Aspects:<br /> <br /> Immortal Flesh: True Fae are fantastic beings made of the fabric of dreams and madness. When manifested in the mortal world, they can shrug off the attempts of the mundane to damage them, and even the most destructive of harms will not be as severe to them. Any physical damage that does not come from Cold Iron will deal only bashing to the True Fae. Certain supernatural sources of damage can deal lethal to the Gentry, but only Hand-Forged Iron will deliver aggravated damage. Additionally, they are not affected by Combat Tilts unless they were caused by cold iron, hand-forged iron, or supernatural powers. Their flesh is also immune to natural infirmities. They do suffer wound penalties, but they can't be knocked unconscious by Bashing damage.<br /> <br /> Change of Heart: The True Fae are entities almost embodied by their passions and vices, with higher morality and self-denial little more than a whim to them. For them, passion is virtue, and the denial of passion an affectation. Their supernaturally amoral nature is reflected in an inverted ability to regain Willpower. They regain one Willpower point from indulging their Virtue, but refresh their whole pool when satiating their Vice.<br /> <br /> The Doctor, on the other hand, has spent enough time on the mortal world to absorb part of humanity\u2019s nature. He can remain on Earth without suffering damage, regains Willpower normally, can harvest Glamour from selfless emotions, can create Hedgespun items and does not have the Skill limits of most True Fae. However, his mindset is still very much alien, and thus he has no Morality or Clarity meter, nor can his strange thought processes be represented by Derangements, as is the case with the other True Fae.<br /> <br /> Regeneration: The Doctor can completely heal himself when severely ill or wounded. He may also do this at will if necessary. This process causes changes in appearance, virtue, vice, attributes, skills and merits. New Fae Aspects and Mien Blessings may manifest. He may only use this ability twelve times. Temporary side effects may include amnesia, black outs, erratic behavior and loss of motor control.<br /> <br /> Advanced Automatons: this Fae Aspect is based on the <a href=\"http://thereachmux.org/wiki/Changeling/Hedgespinning#Automatons\" target=\"_blank\">ReachWiki\u2019s</a> house rules for Hedgespun Automatons. The Doctor gains the following benefits when building Hedgespun automatons \u2013 he can invest 10 dots in each automaton, each dot above 5 grants +1 Attribute and +2 Skills, their Wits and Intelligence scores can be above 3, they have a Seeming and up to 2 kiths, they start with Wyrd 3 and can have up to Wyrd 5 by spending 1 Merit dot per Wyrd point, they can use tokens, can enter the Hedge, can swear Pledges, can harvest glamour, have Virtues and Vices, they start with 10 dots of Contracts, they can gain and spend xp, total xp cost divided by half.<br /> <br /> Titles: the Doctor (Actor), TARDIS (mobile Realm), Sonic Screwdriver (Prop)<br /> <br /> The Tell: the Doctor\u2019s Tells are eccentric clothing, mannerisms, technologies and accessories. Colorful question marks may also appear.<br /> <br /> The Doctor: he looks like a man of varying appearance. In his Mien, he is always illuminated by tiny stars, galaxies, nebulae and planets that appear and disappear. His eyes, although normal, can cause a person to become lost in them, as if they were abysses into every experience of his extremely long life. His Fae Weakness is having both his hearts destroyed.<br /> <br /> TARDIS: the entrance to this Realm looks like a police call box. The inside is a giant computer station filled with strange technologies, beings and relics from different places and eras. This Realm is capable of flying and traveling through space and time, as well as entering the Hedge. The Doctor automatically arrives at his chosen location and time period, unless the ST says otherwise. Other characters may use the TARDIS if the Doctor teaches them how to operate it.<br /> <br /> Sonic Screwdriver: this small handheld device has a large number of uses (see below). The Sonic Screwdriver does not work on anything made of wood and cannot kill, wound or maim living things.<br /> <br /> Lock/Unlock Doors And Similar Objects: no roll is necessary, as success is automatic for most locks.<br /> <br /> Control/Locate/Improve Machines: Dexterity + Science or Computer + 8, with a penalty depending on the complexity of the device.<br /> <br /> Build/Repair/Damage Objects: Dexterity + Crafts + 8. Each roll represents a period of work determined by the ST. Each success restores/removes one point of Structure. Also add +8 to the Wyrd + Crafts roll for making Tokens.<br /> <br /> Analyze Biological, Chemical And Physical Phenomena: Intelligence + Science + 8.<br /> <br /> Miscellaneous Stuff From The Show: use with permission from the ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-31-2014, 09:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T12:10:16-08:00","id":356739,"title":"","content":"Hellboy (Dark Horse Comics): a Supernal Demon of the Mind Arcanum that somehow didn't return to Pandemonium and acquired human characteristics/stats due to his upbringing.<br /> <br /> Virtue: Charity/Justice<br /> <br /> Vice: Wrath<br /> <br /> Rank: 4<br /> <br /> Attributes: Power 9, Finesse 5, Resistance 12<br /> <br /> Mental Skills: Academics (Folklore &amp; Mythology) 3, Computer 2, Crafts (Firearm Maintenance) 3, Investigation (Detective Work) 5, Medicine 2, Occult (Cryptozoology, Supernal) 4, Science 2<br /> <br /> Physical Skills: Athletics 3, Brawl 6, Drive 2, Firearms (Revolvers) 1, Larceny 1, Stealth (Urban) 4, Survival 3, Weaponry (Swords) 5<br /> <br /> Social Skills: Animal Ken (Cats) 3, Empathy 3, Expression (Humor) 3, Intimidation (Physical Threats) 4, Persuasion 2, Socialize 1, Streetwise 4, Subterfuge 4<br /> <br /> Skill Tricks: Pattern Expert (Investigation), Myth Expert (Occult), Knockout Punch (Brawl), Concrete Jungle (Survival), Rumor Mill (Streetwise)<br /> <br /> Hunter Tactics: up to the ST.<br /> <br /> Merits: Virtuous, Area Of Expertise (Detective Work), Encyclopedic Knowledge, Ambidextrous, Disarm, Danger Sense, Direction Sense, Very Quick Healer (see below), Innate Multilingualism (see below), Fast Reflexes 3, Iron Stamina 3, Fleet Of Foot 3, Heavy Weapons (Swords, Right Hand) 5, Trained Observer 3, Eye For The Strange, Tolerance For Biology, Demolisher 3, Inspiring, Allies 3/Status 3/Contacts (BPRD), Striking Looks +2, Professional Training 3 (Occultist: Occult, Investigation, Academics), Naturalized Hunter (see below)<br /> <br /> Naturalized Hunter: Hellboy may Risk Willpower like Hunters do.<br /> <br /> Very Quick Healer: Hellboy heals 1 bashing each turn, 1 lethal each minute and 1 aggravated each hour.<br /> <br /> Innate Multilingualism: Hellboy has an instinctive understanding of ancient and supernatural languages, including the Spirit Tongue and High Speech.<br /> <br /> Willpower: 10<br /> Maximum Essence/Per Turn: 40/12<br /> Initiative: 12<br /> Defense: 5<br /> Speed: 15<br /> Health: 18 (Size 6)<br /> Integrity: 6<br /> Influence: Relics &amp; Artifacts 3, Medicine 3, Mind 2<br /> <br /> Numina:<br /> <br /> Mortal Mask<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://thereachmux.org/wiki/Numina/House_Rules\" target=\"_blank\">Ephemeral Armor</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://thereachmux.org/wiki/Numina/House_Rules\" target=\"_blank\">Ephemeral Weapon</a><br /> <br /> Elemental Immunity (Fire)<br /> <br /> Essence In Unveiling: Every time Hellboy gains a Beat while he investigates, researches, confronts or reasons with the supernatural or those affiliated with it, he rolls Finesse + Investigation + Rank with NO willpower boosting or 9 Again. Success = the Beat comes with 1 Essence. Exceptional Success = the Beat comes with [Rank] Essence. Secondly, whenever he completes a mission relating to supernatural or those affiliated with it, he rolls Finesse + Investigation + Rank, with the Rote Quality. Each success gives him 1 Essence. Lastly, if he is in big trouble, he may turn his GMC Experience Points into Essence. No roll is required: each GMC Experience Point becomes 10 Essence reflexively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-15-2015, 07:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T07:21:17-08:00","id":358298,"title":"","content":"Jeeves (from Jeeves and Wooster) is a normal human, albeit one who is clued in. However, all of Woosters friends are high Wyrd changelings, which would explain their eccentricities and seeming near total blindness to others. Wooster himself is a Fairest of a musical bent, with Wyrd 6 and a frailty preventing him from refusing or breaking a marriage engagement. His Clarity is pretty high, about 7 or 8.<br /> <br /> Jeeves mostly gets as successful results as he does through careful knowledge of the other changelings frailties and bans, as well as benefits from a pact he struck with Wooster to get Glamour sight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T19:00:39-08:00","id":358704,"title":"","content":"<b>Monkey D. Luffy (One Piece)</b><br /> <br /> EDIT: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1011999#post1011999\"><b>Updated the sheet.</b></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-21-2016, 12:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T11:13:52-08:00","id":367566,"title":"","content":"<b>The Batter (Mortis Ghost's OFF)</b><br /> <br /> EDIT: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1020156#post1020156\"><b>Updated the sheet</b></a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-21-2016, 12:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T08:11:43-08:00","id":369755,"title":"","content":"I had this idea once, to recreate the Doom Marine as a Dark Hero/Hunter combo, with all Masteries and Asset Skills dumped into Firearms and Brawl. I supose something simmilar could be done with Duke Nukeem, if it suited anyones fancy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T18:37:16-08:00","id":376811,"title":"","content":"For giggles, here's an attempt to integrate the Originals into the World of Darkness. Yeah, I know; it's my favorite guilty pleasure. Not providing stats, because, quite frankly, they'd be ridiculously OP by standard NWoD definitions.<br /> <br /> The Mikaelsons<br /> <br /> A family of Converted Vampires, much like Longinus and Dracula. Over a thousand years old, and currently in torpor, their story is the favorite legend of &quot;named&quot; Methuselahs that gets bandied about. Supposedly, they're the founders of the Original Vampire Clans, or at least their modern incarnation (after all the Clans date back to Rome, which is older even than them). So yeah, no one really believes this tale, but every now and again, someone claims to have met one... and wound up very messily dead shortly thereafter, or so the urban legend goes.<br /> <br /> Mikael, the Patriach; Clan Gangrel, if any. Supposedly hunts his children down, and kills any other Kindred he comes across while he's at it. Typical Vampire-as-Hunter boogeyman. Another mystical figure the rumor mill attributes the mystical VII to. Why? Supposedly the family originally had SEVEN children, but something awful happened to two of them before they all Turned.<br /> <br /> Esther, the Thrysus Mage. One of the most powerful in history, apparently, since she supposedly turned her entire family into vampires to fight off some local werewolf tribe. Please, witches are powerful, but there's never been even the slightest hint they were capable of creating whole species. Also seeks to destroy vampire-kind, but is trying to magick up a way to do the entire species in all at once. *Yawn* Yeah, right.<br /> <br /> Finn, Clan Nosferatu. Eldest sibling. Total mama's boy. Creepy in the extreme, and tends to unnerve anyone who sticks around him too long. Supposedly has a deathwish, and happily assists Mommy Dearest in her latest scheme to end her spawn.<br /> <br /> Elijah, Clan Ventrue. The Responsible One. keeps his siblings in check, and has the whole Ventrue &quot;noblesse oblige&quot; thing going on. Supposedly the cool, rational member, up until the point you press him too far, and then he turns like a snake.<br /> <br /> Rebekah, Clan Daeva. Typical Daeva bullshit. Always falls in love with mortals, gets burned, whines for the good old days of mortality, and typically makes very poor unlife choices. Just more typical Patriarchy BS, about how women can't be trusted with power.<br /> <br /> Kol, Clan Mekhet. This one's fairly interesting. Standard &quot;impulsive&quot; vampire, though he's got an obsession with mystical knowledge. Tracks well with the Mekhet. Still looks like a punk kid and exploits that fact so no one takes him seriously.<br /> <br /> Niklaus, Clan Gangrel. Oh, THIS guy. This one takes the cake. The REALLY crazy tales insist he's some kind of vampire/werewolf abomination. That's what really clinches this as some crazy story told to wow the neonates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3200,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","user":"Barachiel","date":". 01-20-2015, 09:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T09:48:32-08:00","id":384301,"title":"","content":"I like that, Barachiel. With just a little fudging you could make them older and actually have people claim they are the original five Clan sires, even. Or, you could have an Originals/Vampire Diaries game using nWoD mechanics this way, too. Neat.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T14:15:54-08:00","id":384486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=352602#post352602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Slender Man: he shows up in woods, his mind is alien to us, shows up using different forms in the stories of different cultures spanning wide temporal gaps, he kidnaps people (often children) and has strange powers. Sounds like a True Fae to me. He would have the following stats:<br /> <br /> Virtue and Vice: See below, under Fae Aspects<br /> Concept: Mysterious Boogey Man</div> </div> </div> </div>After Nightmare before Christmas, I can't really take the concept of Boogey Man without having it include some social skills in singing and dancing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iy9ha3qLU8Y\" data-code=\"iy9ha3qLU8Y\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/iy9ha3qLU8Y/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T20:42:54-08:00","id":401396,"title":"","content":"Master Xehanort from the Kingdom Hearts franchise is a god damned, motherfucking Acanthus Scelesti. That fucker has things more planned out than Awakening's Merlin.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, the Doctor is a Psychopomp Inquisitor/Tempter. It explains why Colin Baker and Peter Capaldi show up as faces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T13:35:58-08:00","id":402342,"title":"","content":"For fun, since we've had arguments for nearly every other gamelines, enjoy a Promethean Doctor, the only option that comes with rules for an extra heart! And have some Pandoran Weeping Angels<br /> <br /> <b>The Doctor</b><br /> <b>Lineage: Osiran</b><br /> <b>Refinement: Aes</b><br /> <b>Mental Attributes: </b>Intelligence 5 Wits 4 Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes: </b>Strength 2 Dexterity 2 Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social Attributes: </b>Presence 4 Manipulation 5 Composure 3<br /> <b>Mental Skills: </b>Academics 3, Investigation 4, Occult (Prometheans) 4, Science 3<br /> <b>Physical Skills: </b>Athletics (Sprinting) 2, Brawl 1, Larceny 1, Stealth 1, Survival 1, Weaponry (Fencing) 2<br /> <b>Social Skills: </b>Animal Ken 1, Empathy 3, Intimidation 3, Persuasion (Fast-Talking) 4, Socialize 3, Subterfuge (Hiding Emotions) 2<br /> <b>Merits: </b>Inspiring 4, Eidetic Memory 2, Encyclopaedic Knowledge 4, Shepherd 4, Elpis 4, Repute 3 (The Doctor)<br /> <b>Willpower: </b>7<br /> <b>Health: </b>8<br /> <b>Humanity: </b>5 (Narcissism)<br /> <b>Virtue: </b>Justice<br /> <b>Vice: </b>Pride<br /> <b>Size: </b>5<br /> <b>Defense: </b>2<br /> <b>Initiative: </b>5<br /> <b>Speed: </b>9<br /> Azoth: 3<br /> Pyros/Turn: 12/3<br /> Bestowment: Revivification<br /> Transmutations: Benefice \u2013 Able Worker 2, Protective Boon 4. Deception \u2013 Incognito 2. Disquietism \u2013 Soothe Disquiet 5, Quell Disquiet 5. Saturnius \u2013 Refined Masquerade 2, Refine Bestowment 5. <b>Sensorium \u2013 Discriminating Tongue 1,Translator\u2019s Eye 1</b>. Vulcanus \u2013 Sense Flux, Sense Pyros 1, Sense Refinement 1. <b>Pandoran \u2013 Hundred Hands: Heart 3.</b><br /> <br /> Torment: When the Doctor suffers from Torment, he loses all empathy and understanding of the emotions of other beings. Any actions that result from emotional attachments confuse him and he openly holds himself apart from and superior to other beings.<br /> Disquiet: The Doctor is adept at slowing the growth of his Disquiet, but still moves around as quickly as possible, so he rarely has to deal with its more extreme manifestations. Those near him become irrational and entirely driven by their emotions and whims, becoming illogical and even deranged. His own logical approach clashes horribly with those infected and, when the Disquiet has suitably advanced, even the slightest frustration towards him will result in violence.<br /> <br /> <b>The Weeping Angels</b><br /> <br /> <b>Mockery: </b>The Silent<br /> <b>Rank: </b>3<br /> <b>Mental Attributes: </b>Intelligence 1, Wits 6, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes: </b>Strength 4, Dexterity 6, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes: </b>Presence 1, Manipulation 2, Composure 2<br /> <b>Physical Skills: </b>Athletics (Flight) 2, Brawl (Wings) 4, Stealth (Hiding in Plain Sight) 4, Survival 2<br /> <b>Social Skills: </b>Intimidation 3<br /> <b>Willpower: </b>5<br /> <b>Vice: </b>Envy<br /> <b>Initiative: </b>9<br /> <b>Defence: </b>6<br /> <b>Speed: </b>16 (20)<br /> <b>Size: </b>4<br /> <b>Health: </b>7<br /> <b>Transmutations: </b>Pandoran \u2014Bizarre Weaponry (Fangs \u2022, Bone Spurs \u2022\u2022), Scurry (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022),<br /> Flux Within the Shade (\u2022\u2022), Perfected Bezoar - Sharp Weapons (\u2022\u2022\u2022), Blunt Weapons (\u2022\u2022).<br /> <b>Bestowment: </b>Wings (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Pyros/per Turn: </b>14/3<br /> Special Ability \u2013 Blink: The Weeping Angels have an unusual relationship with Dormancy \u2013 they are less able to resist it when witnessed by a human. Mechanically, a Weeping Angel suffers a -2 on rolls to resist Dormancy before any other modifiers come into play. They may, however, reanimate as a reflexive action when they are not being looked at, provided they have Pyros in their system.<br /> <b>Attacks:</b><br /> Bite \u2013 8 (L)<br /> Wing-spurs \u2013 11 (L)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T10:44:34-08:00","id":403482,"title":"","content":"Commander Samuel Vimes from Discworld... I'd see him as a Sin-Eater probably.... His Geist is his &quot;Internal Copper&quot; that keeps him more in check and balances his Sense of Justice (Because he could very well go too far into Vengance).<br /> <br /> Captain Carrot, Either a Dhampir of a Venture or a Scion. (A Promethean Scion that is, he is generally unfazed by most things that are &quot;Weird&quot;) Born too Rule, but realizing that the world doesn't need another &quot;King&quot; he'd rather just be a good man/Copper. (You could also have him as a.. Lucifuge from Hunter... Again Born too rule, but would rather help the common folk.)<br /> <br /> Issac Clarke (Dead Space) A Human/Embed that has knowledge and is just the right size/shape for the Cog too begin the awakening of some form of Spirit/virus (Idigam Release mechanism anyone?) Eventually freed from his programming/brainwashing by a Demon that helped him overcome it.<br /> <br /> Freddy Fazbear, Bonnie, Chica and Foxy the Pirate, Pandorans... And the Security Guard is a Promethean. (Had too mention it since i've seen to many Five Nights at Freddie's Videos Lately)<br /> <br /> All i got for now.. not gonna Stat them.. but that's my ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T06:12:54-08:00","id":404419,"title":"","content":"The Doctor being True Fae makes sense. That non violence thing? must be a pact of some sort. Companions? definitely get changed. He's immortal, and tends to do things for seemingly incomprehensible reasons. He travels between worlds. He has multiple titles, but no one seems to know his real name.<br /> <br /> The G-Man from Half-Life is an Angel. He moves the pieces without appearing to do anything, almost never talking to anyone. In the middle of a chaotic invasion he doesn't seem concerned. He's able to open portals and take you to a place out of time and space. His motivations don't appear to make any sense and certainly don't appear aligned with that of mankind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":4046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","user":"xenoterracide","date":". 02-13-2015, 09:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T14:36:59-07:00","id":443122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=401396#post401396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Master Xehanort from the Kingdom Hearts franchise is a god damned, motherfucking Acanthus Scelesti. That fucker has things more planned out than Awakening's Merlin.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, the Doctor is a Psychopomp Inquisitor/Tempter. It explains why Colin Baker and Peter Capaldi show up as faces.</div> </div> </div> </div> That can work. Inspired by your comment, I made a Demon sheet for the Doctor. <br /> <br /> EDIT: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/621918-the-doctor-as-an-unchained-cipher\"><b>updated the sheet.</b></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-10-2015, 07:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T13:43:03-07:00","id":460384,"title":"","content":"<b><i>Notes</i></b><br /> These traits represent Sam and Dean during the third season of <i>Supernatural</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Dean Winchester</b><br /> <b>Virtue: </b>Loyalty \u2013 Dean is intensely loyal; he is willing to go to hell and back (literally) for his allies.<br /> <b>Vice: </b>Impulsive \u2013 Dean often makes decisions with little forethought or consideration of consequence. <br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 3, Stamina 4<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 2, Brawl 4, Crafts 2 (Automobiles, Explosives), Drive 3, Firearms 3(Pistol, Shotgun), Intimidate 2, Investigation 2, Larceny 3, Medicine 1(First Aid), Occult 2(Banes, Demons, Exorcism), Persuasion 3 (Seduction), Science 1, Subterfuge 2 (Disguise), Stealth 3, Streetwise 3, Survival 2, Weaponry 3(Knife)<br /> <b>Endowments: </b>Benediction 1 (Vade Retro Satana)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Allies 2 (Hunters), Area of Expertise (Automobiles, Banes), Barfly, Cheap Shot, Close Quarter Combat 2, Contacts 2 (Prior Cases), Crack Driver 2, Cursed, Defensive Combat (Brawl), Eye for the Strange, Fame 1 (Hunters), Fast Reflexes 2, Fast Talking 1, Firefight 1, Hardy 2, Improvised Weaponry 1, Iron Skin 2, Iron Stamina 2, Iron Will, Library 2 (John Winchesters Journal; Occult), Light Weapons 3, Martial Arts 2, Mentor 3 (Bobby Singer), Professional Training 3 (Hunter; Larceny, Occult, Weaponry), Quick Draw (Pistols), Safe Place 2, Sleight of Hand, Small Unit Tactics, Street Fighting 3, Striking Looks 2, Strong Back, Tolerance for Biology, Trained Observer<br /> <b>Special Merits: </b>Ward Tattoo (Dean is marked with a tattoo that prevents the Possess or Claim conditions)<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 5<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 7<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 8<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 7<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 1 vs. Bashing<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 11<br /> <b>Health:</b> 9<br /> <b>Condition: </b>Connected (Hunters), Obsession (Protecting Sam)<br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Sam Winchester</b><br /> <b>Virtue: </b>Empathy \u2013 Sam connects with people easily, and seeks to understand people before making any judgments.<br /> <b>Vice: </b>Stubborn \u2013 Once Sam has decided on a course of action, he is loath to change it.<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 3, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 4<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 2(Law, Research), Athletics 2, Brawl 3, Computers 3, Crafts 1, Empathy 2(Trust), Firearms 3(Pistol), Intimidate 1, Investigation 3, Larceny 1, Medicine 1, Occult 2(Demons, Exorcism, Urban Legends), Persuasion 2, Science 1, Streetwise 1, Subterfuge 2 (Disguise), Stealth 2, Survival 1, Weaponry 2<br /> <b>Endowments: </b>Benediction 2 (Blessed Protection, Vade Retro Satana)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Allies 2 (Hunters), Allies 2 (Ruby), Area of Expertise (Exorcism, Research), Close Quarter Combat 1, Common Sense, Contacts 1 (Prior Cases), Danger Sense, Defensive Combat (Brawl), Direction Sense, Eye for the Strange, Fame 1 (Hunters), Fast Reflexes 1, Firefight 1, Fleet of Foot 1, Good Time Management, Improvised Weaponry 2, Language (Latin), Library 1 (Occult), Light Weapons 2, Martial Arts 2, Mentor 3 (Bobby Singer), Professional Training 2 (Hunter; Investigation, Occult, Weaponry), Quick Draw (Pistols), Safe Place 2, Street Fighting 2, Striking Looks 2, Sympathetic, Tolerance for Biology, Trained Observer, Unseen Sense (Demons)<br /> <b>Special Merits: </b>Ward Tattoo (Sam is marked with a tattoo that prevents the Possess or Claim conditions)<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 6<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 7<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 8<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 12<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <b>Conditions: </b>Connected (Hunters), Obsession (Saving Dean)<br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Relic: The Colt </b><b>\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</b><br /> \u201cThe Colt\u201d is a heavy revolver made by Samuel Colt in 1835. When used with the supernatural bullets made specifically for it, the gun can kill nearly any supernatural being.<br /> The blessed rounds fired by the Colt are a deadly bane to any supernatural being. Against Supernatural targets, the weapon deals 4 aggravated damage with the Rote quality, and bypasses any armor or damage reducing abilities the target might have (even to targets in Twilight). Even creatures that might otherwise be immortal can be destroyed permanently by the Colt.<br /> <b>Damage</b>: 2L (against mortals) <b>Initiative:</b> -2 <b>Capacity:</b> 6 <b>Range: </b>20/40/80<br /> <br /> <b>Relic: The Impala </b><b>\u25cf\u25cf</b><br /> Dean\u2019s 1967 Chevrolet Impala does not technically have any supernatural or unusual properties, but means far more to the Winchester\u2019s than just a mode of transport. The Impala has the <i>Battery of Will</i> ability (Reliquary, pg. 88). This ability may only be used by Sam or Dean. To anyone else, the Impala is just a sweet ride.<br /> <br /> <b>Relic: Ruby\u2019s Knife </b><b>\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</b><br /> Given to the Winchester\u2019s by the demon known as Ruby, the knife has properties that allow it to slay demons.<br /> Against Demons and those Possessed or Claimed by demons (similar to the type detailed in <i>Inferno)</i>, the weapon deals 3 damage, has the 8-again quality, and is considered a Bane (dealing Aggravated Damage and bypassing any Armor or other damage reducing abilities). Some high ranked Demons have been known to resist the effect of the knife, but they remain thankfully rare.<br /> <b>Damage</b>: 1L (against mortals) <b>Initiative:</b> -1<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T13:49:24-07:00","id":460391,"title":"","content":"That's fun, Reigninhell. If you've got any more in your brain, please share!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T13:57:49-07:00","id":460394,"title":"","content":"ok! - another dynamic duo -<br /> <br /> <b><i>Notes</i></b><br /> These traits represent Walter and Jesse during the third season of <i>Breaking Bad</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Walter White</b><br /> <b>Virtue: </b>Paternal \u2013 Walter goes to great lengths to protect those he cares about, even from himself.<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Greedy \u2013 The more Walter achieves, the more he wants.<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 5, Wits 3, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 2, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 4, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 3(Teaching), Crafts 2(Explosives), Drive 2, Empathy 2(Teaching), Firearms 1, Intimidation 2(Heisenberg), Medicine 1(Poison), Persuasion 2(Logic), Politics 2, Science 4 (Chemistry), Stealth 2, Streetwise 1(Drugs), Subterfuge 3(Lies), Weaponry 1 (Improvised)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Allies 3 (Gus Fring), Allies 2 (Saul Goodman), Alternate Identity 1(Heisenberg), Area of Expertise (Chemistry, Lies), Common Sense, Encyclopedic Knowledge (Science), Good Time Management, Interdisciplinary Specialty (Chemistry), Patient, Professional Training 5 (Scientist; Academics, Crafts, Science), Pusher, Resources 3, Tolerance for Biology<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 5<br /> <b>Willpower: </b>7<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 5<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 2<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 9<br /> <b>Health:</b> 7<br /> <b>Conditions: </b>Embarrassing Secret<b> (</b>Heisenberg), Leveraged (Gus)<br /> -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <b>Jesse Pinkman</b><br /> <b>Virtue: </b>Compassionate \u2013 Jesse has a big heart, and creates emotional attachments easily.<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Na\u00efve \u2013 Jesse continually underestimates the depths to which others will sink to.<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 4, Resolve 2<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 2, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 1, Athletics 2, Brawl 1, Crafts 2, Empathy 3, Drive 1, Expression 1(Drawing), Firearms 2, Larceny 2(B&amp;E), Persuasion 2, Politics 1(Criminal), Science 2 (Cooking Meth), Socialize 2, Stealth 2, Streetwise 3(Drug Dealing), Subterfuge 2 (Alibi), Weaponry 1<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Allies 2 (Saul Goodman), Area of Expertise (Cooking Meth, Drug Dealing), Contacts 2(Addicts, Drug Dealers), Danger Sense, Fast Talking 2, Fixer, Fleet of Foot 1, Hardy 2, Interdisciplinary Specialty (Drug Dealing), Iron Stamina 1, Language (Spanish), Professional Training 3 (Criminal; Larceny, Persuasion, Streetwise), Staff 1 (Small-Time Dealers; Streetwise), Sympathetic<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 5<br /> <b>Willpower: </b>5<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 6<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 5<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 11<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <b>Conditions: </b>Addicted (Heroin), Connected (Drug Dealers), Guilty, Leveraged (Mr. White), Notoriety (Criminal)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T10:06:07-07:00","id":461147,"title":"","content":"<b>Dexter </b>(of the TV show of the same name) is a Sin-Eater, of the Torn Threshold and the Reaper archetype, who's Geist, the Dark Passenger, has a strange sense of 'honour' and masquerades as his beloved father-figure.<br /> <br /> <b>Will Graham</b> (from the Hannibal TV series) is a Mastigos of the Guardians of the Veil, mind twisted by too much use of Goetic magic - his specialty in taking on the vices of the criminals he hunts to learn more about them, but each time tattering his mind a little more.<br /> <br /> <b>Hannibal </b>(from the same show) is a Demon, a Messenger Tempter who found the more... visceral delights of the world far too tempting to leave, and now hides in plain sight as he indulges his new-found nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T04:09:34-07:00","id":462085,"title":"","content":"As the DtD core gives &quot;Person of Interest&quot; as an inspiration source, listing Harold as a Psychopomp Inquisitor and John as a Destroyer Saboteur (though I'd argue one with slight antinomian tendencies; he doesn't full on reject his Destroyer origins like a pacifist Antinomian, but he's definitely trying to be more of a &quot;Guardian&quot; than a straight up Destroyer - contrast with Shah for someone with no qualms are about her Destroyer Incarnation).... I did have to think through a couple of other characters, most notably a Messenger Tempter who transitions to an Integrator (either of those can be paired with Inquisitor as well, but the transition from Tempter to Integrator is central). I'm thinking Virtue: Ruthless, Vice: Compassionate for her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T10:42:37-07:00","id":470245,"title":"","content":"<br /> These stats represent Dipper Pines and Mabel Pines from &quot;Gravity Falls&quot;, as normal humans. Should they be Hunters, they could belong to the Union. Should they be supernaturals, Dipper would be a Mastigos Mage, and Mabel would be an Acanthus Mage. Both would likely belong to the Mysterium.<br /> <br /> <b>Name</b>: Dipper Pines<br /> <b>Virtue</b>: Wise<br /> <b>Vice</b>: Curious<br /> <b>Concept</b>: Logical Adventurer<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 4, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 1, Dexterity 4, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 2, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics (Logic) 3, Crafts 2, Computer 2, Medicine 1, Occult (Cryptids) 3, Politics 1, Investigation (Clues, Puzzles, Riddles) 4, Science 2<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics (Running) 2, Brawl 3, Drive 1, Larceny 2, Stealth 3, Survival 1, Weaponry 3<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken 1, Empathy 2, Expression (Lamby Lamby Dance, Sousaphone) 2, Intimidation 1, Persuasion 3, Socialize 2, Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 3<br /> <br /> <b>Skill Tricks:</b> Quick Cram (Academics), Always Investigating (Investigation), Pattern Expert (Investigation), Myth Expert (Occult), Occam\u2019s Razor (Science)<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area of Expertise (Cryptids, Clues), Striking Looks +1, Eye For The Strange, Trained Observer 3, Encyclopedic Knowledge, Common Sense, Danger Sense, Direction Sense, Fast Reflexes 2, Fleet of Foot 3, Fighting Finesse, True Friend (Mabel), Allies (Soos, Wendy, Grunkle Stan)<br /> <br /> <b>Flaws</b>: Thinks Too Logically<br /> <br /> <b>Derangements:</b> None<br /> <br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 4<br /> <b>Initiative Mod:</b> 9<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 10<br /> <b>Conviction:</b> 6<br /> <b>Integrity</b>: 7<br /> <br /> <b>Name:</b> Mabel Pines<br /> <b>Virtue: </b>Optimistic<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Naive<br /> <b>Concept:</b> Cheerful Adventurer<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes: </b>Intelligence 3, Wits 4, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 1, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics (Art) 2, Crafts (Knitting, Sculpting) 4, Computer 2, Medicine 1, Occult (Cryptids) 3, Politics 1, Investigation 2, Science 1<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics (Running) 2, Brawl 2, Firearms (Grappling Hook) 2, Larceny (Lock-Picking) 2, Stealth 3, Survival 1, Weaponry 3<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken 3, Empathy 3, Expression (Dancing) 2, Intimidation 1, Persuasion 3, Socialize 3, Streetwise 2<br /> <br /> <b>Skill Tricks:</b> Trick Shot (Firearms), Whisperer (Animal Ken), All Doors Open (Larceny), Improvised Tools (Crafts), Fire Up The Crowd (Expression)<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area of Expertise (Cryptids, Sculpting), Striking Looks +1, Eye For The Strange, Danger Sense, Fast Reflexes 2, Fleet of Foot 3, Fighting Finesse, True Friend (Dipper), Allies (Soos, Wendy, Grunkle Stan)<br /> <br /> <b>Flaws:</b> Easily Distracted<br /> <br /> <b>Derangements:</b> None<br /> <br /> <b>Health</b>: 8<br /> <b>Willpower</b>: 6<br /> <b>Defense</b>: 3<br /> <b>Initiative Mod:</b> 8<br /> <b>Speed</b>: 9<br /> <b>Conviction</b>: 6<br /> <b>Integrity</b>: 7","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-06-2015, 07:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T11:28:20-07:00","id":470286,"title":"","content":"Dipper would probably be a Network Zero member waiting to happen, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T16:07:24-07:00","id":477369,"title":"","content":"<b>Freddy Krueger </b><br /> <b>Rank:</b> 3 [Ghost]<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 8, Finesse 8, Resistance 6<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 20<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 14<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 8<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 21<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 11<br /> <b>Influences:</b> Nightmares 4<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Freddy is wounded by virtue. Characters fighting Freddy who have regained willpower from their virtue gain a +2 bonus to all dice rolls, resistance traits and Armor against Freddy for the remainder of the scene.<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Fire<br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Fetter, Possess, Unfetter, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Aggressive Meme, Dement, Hallucination, Phantom Arsenal, Seek, Telekinesis<br /> <br /> <i><b>Notes</b></i><br /> <i>I am using the character as depicted in the original A Nightmare on Elm Street series (primarily 1 -3).</i><br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Jason Voorhees </b><br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 1, Wits 2, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 6, Dexterity 3, Stamina 6<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 4, Manipulation 1, Composure 5<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 3 (Pursuit), Brawl 3(Choke), Crafts 2, Firearms 2, Larceny 2, Intimidation 4 (Silent), Stealth 4(Ambush, Forest), Survival 3(Tracking), Weaponry 4<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Atavism, Choke Hold, Direction Sense, Giant, Heavy Weapons Style 3, Improvised Weaponry Style 1, Iron Stamina 3<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Size:</b> 6<br /> <b>Initiative: </b> 8<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 1/1<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 14<br /> <b>Health:</b> 11<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers/ Talents &amp; Frailties</b><br /> <br /> <b>Blinded by Blood: </b>All Perception rolls made by Jason suffer a \u20133 penalty. On any opposed rolls made to notice a hiding opponent, ties always go to the opponent.<br /> <br /> <b>Crushing Blow: </b>1w; All bashing damage that Jason deals with his body (fist, foot, head, elbow, whatever) is instead done as lethal damage. This power lasts until the end of the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>No Mind but for Murder: </b>Jason cannot speak, write or generate language in any meaningful way. He might be able to indicate a direction or intent to kill with a nod of the head or a wave of the knife, but complicated gestures are beyond him.<br /> <br /> <b>Revivify </b><b>\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</b>: 1w; Stamina + Survival + Revivify. Jason can use this power to return from the dead, provided his entire health track isn\u2019t full of aggravated damage. Successes heal two bashing or one lethal damage each. On an exceptional success Jason rises fully healed of <i>all </i>damage, aggravated or otherwise.<br /> <br /> <b>Unholy Stamina </b><b>\u25cf\u25cf</b>: 1w; Add +3 to Stamina until the end of the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Unholy Strength</b> <b>\u25cf\u25cf</b>:1w; Add +2 to Stamina until the end of the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Unstoppable Killing Machine: </b>Jason does not suffer wound penalties and does not need to check for unconsciousness when his Health track fills with bashing damage. He does not need sleep, food or air. Every successful attack made on Jason inflicts one point of damage, no matter how many successes are actually rolled. This includes supernatural attacks. Incidental damage (falling, electrocution, drowning, fire) inflicts its usual damage.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Notes</i></b><br /> <i>This write up is Jason as he appeared in the Friday the 13th series (primarily 3, 4, and 6)<br /> Jason is ungodly strong and tough, and has taken a degree of injury that would have killed anyone else several times over\u2026 and that was before he became undead. Jason is developmentally disabled and therefore has low intelligence and manipulation, while his stature and demeanor give him a high presence. Jason is relentless and remorseless, and though he has proven vulnerable to trickery, he largely remains focused on his single minded rampage. Systems wise, Jason is the archetypal Mask Undertaking Slasher, with a collection of Dread Powers to augment his abilities further.</i><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T16:37:14-07:00","id":477378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=477369#post477369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Freddy Krueger </b><br /> <b>Rank:</b> 3 [Ghost]<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 8, Finesse 8, Resistance 6<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 20<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 14<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 8<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 21<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 11<br /> <b>Influences:</b> Nightmares 4<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Freddy is wounded by virtue. Characters fighting Freddy who have regained willpower from their virtue gain a +2 bonus to all dice rolls, resistance traits and Armor against Freddy for the remainder of the scene.<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Fire<br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Fetter, Possess, Unfetter, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Aggressive Meme, Dement, Hallucination, Phantom Arsenal, Seek, Telekinesis<br /> <br /> <i><b>Notes</b></i><br /> <i>I am using the character as depicted in the original A Nightmare on Elm Street series (primarily 1 -3).</i><br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Jason Voorhees </b><br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 1, Wits 2, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 6, Dexterity 3, Stamina 6<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 4, Manipulation 1, Composure 5<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 3 (Pursuit), Brawl 3(Choke), Crafts 2, Firearms 2, Larceny 2, Intimidation 4 (Silent), Stealth 4(Ambush, Forest), Survival 3(Tracking), Weaponry 4<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Atavism, Choke Hold, Direction Sense, Giant, Heavy Weapons Style 3, Improvised Weaponry Style 1, Iron Stamina 3<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Size:</b> 6<br /> <b>Initiative: </b> 8<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 1/1<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 14<br /> <b>Health:</b> 11<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers/ Talents &amp; Frailties</b><br /> <br /> <b>Blinded by Blood: </b>All Perception rolls made by Jason suffer a \u20133 penalty. On any opposed rolls made to notice a hiding opponent, ties always go to the opponent.<br /> <br /> <b>Crushing Blow: </b>1w; All bashing damage that Jason deals with his body (fist, foot, head, elbow, whatever) is instead done as lethal damage. This power lasts until the end of the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>No Mind but for Murder: </b>Jason cannot speak, write or generate language in any meaningful way. He might be able to indicate a direction or intent to kill with a nod of the head or a wave of the knife, but complicated gestures are beyond him.<br /> <br /> <b>Revivify </b><b>\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</b>: 1w; Stamina + Survival + Revivify. Jason can use this power to return from the dead, provided his entire health track isn\u2019t full of aggravated damage. Successes heal two bashing or one lethal damage each. On an exceptional success Jason rises fully healed of <i>all </i>damage, aggravated or otherwise.<br /> <br /> <b>Unholy Stamina </b><b>\u25cf\u25cf</b>: 1w; Add +3 to Stamina until the end of the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Unholy Strength</b> <b>\u25cf\u25cf</b>:1w; Add +2 to Stamina until the end of the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Unstoppable Killing Machine: </b>Jason does not suffer wound penalties and does not need to check for unconsciousness when his Health track fills with bashing damage. He does not need sleep, food or air. Every successful attack made on Jason inflicts one point of damage, no matter how many successes are actually rolled. This includes supernatural attacks. Incidental damage (falling, electrocution, drowning, fire) inflicts its usual damage.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Notes</i></b><br /> <i>This write up is Jason as he appeared in the Friday the 13th series (primarily 3, 4, and 6)<br /> Jason is ungodly strong and tough, and has taken a degree of injury that would have killed anyone else several times over\u2026 and that was before he became undead. Jason is developmentally disabled and therefore has low intelligence and manipulation, while his stature and demeanor give him a high presence. Jason is relentless and remorseless, and though he has proven vulnerable to trickery, he largely remains focused on his single minded rampage. Systems wise, Jason is the archetypal Mask Undertaking Slasher, with a collection of Dread Powers to augment his abilities further.</i><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Excellent write ups! Much better than the True Fae versions I wrote elsewhere. Only one problem: Freddy needs to be Rank 4 before he can have Influence (Nightmares) 4. If you make him Rank 4, I'd suggest raising either Power or Resistance. I'd also give him the Avernian Gate Manifestation as well as the Regenerate Numen. Finally, he'd have the Cunning Virtue, Sadistic Vice, and Integrity 0. Jason should have Heavy Weapons 5, Frenzied Assault 5, Health 12, the Implacable Virtue, Vengeful Vice and Integrity 0 (maybe Integrity 1, depending on how self-aware he really is)..<br /> <br /> I'd also use these ephemeral being house rules:<br /> <br /> Normal Attack = Power + Rank<br /> <br /> Willpower = Resistance + Rank (max 10)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Maximum Essence / Per Turn = Rank x 10/Rank x 3</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Initiative = Finesse + Resistance/2 round up</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Defense = Finesse + Rank/2 round up (max 10)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Speed = highest between Power and Finesse + Rank</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Corpus = Size + Resistance, as before<br /> <br /> Thus, if Freddy had Power 9, Finesse 7 and Resistance 12, he would have Willpower 10, Max Essence 40, Max Essence Per Turn 12, Initiative 10, Defense 6, Speed 13 and Corpus 17. Seems more balanced to me.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-11-2015, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T21:13:11-07:00","id":477486,"title":"","content":"<b>RE: Freddy &amp; Jason</b><br /> <br /> Thanks for the feedback. I had forgotten that influence was capped by rank. But even then I would be inclined to keep Freddy at a Rank 3 (which i think are consistent with his abilities in the first 3 films). Rank 4 (more appropriate to the later films) Freddy would be beyond a normal mortals ability to deal with (even with knowledge of his weaknesses).<br /> But your virtue/vice assessments are spot on. The only thing I disagree on Integrity - a ghosts Integrity is fixed at the level it was when they were alive.Freddy was a serial killer who was taking frequent breaking points for killing, but was together enough to keep his activities well hidden for a long time - I would peg him at a Integrity 4.<br /> <br /> As for Jason, I tried to restrain myself a bit. It would be too easy to give him every combat merit at 5 and call it good, but I went over the movies (particularly 3and 4, when he was still &quot;mortal&quot;, and 6 (when he became an undead killing machine). That being said, after looking at the Heavy Weapons and Frenzied Assault Merits, Jason having 5 in each would not be inappropriate (campers beware).<br /> <br /> Once again, we are in agreement on the Virtue/Vice for Jason, but Integrity 0/1 feels like a poor mainly (mainly because Jason may not be human enough for something like Integrity to be applied).<br /> Its a question that I think may be answered with Hunter 2nd edition. Many of the slasher rules were tied to Morality, and Integrity operates different on both a mechanical and thematic level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T04:37:41-07:00","id":477793,"title":"","content":"I decided to make stats for the Slender Man, as a God-Machine Angel.<br /> <br /> Programming: Psychopomp<br /> <br /> Virtue: Hidden<br /> <br /> Vice: Observant<br /> <br /> Rank: 5<br /> <br /> Attributes: Power 15, Finesse 9, Resistance 12<br /> <br /> Corpus: 20 (Size 8)<br /> <br /> Willpower: 10<br /> <br /> Defense: 7<br /> <br /> Initiative Mod: 11<br /> <br /> Speed: 20<br /> <br /> Max Essence/Per Turn: 50/15<br /> <br /> Influence: Perceptions 5, Sigma Radiation 5<br /> <br /> Manifestation: Twilight Form, Materialize, Avernian Gateway, Shadow Gateway, Astral Sojourn<br /> <br /> Ban: the Slender Man is immensely powerful, but he is constrained by the power of the human mind. At the start of each chapter (game session), the Slender Man uses the Aggressive Meme Numen, spreading an evolving mythos about itself to the people of the region. If he steps out of the rules of this mythos, he is reduced to Power 1, Finesse 1 and Resistance 1 (with decreased Advantages) and loses access to Numina, Influences and Manifestations for one scene. The rules must be reasonably coherent in the consciousnesses of the people in the region.<br /> <br /> Bane: anyone who was taken by the Slender Man to a Facility, reconfigured for the God-Machine, reclaimed their original configuration and returned to their home will deal aggravated damage to the Slender Man with all Brawl, Weaponry and Firearms rolls.<br /> <br /> Numina: Aggressive Meme, <a href=\"http://thereachmux.org/wiki/Numina/House_Rules\" target=\"_blank\">Ephemeral Weapon, Ephemeral Armor,</a> Essence Thief, Regenerate, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/480962-ephemeral-being-house-rules-new-epic-numen\">Mirage</a>, Speed","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-18-2015, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T08:44:39-07:00","id":477969,"title":"","content":"an old favorite -<br /> <br /> <b>Alien/Xenomorph Warrior</b><br /> Xenomorphs are terrifying opponents. They are fast, strong, and tough, bristling with natural weapons, including claws, two sets of jaws, spear like tail, and corrosive blood. The entire gruesome package is wrapped in a durable exoskeleton and guided by savage instincts that seem bent on expanding the colony and consuming everything in their path. They operate much like social insects, with larva, drones, warriors, and a Queen all operate as a part of a hive-like collective.<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 1, Wits 3, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 4, Dexterity 5, Stamina 4<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 1, Composure 2<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 3(Climbing), Brawl 3 (bite/claw), Crafts 2 (Resin), Intimidation 3, Larceny 2, Stealth 4, Survival 4<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Fast Reflexes 3, Fleet of Foot 2, Hardy 2<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 10<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 8<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 2/1<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 19 (Species Factor 8)<br /> <b>Health:</b> 9<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers </b><br /> <br /> <b>Agility:</b> The Xenomorphs are fast and mobile. They can scale across walls and ceilings with ease (of course, they are still affected by gravity and are limited to structures than can support their weight). They may squeeze through narrow spaces as if they were one size level smaller (Humanoid Incubated Aliens are Size 5). In addition, they can leap 4 times as far as a human.<br /> <br /> <b>Animalistic:</b> Xenomorphs are guided by instinct and operate on the level of exceptionally clever animals. They may even figure out rudimentary uses of simple devices but anything more complicated is beyond them. They communicate with each other with a complex series of pheromone signals and their vocalizations consist primarily of shrieks, hisses and growls. The creature\u2019s instincts allow it to use the <i>Higher</i> of Wits or Dexterity for Defense.<br /> <br /> <b>Carapace:</b> Xenomorph\u2019s are covered in a durable, glassy exoskeleton. They are considered to have Armor 2/1. Xenomorph\u2019s do not suffer wound penalties and do not fall unconscious until their rightmost health box is filled with lethal damage. Their dark coloration gives them an additional +2 dice to Stealth rolls made under cover of darkness or in poor lighting. The armor bonus granted from their Carapace does not apply to injuries caused by fire or extreme heat.<br /> <br /> <b>Fearless:</b> The Xenomorphs mindset does not recognize fear in most situation and they are immune to any fear causing supernatural compulsion. Likewise, any method of supernatural coercion that works on humans or animals automatically fails as well. If successfully intimidated by mundane means, the Xenomorph will retreat and more than likely stage another attack at a later time. The only thing that seems to honestly frighten the creatures is fire (see further down).<br /> <br /> <b>Natural Weapons:</b> The Xenomorph makes use of several distinct natural weapons<br /> <br /> <i>Bite/Claws:</i> The Xenomorph can attack interchangeably with their claws and mandibles, treating either as a +0 weapon attack.<br /> <br /> <i>Corrosive Viscera:</i> The Xenomorph\u2019s blood is incredibly corrosive. Any creature or object that comes in contact with the substance is damaged as if burned by Bunsen burner (+2 damage). The corrosive blood of a Xenomorph is considered to have Armor Piercing 2.<br /> <br /> <i>Mandible:</i> Xenomorphs have a secondary set of jaws, which lashes out with incredible speed and force. The additional power allows the mandible to punch through armored resistance. This is a +1 weapon attack with Armor Piercing 2.<br /> <br /> <i>Tail Barb:</i> The Xenomorphs long whip-like tail ends in a sharp barb. This is a +2 weapon attack with Armor Piercing 1.<br /> <br /> <b>Resin:</b> Xenomorphs can secrete a durable, sticky resin. They use this resin to create hive like structures or cocoon victims to be eaten or impregnated with larvae at a later time. This substance has a Durability of 2 and a xenomorph can create an amount of Resin equal to its size every 24 hours (with regular meals).<br /> <br /> <b>Senses:</b> The creature\u2019s sensory organs are shielded behind the transparent carapace of its face. It can see effectively in pure darkness and has a keen sense of smell.<br /> <br /> <b>Vulnerability:</b> The creatures fear fire; they must make a (Resolve +Composure \u2013 (Size of the Fire)) roll to approach an open flame. Characters brandishing open fire as a weapon gain a +2 equipment bonus to Intimidate checks against a Xenomorph.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T02:43:21-07:00","id":480029,"title":"","content":"For your viewing pleasure, here are two of the most famous monsters from the SCP Foundation: SCP-076-2 (Able) and SCP-682 (The Hard To Destroy Reptile).<br /> <br /> EDIT: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-the-nwod?p=842241#post842241\"><b>I updated the sheets.</b></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 03-04-2016, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T08:56:28-07:00","id":482429,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Updated <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1019276#post1019276\"><b>Jackie Estacado's sheet</b></a>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-19-2016, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T23:45:28-07:00","id":483234,"title":"","content":"Alex Mercer (Prototype): a Gangrel scientist hired by a genetic research corporation controlled by the Ordo Dracul. The owners of the corporation seek to take the vampire curse to its full militaristic potential. His research leads him into finding and experimenting with a Strix called &quot;The Blacklight&quot;, giving it the power to infect and spread beyond what any other Strix can. When he learned that the employees of the corporation where being killed by Hunters to cover the research up, Alex took the Strix, bound into a vial of blood, and unleashed it into the world.<br /> <br /> Infected Alex Mercer:<br /> <br /> Shadow Potency: 10<br /> <br /> Max Vitae/Per Turn: 75/15<br /> <br /> Vice: Proliferate<br /> <br /> Attributes: Power 10, Finesse 6, Resistance 8<br /> <br /> Host Attributes: Strength 6, Dexterity 4, Stamina 5<br /> <br /> Skills: Academics 3, Crafts 3, Computer 3, Medicine 3, Occult 3, Politics 1, Investigation 5, Science 5, Athletics 5, Brawl 5, Drive 3, Firearms 3, Larceny 3, Stealth 3, Survival 3, Weaponry 5, Empathy 3, Expression 1, Intimidation 5, Persuasion 3, Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 4<br /> <br /> Corpus: 14 (Size 6)<br /> <br /> Host Health: 10<br /> <br /> Willpower: 10<br /> <br /> Defense: 4 + Athletics/Brawl/Weaponry<br /> <br /> Initiative Mod: 14<br /> <br /> Speed: 15<br /> <br /> Dread Powers:<br /> <br /> Doom \u2013 See The Cracks, Web Of Destiny<br /> Host \u2013 Breath Eater, Hollow Bones<br /> Shadow \u2013 Sudden Surprise<br /> Vitae \u2013 Indomitable, Kindred Disciplines x 4<br /> <br /> Disciplines: Protean 5, Resilience 5, Vigor 5, Celerity 5, Obfuscate 4, Auspex 3, Nightmare 2<br /> <br /> Devotions: Body Of Will, Force Of Nature, Juggernaut\u2019s Gait, Hint Of Fear, Shatter The Shroud, Abominable Weaponry, Abominable Armor, One Drop Great Mending (Advanced), Relentless Mauling (Advanced), Quicken Sight, The Blacklight Virus<br /> <br /> Embodiments: Shadow Form, Possess Corpse, Possess Revenant, Possess Kindred, Possess Living, Synthesis, Materialize, Enter Twilight, Shadow Jump, Dark Places<br /> <br /> Banes: up to the ST.<br /> <br /> Abominable Weaponry (Vigor 5, Protean 4)<br /> <br /> The Kindred who possess this Devotion are not to be trifled with. They can manifest truly horrible natural weapons.<br /> <br /> Cost: 10 Vitae<br /> Dice Pool: None<br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> <br /> The Kindred grows thrashing, barbed tendrils from all over his body, changes his hands into humongous claws or his arm into a steel piercing sword and so on. He may make Brawl or Weaponry attacks that have a +2A damage bonus and Armor Piercing 4 for the rest of the scene. Resilience offers no protection against this Devotion, but a related Devotion does (see below). This Devotion costs 5 Experiences.<br /> <br /> Abominable Armor (Resilience 5, Protean 4)<br /> <br /> The Kindred who possess this Devotion are hard to take down. They can manifest very persistent natural armor.<br /> <br /> Cost: 10 Vitae<br /> Dice Pool: None<br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> <br /> The Kindred applies his Resilience as Armor against all attacks (including the previous Devotion) for the remainder of the scene, but he is covered in some obvious protection: chitin or bone plates, jagged obsidian or crystallized blood. This Devotion costs 5 Experiences.<br /> <br /> One Drop, Great Mending (Vigor 3, Resilience 3, Celerity 3)<br /> <br /> The Kindred\u2019s Vitae is more efficient at regenerating his undead body than usual.<br /> <br /> Cost: None<br /> Dice Pool: None<br /> Action: None (always active)<br /> <br /> Every point of Vitae heals 2 lethal or 3 bashing. Healing 1 aggravated only costs 3 Vitae. This Devotion costs 3 Experiences. There is an advanced version which requires Vigor 4, Resilience 4, Celerity 4 and Blood Potency 6. This version makes each Vitae heal 3 lethal, and allows you to heal 1 aggravated with 3 Vitae and no sleeping. The advanced version costs 6 Experiences.<br /> <br /> Relentless Mauling (Vigor 3, Resilience 3, Celerity 3)<br /> <br /> The Kindred can strike multiple foes in one turn.<br /> <br /> Cost: 3 Vitae or 5 Vitae (Advanced)<br /> Dice Pool: None<br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> <br /> Upon a successful Brawl or Weaponry attack, double the amount of total points of damage dealt and divide them between two or more targets. Each target may only receive as much damage as your base successes. Example: your vampire grows natural weapons by using Predatory Aspect, Unnatural Aspect, Abominable Aspect or some other power. Let\u2019s say you get 3 successes and your weapon has a damage bonus of 2. [3 + 2] x 2 = 10 points of damage to be distributed, but each target may only receive up to 3 points of damage. This Devotion costs 3 Experiences. The advanced version requires Vigor 5, Resilience 5 and Celerity 5, which quadruples your total success before division. The advanced version costs 6 Experiences.<br /> <br /> The Blacklight Virus (Protean 5, Vigor 5, Resilience 5, Celerity 5, Blacklight)<br /> <br /> The Strix known as Blacklight has been infused into a viral medium that is much faster than anything it could accomplish on its own. The Blacklight Virus spreads through contact with infected blood, turning victims into Draugr, huge Larvae with natural weapons and other blasphemies against nature. Only occasionally does the Blacklight Virus turn a victim into a Kindred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-19-2015, 02:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T09:33:51-07:00","id":486473,"title":"","content":"Bat Family: Hunters and/or Geniuses. Batman himself is either Klagen or Grimm.<br /> <br /> Joker: Klagen Genius or Maniac Slasher.<br /> <br /> Scarecrow: Grimm Genius or Maniac Slasher.<br /> <br /> Riddler: Neid Genius.<br /> <br /> Mr. Freeze: Legend Slasher or Grimm Genius.<br /> <br /> Poison Ivy: Grimm Genius or Thyrsus Mage.<br /> <br /> Two Face: Legend Slasher.<br /> <br /> Killer Croc: Mutant Slasher or Makara Beast.<br /> <br /> Penguin: Grimm Genius.<br /> <br /> Bane: Hoffnung Genius or epic mortal with access to Thaumatechnology..<br /> <br /> Catwoman: mortal, albeit extremely skilled at what she does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T13:49:08-07:00","id":491934,"title":"","content":"The ponies and other creatures from &quot;My Little Pony: Friendship Is Magic&quot; can be adapted to the NWOD in two ways. If they are straight up mystical, intelligent anmals, they are hobgoblins living in a massive Hedge Kingdom (NOT an Arcadian Realm). The Princesses and major antagonists are elder hobgoblins with access to Contracts that have Archmage level effects.<br /> <br /> If they are adapted as humans, they'd work nicely as Mages. Their &quot;Cutie Marks&quot; are actually their Nimbuses. Of note is that all major antagonists in the series so far wanted power. An interesting finale for Mage FiM would be the Mane Six teaming up with Discord and the Princesses against a pony equivalent of an Aswadim (Scelestus Archmage). This finale is not likely to happen in the original FiM anytime soon, as it would go against Hasbro's interests to keep the series going on for as long as it can.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 50px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 5px; padding: 1px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Character</span></b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 5px; padding: 1px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Path</span></b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 5px; padding: 1px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Order</span></b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 5px; padding: 1px\">Twilight</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 5px; padding: 1px\">Obrimos</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 5px; padding: 1px\">Mysterium</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 5px; padding: 1px\">Pinkie</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 5px; padding: 1px\">Acanthus</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 5px; padding: 1px\">Free Council</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 5px; padding: 1px\">Applejack</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 5px; padding: 1px\">Thyrsus</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 5px; padding: 1px\">Adamantine Arrow</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 5px; padding: 1px\">Rarity</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 5px; padding: 1px\">Moros</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 5px; padding: 1px\">Silver Ladder</td> </tr> <tr 