height: 50px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Character</span></b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Type</span></b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Sub-type</span></b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Faction</span></b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Notes</span></b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Sub-zero</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mage</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Moros</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Adamantine Arrow</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Uses Forces/Matter to redirect heat and create ice.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Scorpion</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mage</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mastigos</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Apostate</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Gains attack bonuses when uncloaking his Nimbus.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Reptile</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mage</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Thyrsus</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Seers Of The Throne</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Uses Life to gain his powers of acid spit/natural weaponry/long tongue and Forces for his chi blasts/invisibility.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Baraka</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Beast</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Namtaru</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Tyrant</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Expert user of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=230692#post230692\">Claws Of The Motherfucker.</a></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Shokans And Centaurians</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Pandorans</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Torch- born</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Seers Of The Throne</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Have been blessed through the Practice of Excision by Shao Khan so that they do not suffer from Dormancy and can regain Pyros by fighting non-Prometheans.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Cyrax</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mortal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Hunter</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Task Force: Valkyrie</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">A whole lot of money went into his Endowments. they can tell you that much.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Sektor</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Genius</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Grimm</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Rogue</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Used the Endowments he received from Valkyrie as inspiration for his own Wonders. He goes from unmada to Illuminated rapidly.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Smoke</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mage</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mastigos</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Adamantine Arrow</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Uses a mix of Space and Mind for his stealth, and Matter to conjure his namesake.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Johnny Cage</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mortal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Psychic/Hunter</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Task Force: Valkyrie</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Uses Telekinesis to speed himself up and fire kinetic blasts.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Sonya Blade</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mortal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Psychic/Hunter</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Task Force: Valkyrie</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Uses Telekinesis to fire kinetic blasts and ESP to investigate.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Jax</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mortal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Hunter</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Task Force: Valkyrie</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">See Cyrax.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Quan Chi</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mage</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Moros</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Apostate</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Is a member of the Bokor Legacy, which gives him voodoo necromancy.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Shang Tsung</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mage</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Moros</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Seers Of The Throne</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Is a member of the Tremere Lich Legacy, which allows him to stay young by stealing souls.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Stryker</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mortal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Hunter</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Task Force: Valkyrie</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Is very unpopular.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Kitana</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Changeling</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Fairest</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Winter Court</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Eden is actually a Hedge Kingdom. The King and Queen of Eden are benevolent Charlatan Gentry.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Jade</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Changeling</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Fairest</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Winter Court</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">See above.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Sindel</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Gentry</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Fairest</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Seers Of The Throne</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">She returns to her usual Gentry wickedness while under Shao Khan's spell.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mileena</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mage</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mastigos</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Seers Of The Throne</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Originally a soulless creation of Shang Tsung, she learned how to steal souls by observing him and used a stolen Mage soul as a weak link to the Supernal. She suffers from Branding and Bedlam Paradoxes often due to her counterfeit Awakening, and even her Nimbus is monstrous.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Raiden</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Spirit</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Thunder</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Adamantine Arrow</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Despite not being a Mage, he is still considered an honorary member of the Arrow due to his wisdom and combat skills.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Liu Kang</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mage</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Obrimos</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Adamantine Arrow</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Often lets hubris dictate his actions. Probably has lower Wisdom than average.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Kung Lao</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mortal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Psychic</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Adamantine Arrow</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Despite not being a Mage, is still considered an honorary member of the Arrow for displaying great combat skills. Uses Telekinesis to control his hat, which is Enhanced by the Matter Arcanum.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Kano</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Slasher</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Psycho</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Seers Of The Throne</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Has access to Imbued and Enhanced items created by kidnapped Mages. Is obsessed with Sonya, as per usual for his Undertaking.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Kenshi</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mortal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Psychic/Hunter</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Task Force: Valkyrie</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Is very good with Telekinesis and compensates his blindness with ESP.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Nightwolf</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mage</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Thyrsus</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Apostate</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mostly does his own thing, but joins the Arrow/Valkyrie to defend Earth when necessary.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Shao Khan</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Exarch</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Unknown</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">See Notes</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">What we see as Shao Khan is actually just an Ochemata (extremely powerful sub-soul of the REAL Shao Khan). All characters that are listed above as Seers Of The Throne are serving him. Baraka is a Tyrant instead because he takes over Khan's throne in his Mortal Kombat 2 ending.</td> </tr> </table></div> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-26-2015, 02:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T05:27:28-07:00","id":492534,"title":"","content":"<b>Roland Deschain \u201cThe Gunslinger\u201d </b><br /> <br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Perseverance; in his quest for the tower, Roland continued onward while everything he cared about fell to the wayside.<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Hardened; Roland has become hardened and detached, and quickly loses patience with fools, cowards or weaklings.<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 4, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 4, Dexterity 5, Stamina 4<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 4, Manipulation 2, Composure 4<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 2 (History, Mythology), Animal Ken 3 (Raptors), Athletics 3, Brawl 4, Crafts 2 (Gunsmith), Empathy 3 (Body Language), Expression 1 (High Speech, Storytelling), Firearms 5 (Revolvers), Intimidation 4, Investigation 2 (Enigmas), Larceny 2, Medicine 2 (Holistic, Hypnotism), Occult 2 (Dark Tower, Spirits, Superstitions), Persuasion 2 (Gaining Trust), Politics 2 (Gilead), Ride 3 (Horses), Socialize 2(Mid-World), Stealth 3, Subterfuge 3 (Detect Lies, Omission), Survival 4, Weaponry 4 (Knives)<br /> <b>Skill Tricks: </b>Athletics (Size Up), Firearms (Ammunition Count, Cover Fire, <i>Lightning Reload,</i>Trick Shot), Investigation (Always Investigating), Stealth (Find Cover)<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Ambidextrous, Area of Expertise (Dark Tower, Revolvers), Armed Defense Style 4, Close Quarters Combat Style 1, Common Sense, Danger Sense, Defensive Combat (Brawl, Weaponry), Demolisher 2, Fame 1, Fast Reflexes 3, Firefight Style 3, Fleet of Foot 2, Hardy 3, Holistic Awareness, Inspiring, Indomitable, Iron Skin 4, Iron Stamina 2, Iron Will, Light Weapons Style 4, Marksmanship Style 4, Meditative Mind 2, Patient, Police Tactics Style 2, Professional Training 5 (Gunslinger, Firearms, Socialize, Survival), Quick Draw (Knives, Revolver), Quick Healer, Street Fighting Style 5, Striking Looks 1, Tolerance for Biology, Trained Observer 3, Unarmed Defense Style 3<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 6<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 9 [Risk Willpower]<br /> <b>Conviction:</b> 5 [Mirrors, pg.32-33]<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 12<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 8<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 13<br /> <b>Health:</b> 9<br /> <b>Condition: </b>Obsession (The Dark Tower)<br /> <br /> <b>Relic: </b>The Guns of Arthur Eld<br /> This set of twin blue-steel revolvers is large and heavy and have grips fashioned from fragrant sandalwood. Despite the weapons being centuries old they remain in perfect working conditions (in part due to regular expert maintenance and other less definable qualities). The weapons are functionally identical to the Colt Single Action Revolver but are somewhat heavier. Legend states the weapons were forged from Excalibur\u2019s blade; as such they are functionally immune to all forms of damage or effect that would alter is shape, durability or structure.<br /> <b>Damage</b>: 3L <b>Initiative:</b> -2 <b>Capacity:</b> 6 <b>Range:</b> 20/40/80<br /> <br /> <b><i>Notes</i></b><br /> <br /> The above reflects Roland at the opening of <i>The Dark Tower: The Gunslinger</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 04-26-2015, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T07:43:25-07:00","id":492575,"title":"","content":"<b>Albert Wesker</b><br /> <br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Ambitious; Wesker set lofty goals for himself, and frequently achieved them.<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Conceited; Wesker is supremely assured of his physical and mental superiority.<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 5, Wits 4, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 5, Dexterity 5, Stamina 5<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 4, Manipulation 3, Composure 5<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 4(Research, Tactics), Animal Ken 2 (Test Subjects), Athletics 4, Brawl 5, Computers 2, Drive 2 (Helicopter),Firearms 3, Intimidation 4(Superiority), Investigation 3, Persuasion 4 (Blackmail, Negotiation), Politics 3 (Corporate, Military), Science 5 (B.O.W\u2019s, Virology), Socialize 2 (Corporate), Stealth 3, Streetwise 2 (Black Markets), Subterfuge 4(Espionage), Survival 2, Weaponry 2(Improvised)<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Allies 4(TRICELL), Area of Expertise (B.O.W\u2019s), Close Quarters Combat Style 2, Contacts (Many), Danger Sense, Defensive Combat (Brawl), Eidetic Memory, Encyclopedic Knowledge (Science), Fast Reflexes 3, Fire Fight Style 2, Fleet of Foot 3, Hardy 3, Heavy Weapons Style 3, Improvised Weaponry Style 1, Interdisciplinary Specialty (Tactics), Iron Will, Language (Many), Library 5 (Umbrella Archive; Academics, Politics, Science), Martial Arts Style 4, Patient, Professional Training 5 ( Scientist; Academics, Science, Subterfuge), Resources 5, Striking Looks 2, Trained Observer 1, Unarmed Defense Style 5<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 6<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 9<br /> <b>Potency: </b>4 [Mortal Remains, pg. 104-105]<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 16<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 9<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 18<br /> <b>Health:</b> 10<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 3/3<br /> <b>Condition: </b>Megalomania<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers</b><br /> <br /> <b>Dead Flesh</b><br /> From each source of harm, the Wesker downgrades up to 3 levels of damage from lethal to bashing, or from bashing to nothing. This Dread Power has no effect on aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Flicker and Flash</b><br /> This Dread Power allows Wesker to step across spaces so quickly; he may as well be teleporting.<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Willpower <b>Action:</b> Reflexive <b>Dice Pool:</b> 12 dice<br /> Successful use of this Dread Power adds the number of successes to Wesker\u2019s Defense for the turn, and allows him to reflexively move his Speed +3. If he uses Flicker and Flash reflexively before an attack roll is made, he might move out of its range and avoid it altogether.<br /> Wesker can only activate Flicker and Flash three times in a turn. However, take the highest rolled successes to modify her Defense; the effect is not cumulative.<br /> <br /> <b>Immune to Pain</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2 Willpower <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> Wound penalties do not apply to Wesker, no matter how badly he is hurt. Stamina rolls to remain conscious aren\u2019t made when a bashing wound is marked in his rightmost Health box. He remains conscious automatically, collapsing only when a lethal or aggravated wound is marked in that box (and he is dying or dead). This power lasts until the end of the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Inhuman Alacrity</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Willpower <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> Wesker has speed, coordination and reflexes above and beyond human limits. Until the end of the turn, Wesker may add his full Defense against ranged attacks. Wesker must still be aware of incoming attacks to defend against them.<br /> <br /> <b>Regeneration</b><br /> Wesker heals at an unnatural rate; Bashing damage heals at one point per turn. Lethal damage disappears at a rate of one point per 15 minutes. Aggravated damage, however, is not affected by this ability.<br /> <br /> <b>Sharp Senses</b><br /> Wesker\u2019s senses are especially keen. He receives +2 to all perception rolls, and may track by scent. Wesker can also ignore up to three dice of distance-related penalties to any perception roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Swift Intercession</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Willpower <b>Action:</b> reflexive<br /> This dread power gives Wesker a +3bonus to Initiative. By spending a point of Willpower, he can immediately move to the head of the Initiative queue. This boost in Initiative lasts only one turn, after which all combatants return to acting in their rolled order.<br /> <br /> <b>Unholy Dexterity: </b>Wesker may spend 1 Willpower to gain a +2 bonus to dexterity. This bonus lasts until the end of the scene. Recalculate appropriate traits (Speed, Health, Initiative, Defense) using the new Attribute score.<br /> <br /> <b>Unholy Stamina: </b>Wesker may spend 1 Willpower to gain a +4 bonus to stamina. This bonus lasts until the end of the scene. Recalculate appropriate traits (Speed, Health, Initiative, Defense) using the new Attribute score.<br /> <br /> <b>Unholy Strength: </b>Wesker may spend 1 Willpower to gain a +4 bonus to strength. This bonus lasts until the end of the scene. Recalculate appropriate traits (Speed, Health, Initiative, Defense) using the new Attribute score.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Notes</i></b><br /> <br /> The above reflects Albert Wesker shortly after the dissolution of the UMBRELLA Corporation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 04-26-2015, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T10:41:20-07:00","id":492726,"title":"","content":"Argh, beaten to the punch by Reighnnhell once again! I had a write up for Roland ready to post, but yours is better. I would add and change a few things on his sheet, though:<br /> <br /> <i><b>Integrity:</b></i> I would lower it to <i><b>5</b></i>.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Conviction: </b></i>I'd make it a <i><b>7</b></i>, not 4. I would also make it explicit that he can<i><b> Risk Willpower</b></i> like a Hunter, or even make him a straight up Hunter.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Attributes &amp; Skills:</b></i> Roland has Resolve <i><b>6</b></i> and Firearms <i><b>6</b></i> because he has the Prodigy Merit for both.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Merits:</b></i> Giant, Favored Weapon (Guns Of Arthur Eld), Fleet Of Foot 2, Tolerance for Biology, Quick Healer, Inspiring, Demolisher 2, increase Hardy to <i><b>3</b></i>, Prodigy (homebrewed by Pendragon, this allows you to raise an Attribute/Skill to <i><b>6</b></i> if you are the best of the best) and his signature <i><b>Lightning Reload</b></i> technique.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Lightning Reload:</b> </i>Roland does not need to spend a turn to reload his revolvers. However, every time he uses this Merit, he must roll Stamina + Resolve, with a cumulative -1 penalty. If he fails, he gains the Impaired Condition in relation to his hands. The cumulative penalty is reset at the end of the scene.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Impaired (Persistent):</b></i> the specific body part is damaged, but still usable. Rolls involving it lose the 10 Again bonus, suffer a -2 penalty and turn into failures if any 1s come up. <i><b>Beat:</b></i> you fail a roll due to the Condition. <i><b>Resolution</b></i>: proper medical treatment.<br /> <br /> Wesker's Trained Observer Merit lacks a number. I assume it is <i><b>3</b></i>. His stats are spot on!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-26-2015, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T12:44:23-07:00","id":492804,"title":"","content":"<b>RE - The Gunslinger </b><br /> <br /> I was writing up Roland as he was at the start of the first book.I set his integrity at 6,as he seemed to be in a relatively good place at the time. The events of Tull, Losing Jake, and his palaver with Walter would all have been breaking points that could have brought him to a 5 or lower.<br /> <br /> Whenver I stat (especially for Heroic Mortals) I try not to over do it.With a really high conviction, Roland would have been able to see through more of the tricky used by Rhea of the Coos and Martin Broadcloak. He also would not have needed a new Ka-Tet as much as he did.<br /> Total agree on risking willpower. The mechanic was designed for mortals in a dark supernatural world, and the World of Darkness could easily be played as a level of the Tower.<br /> <br /> Rather than giving Firearms 6, I used Area of Expertise to give Roland an effective Firearms score of 7 when using his revolvers. Still pretty epic, but I think that minor variance makes him more of a man than a super human.<br /> <br /> Some disagreement on the Merits; Its been a few years since I read the books, but I don't recall Roland being unusually large (I reserve the giant merit for people over 6'5 and at least 250lbs -300lbs). Not certain where &quot;Favored Weapon&quot; comes from, but it sounds like a good fit.<br /> <br /> Now to figure out Walter O'Dim/Martin Broadcloak/Richard Fannin/Randall Flagg.<br /> <br /> <b>RE: Wesker</b><br /> <br /> That should be Trained Observer 1 . As ridiculously good as Wesker is, its good to leave a few blind spots and exploits in his build, otherwise how would you beat him?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 04-26-2015, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T13:27:11-07:00","id":492872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=492804#post492804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>RE - The Gunslinger </b><br /> <br /> I was writing up Roland as he was at the start of the first book.I set his integrity at 6,as he seemed to be in a relatively good place at the time. The events of Tull, Losing Jake, and his palaver with Walter would all have been breaking points that could have brought him to a 5 or lower.<br /> <br /> Whenver I stat (especially for Heroic Mortals) I try not to over do it.With a really high conviction, Roland would have been able to see through more of the tricky used by Rhea of the Coos and Martin Broadcloak. He also would not have needed a new Ka-Tet as much as he did.<br /> Total agree on risking willpower. The mechanic was designed for mortals in a dark supernatural world, and the World of Darkness could easily be played as a level of the Tower.<br /> <br /> Rather than giving Firearms 6, I used Area of Expertise to give Roland an effective Firearms score of 7 when using his revolvers. Still pretty epic, but I think that minor variance makes him more of a man than a super human.<br /> <br /> Some disagreement on the Merits; Its been a few years since I read the books, but I don't recall Roland being unusually large (I reserve the giant merit for people over 6'5 and at least 250lbs -300lbs). Not certain where &quot;Favored Weapon&quot; comes from, but it sounds like a good fit.<br /> <br /> Now to figure out Walter O'Dim/Martin Broadcloak/Richard Fannin/Randall Flagg.<br /> <br /> <b>RE: Wesker</b><br /> <br /> That should be Trained Observer 1 . As ridiculously good as Wesker is, its good to leave a few blind spots and exploits in his build, otherwise how would you beat him?</div> </div> </div> </div>All fair points. But Roland <i><b>does</b></i> have Lightning Reload in the first book. It even says so in his Wikipedia page.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T13:39:06-07:00","id":492877,"title":"","content":"<b>The Executioner (AKA Pyramid Head)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Quote: </b>(heavy breathing and the high pitched scraping of metal on metal)<br /> <br /> <b>Background: </b>the Executioner, more so than other monsters of Silent Hill, exists to deliver judgement. It represents repressed urges and the desire to be punished, taken to nightmarish and extremely grotesque levels..<br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> the Executioner manifests as a very tall, vaguely masculine humanoid with the trademark burnt flesh of Silent Hill\u2019s monsters. It either wears minimal clothing made from human skin or is naked. Its head is covered by a contraption of rusted metal and varying shape, from which its hideous vocalizations can sometimes be heard. Whatever is hidden inside its helmet is best left undiscovered. Even when not carrying its massive weapons, fighting the Executioner can mean agonizing injuries that quickly lead to death.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling Hints:</b> the Executioner is good for visceral horror, but it represents heavy themes. You should make sure your players are OK with graphic description of extreme violence before including the Executioner. Even then, use it sparingly, so as to not diminish the impact of its appearance or cause unfair deaths. The only way to truly confront it is coming to terms with your guilt. What this means varies according to character, should be carefully discussed and a major plot point.<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 1, Wits 2, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 5, Dexterity 2, Stamina 4<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 5, Manipulation 1, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Investigation (Searching) 2<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics (Throwing) 3, Brawl (Grappling) 5, Weaponry (Great Knife, Great Spear) 5<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Intimidation 3<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Giant, Bound To The Town 5, Heavy Weapons 3 (Great Knife, Great Spear), Demolisher 3<br /> <br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 5<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 2 + Athletics/Brawl/Weaponry<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 11<br /> <b>Health: </b>10<br /> <b>Static Rating:</b> 10<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Bare Hands</b>: +0L. Dice Pool: 10. Special: after grappling, spend 1 willpower point to strike a Killing Blow by flaying the skin.<br /> <b>Great Knife:</b> +4L. Dice Pool: 11. -3 Initiative. -6 Speed.<br /> <b>Great Spear:</b> +3L. Dice Pool: 7 for throwing, 11 for melee. -2 Initiative. -3 Speed. Range: 20/40/80<br /> <br /> <b>Note: </b>I am using the template included in <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/NWOD/Silent_Hill.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Mr Gone\u2019s Silent Hill Supplement for the NWOD.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-09-2015, 02:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T14:58:18-07:00","id":492935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=358298#post358298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jeeves (from Jeeves and Wooster) is a normal human, albeit one who is clued in. However, all of Woosters friends are high Wyrd changelings, which would explain their eccentricities and seeming near total blindness to others. Wooster himself is a Fairest of a musical bent, with Wyrd 6 and a frailty preventing him from refusing or breaking a marriage engagement. His Clarity is pretty high, about 7 or 8.<br /> <br /> Jeeves mostly gets as successful results as he does through careful knowledge of the other changelings frailties and bans, as well as benefits from a pact he struck with Wooster to get Glamour sight.</div> </div> </div> </div>I absolutely love this. Fun fact - last year, I had the very good fortune to play Mr. Bertram Wilberforce Wooster in a production of &quot;Jeeves in Bloom.&quot; It's probably my second-favorite role I've ever had, being recently supplanted by playing...well, myself, in a way, in &quot;The Complete Works of William Shakespeare (Abridged).&quot; <br /> <br /> So I saw this and a grin immediately broke out. Since the latter show just closed (I just got home from strike, actually), it was good to read something to shove the sadness of a show closing off to the side. So thanks for that! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T16:05:57-07:00","id":492982,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Splatterhouse\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>The Terror Mask</b></span></a><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Mask is a Relic containing a Rank 4 violence spirit. Whoever wears it is treated as one of the Claimed.<br /> <br /> <b>Attribute Bonuses:</b> +9 Strength, +2 Presence, +1 Intelligence, +3 Dexterity, +0 Manipulation, +5 Wits, +7 Stamina, +2 Composure, +3 Resolve. These increase derived traits and may bring the Attributes beyond 10 dots.<br /> <br /> <b>Maximum Essence/Per Turn:</b> 40/12<br /> <br /> <b>Influences:</b> Carnage 4 (May Be Used To Create Temporary Skill Dots And Natural Weaponry)<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Armored Hide 2, Leap, Monstrous Resilience, Numen (Drain), Regenerate 4, Wall Climb<br /> <br /> <b>Merits: </b>Indomitable (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration\"><b>Advanced</b></a>), Tolerance For Biology, Vice-Ridden (Violent), Ambidextrous, Demolisher 3, Fleet Of Foot 3, Giant (Advanced), Hardy 3, Iron Stamina 3, Parkour 4, Air Of Menace, Iron Will, Striking Looks 2 (Monstrous), Heavy Weapons 5, Iron Skin 2 (Advanced 2), Martial Arts 4, Relentless Assault 5</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-30-2016, 06:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T17:28:25-07:00","id":493049,"title":"","content":"Man I remember that game for the Turbo Grafx.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T18:07:28-07:00","id":493069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=493049#post493049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man I remember that game for the Turbo Grafx.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I remember its remake better.<br /> <br /> Of course, that was only because it's more recent, given it's non-ending leaving a bad taste in my mouth. I did think the fact that Rick's voice sounds the same when he bulks up is hilarious (for the uninformed, Rick without the Terror Mask is about the nerdiest teenager possible without being a walking stereotype).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T18:10:20-07:00","id":493088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=493069#post493069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I remember its remake better.<br /> <br /> Of course, that was only because it's more recent, given it's non-ending leaving a bad taste in my mouth. I did think the fact that Rick's voice sounds the same when he bulks up is hilarious (for the uninformed, Rick without the Terror Mask is about the nerdiest teenager possible without being a walking stereotype).</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. They could have made his voice while wearing the Mask a bit deeper.<br /> <br /> I also didn't like the Mask's personality in the remake. It lost much of its appeal as a shadowy demon in favor of being a wisecracking clown. At least to me. It's not really how often it talks, but the way it talks. In the remake, it is just too...human, you know? Again, just my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-26-2015, 09:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T19:41:15-07:00","id":493164,"title":"","content":"As a follow up to my stats for <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-the-nwod?p=492877#post492877\">Pyramid Head</a>, here are stats for another famous survival horror monster: Nemesis!<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue: </b>Implacable<br /> <b>Vice: </b>Destructive<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 3, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 7, Dexterity 3, Stamina 7<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 5, Manipulation 1, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics 1, Crafts 1, Medicine 1, Occult 0, Politics 0, Investigation (Searching) 3, Science 1<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics (Running) 6, Brawl (Fists, Tentacles) 6, Drive 0, Firearms (Rocket Launcher) 4, Larceny 0, Stealth 1, Survival (Tracking) 3, Weaponry 3<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken 0, Empathy 0, Expression 0, Intimidation 3, Persuasion 0, Socialize 0, Streetwise 0, Subterfuge 1<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Trained Observer 1, Demolisher 3, Heavy Weapons 3 (Fists), Direction Sense, Danger Sense, Fleet Of Foot 3, Fast Reflexes 3, Iron Stamina 3, Iron Will, Indomitable, Striking Looks +2<br /> <br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 8<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 9<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 3 + Athletics/Brawl/Weaponry<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 24<br /> <b>Health: </b>15 (Size 8)<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 7<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers: </b>Biomechanical Nightmare 5 (Armor 5/5, Rocket Launcher +5L, Implacable Speed +5, Crushing Fists +5L, Tracking +5), Dead Flesh 3, Tendrils, Unholy Attribute (Strength 3, Stamina 3), Revivify 5, Titan\u2019s Strength 5","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-29-2015, 09:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T20:32:35-07:00","id":493185,"title":"","content":"My six year old watches Teen Titans which of course means I watch Teen Titans. Anyway, I noticed each character neatly syncs with a path in Mage The Awakening. Beast Boy is clearly a Thyrus, Cyborg, half man half metal, a Moros. Firestar is dfinitely an Obrimos, Raven undoubtedly a Mastigos and Robin? The only character without a super power must be relying on luck, an Acanthus for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5722-mikepgs","name":"MikePGS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T03:59:47-07:00","id":493419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MikePGS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=493185#post493185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My six year old watches Teen Titans which of course means I watch Teen Titans. Anyway, I noticed each character neatly syncs with a path in Mage The Awakening. Beast Boy is clearly a Thyrus, Cyborg, half man half metal, a Moros. Firestar is dfinitely an Obrimos, Raven undoubtedly a Mastigos and Robin? The only character without a super power must be relying on luck, an Acanthus for sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd Put Robin as a Well Trained Hunter who cares more about keeping the rest from going too far away from humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T14:41:37-07:00","id":493953,"title":"","content":"<b>Subject Delta (Bioshock 2)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Virtue: </b>Protective<br /> <b>Vice: </b>Violent<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 4, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 6, Dexterity 4, Stamina 6<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 4, Manipulation 2, Composure 4<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics 2, Crafts (Tools &amp; Firearms) 3, Computer 2, Medicine 3, Occult 2, Politics 0, Investigation (Searching) 3, Science (Hacking) 3<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics (Running, Swimming) 4, Brawl (Fists) 5, Drive 1, Firearms (Rivet Gun) 4, Larceny (Security Systems) 3, Stealth 1, Survival 3, Weaponry (Drill) 5<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken 1, Empathy (Little Sisters) 2, Expression 0, Intimidation 3, Persuasion 1, Socialize (Little Sisters) 1, Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 1<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area Of Expertise (Tools &amp; Firearms, Hacking), Trained Observer 1, Demolisher 3, Heavy Weapons 5 (Drill), Direction Sense, Danger Sense, Fleet Of Foot 3, Fast Reflexes 3, Iron Stamina 3, Iron Will, Indomitable, Professional Training 5 (Big Daddy: Crafts, Science, Weaponry), True Friend (Eleanor Lamb)<br /> <br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 8<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 11<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 4 + Athletics/Brawl/Weaponry<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 17<br /> <b>Health: </b>13 (Size 7)<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 6<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 5<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Mute<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers: </b>Biomechanical Nightmare 3 (Armor 3/3, Drill +3L, Rivet Gun +3L: cost no willpower due to EVE supplying tank), Blast 3 (Various Plasmids, which use Athletics instead of Occult), Crushing Blow, Drain 1 or 3 (Special), Titan\u2019s Strength 5, Unholy Attribute (Strength 3, Stamina 5)<br /> <br /> <b>Draining ADAM:</b> with this Variant, Delta may gather ADAM Beats by adopting or harvesting Little Sisters. Adopting them lets Detla drain 1 ADAM Beat per scene. Harvesting them lets him drain 3 ADAM Beats immediately. 5 ADAM Beats = 1 ADAM Experience. ADAM Experiences can be used to buy Dread Powers, Physical/Mental Attributes and Potency. EVE and willpower points are treated as synonyms for the purposes of Dread Powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-27-2015, 08:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T17:38:37-07:00","id":496911,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:14px\">More Resident Evil </span></i><b><i>...</i><br /> <br /> T-Virus Zombie</b></span><br /> Zombies are humans resurrected from the dead due to T-Virus infection. Symptoms of the T-Virus include mutation and progressive necrosis. A T-Virus infection destroys all higher brain function, leaving only the cerebellum to govern behavior. This leaves the infected host with a very animalistic behavior. They are known as &quot;Zombies&quot; due to their grotesque, corpse-like appearance. They wander in search of human flesh, their only source of nutrition, as they constantly require vast amounts of energy to sustain the sudden increase in metabolic demand. Although small amounts of damage will not deter a Zombie, they can be terminated by destroying the head.<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 4, Finesse 2, Resistance 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Brawl 2<br /> <b>Potency: </b>1 [Mortal Remains, pg. 104-105]<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 2 (5 Lunge)<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 0<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 2 (8 Lunge)<br /> <b>Health:</b> 3<br /> <b>Physical Integrity: </b>10<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 1/1<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers</b><br /> <br /> <b>Contagious</b>: Zombies created by the T-Virus can transmit it to other creatures, with those killed by the zombie\u2019s bite rising to join their ranks. Anyone bitten by a T-Virus zombie makes a Stamina +Resistance roll. If failed, the victim gains the <i>T-Virus </i>condition.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b><i>[Condition T-Virus</i></b> ]<br /> <i>You have been infected by a strain of the T-Virus. If you die with this condition, your body will rise as a T-Virus Zombie. </i><br /> <b><i>Possible Sources:</i></b><i> Bite from a T Virus infected creature. </i><br /> <b><i>Resolution:</i></b><i> Antidote; or You may make a Stamina +Resistance roll once a month to shed this condition. </i><br /> <b><i>Beat:</i></b><i> N/A</i></span><br /> <br /> <b>Physical Integrity: </b>Physical Integrity is a special trait describing the state of the zombie's body. A zombie with all of its limbs and no missing parts starts with an Integrity of 10.<br /> This trait also describes the overall functionality of the zombie. Every (Resilience) days, zombies lose one point of Physical Integrity. Under most circumstances, Physical Integrity cannot be replenished once it is lost. Once all of a zombie's Health boxes are filled with lethal damage any additional damage done is subtracted from the remaining points of Physical Integrity. Once this trait reaches zero the zombie is neutralized. The maximum number of dice in a zombies dice pools is capped by its current Physical Integrity.<br /> <br /> <b>Special Attacks:</b> A T-Virus Zombie instinctively attacks living creatures.<br /> <i>Bite:</i> The bite of a T-Virus zombie is considered a +0 weapon.<br /> <i>Entangle:</i> Zombies fall upon targets with their full mass, giving them a +2 bonus to initiate or maintain a grapple.<br /> <i>Lunge: </i>A T-Virus zombie typically lacks the coordination to move at more than a clumsy shamble. Once prey is within reach, it can move with alarming speed. When the creature is within 15 meters of viable prey that it can perceive, its speed increases by 6 and it gains a +3 bonus to Initiative.<br /> <br /> <b>Vulnerability: </b>T-Virus zombies still require a somewhat functioning brain and nervous system. A successful targeted attack to the head will destroy a T-Virus zombie instantly. T-Virus Zombies also do not have the survival instinct necessary to dodge or block incoming attacks. As such, their Defense is 0<br /> <br /> <b><i>Notes</i></b><br /> The above reflects the typical t-virus zombie featured through most of the Resident Evil series. <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Licker</b></span><br /> Lickers are the result of a mutation caused by the progression of the T-Virus infection in a zombified human host's body. They were named by Raccoon City Police Department personnel for their peculiarly long tongues. Having completely lost all sense of sight, Lickers are unable to track prey visually; to compensate they have an overdeveloped sense of hearing, and will attack victims with their tongue and claws at the slightest sound.<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 4, Finesse 4, Resistance 4<br /> <b>Skills: </b>Athletics 2, Brawl 2, Stealth 3<br /> <b>Willpower: </b>4<br /> <b>Potency: </b>2 [Mortal Remains, pg. 104-105]<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 8<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 14 [Species Factor 6]<br /> <b>Health:</b> 9<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 1/1<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers</b><br /> <br /> <b>Blind Sense</b><br /> Lickers have mutated to a degree that they have no eyes and are completely blind. However, they compensate by tracking their prey through hearing and smell. The Licker uses its defense and make attacks normally.<br /> <br /> <b>Clamber</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Willpower <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> For the remainder of the scene, the monster can climb on all fours up impossible to climb surfaces such as walls, ceilings, windows and the like. The monster moves as if she were walking or running on normal ground<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Attack</b><br /> <b><i>Lashing Tongue:</i></b> The Lickers tongue is long and whip-like, ending a bard sharp enough to rend flesh. This is a +1 weapon attack with Armor Piercing 1 and an initiative penalty of -2.<br /> <b><i>Talons: </i></b>The Licker has razor sharp claws on its hands and feet. This is a +0 weapon attack.<br /> <br /> <b>Echolocation</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Willpower<br /> A creature with Echolocation can use sonic echoes to \u201cread\u201d his immediate surroundings without actually having to see them. When activated, it can ignore all visually-based penalties such as darkness, fog, smoke or blindness for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Immune to Pain</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2 Willpower <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> Wound penalties do not apply to the Licker, no matter how badly it is hurt. Stamina rolls to remain conscious aren\u2019t made when a bashing wound is marked in its rightmost Health box. It remains conscious automatically, collapsing only when a lethal or aggravated wound is marked in that box (and it is dying or dead). This power lasts until the end of the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Leaping:</b> The Licker can leap and jump twice as far as a human.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Notes</i></b><br /> The above reflects the mutant strain of T-Virus infection featured through most of the Resident Evil series. <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Tyrant (Nemesis-T Type)</b></span><br /> The Nemesis-T Type (also known as the &quot;Pursuer&quot;) was an experimental form of intelligent Tyrant created by the Umbrella Europe Sixth Laboratory in France under the direct administration of Umbrella Headquarters. Its purpose was to prove that a t-Virus infected creature could retain most of its intelligence and follow specific orders. It was named after Nemesis, the Ancient Greek goddess of divine vengeance.<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 8, Dexterity 4, Stamina 8<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 1, Composure 5<br /> <b>Skills: </b>Academics 2 (Tactics), Athletics 3(Climb), Brawl 4, Crafts 2, Firearms 4 (Heavy Weapons), Intimidate 4, Stealth 3 (Ambush), Survival 3 (Tracking), Weaponry 3<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area of Expertise (Tracking), Armored Combat Style 1 [Hurt Locker playtest] Direction Sense, Fire Fight Style 2, Frenzied Assault Style 5, Hardy 3, Heavy Weapons Style 5, Interdisciplinary Specialty (Heavy Weapons), Professional Training 3 (Soldier; Athletics, Firearms, Survival), Striking Looks 2 (Monstrous), Trained Observer 2<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 9<br /> <b>Potency: </b>3 [Mortal Remains, pg. 104-105]<br /> <b>Size:</b> 6<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 9<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 8 (7 Kevlar Trenchcoat)<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 4/2; Kevlar Trenchcoat (3/5); 7/7 total<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 20 [Species Factor 7]<br /> <b>Health:</b> 14<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers </b><br /> <b>Atavism: </b>When determining Defense, the Nemesis chooses the higher of Wits and Dexterity, not the lesser of the two.<br /> <br /> <b>Crushing Blow</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>2 Willpower<b> Action: </b>Instant<br /> All bashing damage that the Nemesis deals with its body (fist, foot, head, elbow, whatever) is instead done as lethal damage. This power lasts until the end of the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Dead Flesh: </b>From each source of harm, the Nemesis downgrades up to 3 levels of damage from lethal to bashing, or from bashing to nothing. This Dread Power has no effect on aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Equipment: </b>The Nemesis wears a Kevlar Trenchcoat and carries a rocket launcher or machine gun.<br /> <b><i>HEAT Rocket</i></b><i> - <b>Damage </b>10<b> Blast </b>5<b> Force </b>3<b> Range </b>500/1000/2000<b> Effect </b>AP 17, Knockdown</i><br /> <b><i>GE M134 Mini Gun - Damage </i></b><i>4(8-again) <b>Range </b>150/300/600 <b>Capacity</b> 100 S<b>trength</b> 4 <b>Size</b> 5</i><br /> <br /> <b>Immune to Pain</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>2 Willpower<b> Action: </b>Instant<br /> Wound penalties do not apply to the Nemesis, no matter how badly it is hurt. Stamina rolls to remain conscious aren\u2019t made when a bashing wound is marked in its rightmost Health box. It remains conscious automatically, collapsing only when a lethal or aggravated wound is marked in that box (and it is dying or dead). This power lasts until the end of the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Leaping:</b> The Nemesis can leap and jump twice as far as a human.<br /> <br /> <b>Regeneration: </b>The Nemesis heals at an unnatural rate; Bashing damage heals at one point per turn. Lethal damage disappears at a rate of one point per 15 minutes. Aggravated damage, however, is not affected by this ability.<br /> <br /> <b>Tentacles</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2 Willpower <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> Nemesis possesses a network of tentacles that cover its body. When used in combat, these appendages are powerful enough to tear through a human body. These tentacles can be used to attack with a Dexterity + Brawl roll and a +0 damage weapon. The reach of the tentacles gives a +1 Defense bonus against opponents who are unarmed or wield weapons of Size 1<br /> <b><i>Drawback:</i></b> The tentacles can also be attacked directly (-3 to the attack): a single lethal level done against them severs the tentacle.<br /> <br /> <b>Titan\u2019s Strength: </b>The Nemesis can automatically lift anything with a Size equal to or less than 10. If she throws lighter objects like a weapon, that item is considered aerodynamic. Nemesis gains an additional 3 dots to any roll involving a feat of strength. These dice do not apply to combat actions, only feats.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Notes</i></b><br /> The above reflects The Nemesis as depicted in <i>Resident Evil 3</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 04-29-2015, 08:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T20:55:36-07:00","id":497043,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:24px\">Hunter Batman &amp; Slasher Joker</span><br /> <br /> Virtue: </b>Prudence/Justice<br /> <b>Vice: </b>Wrath<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 6, Wits 5, Resolve 6<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 5, Dexterity 4, Stamina 5<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 5, Manipulation 3, Composure 4<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics (Criminology, Art) 3, Crafts (Repair Gadgets) 3, Computer (Hacking) 3, Medicine (Quick Patch Up) 3, Occult 3, Politics (Police, Corporate) 3, Investigation (Detective Work) 6, Science (Invent Gadgets) 4<br /> <br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics (Running, Jumping) 4, Brawl 6, Drive (Batmobile) 3, Firearms (Grappling Hook) 4, Larceny 3, Stealth 4, Survival 3, Weaponry 4<br /> <br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken 1, Empathy 3, Expression 2, Intimidation (Physical Threats) 4, Persuasion (Business) 3, Socialize 3, Streetwise (Criminals) 5, Subterfuge (Hide Emotions, Protect Identity) 4<br /> <br /> <b>Skill Tricks:</b> Investigation (Incisive Mind, Pattern Expert, Just A Red Herring), Academics (Quick Cram), Computer (No Internet Footprint), Brawl (Knockout Punch), Drive (Demolition Derby), Firearms (Trick Shot), Larceny (All Doors Open), Streetwise (Network Of Eyes), Subterfuge (Perfect Disguise)<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Prodigy (Intelligence, Resolve, Investigation, Brawl), Virtuous, Resources 5, Professional Training 5 (Detective: Empathy, Investigation, Brawl), Parkour 5, Close Quarters Combat 5, Martial Arts 5, Police Tactics 3, Iron Skin 4, Area Of Expertise (Detective Work), Trained Observer 1, Crack Driver, Demolisher 3, Danger Sense, Good Time Management, Patient, Indomitable, Iron Will, Encyclopedic Knowledge (Science, Investigation, Persuasion), Eye For The Strange, Tolerance For Biology, Fast Reflexes 3, Fleet Of Foot 3, Iron Stamina 3, Hardy 3, Quick Draw, Inspiring, Striking Looks +2, Safehouse (Bat Cave: Housing 5, Safe Place 5, Cache 5+, Secrecy 5), Taste, Status (Wayne Enterprises 5, Gotham Police 3), Allies (Wayne Enterprises 5, Gotham Police 3), Contacts 3 (Wayne Enterprises, Gotham Police, Super Heroes), Fixer, Staff 5 (Wayne Enterprises), Fame 3, Alternate Identity 3,True Friend (Bat Family)<br /> <br /> <b>Health: </b>10<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 4 + Brawl/Weaponry/Athletics<br /> <b>Initiative Mod:</b> 11<br /> <b>Speed: </b>16<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> Depends on how stable you want his psyche to be, likely 5 or thereabouts.<br /> <b>Conviction:</b> 7<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue: </b>Cunning<br /> <b>Vice: </b>Arrogant/Cynical<br /> <br /> <b>Undertaking: Maniac</b><br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 6, Wits 4, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 4, Stamina 4<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 5, Manipulation 4, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics (Art) 3, Crafts (Traps) 3, Computer 2, Medicine (Joker Venom) 4, Occult 2, Politics 2, Investigation 3, Science (Chemistry) 3<br /> <br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics (Running) 3, Brawl 3, Drive 2, Firearms 4, Larceny 4, Stealth (Killing Blows) 3, Survival 2, Weaponry (Knives) 4<br /> <br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken 1, Empathy 1, Expression (Humor) 3, Intimidation (Crazy) 5, Persuasion (Drive Insane) 4, Socialize 1, Streetwise (Criminals) 5, Subterfuge 4<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Vice-Ridden, Resources 4, Professional Training 5 (Criminal: Larceny, Streetwise, Intimidation), Area Of Expertise (Joker Venom), Light Weapons 5, Shiv 2, Firefight 5, Danger Sense, Good Time Management, Patient, Indomitable, Iron Will, Encyclopedic Knowledge (Medicine, Subterfuge, Intimidation), Tolerance For Biology, Fast Reflexes 3, Fleet Of Foot 3, Iron Stamina 3, Hardy 3, Quick Draw, Sleight Of Hand, Taste, Status 5/Allies 5 (Gotham Criminals), Contacts 2 (Gotham Criminals, Super Villains), Fixer, Tell Tale Murder, Murder Expert, Frenzied Assault 3, Morbid Fascination<br /> <br /> <b>Health:</b> 9<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 7<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 4 + Brawl/Weaponry/Athletics<br /> <b>Initiative Mod: </b>11<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 13<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> depends on how crazy you want him to be, but is definitely very low.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/155637-slasher-gmc-port\"><b>Nightmare:</b></a> 3<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Obsessed (Batman)<br /> <br /> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/155637-slasher-gmc-port\">Extra Talents:</a> </b>Back For The Sequel, You Complete Me<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers: </b>Lord Of The Manor 5, Transmutation 5, Cloak Of Authority 5, Dement 5<br /> <br /> <b>Notes:</b> Dement uses Persuasion instead of Occult, and the \u201cDrive Insane\u201d specialty applies to the activation roll. Lord Of The Manor uses Streetwise instead of Survival and applies temporarily to the \u201cdark side of the city\u201d, which includes both areas run by criminals and areas where criminals are detained. This explains how he always escapes from the Arkham Asylum or any other prison. Transmutation uses Medicine instead of Occult if he is creating Joker Venom, and the Specialty with Area Of Expertise applies to the activation roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 05-01-2015, 08:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T02:27:09-07:00","id":497252,"title":"","content":"Edward scissorhands is clearly a Wretched Promethean with a particular refinement that explains his hands. Unfortunately he stays to long in the village/town and his level of disquiet grows to the point people take action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5544-ancientswordrage","name":"AncientSwordRage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T02:41:39-07:00","id":497272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=496911#post496911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[SIZE=16px]<i><span style=\"font-size:14px\">More Resident Evil </span></i>[B]<i>...</i><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Licker</b></span><br /> Lickers are the result of a mutation caused by the progression of the T-Virus infection in a zombified human host's body. They were named by Raccoon City Police Department personnel for their peculiarly long tongues. Having completely lost all sense of sight, Lickers are unable to track prey visually; to compensate they have an overdeveloped sense of hearing, and will attack victims with their tongue and claws at the slightest sound.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nitpick..... Lickers were Mutated Rats with the T-Virus. Over then that Grand.<br /> Also the T-Virus had Different Effects on Living Animals then Dead ones and Humans.<br /> <br /> Hunters if i recall Right were infected Frogs/Toads. (Atleast the Gamma Versions)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T08:53:01-07:00","id":497507,"title":"","content":"<b>RE: Licker</b><br /> I read up on the Lickers on a few RE wikis before my write up, most of them said that Lickers were mutated humans, so that's what I went with.<br /> <br /> <b>RE: Batman and Joker</b><br /> <br /> While I would still shy away from giving either characters 6 dots in anything (I like my mortals -even exceptional ones- to still feel mortal), its minor nit-pick. Otherwise excellent work.<br /> and would you be able to give more detail on the &quot;Back For The Sequel&quot; and &quot;You Complete Me&quot; talents. They sound like fun!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T11:55:49-07:00","id":497703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=497507#post497507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>RE: Licker</b><br /> I read up on the Lickers on a few RE wikis before my write up, most of them said that Lickers were mutated humans, so that's what I went with.<br /> <br /> <b>RE: Batman and Joker</b><br /> <br /> While I would still shy away from giving either characters 6 dots in anything (I like my mortals -even exceptional ones- to still feel mortal), its minor nit-pick. Otherwise excellent work.<br /> and would you be able to give more detail on the &quot;Back For The Sequel&quot; and &quot;You Complete Me&quot; talents. They sound like fun!</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are also from King's Raven's rewrite:<br /> <br /> Back for the Sequel means Joker will not die-or stay dead-until something very specific happens to him, while You Complete Me is Foe Yay, as TV Tropes puts it, he understands Batman better than anyone else but can't just <i>kill </i>him until Bruce knows it was the Joker who beat him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T13:23:28-07:00","id":497801,"title":"","content":"<i>Fate/Stay Night</i>'s Archer is a Prime-focused Obrimos Adamantine Arrow.<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Int 2, Wits 3, Resolve 5, Str 4, Dex 4, Stam 4, Pres 3, Man 3, Comp 4<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Occult 2, Craft 5, Athletics 5 (Archery), Brawl 1, Stealth 2, Weaponry 5 (Swords), Subterfuge 2, Streetwise 2, Intimidation 1<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> {Archery and sword merits, and merits that combine those with spellcasting}, Interdisciplinary Specialist (Weaponry: Swords), Area of Expertise (Swords, Archery)<br /> <br /> <b>Arcana:</b> Forces 2, Matter 3, Prime 5<br /> <br /> <b>Gnosis:</b> 3<br /> <br /> <b>Signature Rotes:</b> <i>Reinforcement </i>(Comp + Craft + Matter), <i>Phantasmal Weapon</i> (Resolve + Craft + Prime), <i>Unlimited Blade Works</i> (Resolve + Craft + Prime) [Prime 5 spell, imposes the Truth of the Reality Marble onto the Fallen World]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 04-30-2015, 04:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T14:48:44-07:00","id":497903,"title":"","content":"Of course there's always the possibility he's something more.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/sITqCob.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T17:49:58-07:00","id":498044,"title":"","content":"Eh, there's something about making Joker something inhuman has never felt right to me. It's like why World of Darkness always avoided using supernaturals as an explicit cause for nazism and World War II, there's just about human monsters that brings so much more for horror than another inhuman monstrosity. Plus that's always been part of the appeal of the Joker to me, there's no explanation for his actions, no one knows who he was and where he comes from and for all intents and purposes he's really just an ordinary guy who happens to be crazier than any scale can measure. The only template I'd ever be interested in giving him would be a slasher. (Since for all their quasi-supernatural powers, they're still the best template for human monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5823-ravian3","name":"Ravian3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T17:12:53-07:00","id":499508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=497507#post497507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>RE: Licker</b><br /> I read up on the Lickers on a few RE wikis before my write up, most of them said that Lickers were mutated humans, so that's what I went with.<br /> <br /> <b>RE: Batman and Joker</b><br /> <br /> While I would still shy away from giving either characters 6 dots in anything (I like my mortals -even exceptional ones- to still feel mortal), its minor nit-pick. Otherwise excellent work.<br /> and would you be able to give more detail on the &quot;Back For The Sequel&quot; and &quot;You Complete Me&quot; talents. They sound like fun!</div> </div> </div> </div>Those extra Talents are on the same post as the one with the write up for the Nightmare Powerstat for Slashers.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I got beat to the punch by Leliel. He's got the Talents right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T17:48:51-07:00","id":499553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course there's always the possibility he's something more. </div> </div> </div>I liked Arkham City\u00b4s explanation about the Joker having Ra's Al Ghul\u00b4s Lazarus Pit\u00b4s phlebotinum in his blood, explaining his immortality and mental insanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T17:54:00-07:00","id":499559,"title":"","content":"Just updated these to GMC<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>The Ghostbusters</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Egon Spengler</b><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Scientific - Egon had the belief that even the most bizarre paranormal events could be explained in a scientific context.<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Curiosity - Egon will take any opportunity to conduct a proper scientific investigation (even when socially inappropriate).<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 5, Wits 3, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 1, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 4(Research), Athletics 2, Computers 3, Crafts 4 (Ghostbusting Gear), Firearms 2 (Proton Pack), Investigation 3 (Paranormal Events), Occult 3(Ephemeral Entities), Science 5 (Parapsychology, Quantum Physics), Socialize 1 (Academia), Stealth 1, Subterfuge 2(Disguise)<br /> <b>Skill Tricks: </b>Investigation (Always Investigating), Occult (Harmless v. Dangerous), Science (Sound Theory)<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area of Expertise (Ghostbusting Gear, Proton Pack, Quantum Physics), Fame 1, Fire Fight Style 1, Eidetic Memory, Good Time Management, Professional Training 5 (Scientist; Crafts, Investigation, Science), Quick Draw (Proton Pack), Safe Place 3 (Firehouse), Tolerance for Biology<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Behavior Blind [Persistent]<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Behavior Blind [Persistent]</b><br /> Your character doesn\u2019t really understand human behavior and is blind to common social cues that communicate other people\u2019s basic feelings. He can\u2019t tell when others use sarcasm or innuendo, or if he\u2019s boring them. The character suffers a -2 penalty to any roll to detect or understand another person\u2019s moods.<br /> <b>Possible Sources: </b>Neurological conditions, Socially Maladapted, Traumatic Upbringing</span></i><br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Ray Stantz</b><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Enthusiasm - Ray is the heart of the Ghostbusters, and has an almost childlike sense of wonder and enthusiasm for his work.<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Reckless \u2013 Ray\u2019s enthusiasm often causes his to forget many of the dangers involved in his work.<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 3, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 4(Folklore, Paranormal History, Religion), Athletics 2(Throwing), Computers 4, Crafts 5 (Ghostbusting Gear), Drive 2(Pilot), Empathy 2, Firearms 3 (Proton Pack), Investigation 3 (Paranormal Events), Occult 4 (Ephemeral Entities), Science 4 (Metallurgy, Parapsychology), Stealth 2, Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 2 (Disguise)<br /> <b>Skill Tricks: </b>Academics (Befuddling Double-Talk, Quote Master), Crafts (Improvised Tools), Occult (Myth Expert)<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Allies (Academia 2), Area of Expertise (Paranormal History, Parapsychology, Proton Packs, Throwing), Encyclopedic Knowledge (Academics), Eye for the Strange, Fame 1, Fire Fight Style 1, Interdisciplinary Specialty (Paranormal History), Professional Training 4 (Scientist; Crafts, Occult, Science), Quick Draw (Proton Pack), Safe Place 3 (Firehouse)<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Peter Venkman</b><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Justice - Peter looks out for the little guy, tries to sincerely help people, and takes an instant dislike to bullies, petty bureaucrats and power-tripping demi-gods.<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Lecherous - Peter seemed to go out of his way (and perform questionable actions) to gain the attention of attractive women.<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 4, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 4, Composure 4<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 3(Psychology), Athletics 2, Brawl 2, Computers 2, Crafts 2, Drive 2, Empathy 3, Expression 3 (Rants), Firearms 3 (Proton Pack), Intimidate 1, Investigation 3 (Paranormal Events), Larceny 2, Occult 3 (Psychic Phenomena), Persuasion 4, Politics 3, (Academia, Bureaucracy, Local Government), Science 3 (Parapsychology), Socialize 4, Stealth 2, , Subterfuge 3 (Lies), Streetwise 3 (New York)<br /> <br /> <b>Skill Tricks: </b>Academics (Legal Authority), Empathy (Hot Buttons), Politics (Hot Buttons), Streetwise (Lifelong Resident)<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Allies (Local Government 2), Area of Expertise (Proton Packs, Psychology, New York, Psychic Phenomena), Barfly, Fame 1, Fast Talking Style 4, Fire Fight Style 1, Interdisciplinary Specialty (Bureaucracy, New York), Iron Will, Professional Training 4 (Scientist; Investigation, Politics, Science), Pusher, Quick Draw (Proton Pack), Safe Place 3 (Firehouse), Small Unit Tactics<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Winston Zeddemore</b><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Level-Headed - Winston is a down to earth guy who helps moderate the more extreme personalities of the other Ghostbusters.<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Follower; Winston often prefers to lets others make the decisions on a job.<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 3, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 4, Dexterity 3, Stamina 4<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 2, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 2(Archeology, Religion, Tactics), Athletics 3(Climbing, Throwing), Brawl 2(Grapple), Crafts 2 (Repair), Drive 3(Ecto-1), Empathy 2, Firearms 3 (Proton Pack), Intimidate 2, Investigation 2 Occult 2 (Layman\u2019s Terms), Persuasion 2, Science 2, Socialize 2 (Down to Earth), Subterfuge 2, Stealth 2, Streetwise 2 (New York), Survival 2(Urban), Weaponry 2<br /> <b>Skill Tricks: </b>Athletics (Size Up), Drive (Shortcuts), Intimidation (Don\u2019t Mess with Me)<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area of Expertise (Ecto-1, Proton Pack, Repair), Common Sense, Crack Driver, Fame 1, Fire Fight Style 2, Grappling Style 2,Hardy, Interdisciplinary Specialty (Bureaucracy, New York), Patient, Professional Training 3 (Soldier; Drive, Firearms, Survival), Quick Draw(Proton Pack), Safe Place 3, Trained Observer 1<br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"> <b>Ghostbuster Equipment </b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Containment Grid</b><br /> (Size 10, Durability 5)<br /> The Containment Grid stores all captured ephemeral entities. It can hold potentially hundreds, if not thousands of entities. An entity within the Containment Grid has the <i>Contained</i> Tilt, which persists unless the Grid is compromised. If the Grid is damaged or powered down, the contained spirits immediately awaken and escape (and are likely to be in a foul mood)<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Ecto-1</b><br /> Ecto-1 is a modified Cadillac Miller-Meteor Ambulance that serves as the Ghostbusters primary transport. It is heavily outfitted with weapons racks, sensory equipment, lights, and its distinctive siren. The vehicle stores 4 sets of Proton Packs, 6 PKE Meters, Ghost Traps and Ecto Visors, and an assortment of mundane equipment.<br /> <b>Durability:</b> 3, <b>Size:</b> 16, <b>Structure:</b> 19, <b>Acceleration:</b> 13, <b>Safe Speed:</b> 99, <b>Speed:</b> 192, <b>Handling:</b> 2, <b>Occupants:</b> 1+ 4<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Ecto-Visors</b><br /> (Size 1, Durability 1)<br /> These modified Night vision Goggles have the added benefit of being able to detect and perceive ephemeral entities are manifested or in Twilight, but would otherwise be imperceptible.<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Ectoplasm-Blower</b><br /> (Size 4, Durability 3)<br /> These devices project a stream of psycho-magnetherically charged ectoplasm (a.k.a mood slime) over a wide area. This weapon is used infrequently as it requires vast amount of difficult to obtain ectoplasm. The ectoplasm is charged with a strong positive resonance, and targets struck by it must make a Resolve +Composure or gain the [subdued Condition] Entities associated with death or negative concepts treat the charged ectoplasm as a Bane.<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Ghost Trap</b><br /> (Size 2, Durability 2)<br /> This trap is a sturdy box with a hinged lid and tethered to a cable (usually 3-5 yards) with a foot pedal at the end. Pressing the lever opens the box, which generates a force field capable of drawing in and trapping ephemeral entities. Ghost Traps may be positioned, or treated as a thrown weapon. When opened, the trap units a brilliant white cone of energy that draws in any nearby ephemeral entities (manifested, materialized, or in Twilight). Successfully capturing an entity requires that the trap is within 3 yards of the entity and that the user make a Dexterity +Athletics or Crafts roll (resisted by the entities Resistance trait). If the Entity is weakened (reduced to less than half its corpus or Essence) the Ghostbuster gains a +3 bonus to this roll. If successful, the entity gains the C<i>ontained</i> Tilt.<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Jump Suit:</b> The Ghostbusters signature Jumpsuit\u2019s are fire retardant and provide Armor 1/0.<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>PKE Meter</b><br /> (Size 1, Durability 1)<br /> PKE (Psychokinetic Energy) Meters are hand held devices that detect Ephemeral Entities. The device has a light display and arms that raise and lower based on the power and proximity of entity in Twilight.<br /> Reading the Meter is an Intelligence +Science roll. Non-Ephemeral Entities that use essence (Ridden, Hosts, and Werewolves) can also be detected, but at a -3 die penalty.<br /> <br /> For every success, the user may reveal a detail of their choice;<ul><li>Number of Entities</li> <li>Power: Entities Rank, highest trait score, and current essence (or equivalent)</li> <li>Proximity: Close (Less than 10 meters), Medium (11-30 meters), Far (31-60 meters).</li> </ul><br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Proton Pack</b><br /> <b>Damage</b>: +2 <b>Initiative:</b> -2 <b>Capacity:</b> Unlimited <b>Range: </b>25/50/100 <b>Strength:</b> 3, <b>Size:</b> 4<br /> These small charged particle accelerators fire a stream of energy capable of injuring or subduing ephemeral entities. Attacks with the Proton Pack are made with Dexterity +Firearms and have two primary settings.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Disruption:</i></b> The Disruption setting disperses an Ephemeral Entities Essence, essentially robbing it of power. Each success on an attack roll removes a point of essence from the Entity.<br /> If used against a non-ephemeral creature, the weapon only deals bashing damage (unless an exceptional success is scored, which converts the damage to lethal).<br /> <br /> <b><i>Containment:</i></b> The Containment setting holds an entity in place, allowing it to be maneuvered into the range of a ghost trap.<br /> This functions as a grapple attack, substituting Strength + Brawl with Dexterity +Firearms. If the Entity is weakened (reduced to less than half its corpus or Essence) the Ghostbuster gains a +3 bonus to this roll. The only moves than can be utilized this way are <i>Hold</i> and <i>Restrain</i>. The Entity may try to escape the grapple as normal.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Crossing the Streams is Bad.</i></b> It only happens if it done intentionally or a Ghostbusters attacking the same target as another Ghostbuster in the same turn suffers a Dramatic failure. What results is a catastrophic explosion that deals Force 6L (9-again, Knockdown) damage with a blast area of 20 yards. Any ephemeral entities in the area take aggravated damage instead of lethal. <hr /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Contained [Tilt]</b><br /> An ephemeral entity with this tilt is trapped within a particle containment grid. For as long as this entity has this condition, it is dormant \u2013 it cannot use influences, manifestations, or numina, take any actions, and is only vaguely aware of its environment or predicament<br /> <b>Possible sources:</b> Captured within a \u201cghost trap\u201d or \u201ccontainment grid\u201d<b>Resolution:</b> If the containment environment is compromised, either by choice or mishap.</span></i><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><i>Notes</i></b><br /> This write up of the Ghostbusters is based on the first two films, as well as parts from the Real Ghostbusters animated series (and the Ghostbusters RPG by West End Games). In addition, the Ghostbusters are considered Hunters, and may Risk Willpower and use Tactics (Hunter: The Vigil). They most often use the Exorcism, Measurements and Net tactics.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T18:07:45-07:00","id":499572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=499553#post499553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked Arkham City\u00b4s explanation about the Joker having Ra's Al Ghul\u00b4s Lazarus Pit\u00b4s phlebotinum in his blood, explaining his immortality and mental insanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty much what the above storyline suggested. Except R'as' version is a corrupted form. Vandal Savage got it raw. But it's just expanding upon Joker's already ambiguous origins, no clear answer one way or another while also offering fodder for interesting stories. Or in mechanical terms relating to this thread, turning him from Maniac Slasher to Legend Slasher. Though I always thought he had a touch of all the Slasher types, except perhaps Brute or Mask. He's shown himself capable of charm and subtlety, and visually he's a freak.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://www.flickeringmyth.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/02/joker-batman-1-600x404.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T20:02:01-07:00","id":499689,"title":"","content":"Frank Castle, AKA Frank Castiglione, <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/UtOEBmr.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">sadprincess14</a>, the Punisher<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue</b>: Temperance - He lives by a code and goes to great lengths to avoid possibly harming someone who 'doesn't deserve it.'<br /> <b>Vice</b>: Wrath - Born in blood, Frank Castle is a hateful killer to the core.<br /> <br /> Undertaking: Avenger<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes</b>: Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes</b>: Strength 3, Dexterity 3, Stamina 4<br /> <b>Social Attributes</b>: Presence 3, Manipulation 2, Composure 4<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills</b>: Computer 1, Crafts 2 (Ordnance), Investigation 3, Medicine 2, Politics 1 (Criminal), Science 1<br /> <br /> <b>Physical Skills</b>: Athletics 4, Brawl 3 (Dirty Fighting), Drive 3, Firearms 5, Stealth 3, Survival 4, Weaponry 4 (Improvised)<br /> <br /> <b>Social Skills</b>: Empathy 2 (Detecting Lies), Intimidation 4, Streetwise 3, Subterfuge 2<br /> <br /> <b>Merits</b>: Iron Stamina, Safe House (varies), Combat Awareness, Danger Sense, Emotional Detachment, Indomitable 4, Murder Expert, Disarm, Fast Reflexes, Quick Draw, Contacts 2 (Police, Military), Infamous 2 (In addition to being a video game, probably a variant of the Fame merit that allows a bonus to Intimidation instead of Socialize), Combat Marksmanship 5, Dirty Fighting 5, MAC 5, Sniping 5. Professional Training: Soldier 3.<br /> <br /> <b>Humanity</b>: 3. It really depends on the depiction but he usually skirts the edge. I would say he's verging on becoming a Legend but his adherence to his Code keeps him from falling that far.<br /> He would have the Major Calling Card Tell, letting people know the Punisher was there by leaving his symbol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-01-2015, 11:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T22:08:46-07:00","id":499817,"title":"","content":"<b>Pennywise The Dancing Clown (Stephen King's &quot;IT&quot;):</b> he can be multiple things in the NWOD, such as a True Fae, A Namtaru Beast with a Hunger For Prey or an Abyssal. Here are stats for the generic Hunter version.<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Cunning<br /> <b>Vice: </b>Sadistic/Mocking<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 4, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 5, Dexterity 3, Stamina 5<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 6, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics (History) 1, Crafts 1, Medicine 1, Occult 4, Politics 0, Investigation (Searching) 3, Science 1<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics (Chasing) 3, Brawl (Natural Weapons) 3, Drive 0, Firearms 1, Larceny 1, Stealth (Ambush) 3, Survival (Sewers) 3, Weaponry 2<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken 1, Empathy (Fears) 3, Expression (Humor) 1, Intimidation 5, Persuasion (Children) 2, Socialize 0, Streetwise 1, Subterfuge 3<br /> <br /> <b>Merits: </b>Vice-Ridden, Demolisher 3, Heavy Weapons 3 (Natural Weapons), Iron Stamina 3, Striking Looks +2 (Horrifying), Quick Healer<br /> <br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 6 [Inverted Vice/Virtue Refill]<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 6<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 3 + Athletics/Brawl/Weaponry<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 11<br /> <b>Health: </b>10<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 7<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers: </b>Alter Memory 5, Blackout 5, Clamber 3, Corpse Door, Dement 5, Dead Flesh 3, Drain 5 (Willpower), Dread Attack 3 (Natural Weapons), Dream Seeing 5, Giant Size, Hypnotism 3, Lord Of The Manor 5 (Sewers), Lurker In Darkness 3, Mist Form, New Face 5, Revivify 5, Strange Form 5 (Almost Anything), Terrify 5<br /> <br /> <b>Notes:</b> Pennywise uses Dement to inflict thematic hallucinations. These hallucinations cause fitting Conditions, such as Phobia (Vermin) by filling the room with roaches and rats. Pennywise and his Dread Powers can only be seen by certain individuals, usually those who were victims of it during childhood or those who accept that monsters can exist. Hunters find that, while they can see Pennywise\u2019s Clown Form for what it is, the monster\u2019s Dement is often personalized and visible only to each person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 05-02-2015, 01:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T07:44:57-07:00","id":500334,"title":"","content":"I don't know what stats, but <a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-087\" target=\"_blank\">SCP-087-1</a>had to be a Beast, that refuses to leave it's lair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5544,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5544-ancientswordrage","user":"AncientSwordRage","date":".  This isn't mark down, and the creatures not 087, thanks GottaGoFeast 05-02-2015, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5544-ancientswordrage","name":"AncientSwordRage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T11:22:56-07:00","id":500545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AncientSwordRage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=500334#post500334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know what stats, but [scp-87](<a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-087\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-087</a>) had to be a Beast, that refuses to leave it's lair.</div> </div> </div> </div>For starters, SCP-087 is the the staircase itself, while SCP-087-1 is the monster that inhabits the staircase.<br /> <br /> Secondly, SCP-087-1 is too weak to be a Primordial Beast. Furthermore, Beasts who never leave their Lairs can't satiate their Hungers.<br /> <br /> I would interpret SCP-087-1 as the face/projection of a greater Abyssal.<br /> <br /> Where is the rest of this Abyssal, you ask?<br /> <br /> At the bottom of the stairs.<br /> <br /> Of course, due to fluid canon of the SCP Foundation universe, my interpretation is <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/his-kind-eyes\" target=\"_blank\">not the only one</a>.</b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 05-02-2015, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T13:54:50-07:00","id":500751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=500545#post500545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For starters, SCP-087 is the the staircase itself, while SCP-087-1 is the monster that inhabits the staircase.<br /> <br /> Secondly, SCP-087-1 is too weak to be a Primordial Beast. Furthermore, Beasts who never leave their Lairs can't satiate their Hungers.<br /> <br /> I would interpret SCP-087-1 as the face/projection of a greater Abyssal.<br /> <br /> Where is the rest of this Abyssal, you ask?<br /> <br /> At the bottom of the stairs.<br /> <br /> Of course, due to fluid canon of the SCP Foundation universe, my interpretation is <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.scp-wiki.net/his-kind-eyes&amp;quot;]not</a> the only one[/URL].</b></span></div> </div> </div> </div>What's an Abyssal ,when it's at home?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5544-ancientswordrage","name":"AncientSwordRage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T14:01:45-07:00","id":500758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AncientSwordRage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=500751#post500751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What's an Abyssal ,when it's at home?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is still an Abyssal, as far as I know. The bottom of the stairs isn't really the Abyss, it's more of an Abyssal verge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T14:39:04-07:00","id":500786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AncientSwordRage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=500751#post500751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What's an Abyssal ,when it's at home?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> An Abyssal being inside a bigger one.<br /> <br /> The exception are Annunaki, who <i>are </i>the bigger ones. They're a lot like shelled crabs, if the shell was a stillborn universe,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T17:29:35-07:00","id":501010,"title":"","content":"<b>Parker Robins, AKA The Hood</b>. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://img4.wikia.nocookie.net/__cb20100204174629/marveldatabase/images/7/7d/Dark_Reign_The_Hood_Vol_1_4_Textless.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>At the end he got a lot of power but I'm going to mostly stat him around his ascent.<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue</b>: Ambitious<br /> <b>Vice</b>: Deceitful<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes</b>: Intelligence 2, Wits 4, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes</b>: Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes</b>: Presence 2, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills</b>: Computer 1, Occult 2 (Dark Magic), Politics 3 (Underworld)<br /> <br /> <b>Physical Skills</b>: Athletics 2 (Aerial Maneuvers), Brawl 2, Drive 1, Firearms 4 (Handguns), Larceny 2, Stealth 3, Weaponry 1<br /> <br /> <b>Social Skills</b>: Empathy 2, Expression 1 (Piano), Intimidation 1, Persuasion 2, Streetwise 3 (Criminals), Subterfuge 3 (Lying)<br /> <br /> <b>Merits</b>: Common Sense, Fast Reflexes 2, Professional Training 2 (Criminal), Ambidextrous, Fleet of Foot 2, Quick Draw (Handguns), Contacts 3 (Fences, Bruisers, Occultists), Fixer, Mentor 5 (Dormammu), Retainer 2 (John King, cousin and criminal), Status 2 (Underworld, Occultists), Firefight 3, Marksmanship 2<br /> <br /> <i>The Cloak</i> - A voluminous crimson cloak with a deep hood, the Hood is Dormammu's gateway into the world. So far it remains shut, but whoever wears it can gain access to its limited magics and hear the whispering urges of Dormammu.<br /> Mechanically, it works as a Whisperer. As long as someone is wearing it the Whisperer has access to them and can urge them to gather the necessary supernatural relics and spells to break a hole between worlds and let Dormammu in. In exchange, the Whisperer, itself a vestige of Dormammu, can tell its bearer secrets and offer advice, acting as a Mentor, occasionally offering extra abilities in exchange for services. This can lead to the wearer becoming Possessed, but I'll leave that up in the air for now.<br /> <b>Powers</b>:<br /> <i>Invisibility</i>: Whoever wears the cloak can, as an instant action, turn invisible. This does not remove other traces of their presence, only their visible form. If a Willpower point is spent, for the rest of the scene the invisibility can be activated and deactivated reflexively. Attacking breaks the wearer out of the invisibility effect.<br /> <i>True Sight</i>: Providing the wearer is acting in accordance with its Whisperer, with the spending of a Willpower point the cloak can grant them the ability to pierce all illusions and supernatural deceptions for the scene. In the case of a Clash of Wills, the dicepool for the bearer is 5 + Resolve.<br /> <i>Lightning Strike</i>: When the wearer of the cloak is overwhelmed, the Whisperer can summon forth the least of its master's power, firing bolts of arcane lightning at nearby enemies. Treat these attacks similar to those from Firearms, as Defense can not normally be used against them. The dice pool for attacks is 5 and they do Lethal damage. Only one lightning bolt may be sent per round and they use up the wearers instant action for the turn as the Whisperer commandeers their soul.<br /> <br /> <i>The Boots</i> - A pair of tall black boots with a thick cleated heel, the boots offer their wearer a simple gift. The ability to defy gravity. Simply put, with a thought, the boots can be made to hit 'ground' wherever they land. This allows the wearer to 'fly' at natural speeds and ascend as fast as they might climb stairs. It can even allow the wearer to travel upside down. Getting used to the change can take time, and until the wearer learns the Aerial Maneuvers specialty, they suffer a -2 penalty to close combat while up in the air and another -2 penalty to physical actions taken while upside down.<br /> <br /> The relics are a bit powerful for World of Darkness but pretty appropriate considering their source. Like the Hood himself, they're simple things that, when used pragmatically, can reap great rewards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-02-2015, 08:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T02:33:19-07:00","id":501580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=500758#post500758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is still an Abyssal, as far as I know. The bottom of the stairs isn't really the Abyss, it's more of an Abyssal verge.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I mean is, by <a href=\"http://&quot;http://idioms.thefreedictionary.com/What%27s+when+it%27s+at+home%3F\u201d\" target=\"_blank\">When it's at home</a>, is that I have no idea what an abyssal is. And I vaguely know what the abyss is, as it lies between this world and supernal...but no clue what a verge of it would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5544,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5544-ancientswordrage","user":"AncientSwordRage","date":". 05-03-2015, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5544-ancientswordrage","name":"AncientSwordRage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T09:25:06-07:00","id":501774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AncientSwordRage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=501580#post501580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What I mean is, by <a href=\"https://\u201c&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://idioms.thefreedictionary.com/What%27s+when+it%27s+at+home%3F\u201d]When</a> it's at home[/url], is that I have no idea what an abyssal is. And I vaguely know what the abyss is, as it lies between this world and supernal...but no clue what a verge of it would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Abyss is a place formed of all the symbols that are fundamentally untrue. An abyssal verge would be a place where reality as we know it simply...breaks. At extreme levels, 1+1 may not necessarily equal 2, up and down aren't opposite directions, and gravity is a repulsive force.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T09:55:44-07:00","id":503027,"title":"","content":"Today's Submission<br /> <br /> <b>Pinhead</b><br /> The entity known as \u201cPinhead\u201d is a high ranking Cenobite. Cenobites are a caste of Demonic beings that hail from a realm known only as the Labyrinth and do the bidding of a vast alien entity called Leviathan. Pinheads many titles include \u201cThe Black Pope of Hell\u201d, \u201cThe Angel of Suffering\u201d or simply \u201cThe Priest\u201d. As befitting his station, Pinhead is vastly powerful and is largely immune to anything as vulgar as physical violence or the demands of petty conjurers. So great is his power it is said that Pinhead only answers to Leviathan itself. Despite his transformation into a Cenobite, Pinhead retains a significant amount of his former human perspective and retains his Virtue and Vice.<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue: </b>Contemplative \u2013 Pinhead is measured and thoughtful, never taking any action (either merciful or cruel) without due consideration.<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Ennui \u2013 Pinhead is prone to boredom and disenchantment, eventually questioning the purpose of existence entirely. <br /> <br /> <b>Rank:</b> 5 (Dominion)<br /> <b>Malapraxis:</b> Pinhead is linked to the vices exercised in pursuit of extreme forms of pleasure and pain. He also has some power over those with an obsession for solving riddles and puzzles.<br /> <b>Attributes: </b>Power: 14, Finesse: 14, Resistance: 14<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 50<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 28<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 14<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 33<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 19<br /> <b>Influences: </b>Desire 3, Suffering 3<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Pinhead can only use manifestations in the presence of a solved LeMarchand puzzle box. Anyone holding a puzzle box can make an offer or negotiation that Pinhead must hear out before taking any other action.<br /> <b>Bane: </b>LeMarchand\u2019s Puzzle Boxes<br /> <b>Demonic Powers:</b> Corruption, Dragon\u2019s Tongue, Lord of Lies, Keeper of Secrets, Soul of Sin<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Twilight Form*; Avernian Gateway, Discorporate, Image, Materialize, Shadow Gateway<br /> <b>Numina</b>: Awe, Babel (Inferno.pg. 52), Blast, Dement, Ensnare (Book of Spirits, pg. 140), Hallucination, Rapture, Regenerate, Seek, Telekinesis<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>The Lament Configuration</b><br /> It is believed that Phillip LeMarchand (a French architect, artisan, designer, and possibly mass-murderer) constructed more than 270 of his unique puzzle boxes before he vanished. The rumors surrounding the devices suggest that they can provide \u201cthe ultimate pleasure\u201d once solved. Details about what that \u201cpleasure\u201d might be remain vague. This particular puzzle \u201cThe Lament Configuration\u201d is LeMarchand's first and arguably most classic, puzzle construct. When operated properly, a pleasing melody issues from within which belies its true nature.<br /> <b>Size:</b> 1 <b>Durability:</b> 4 <b>Availability: </b>4<br /> <br /> <b>Powers</b><br /> <i>Bad Penny: </i>The Lament Configuration is drawn to those that will use the device to its full potential (most commonly jaded thrill seekers or the insatiably curious).<br /> <br /> <i>Puzzle Box: </i>Wits/Intelligence + Academics/Investigation (extended; 10 minutes/10 successes). A success opens the box and plays a pleasant melody. If willpower were spent for any of the extended rolls, the puzzle box instead summons Pinhead and a cadre of attendant Cenobites. This effect is considered an Invocation (Inferno, pg. 74).<br /> <br /> <i>Reward Temptation:</i> Manipulation +Subterfuge; Success/Days; Regain Willpower when acting in accordance to Vice. While under the influence of this ability, the user cannot regain willpower from Virtue, suffers a -1 to Breaking Point checks and gains the <i>Obsession [Solving the Puzzlebox] </i>Condition<br /> <br /> <i>Unbreakable</i>: Immune to Mundane Damage<br /> <hr /><br /> <b><i>Notes:</i></b> The depiction of Pinhead has varied widely over the series of films, novels, and comics adaptations. The version presented draws inspiration from the first 3 films and the comic series (both the original from Epic and the recent series from BOOM!)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T17:11:44-07:00","id":511322,"title":"","content":"I'm not very good at crunch, but I do like me some Hotline Miami:<br /> <br /> <b>The Fans:</b><br /> <br /> Ashwood Abbey cell. After discovering an almost godlike killer had effectively killed every member of the Russian Mafia in Miami, these five people fell in love, and decided that an escape from their hated, shallow lives would be to cosplay him. Accurately. They're only starting up, but already the changelings of the Court of Eternal Summer quietly trade warnings and legends about a colorful van that disgorges masked killers who do not negotiate, do not speak, only kill, leaving no survivors among their intended targets. All stories of them come from the people they spare, and to their credit they don't hurt innocents, only attacking people they've heard bad stories about. What they <i>don't </i>do, noticeably, is question whether or not the targets deserve mercy...and most of said targets are mortal.<br /> <br /> <b>Tony:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Virtue: </b>Loyal. He's rude, abrasive, and more than a tad cruel, but Tony's the best friend you could ever have. He helps you hide the bodies, after all.<br /> <br /> <b>Vice: </b>Sadistic. You don't develop a killing style based around literally beating the life out of people with nearly-bare fists without the capacity to enjoy it.<br /> <br /> The tiger-masked effective leader of the Fans, Tony is a self-admitted thug with a pair of enchanted brass knuckles that enhance his already-gifted strength, allowing him to kill or incapacitate with a single punch. Of the Fans, he's the most bloodthirsty and least altruistic, seeing the Vigil as mostly a way to indulge his bloodthirst in a borderline-acceptable way.<br /> <br /> <b>Corey<br /> <br /> Virtue: </b>Dedicated. Corey spent years working on her martial arts and reflexes, and she applies that focus to everything in her life.<br /> <br /> <b>Vice</b>: Submissive. She doesn't really like thinking for herself, she finds it a lot easier to let her friends do the planning. If that involves mass murder, so be it.<br /> <br /> The lithe, zebra-masked stealth specialist, Corey is a quiet, meek woman who mostly signed up to sharpen her already masterful skills with a katana. Corey possesses almost superhuman reflexes; if she's anticipating violence, she can actually roll out of the way of gunfire, so long as she knows who's shooting and where from.<br /> <br /> <b>The Swan Twins (Alex and Ash Davis)<br /> <br /> Virtue</b>: Loyal. The Swans define loyalty, to each other and to their friends. It even reflects their hunting style, the twins are always working as a team to counterbalance their weaknesses.<br /> <br /> <b>Vice: </b>Cynical. Alex, and to a lesser extent Ash, are so pessimistic about human nature that killing people honestly doesn't strike hem as an inherently bad thing.<br /> <br /> Alex and Ash Davis are fraternal twins, and revel in the fact that if you can't see their faces it's a bit hard to tell either of the muscular siblings apart (they both wear motorcycle helmets decked out to resemble identical swan heads, with the only clue to who's who being the number on the forehead). Ash is the team's planner and mechanic, while Alex is the muscle-not that it matters much, because the Twins never stray far from each other during a mission. Alex is capable of wielding a chainsaw as a sword, while Ash provides gun support from safely behind her.<br /> <br /> <b>Mark<br /> <br /> Virtue</b>: Kind. Mark's the only Fan for whom altruism is the primary motivation; he honestly thinks they're doing something to help.<br /> <br /> <b>Vice: </b>Indulgent. Mark's a hedonist, born and bred. Food, adrenaline, drugs, you name is, he's done it, and is doing it.<br /> <br /> Tall and wide, bear-masked Mark doesn't really have a role on the team, but given how he can wield a machine gun in each hand without hurting himself, nobody minds. He's about the closest thing to a &quot;true Hunter&quot; of the Fans, being here just as much for the sake of saving people as getting his heroic bloodshed kicks, but he's still an Abbey man; he assigns as much moral weight to his bloodthirst as he does buying pizzas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T18:43:18-07:00","id":511404,"title":"","content":"While I'm at it, 50 Blessings is a Conspiracy (or is it a Cult?) with an Endowment based on masks as a proxy for skinthieving (the Colonel discovered the art during his breakdown, having shapeshifted into an actual panther at one point when parading around in that skin screaming about being a dumb, trained animal).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T03:43:12-07:00","id":512793,"title":"","content":"I've decided that Bruce Banner/Hulk is a Zeko Promethean. His disfigurement is his appearance as The Hulk. His disquiet makes everyone fear him. He has all the refinements that augment strength and stamina. <br /> <br /> The Ultron/Vision paradigm snacks of an unfleshed passing on the divine fire but I've not work out any more specifics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5544-ancientswordrage","name":"AncientSwordRage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T18:08:52-07:00","id":514677,"title":"","content":"Various anime characters as nWoD characters....<br /> <br /> Tuxedo Mask is a Hunter, probably with a Tier 1 Cell as he doesn't have that great of powers<br /> The Sailor Senshi are probably Fairest Changelings, though I could see Acanthus or Thyrsus Mages for some of them<br /> Roy Mustang is a Mage, any kind could work<br /> Motoko Kusanagi is an elite Tier 3 Hunter with cybernetic endowments with Section 9 as a Japanese branch of Task Force Valkyrie<br /> Reika Kitami is obviously a Daeva vampire working for Belial's Brood<br /> Alucard could fit in any of the five clans, and would be Unaligned and allied with Hunters<br /> Seto Kaiba is an Invictus Ventrue<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T18:34:23-07:00","id":514692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=514677#post514677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Various anime characters as nWoD characters....<br /> <br /> Tuxedo Mask is a Hunter, probably with a Tier 1 Cell as he doesn't have that great of powers.<br /> The Sailor Senshi are probably Fairest Changelings, though I could see Acanthus or Thyrsus Mages for some of them</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, his Cell are Inner Senshi. But we know the ALL are Princesess ( and one Prince ) - such <i>Hopefull</i>... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=514677#post514677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Roy Mustang is a Mage, any kind could work</div> </div> </div> </div>Obrimos Adamantine Arrow, with very hgih Matter. In FMA all Mages have Matter Arcanum, others are just for <b>very</b> special effects. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=514677#post514677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Motoko Kusanagi is an elite Tier 3 Hunter with cybernetic endowments with Section 9 as a Japanese branch of Task Force Valkyrie</div> </div> </div> </div>TFV do not have national branches, as far as I know. But I agree that Section 9 would be a mirror represntative of TFV in Japan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=514677#post514677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alucard could fit in any of the five clans, and would be Unaligned and allied with Hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div>He is TOTALLY Gangrel - did you see what his &quot;true form&quot; looks like? A little help...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://static.comicvine.com/uploads/scale_super/13/135592/2996154-0114958427-12247.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Not to forget his bestially outlook on life - he really<i><b> is </b></i>much closer to Beast than most of other vampires in series. Also, he loves to fight and comepete with other Kindreds - to test his mind and body limits. Perfect Gangrel! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T15:23:21-07:00","id":538846,"title":"","content":"Oh cool, this is still going strong. I posted earlier in this about doing up the Originals as part of Vampire the Requiem, basically making them another origin story for the five main clans and VII, even while pointing out no one really believes it because of the obvious contradictions in known vampire history. Decided to try an alternate take, of the &quot;TVD&quot; style vampires as their own clan, based off them.<br /> <br /> Basically, Clan Mikaelson, though they'd probably have a cooler, more ancient sounding name, like the others. Also would allow me to use it, without those pesky copyright issues. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So basically, this particular clan got all the luck. Many of their weaknesses are easily mitigated, except for one. OR, you can skip the Clan business and make them replace the normal vampire template, and treat the Main Five Clans as bloodlines spun off from the five siblings. Can make it work either way.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u>Clan Mikaelson</u></span><br /> <br /> <i>Favored Attributes:</i> Strength, and Charisma<br /> <br /> <i>Clan Disciplines</i>: Celerity, Dominate, and Vigor<br /> <br /> <i>Clan Merits:</i> In a rare display, this clan also has a few Merits all shared by their members. This does not cost extra, and is considered covered by their enhanced Clan Weakness. All Clan members have the <b>Blush of Life </b>and <b>Eat Food</b> merits, always active without spending Blood to activate. They also all possess <b>Heightened Sense</b><b>s</b>.<br /> <br /> For some strange reason, this clan takes less damage from sunlight and fire. While not immune, these are never aggravated damage for them, letting them survive exposure a few precious seconds longer, and allows them to recover from its burns like any other form of damage. Some have even found mages willing to craft them rings that let them avoid sunlight damage completely. Fortunately, these rings are useless to other Clans, and each ring is bound to the vampire it's made for. This comes with a trade-off however.<br /> <br /> <i>Clan Weakness:</i><br /> <b>Flipping the Switch:</b> They have a more intense Beast, due to having ALL their emotions heightened, but they don't seem to suffer from Degeneration in their natural state. Vampires of this Clan have to resist a frenzy check at a -2 penalty, not just for rage or fear, but sadness and grief. But rather than degenerate, when they fail a roll, they have the option of either taking the frenzy OR &quot;flipping the switch&quot;.<br /> <br /> This sets their Humanity to 1, basically becoming either a psychopath or a sociopath, depending on their normal psychological makeup. Rather than going on a rage or fear induced bender on the spot, they're more likely to walk away, and then go on a several weeks-long (or month or even YEARS) murder spree as they do what they want, when they want, how they want, and remove the hearts of anyone who tries to tell them otherwise.<br /> <br /> Normally, the vampire can flip the switch back any time, but... they're usually having too good a time to do so, without some kind of outside stimulus. Usually this involves encountering someone or something that actually manages to make them feel a positive emotion again, which flips their Humanity back to normal, at which point, they have to make a massive Humanity check based on the worst things they did while &quot;off&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Wooden Doom:</b> In trade for their gentler treatment of sunlight, this Clan finds wood to be much more deadly. A wooden weapon of any kind impedes their ability heal, preventing them from spending blood to heal the damage until the weapon is removed. In addition, a successful Stake attack is an instant death sentence, though the vampire does get to attempt to soak the damage normally. If successful, the heart was just missed, or the vampire is managing to hold the weapon back from fully penetrating.<br /> <br /> <b>RSVP: </b> Clan Mikaelson cannot enter a private residence uninvited. The threshold acts like a kind of invisible barrier preventing entry. Only someone in residence can invite them in, though this includes OTHER invited guests. A total stranger cannot invite someone in. Regardless, their powers of Dominate only make this a bothersome effect if no one is home.<br /> <br /> <i>Supernatural Merit</i><br /> <b>Daylight Ring (5 pts) </b>- Requires an Awakened contact, or a Mentor or Ally with said contact. Grants a ring that prevents all damage from sunlight, and even allows the wearer to function normally during the day with no ill effects. Can only be used by vampires of Clan Mikaelson. Each ring is crafted for a specific vampire and cannot be used by any other.<br /> <br /> <u><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Originals</span></u><br /> Supposedly there are six people who founded this Clan, a Nordic (or possibly Celtic) warrior and his five children. They were transformed into vampires by their mother, a powerful witch (Awakened Thrysus Mage) to fight off a tribe of Pure werewolves that were harassing their settlement. Since then, their parents became disgusted by what they had created, and supposedly to this day, the father hunts his children, seeking to destroy their entire bloodline. A boogeyman of vampire lore, he's referred to a &quot;Mikael the Destroyer&quot;, and anytime there's a large number of vampiric deaths that go unexplained, they're attributed to him.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Original&quot; members of this clan are Methuselahs, being over a thousand years old, and have a few unique traits attributed to them.<br /> <br /> <b>Invulnerability: </b>the Originals cannot be destroyed. They are still vulnerable to the weaknesses of a vampire, but this does not kill them, but instead drives them into torpor. While in torpor, their bodies become indestructible. They cannot be burned, mutilated, or harmed in any fashion. Best one can do is lock them up in a box and dump it into the river, and hope you're dead before someone finds them and accidentally lets them out. How? Supposedly some consequence of the spell used to make them what they are.<br /> <br /> Still, no spell is perfect, and there was one weakness: the wood of the venerable white oak trees of the forest used in the ritual. Once they learned of it's effect, the family rightly burned it down, and saw to it that over the centuries, that the forest was eradicated. Only two known weapons are known to exist, a vial of ash, made of the burned remnants of those trees, which when coating a weapon and plunged into the heart, locks the Original in torpor until the item is removed. Vials of this have been passed around fo centuries, and no one is sure how many still exist. A few buy a vial, only to find out to their short-lived surprised, that they bought a fake.<br /> <br /> The other is a white oak stake, enchanted by their now-deceased mother, and given to Mikael the Destroyer. It can not only kill their children instantly, but it can bring the Final Death to ANY vampire staked by it. If true, it would explain the man's legendary death rate. Still, occassionally rumors surface that another object made from a tree of that long-lost forest has been found, and those who believe in these figures scramble over each other to possess it. <br /> <br /> <b>Superior Dominate: </b> the Originals powers of compulsion are far more potent than others of their kind. Basically, an Original, when using Dominate, prevents a character from applying their Supernatural Resistance attribute (Blood Potency for vampires, Gnosis for Mages, etc). to the roll, meaning other supernaturals are no better than your average humans when resisting them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3200,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","user":"Barachiel","date":". 06-03-2015, 06:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T02:38:27-07:00","id":539375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=349438#post349438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't Dr. Who be one of those Reincarnating Immortals?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Doctor who is a demon<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/9chfpZK.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <img