he-Hearse-(A-Geist-The-Sin-Eaters-Manifestation\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.giantitp.com/forums/showt...-Manifestation</a>).</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you put that into PDF format?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T15:45:13-07:00","id":541773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=349489#post349489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kratos (God Of War): probably way too Exalted-like to fit, but maybe he could be an Astral personification of Indignation Against The Divine, or a Mage that was trapped in the Astral Realms and turned into such a personification. Maybe he was an changeling of the Ogre Seeming who reached Wyrd 10 and decided that it was time to bring the fight to the Gentry by harnessing their powers. If he is a True Fae, his Titles would be himself (Actor), the Blades Of Exile (Prop) and the Head Of Medusa (Prop), while the other items are Tokens or Hedgespun. If you want to play as a character in a more mythical NWoD that simply has Kratos' powers, a Thyrsus or Mastigos Mage can work. His Blades Of Exile would be a Pandemonium Artifact with the Ranged Blow spell (Space 3), Mind spells for subduing lesser/median life forms and a Forces spell for ignoring gravity while climbing. Put dots in Life and Matter for physical prowess, super endurance, regeneration and improving/breaking objects. Also put dots in Forces, Death and Prime for imitating his magical abilities from the games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kratos is a Scion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T23:15:15-07:00","id":542314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=492365#post492365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now here goes something very gory: the fighters and fiends of Mortal Kombat!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 700px; height: 50px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Character</span></b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Type</span></b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Sub-type</span></b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Faction</span></b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Notes</span></b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Sub-zero</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mage</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Moros</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Adamantine Arrow</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Uses Forces/Matter to redirect heat and create ice.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Scorpion</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mage</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mastigos</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Apostate</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Gains attack bonuses when uncloaking his Nimbus.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Reptile</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mage</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Thyrsus</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Seers Of The Throne</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Uses Life to gain his powers of acid spit/natural weaponry/long tongue and Forces for his chi blasts/invisibility.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Baraka</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Beast</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Namtaru</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Tyrant</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Expert user of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=230692#post230692\">Claws Of The Motherfucker.</a></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Shokans And Centaurians</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Pandorans</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Torch- born</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Seers Of The Throne</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Have been blessed through the Practice of Excision by Shao Khan so that they do not suffer from Dormancy and can regain Pyros by fighting non-Prometheans.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Cyrax</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mortal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Hunter</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Task Force: Valkyrie</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">A whole lot of money went into his Endowments. they can tell you that much.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Sektor</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Genius</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Grimm</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Rogue</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Used the Endowments he received from Valkyrie as inspiration for his own Wonders. He goes from unmada to Illuminated rapidly.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Smoke</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mage</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mastigos</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Adamantine Arrow</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Uses a mix of Space and Mind for his stealth, and Matter to conjure his namesake.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Johnny Cage</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mortal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Psychic/Hunter</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Task Force: Valkyrie</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Uses Telekinesis to speed himself up and fire kinetic blasts.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Sonya Blade</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mortal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Psychic/Hunter</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Task Force: Valkyrie</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Uses Telekinesis to fire kinetic blasts and ESP to investigate.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Jax</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mortal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Hunter</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Task Force: Valkyrie</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">See Cyrax.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Quan Chi</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mage</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Moros</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Apostate</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Is a member of the Bokor Legacy, which gives him voodoo necromancy.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Shang Tsung</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mage</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Moros</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Seers Of The Throne</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Is a member of the Tremere Lich Legacy, which allows him to stay young by stealing souls.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Stryker</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mortal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Hunter</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Task Force: Valkyrie</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Is very unpopular.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Kitana</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Changeling</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Fairest</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Winter Court</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Eden is actually a Hedge Kingdom. The King and Queen of Eden are benevolent Charlatan Gentry.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Jade</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Changeling</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Fairest</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Winter Court</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">See above.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Sindel</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Gentry</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Fairest</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Seers Of The Throne</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">She returns to her usual Gentry wickedness while under Shao Khan's spell.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mileena</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mage</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mastigos</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Seers Of The Throne</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Originally a soulless creation of Shang Tsung, she learned how to steal souls by observing him and used a stolen Mage soul as a weak link to the Supernal. She suffers from Branding and Bedlam Paradoxes often due to her counterfeit Awakening, and even her Nimbus is monstrous.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Raiden</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Spirit</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Thunder</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Adamantine Arrow</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Despite not being a Mage, he is still considered an honorary member of the Arrow due to his wisdom and combat skills.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Liu Kang</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mage</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Obrimos</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Adamantine Arrow</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Often lets hubris dictate his actions. Probably has lower Wisdom than average.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Kung Lao</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mortal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Psychic</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Adamantine Arrow</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Despite not being a Mage, is still considered an honorary member of the Arrow for displaying great combat skills. Uses Telekinesis to control his hat, which is Enhanced by the Matter Arcanum.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Kano</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Slasher</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Psycho</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Seers Of The Throne</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Has access to Imbued and Enhanced items created by kidnapped Mages. Is obsessed with Sonya, as per usual for his Undertaking.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Kenshi</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mortal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Psychic/Hunter</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Task Force: Valkyrie</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Is very good with Telekinesis and compensates his blindness with ESP.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Nightwolf</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mage</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Thyrsus</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Apostate</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Mostly does his own thing, but joins the Arrow/Valkyrie to defend Earth when necessary.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Shao Khan</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Exarch</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Unknown</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">See Notes</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">What we see as Shao Khan is actually just an Ochemata (extremely powerful sub-soul of the REAL Shao Khan). All characters that are listed above as Seers Of The Throne are serving him. Baraka is a Tyrant instead because he takes over Khan's throne in his Mortal Kombat 2 ending.</td> </tr> </table></div> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with most of these, but Scorpion is either a Torn Sin-Eater, with similar stats as your Ghostrider write up, or a Legend Slasher. Reptile was never human to begin with; Hobgoblin? Mutant? Some kind of Beast?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T00:58:24-07:00","id":542378,"title":"","content":"Are any of you familiar with Gogo Bomango? I was thinking of the character in terms of Beast. Which fits surprisingly well.<br /> <br /> While Gogo adores a dragon, she comes off as an Anakim with a hunger for punishment despite her talent for ruining things. Thinking of the other other two main characters in WoD terms. Gogo's sister, Didi, comes off as a Mage, and Andy, her human best friend/leash/something... to borrow the phrase, her Other, would be a mortal and the human reflecting Gogo's Trusted Friend merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T00:03:55-07:00","id":543583,"title":"","content":"All the Soul Reaper characters from the anime Bleach are Sin-Eaters, with a special Sword Manifestation. (If someone wants to stat that up, let me know.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T01:43:44-07:00","id":543627,"title":"","content":"My double check says the math is wrong but <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=538993#post538993\">Elsa </a>has shown up before.<br /> Rather recently too...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T00:52:47-07:00","id":556661,"title":"","content":"Some people have all ready listed a few superheroes, so I feel it's worth pointing out that there's a far more appropriate system for the VAST majority of comicbook characters: Sardonyx. That said, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Marvel's</span> Punisher is clearly a High-Morality Slasher, of the (somewhat ironic) Avenger Undertaking. A very effective one at that, with 48,502 confirmed kills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T08:26:47-07:00","id":561952,"title":"","content":"<b>Betelgeuse \u201cBeetlejuice\u201d </b><br /> <b>Virtue: </b>Humor \u2013 Betelgeuse is an irreverent wisecracker who makes light of any situation, no matter how grim, dire, or morbid.<br /> <b>Vice: </b>Troublemaker - Betelgeuse is an incorrigible mischief maker and driven to cause trouble wherever he goes. He is also a lecherous, debauched creature that lives (un) life to its fullest. <br /> <br /> <b>Rank:</b> 3 [Ghost]<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 8, Finesse 8, Resistance 8<br /> <b>Integrity: </b>5<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 20<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 16<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 8<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 21<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 13<br /> <b>Influences:</b> Fear 3<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Speaking his name 3times in his presence forces Betelgeuse to discorporate.<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Sandworms<br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Discorporate, Materialize, Possess, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Awe, Dement, Flight of Shadows, Hallucination, Seek, Phantom Arsenal, Telekinesis<br /> <br /> <b>Notes:</b> This presents the title character (and \u201cGhost with the Most\u201d) from the film. Betelgeuse is considered to be a very potent Ghost of indeterminate age (no one knows for sure, but he jokes about having lived through the Black Plague). He has immense raw power, he is quick witted (even though he is as subtle as a sledgehammer) and shows remarkable tenacity (even though he is a slave to his many, many vices). He find\u2019s existence in the Underworld terribly boring and is constantly seeking ways to permanently anchor himself in the material world.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T09:18:39-07:00","id":563072,"title":"","content":"<b>Goliath</b><br /> <br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Justice; Goliath is bold and fiercely protective of his people. While occasionally stubborn, his sense of righteousness always guides his actions.<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Temper; Goliath\u2019s anger is a terrible thing to behold, and he can become bitterly vengeful against persistent foes.<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 3, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 5, Dexterity 4, Stamina 5<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 5, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 2 (Literature), Athletics 4 (Climbing), Brawl 5, Crafts 1 (Masonry), Empathy 2, Expression 3(Inspiring), Intimidation 5, Investigation 3, Occult 2 (Sorcery), Persuasion 3(Leadership), Politics 2, Stealth 4(Castles), Survival 4 (Navigation), Weaponry 2 (Improvised)<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area of Expertise (Climbing, Leadership), Common Sense, Defensive Combat (Brawl), Demolisher 2, Direction Sense, Giant, Hardy 3,Inspiring, Iron Stamina 3, Iron Will, Language (Archaic English, Modern English, likely others), Professional Training 4(Warrior; Brawl, Intimidation, Persuasion), Safe Place 4 (Clock Tower), Status 5 (Manhattan Clan), Striking Looks 2, Style: Close Quarter Combat 4, Style: Grappling 2, Style: Heavy Weapons 1, Style: Street Fighting 5, Trained Observer 1, True Friend (Det. Elisa Maza)<br /> <br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 8<br /> <b>Potency: </b>4 [Mortal Remains, pg. 104-105]<br /> <b>Size:</b> 6<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 8<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 3/1<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 8<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 15 [Species Factor 6]<br /> <b>Health:</b> 11<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers</b><br /> <b>Dread Attack: </b>Goliath has claws that are razor sharp and hard as stone; they are considered a +1 weapon with AP 1.<br /> <br /> <b>Leaping:</b> Goliath\u2019s leaping and jumping distances are tripled.<br /> <br /> <b>Monstrous Resilience: </b>Goliath is incredibly sturdy and can shrug off grievous wounds. When he suffers a physical Tilt, he may spend 1 willpower as a reflexive action, ending the Tilt immediately.<br /> <br /> <b>Roar</b>: This Dread Power allows Goliath to unleash an unearthly bellow, striking fear into the hearts of his enemies.<br /> <i><b>Cost:</b> 1 Willpower <b>Action:</b> Instant <b>Dice Pool:</b> Presence + Expression + Potency versus Composure</i><br /> The roar can be heard for miles, but the Dread Power takes effect on any targets within 40 yards. Affected subjects are overcome by fear and gain the \u201cFrightened\u201d Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Sharp Senses:</b> Goliath\u2019s senses are especially keen. He receives +1 to all perception rolls, and can see clearly in almost total darkness.<br /> <br /> <b>Stone Sleep:</b> Goliath turns to stone during the day. From dawn until dusk, regardless of whether or not he is actually exposed to daylight, his body transforms into a granite statue with a Durability of 3 and Structure equal to his health boxes. Goliath is immobile and unaware of any outside events in this state and is exceptionally vulnerable. On the plus side, Stone Sleep always refreshes a point of willpower and completely heals any and all non-aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Tail: </b>Goliath has a thick, muscular tail. This tail grants Goliath a +2 bonus to rolls involving balance, and may be used to make unarmed attacks.<br /> <br /> <b>Titan\u2019s Strength: </b>Goliath can automatically lift anything with a Size equal to or less than 9. If he throws lighter objects like a weapon, that item is considered aerodynamic. Goliath gains an additional 3 dots to any roll involving a feat of strength. These dice do not apply to combat actions, only feats.<br /> <br /> <b>Unholy Stamina: </b>Goliath may spend 1 Willpower to gain a +2 bonus to stamina. This bonus lasts until the end of the scene. Recalculate appropriate traits (Speed, Health, Initiative, Defense) using the new Attribute score.<br /> <br /> <b>Unholy Strength: </b>Goliath may spend 1 Willpower to gain a +3 bonus to strength. This bonus lasts until the end of the scene. Recalculate appropriate traits (Speed, Health, Initiative, Defense) using the new Attribute score.<br /> <br /> <b>Wings: </b>Goliath\u2019s wings allow him to glide at 3 times his normal speed. As long as the he has a way to gain some altitude, Goliath can glide up to 1 mile in distance and can change direction at will. With a successful Dexterity + Athletics roll, he can swoop upwards; effectively climbing without using handholds.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Notes:</i></b><br /> This write up is based on Goliath from the Gargoyles animated series. It uses the Monster rules presented in Hunter: The Vigil, and updated in Mortal Remains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 08-20-2015, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T19:17:02-07:00","id":618313,"title":"","content":"Ok, so...my first attempt at writing stats for the Slender Man as a God-Machine Angel didn't turn out so well. I decided to try again, with an additional suggestion for how to use him in the NWOD.<br /> <br /> If Slendy is an Angel, the Proxies could be Stigmatics or low Rank Angels, the locations with irregular space-time are part of Infrastructures and the occasional mutated critters like the Rake are Cryptids. Here are the updated Angel stats:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Virtue:</b> Hidden<br /> <br /> <b>Vice:</b> Observant<br /> <br /> <b>Rank:</b> 4<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 10, Finesse 8, Resistance 10<br /> <br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 17<br /> <br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <br /> <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 9<br /> <br /> <b>Speed:</b> 14<br /> <br /> <b>Max Essence/Per Turn:</b> 40/12<br /> <br /> <b>Influence:</b> Darkness &amp; Mist 4, Memories 3<br /> <br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Twilight Form, Materialize, Discorporate<br /> <br /> <b>Suggested Ban:</b> The Slender Man cannot communicate in immediately understandable ways. He might use Numina, Manifestations, Influences and similar methods to manipulate people with varying degrees of subtlety and success. Despite this, any clear use of speech or the written word is beyond him.<br /> <br /> <b>Suggested Bane:</b> There is no definitive answer for this, but the Tulpa Effect is the most prominent idea.<br /> <br /> <b>Numina:</b> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/480962-ephemeral-being-house-rules-new-epic-numen\">Ravage, Aegis,</a></b> Awe, Hallucination, Implant Mission, Fluid Form, Regenerate, Sign</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Alternate Interpretation:<br /> <br /> He might have started out as an internet meme like in real life. However, the Mythos carried such powerful symbols that the resulting collective belief that the Slender Man could be real made him so. In this scenario, the Slender Man is a being from the Temenos. However, since he is the central figure of an entire mythology that portrays him as very powerful, he has higher Rank than the God-Machine Angel version. I also like the idea that Slender Man is simply the projection of an unseen entity into our world. So I made Astral Slender Man the Royal Avatar of a Rank 6 entity. Determining what said entity might be like is better off in the hands of more experienced Storytellers. Here are the Royal Avatar stats:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Rank:</b> 5<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 13, Finesse 11, Resistance 15<br /> <br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 22<br /> <br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <br /> <b>Defense:</b> 8<br /> <br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 13<br /> <br /> <b>Speed:</b> 18<br /> <br /> <b>Max Essence/Per Turn:</b> 50/15<br /> <br /> <b>Influence:</b> Darkness &amp; Mist 5, Memories 5<br /> <br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Twilight Form, Materialize, Astral Sojourn<br /> <br /> <b>Suggested Ban &amp; Bane/Numina:</b> Same as those of the updated Angel version, plus &quot;Astral Road&quot; (Use the Astral as a sort of hyperspace between two points in mundane space. May be combined with Astral Sojourn to bring others with you, but time may pass differently on Earth. Clash Of Wills might also happen. I can't think of detailed mechanics, unfortunately).</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-07-2015, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T21:01:48-07:00","id":618422,"title":"","content":"I figured I'd do something here. It came to mind a bit earlier and I thought it'd be cool. For those not familiar, Illusion of Time/Illusion of Gaia is a Super Nintendo action adventure game similar in vein of Legend of Zelda. The plot consists of the main character, Will, travelling to the wonders of the ancient world to uncover their mysteries, discover the fate of his father after a fateful trip to the Tower of Babel and to discover the what the meaning of an Impending comet means for the world.<br /> <br /> <b>Will</b> (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Illusion_of_time\" target=\"_blank\">Illusion of Time - SNES</a>)<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Background: Will is a youth who can see the truth of the world, he alone can commune with Gaia, the living spirit of the world. Will engages on a journey to find the artefacts that would drive off Dark Gaia, an evil presence who rewrites the world every 800 years as it passes guiding the evolution of the world.<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Heroism<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Trust<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 4, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 2, Manipulation 1, Composure 2<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 1 (History), Investigation 3 (Ancient Ruins), Occult 3 (Ancient Ruins), Athletics 4 (Sliding), Brawl 1, Stealth 1, Survival 2, Weaponry 3(Flute), Animal Ken 2, Empathy 2, Expression 2 (Flute)<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Medium \u2022\u2022\u2022, Telekinesis \u2022\u2022, Psychometry \u2022\u2022\u2022, Interdisciplinary Specialty \u2022\u2022 (Ancient Ruins, Flute)<br /> <b>Gear:</b><br /> Flute: Melee Weapon - 0L, 2 Size, -1 Initiative, 1 Strength, Special: +1 when used for Expression. Will's Flute. Is a poor weapon but good at playing songs.<br /> Psycho Dash: Melee Weapon - 0L, Special: Uses Telekinesis + Strength to attack. Armour Piercing 1, Ignores Durability 1. Will's psychically enhanced body slam granted by Dark Gaia. Smashes through walls, obstacles and enemies.<br /> Psycho Slider: Melee Weapon - 2B, Special: Uses Telekinesis + Athletics to attack. Inflicts the Knockdown tilt if damage greater than target's stamina. Will's psychically enhanced slide attack granted by Dark Gaia. Knocks foes down and away.<br /> Psycho Spin: Melee Weapon - 1L, Special: Uses Telekinesis + Dexterity + Athletics to attack. Requires a successful Dexterity + Athletics roll next turn to not fall over. Can be used to leap long distances. Will's psychically powered tornado spin. The spin moves incredibly fast and is capable of launching Will long distances but needs time to recover.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Freedan</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Background: Freedan is the soul of an ancient Hero, one who suffered at the hands of the Comet the last time it came to Earth. Gaia can transform Will's body into Freedan's, gaining his skills and abilities but losing Will's own.<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 4, Dexterity 4, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 1, Manipulation 1, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Investigation: 1 Occult: 3 (Fire), Athletics 2, Brawl 3, Survival 2, Weaponry 4 (Sword, Shield), Intimidation 2, Animal Ken 2, Empathy 2, Persuasion 1<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Telekinesis \u2022\u2022, Psychokinesis \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 (Pyrokinesis), Style: Armed Defence \u2022\u2022\u2022, Defensive Combat \u2022 (Weaponry)<br /> <b>Gear:</b><br /> Sword (as Machete). Every knight needs a sword, right?<br /> Dark Friar (as Psychokinesis). Freedan can manifest his psychic abilities to send spheres of hurtling aura flame at his opponents.<br /> Aura Barrier: Melee Weapon - 2L, -4 Initiative, Size 4, Special: Concealed. Uses no hands. Cannot be used unless manifested with an Instant Resolve + Occult roll and lasts turns equal to successes.<br /> Earthshaker: Special Weapon - Roll Strength + Athletics. All targets in a 5 metre radius are knocked down and insensate for a turn. Requires jumping down at least some height to activate.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Shadow</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Background: Shadow is a second soul, the soul of an individual who was bathed completely in the light of the Comet, transforming xem into a being of pure aura. Xe are the only being capable of surviving into space and reaching the comet from the Tower of Babel. Gaia transforms Will into xyrs' form.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank:</b> 3<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 5, Finesse 8, Resistance 6<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Gaia \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 (Strengthen, Manipulate, Control, Create)<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Pathfinder, Blast, Telekinesis<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Corporeal - Shadow must manifest at all times. Xe can discorporate by spending willpower to clear xyrs' mind (Shadow's &quot;Aura&quot;), but only lasts for three turns/a minute.<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Dark Gaia - the true form of the Comet inflicts heinous damage to Shadow's aura-flesh.<br /> <br /> <b>Gear:</b> The Firebird (as Blast Numina)</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Phew, that was fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1462,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","user":"Xenesis","date":". 08-07-2015, 12:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T20:04:45-07:00","id":630587,"title":"","content":"Ok, so, I kept thinking about my previous write ups for the Slender Man. The True Fae version was the most accurate, but I figured I'd try to redo it, this time with the generic Hunter stats. It\u2019s difficult to accurately portray the extent of Slender Man\u2019s teleportation and remote perception powers. The Dread Powers are more like suggestions. However, it is often said that the Slender Man needs to inflict fear and madness before going in for the kill or taking the victim to a fate unknown. I decided to include guidelines for portraying this rising tension and dread of most Slender Man stories. I didn't give him a Virtue nor Vice, because I'm not sure if these specific traits can apply to him. I would greatly appreciate your two cents.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 3, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 6, Dexterity 3, Stamina 4<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 5, Manipulation 1, Composure 6<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics 1, Computer 1, Crafts 1, Investigation (Searching) 4, Medicine 1, Occult 3, Politics 0, Science 1<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics (Chasing) 3, Brawl (Claws &amp; Tentacles) 3, Drive 0, Firearms 0, Larceny 3, Stealth (Plain Sight) 6, Survival (Forests &amp; Woodlands) 4, Weaponry 0<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken 1, Empathy (Children) 1, Expression 1, Intimidation (Appearing Out Of Nowhere) 5, Persuasion 2, Streetwise 0, Subterfuge (Mimic Sounds) 4<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Interdisciplinary Specialty (Claws &amp; Tentacles, Mimic Sounds), Eidetic Memory, Patient, Tolerance For Biology, Direction Sense, Ambidextrous, Double Jointed, Demolisher 1, Choke Hold, Quick Healer, Hardy 3, Iron Stamina 3, Fleet Of Foot 3, Light Weapons 5 (Claws &amp; Tentacles), Retainer (Proxies), Iron Will, Striking Looks +2<br /> <br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10 + 7 Dots From Potency<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 3 + Athletics/Brawl/Weaponry<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 9<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 15<br /> <b>Health:</b> 11 (Size 7)<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 7<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Alter Memory 3, Black Out 5, Clamber 3, Dark Gate 5, Dead Flesh 5, Dement 3, Drain 5 (Sleep Variant), Dread Attack 2 (Claws &amp; Tentacles), Dream Seeing 3, Dream Shaping 3, Dream Walking 3, Flicker And Flash 4, Giant Size, Haunting 3, Hypnotism 5, Lord Of The Manor 5 (Temporary: Forests &amp; Woodlands), Lurker In Darkness 5, Mist Form, New Face 4, Revelation 3, Revivify 5, Sleep 3, Strange Form 3 (Tree-Like: +3 Dexterity, +3 Composure), Titan's Strength 5, Unholy Attribute (Stamina 3)<br /> <br /> When a character fails a Breaking Point roll for Integrity or equivalent stat due to the Slender Man or Proxies, add 1 die to a pool specific to that character. Suffering a Dramatic Failure on the Breaking Point roll adds 2 dice. This dice pool has a limit of 10 and cannot be decreased, barring the use of the Informed Condition. The ST can roll this dice pool for the Slender Man once per chapter, contesting it against the character\u2019s unmodified Resolve + Composure, with no Willpower expenditure allowed.<br /> <br /> If the character completes an extended action to investigate and research the Slender Man, a +3 bonus is applied to her future Resolve + Composure rolls for the purposes of contesting the Slender Man\u2019s dice pool. In the case of an Exceptional Success during this extended action, it may be traded for the Informed Condition if the action is completed. This Condition may be applied to a roll meant for resetting and locking the Slender Man\u2019s dice pool. The target number of successes for this extended action is 20. Teamwork is allowed, but those who help may have to roll for Breaking Points and be marked as well. Ties on this contested roll go for the Slender Man.<br /> <br /> As the characters delve further, Proxies both human and monstrous may be sent after them or take interest, possibly inducing more Breaking Point rolls. As the Slender Man approaches, the ST should give signs of his presence, such as audiovisual distortions in recording devices, small fragments of bodies or personal possessions, sudden sickness and strange carvings. Being found and captured doesn\u2019t always mean game over. Despite this, the ST is encouraged to at least give the Amnesia Condition to the character in question. Additional changes are done at the ST\u2019s discretion.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-17-2015, 11:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T16:21:15-07:00","id":633927,"title":"","content":"A little Metal Gear<br /> <br /> <b>Solid Snake</b><br /> <b>Virtue: </b>Hopeful \u2013 Snake believes he fights to make the world a better place, and one can find friendship and even love in the worst of conflicts.<br /> <b>Vice: </b>Repressed \u2013 Snake has spent his life on the battlefield and has learned to bury his emotions; causing him to appear callous and uncaring.<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 4, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 4, Dexterity 4, Stamina 5<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 4<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 4(Tactics), Animal Ken 2 (Dogs), Athletics 4(Climbing), Brawl 5(Superior Opponents), Computers 1, Crafts 3 (Demolitions, Sabotage), Drive 4 (Helicopter, Off-Road Vehicles, Tank), Firearms 4 (Pistol, Sniper), Intimidation 3(Interrogation), Investigation 3, Larceny 4, Medicine 2, Persuasion 2 (Seduction),Politics 3 (Private Military), Science 1, Socialize 1 (Soldiers), Stealth 5 (Ambush, Infiltration), Streetwise 3 (Black Markets), Subterfuge 3 (Disguise), Survival 5(Arctic, Jungle), Weaponry 3 (Knives)<br /> <b>Skill Tricks: </b>Athletics (Size Up), Firearms(Gun Catalog, Trick Shot) , Stealth (Backstab, Find Cover)<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Allies 4(Otacon), Allies 4 (Colonel Roy Campbell), Anonymity 4, Area of Expertise (Infiltration, Private Military, Superior Opponents), Choke Hold, Close Quarters Combat 5, Common Sense, Danger Sense, Defensive Combat (Brawl), Demolisher 2, Direction Sense, Fast Reflexes 3, Hardy 2, Interdisciplinary Specialty (Infiltration, Private Military, Tactics), Iron Skin 4, Iron Stamina 2, Iron Will, Language (English (native), Algonquin, Arabic, French, Japanese, Spanish), Patient, Professional Training 5 (Soldier; Firearms, Stealth, Survival), Quick Draw (Pistols), Small Unit Tactics, Strong Back, Striking Looks 1, Style: Firefight 3, Style: Light Weapons 2, Style: Marksmanship 4, Style: Martial Arts 4, Style: Street Fighting 5, Style: Unarmed Defense 4,Tolerance for Biology, Trained Observer 3<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 6<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 9<br /> <b>Conviction:</b> 6 [Mirrors, pg.32-33]<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 11<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 9<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 2/3 [sneaking suit]; 2 vs. Bashing<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 13<br /> <b>Health:</b> 10<br /> <b>Condition: </b>Addiction (Cigarettes), Post-Traumatic Stress<br /> <br /> <b>Equipment: </b>When entering a mission, snake caries little beyond a socom pistol, his stealth suit, and a pack of cigarettes.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Notes</i></b><br /> <br /> The above represent Solid Snake during Metal Gear: Solid. Snake is a former Green Beret who has spent the majority of his adult life as a soldier, spy, and mercenary. Physically, he is near-peak human capability, with his reflexes and endurance augmented by nano-machines in his blood stream. He also has a documented IQ of 180 (by comparison, Stephen Hawking has an IQ of 160).<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:12px\">As noted down-thread, Snake is attributed a exceptional degree of intelligence, but does not frequently exercise it to its fullest potential. Also adjusted his presence to 3, as Snake was commonly depicted as commanding, but more of a loner than a leader.<br /> I increased Conviction to 6, which seems about the right level for a Protagonist that can take on attack helicopters and win. </span></i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 08-22-2015, 01:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T07:43:17-07:00","id":634587,"title":"","content":"I wonder if those Mental and Social attributes are a bit too high for Snake. Throughout the series he's basically spoon-fed all his information and still manages to act like he hasn't heard of anything that wasn't inside an army field guide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T08:25:48-07:00","id":634609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=634587#post634587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if those Mental and Social attributes are a bit too high for Snake. Throughout the series he's basically spoon-fed all his information and still manages to act like he hasn't heard of anything that wasn't inside an army field guide.</div> </div> </div> </div> I agree. I'd make his Intelligence 4, not 5. Perhaps his Presence could be 3. I'd make his Manipulation 2 and his Persuasion 3, not the other way around. His Conviction could be 5, maybe even 6. He could have the Patient Merit to help with extended actions like shadowing and interrogation.<br /> <br /> The write up is still excellent, though!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-21-2015, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T08:34:26-07:00","id":634633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=634609#post634609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The write up is still excellent, though!</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh agreed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T15:24:59-07:00","id":635096,"title":"","content":"My body is ready for some Twin Peaks in 2017.<br /> <br /> <b>Name: </b>Special Agent Dale Cooper<br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Honest<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Eccentric<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 4, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 3, Stamina 4<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 2, Composure 4<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics (Law) 3, Craft 1, Investigation (Quirky methods) 4, Occult (Tibet) 1<br /> <b>Physical Skills: </b>Athletics 3, Brawl 1, Drive 2, Firearms (\u201cTwo through each nostril\u201d) 4, Stealth 2<br /> <b>Social Skills: </b>Empathy (Relationships) 4, Expression 1, Intimidation 2, Socialize 3, Streetwise 2<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Eye of the Strange 2, Fast Reflexes 2, Meditative Mind 2, Professional Training (Detective: Empathy, Investigation, Firearms) 3, Tolerance for Biology 1, Trained Observer 3, Hardy 3, Iron Stamina 3, Allies (FBI) 2, Allies (Bookhouse Club) 4, Contacts (FBI, Twin Peaks Police) 2, Iron Will 2, Resources 2, Small Unit Tactics 2, Status (FBI) 3, Striking Looks 1, Sympathetic 2, True Friend (Harry Truman) 3<br /> <b>Styles: </b>Firefight 3, Police Tactics 3<br /> <b>Supernatural Merits: </b>Dream 3<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity: </b>8<br /> <br /> <b>Notes: </b>Maaaybe I made him much powerful than he is. But he is the cream of the top, one of the best agents.<br /> <br /> Aaand, mega spoiler. For a show made 25 years ago, yes.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <b>Name:</b> BOB<br /> <b>Rank:</b> 2<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Sadistic<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 4, Finesse 3, Resistance 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Brawl 3, Weaponry 3 (replace these skills with the subject\u2019s if higher)<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Fear 2<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Dream Seeing 4, Dream Shaping 4, Eye Spy (The Owls Are Not What They Seem), Home Ground (Black Lodge)<br /> <b>Manifestations:</b> Twilight Form, Image, Possess, Claim<br /> <br /> <b>Notes: </b>BOB is a mix-and-match of different critters. He works as a spirit, mostly, but he is not, so I added some dream powers from Mortal Remains. I picture the Black Lodge as one of the Lower Depths: its inhabitants lack fear, and they look for it in the material world. Classic Lower Depths, if not for the fact that it intersect with the Astral.<br /> He is not that strong in the Fallen World, but Twin Peaks is a human game/show. Also, BOB doesn't have bans nor banes, and he is though as hell on his turf. Don't seek the Black Lodge.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Will the creatures from the Lower Depths use the spirit rules in 2e? Well, it works for now, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Italian nuisance. English is my second language, so be patient!<br /> <br /> <b>My homebrew:</b><br /> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/270766-domain-light-from-a-dead-star-rome\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">[VtR 2e] Light From a Dead Star: Rome</span></a></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1117941-hunting-ground-the-past-is-another-country-rome\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><b>[WtF 2e] The Past Is Another Country: Rome</b></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3765-snesferatu","name":"SNESferatu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3765_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T21:52:23-07:00","id":635437,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Mask\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Loki's Mask:</b></span></a><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Mask is a Relic containing a Rank 5 mischief spirit that is one of the Royal Avatars of a Rank 6+ entity. Whoever wears the Mask is treated as one of the Claimed.<br /> <br /> <b>Attribute Bonuses:</b> +5 Strength, +3 Presence, +2 Intelligence, +3 Dexterity, +7 Manipulation, +5 Wits, +5 Stamina, +2 Composure, +3 Resolve. These increase derived traits and may bring the Attributes beyond 10 dots.<br /> <br /> <b>Maximum Essence/Per Turn:</b> 50/15<br /> <br /> <b>Influences:</b> Mischief 5 (May Be Used To Create Equipment, Weapons, Firearms And Temporary Skill Dots)<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Armored Hide 3, Leap, Monstrous Resilience, Numen (Drain, Essence Thief, Hallucination, Mortal Mask, Speed), Reality Stutter, Regenerate 5, Swift, Unbreakable<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Indomitable (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration\"><b>Advanced</b></a>), Vice-Ridden (Mischievous), Ambidextrous, Crack Driver 3, Demolisher 3, Double Jointed (Advanced), Fleet Of Foot 3, Iron Stamina 3, Parkour 4, Sleight Of Hand, Stunt Driver 3, Barfly, Closed Book 4, Fast-Talking 5, Iron Will, Pusher, Striking Looks 2 (Cartoonish), Table Turner, Cheap Shot, Heavy Weapons 5, Martial Arts 4<br /> <br /> <i>Liar's Tongue</i> - Same as the one of the Unchained (Demon: The Descent, Pages 182-183)<br /> <br /> <i>Fiendish Deceit</i> - Gain an Interdisciplinary Specialty with Area Of Expertise for Mischief. Anytime this Specialty might apply to a roll, you may spend 1 Essence to give it 8 Again. You suffer no untrained penalties for Skills you do not have, as long as you use them for mischief.<br /> <br /> <i>Tazmanian Whirlwind</i> - Spend 1 Essence and roll Stamina + Athletics. You inflict the Heavy Winds Environmental Tilt around yourself with an intensity equal to Successes for one turn, capping at intensity 5. The Essence cost may be paid again on subsequent turns to keep this power activate.<br /> <br /> <i>Incite Bedlam</i> - Same as the one of the Lost, spending Essence instead of Glamour and using Rank instead of Wyrd.<br /> <br /> <b>Ban:</b> Can only be used at night.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-30-2016, 06:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T23:05:54-07:00","id":635456,"title":"","content":"more Metal Gear<br /> ---------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Psycho Mantis</b><br /> <b>Virtue: </b>Hope; Despite the things that he had seen and done, Psycho Mantis retained a small shred of hopefulness about humanity.<br /> <b>Vice: </b>Nihilism; Psycho Mantis was disgusted by humanity, and wanted to kill as many people as he could. <br /> <b>Undertaking: </b>Genius [Empathy, Investigation]<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 5, Wits 4, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 4, Manipulation 5, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 4(Psychology), Athletics 2 (Throwing), Empathy 4(Insecurities), Brawl 1, Firearms 2, Investigation 4(Profiling), Intimidation 4 (Interrogation), Larceny 2, Medicine 2, Occult 4 (Psychics), Persuasion 3(Conditioning), Politics 2, Science 2, Streetwise 2 (Serial Killers), Subterfuge 4, Survival 2<br /> <b>Skill Tricks: </b>Empathy (Emotional Attack), Investigation (Riddle Master), Occult (Symbolic Intent), Subterfuge (Doubt)<br /> <b>Talent: </b>Profiling \u2013 (Intelligence + empathy); if successful, Psycho Mantis wins all ties in contested rolls against the target(s), and always wins initiative against him/them.<br /> <b>Frailty: </b>Intolerance for Chaos - If Psycho Mantis fails an Intelligence or Undertaking Skill roll; he loses two points of Willpower<b>.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Allies 4 (FOXHOUND), Area of Expertise (Psychics, Psychology, Profiling, Serial Killers), Danger Sense, Interdisciplinary Specialty (Psychology), Fast Reflexes1, Language (English, Russian, and others), Meditative Mind 2, Mental Scarring*, Power Object (Gas Mask)*, Professional Training 4 (Investigator; Empathy, Investigation, Intimidation), Status 3 (FOXHOUND), Status 2 (FBI, KGB), Striking Looks 1 (Disfigured), Trained Observer 1<br /> <b>Supernatural Merits: </b>Aura Reading, Mind Control 4*, Mind of a Madman, Psychic Onslaught*, Psychic Poltergeist,*, Tactical Telepathy 2*, Telekinesis 5, Telekinetic Evasion*, Telepathy 5<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 4<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 8<br /> <b>Conviction:</b> 4 [Mirrors, pg.32-33]<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 7<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 5<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 1/0 [body suit]<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 10<br /> <b>Health:</b> 7<br /> <b>Condition: </b>Madness<br /> <br /> <b>Equipment: </b>Psycho Mantis wears a gas mask, for both practical and psychological reasons. He also wears a lightly armored body suit or trench-coat.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Notes</i></b><br /> Merits noted with asterisk (*) are from the Hurt Locker playtest document.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T01:13:05-07:00","id":635502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=635437#post635437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Mask\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Loki's Mask:</b></span></a></div> </div> </div> </div>You seriously read my mind.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T20:52:32-07:00","id":637668,"title":"","content":"You know how the relationship between power and responsibility is one of the main themes in Mage? And how Spider-Man\u2019s adopted motto is \u201cWith Great Power, Comes Great Responsibility\u201d? That encouraged me to write stats for him as a Mage, as per the crunch and fluff of 2ed. His Path works the best as <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxveHUKxwBU9WFJTQlZfcDA1aE0/edit?pli=1\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Acanthus</b></a>. His Order is <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxveHUKxwBU9V1R3RmZuWm5xbE0/edit?pli=1\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Free Council</b></a> because he is a hero and admirer of the Sleepers, not an unseen and dusty law enforcer. He is on good terms with the Guardians Of The Veil and Adamantine Arrow, however. Spidey may turn out to be more fitting as a Deviant, at least in crunch.<br /> <br /> His Persona Merit (combination of magical style, Shadow Name and personal mysteries that grants Supernal Sympathy) is likely to be reasonably powerful. The Web-Slingers are an Imbued/Enhanced Item. His spider-sense, wall-crawling, enhanced physical capabilities in general, superlative reflexes and impressive luck are a combination of mundane Merits, Life, Mind, Forces, Fate and Time. The costume itself could also be Enhanced for greater flexibility and protection, maybe also Imbued with a Mind Veiling spell to improve the disguise. Spidey also uses Space to conceal his sympathetic connections to his loved ones, and for Scrying both friend and foe. Even without spells, his stats are still very formidable.<br /> <br /> I am not sure how to translate his standard back-story into an Awakening, be it a Mystery Play or Astral Journey. His Nimbus might include webs as a symbol of personal connections, binding promises and karma. Spiders themselves might symbolize Fate: both of them can weave and cut webs in their own way, be it to connect, restrain, protect or harm. The members of Spidey\u2019s Rogue Gallery work well as Deviants, Slashers and the occasional unscrupulous Mage. The symbiotes, though? They definitely work as scarily intimate Abyssals. Madame Web is a Mastigos. Aunt May, Mary Jane and similar characters could be Sleepwalkers, depending on how much they know about Peter.<br /> <br /> Feedback is appreciated! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Virtue:</b> Responsible/Inventive<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Short-Tempered<br /> <b>Concept:</b> Genius Superhero<br /> <br /> <b>Path:</b> Acanthus<br /> <b>Order:</b> Free Council<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 5, Wits 6, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 5, Dexterity 6, Stamina 5<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 2, Manipulation 2, Composure 4<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics (Journalism) 3, Crafts (Engineering) 4, Computer 3, Medicine 2, Occult 2, Politics 1, Investigation (Scoops) 3, Science (Biology) 4<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics (Climbing, Gymnastics) 6, Brawl 4, Drive 1, Firearms (Web-Slingers) 2, Larceny 2, Stealth (Ambush) 3, Survival 2, Weaponry (Improvised) 4<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken 1, Empathy 3, Expression (Humor) 3, Intimidation (Bluff) 3, Persuasion (Diplomacy) 3, Socialize (Office) 2, Streetwise (New York City) 3, Subterfuge (Excuses) 3<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Virtuous, Ambidextrous, Encyclopedic Knowledge (Crafts, Science, Expression), Area Of Expertise (Scoops, Engineering), Interdisciplinary Specialty (Humor, Gymnastics, Engineering), Patient, Common Sense, Indomitable, Professional Training 3 (Journalist: Empathy, Investigation, Persuasion), Trained Observer 3, Danger Sense, Direction Sense, Tolerance For Biology, Demolisher 3, Double Jointed, Disarm*, Iron Stamina 3, Fleet Of Foot 3, Fast Reflexes 3, Hardy 3, Parkour 5, Improvised Weapons 3, Martial Arts 3, Firefight 3 (Web-Slingers), Unarmed Defense 5, Quick Healer, Allies 3/Status 1 (Daily Bugle), Allies 3/Status 2 (Free Council), Contacts 6 (Journalists, Researchers, Law Enforcers, Free Council, Guardians Of The Veil, Adamantine Arrow), Resources 2, Striking Looks +1, Alternate Identity 1 (Spider-Man), Fame 2 (Spider-Man), Fixer, Iron Will, Inspiring, Pusher, Sympathetic, True Friend (Mary Jane, Aunt May), Web-Slinger Style 5**<br /> <br /> *Spidey normally disarms opponents with his webs, or fists hardened with Life spells. He can do it with Weaponry too.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>**<i>Web-Slinger Style</i></b></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Eight Eyes (\u2022):</b> Web-Slinging is practically the same as walking for Spidey. Most difficulties that people experience when trying to use the web-slingers never apply to him. Ignore environmental penalties to Perception rolls and Range penalties equal to your dots in Web-Slinger for the purposes of the namesake. Other Perception rolls and Ranges are not affected.<br /> <br /> <b>Multi-Purpose (\u2022\u2022):</b> Spidey knows very well that the web-slingers aren\u2019t just for swinging around and tying people up. They\u2019re also useful for keeping ramshackle repairs together, making traps, quick patch-ups for wounds and creative expression. He is considered to have an Interdisciplinary Specialty of Web-Slinging with Area Of Expertise built-in, even if the Skill in question is not Mental, lower than 3, or lowered from 3 through whatever means.<br /> <br /> <b>Pin-Point (\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> Spidey can calculate angles and distance with lightning speed and amazing precision, especially for disarming and stunning. Every 2 dice he subtracts from his Dexterity + Firearms pool becomes a +1B for attacks with webs. An Exceptional Success on this roll also inflicts a fitting Tilt, usually Arm Wrack, Leg Wrack, Knocked Down or Immobilized. Inflicting the Blinded Tilt doesn\u2019t stand to gain with a reduced dice pool, as it only requires Spidey to roll Dexterity + Firearms \u2013 3 for targeting the opponent\u2019s head.<br /> <br /> <b>Arachnid Focus (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> If he completely concentrates on a target, Spidey is virtually guaranteed to hit as intended. Instead of gaining +2 or more when making an All-Out Attack with the web-slingers, he may receive the Rote Quality. He may use this maneuver at the same time as the previous one, but doing so requires 1 willpower point.<br /> <br /> <b>Ultimate Web-Spinning (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> It is often when a split second can mean the difference between life and death that Spidey makes the most of his web fluid/Mana. He spends 1 willpower point, and all Mana costs for Reach and mitigation of Paradox are halved, round down. This maneuver may be combined with Arachnid Focus OR Pin-Point. The situation does need to be so drastic for him to use this maneuver.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Health:</b> 10<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 9<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 6 + Athletics/Brawl/Weaponry<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 12<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 20<br /> <b>Gnosis:</b> 6<br /> <b>Wisdom:</b> 8<br /> <b>Arcana:</b> Life 3, Matter 3, Forces 2, Fate 2, Time 2, Space 2, Mind 2</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-24-2015, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T21:02:55-07:00","id":637673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=637668#post637668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spidey may turn out to be more fitting as a Deviant, at least in crunch.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm reminded of an old conversation on the Exalted forum that contrasted the construction paradigms for Solar and Infernal Exalted characters using Spider-Man as an example: Peter Parker is a teen genius, but he's Spider-Man because <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/36866-infernals-why-so-weak?p=36980#post36980\">he got spider-themed superpowers instead of teen-genius superpowers</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T01:30:40-07:00","id":637768,"title":"","content":"I would give Spidey more Intelligence and Strength. Without effort, he is both among the great geniuses and strong hitters of the Marvel-verse. It isn't always apparent because is overshadowed by characters truly focused on such areas, but them we're talking about Reed Richards and Tony Stark, or Thor and The Hulk. The social Attributes, though, I would concentrate more on Composure and drop the rest to average levels. The fact that he have quite an intense sexual life have little to be with his own social abilities, he usually can't talk himself out of much, after all. Free Council really fits in.<br /> <br /> On the Skills, Crafts could use a technological specialty instead of webs. Chemistry or engineering, maybe. I wouldn't give him more than a dot in Drive, none at all if you think Drive 0 can still drive in common circumstances. I also want to forget he ever had a Spider-Mobile. But I would also raise Firearms, because I do seem his stunts with webs as Firearms rolls. Maybe Brawl and Weaponry could be partially swapped. Social skills could again be a little lower, though I do think he should have a lot more of Streetwise. He isn't the Punisher or Daredevil, but again, they are another level. He is still your Neighborhood Friend, and he's it in New York.<br /> <br /> Quick-Draw for the Web-Slingers is the only other thing for now that I found a little odd. Hi isn't a quick drawer with them, he just always have them at hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T04:41:28-07:00","id":637883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=637768#post637768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would give Spidey more Intelligence and Strength. Without effort, he is both among the great geniuses and strong hitters of the Marvel-verse. It isn't always apparent because is overshadowed by characters truly focused on such areas, but them we're talking about Reed Richards and Tony Stark, or Thor and The Hulk. The social Attributes, though, I would concentrate more on Composure and drop the rest to average levels. The fact that he have quite an intense sexual life have little to be with his own social abilities, he usually can't talk himself out of much, after all. Free Council really fits in.<br /> <br /> On the Skills, Crafts could use a technological specialty instead of webs. Chemistry or engineering, maybe. I wouldn't give him more than a dot in Drive, none at all if you think Drive 0 can still drive in common circumstances. I also want to forget he ever had a Spider-Mobile. But I would also raise Firearms, because I do seem his stunts with webs as Firearms rolls. Maybe Brawl and Weaponry could be partially swapped. Social skills could again be a little lower, though I do think he should have a lot more of Streetwise. He isn't the Punisher or Daredevil, but again, they are another level. He is still your Neighborhood Friend, and he's it in New York.<br /> <br /> Quick-Draw for the Web-Slingers is the only other thing for now that I found a little odd. Hi isn't a quick drawer with them, he just always have them at hand.</div> </div> </div> </div> All of that makes sense. I just thought of his web-slinging as being Dexterity + Athletics. That's mostly for crunch: that way, he can have large dice pools for web-slinging without having an unfitting Firearms rating. Besides, I'm pretty sure that Firearms is for actual guns that actually kill, or at least seriously hurt. His Matter Arcanum can be raised to 4, depending on how sophisticated and versatile you want the webs to be. His Wisdom drops to 7 in the comics sometimes, depending on how he chooses to deal with his near-omnipresent problems. There have been moments when his Wisdom reached 9, usually when he had to do unsavory business, but said to himself: &quot;never again&quot;. Also, being stalked by a fanboy Deadpool does wonders for temporarily increasing your responsibility, it seems.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the help! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> By the way, if you are playing Spider-Man, Harry Potter or another mega famous character, but adapted into NWOD terms, the franchise centered around that character is replaced with something that has very similar themes, but different visuals and plot details. For example, if you play a Hunter version of Batman, his comics/movies/video games and so on are replaced with a franchise that is also about a traumatized detective that masters his own fears and uses unique resources to combat evil-doers, all the while doing his best to avoid snapping. This Substitute Batman is not called as such, and thus he has no bat-themed gadgets. History as we know it remains much the same, monsters notwithstanding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-24-2015, 08:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T05:14:29-07:00","id":637892,"title":"","content":"I'm personally of the opinion that every roll to hit something at a distance should be done with Firearms.<br /> <br /> Athletics for such doesn't make any real sense for me, the official rule non-withstanding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T05:43:21-07:00","id":637940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=637892#post637892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm personally of the opinion that every roll to hit something at a distance should be done with Firearms.<br /> <br /> Athletics for such doesn't make any real sense for me, the official rule non-withstanding.</div> </div> </div> </div> If it sounds more fitting to you, go ahead. When we factor in his permanent Dexterity dots, spells, willpower expenditure, aiming and All-Out Attacks, a Firearms Skill at 1 or 2 isn't an obstacle for web-slinging. In fact, I'll see if I can make a Web-Slinger Style Merit for him.<br /> <br /> EDIT: There we go, a complete Style for Spidey. I just hope that the fifth maneuver doesn't clash with the second edition's Reach system for spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-24-2015, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T09:31:10-07:00","id":638107,"title":"","content":"Having binged on Linkara recently, I was wondering how one would make Crazy Steve, the &quot;Batman&quot; of Frank Miller that seems to be everything the real Bruce fears becoming.<br /> <br /> Then I realized I'm an idiot, and that's precisely how one should make him. <br /> <br /> &quot;Batman&quot;, the Immaturity of Bruce Wayne<br /> <br /> Rank: 3<br /> <br /> Power 6, Finesse 2, Resistance 5<br /> <br /> Influence: Wrath 3, Punishment 1.<br /> <br /> Numina: Harrow, Awe, Choke, Compulsion, Dement<br /> <br /> Manifestations: Mortal Mask*, Twilight Form<br /> <br /> * Requires a discarded Batman costume not actually ever worn by Bruce Wayne<br /> <br /> Ban: As a goetic demon conjured from Batman's self-loathing over the understanding that much of his heroics are the result of his inability to accept his parents' death, this Batman is emotionally wrecked by reminders of its true nature; it must flee from any &quot;orphan&quot; (which could be metaphorical, an adult student abandoned or betrayed works) that expresses disgust for its way of living up to the elder Waynes' legacy.<br /> <br /> Ban: The blood or flesh (which can still be attached to the actual person) of any person Bruce Wayne considers a friend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 08-24-2015, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T18:16:41-07:00","id":638581,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if Web-Slinger Style is overpowered. I just arrived from my first day at the new job and too tired to think too straight. But I'm almost sure that the last level is too strong, and the others could use some revising.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T02:09:13-07:00","id":641290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=543583#post543583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All the Soul Reaper characters from the anime Bleach are Sin-Eaters, with a special Sword Manifestation. (If someone wants to stat that up, let me know.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> i was always thinking of them as ghosts with their daemon trapped in a fetish sword. do ghosts have daemons???","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T02:42:34-07:00","id":641300,"title":"","content":"maybe someone has a link to crossover discussions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T07:46:52-07:00","id":642952,"title":"","content":"I've been writing up NPCs for a Demon game, and I created <a href=\"http://zeldawiki.org/Fi\" target=\"_blank\">Fi</a> from The Legend of Zelda: Skyward Sword as an angel:<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 2<br /> <b>Virtue</b> Helpful, <b>Vice</b> Thorough<br /> <b>Power </b>3, <b>Finesse</b> 6, <b>Resistance </b>5<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 10, <b>Willpower </b>10<br /> <b>Initiative</b> +11, <b>Speed </b>14<br /> <b>Defense</b> 3 (4 with Sword)<br /> <b>Size</b> 5<br /> <br /> <b>Influence</b> Courage 2<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Must obey the commands of the wielder of the Sword<br /> <b>Bane:</b> A cowardly human. Conditions, Vices, or even Virtues should be considered for what constitutes as &quot;cowardly&quot;.<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Twilight Form, Materialize, Fetter<br /> <b>Numina</b>: Implant Mission, Speed, Seek, Pathfinder, Sign, Innocuous, Strike Blind<br /> <b>Special</b> Can determine the Virtue and Resolve of whoever wields the Sword<br /> <b>Weapons</b><br /> &quot;Goddess&quot; Sword, 9d, 2L, -0, +1 Defense<br /> <br /> <b>Fi</b> is bound to a blade - really an artifact of the God-Machine - and silently appraises those who lay hands upon the sword to determine if they are &quot;worthy&quot;. Usually she picks those with courageous Virtues or great Resolve. If they are worthy, she reveals herself to them and alerts them to their &quot;Great Destiny&quot;, usually an Occult Matrix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T03:37:18-07:00","id":670717,"title":"","content":"Wyrdhamster made a lovely little point <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/670272-awakening-second-edition-awakened-inspirations?p=670320#post670320\">here</a> that Lara Croft was a Sleepwalker on the cusp of Awakening (complete with an Obsession).<br /> <br /> I think that if you wanted to bring them into NWoD, Kristoff from Frozen could be a Fae-Touched from Changeling 2nd with Sven as his Broadback Beast brother. Makes it really easy that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T08:02:07-07:00","id":670955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=637668#post637668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know how the relationship between power and responsibility is one of the main themes in Mage? And how Spider-Man\u2019s adopted motto is \u201cWith Great Power, Comes Great Responsibility\u201d? That encouraged me to write stats for him as a Mage, as per the crunch and fluff of 2ed. His Path works the best as <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxveHUKxwBU9WFJTQlZfcDA1aE0/edit?pli=1\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Acanthus</b></a>. His Order is <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxveHUKxwBU9V1R3RmZuWm5xbE0/edit?pli=1\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Free Council</b></a> because he is a hero and admirer of the Sleepers, not an unseen and dusty law enforcer. He is on good terms with the Guardians Of The Veil and Adamantine Arrow, however. Spidey may turn out to be more fitting as a Deviant, at least in crunch.<br /> <br /> His Persona Merit (combination of magical style, Shadow Name and personal mysteries that grants Supernal Sympathy) is likely to be reasonably powerful. The Web-Slingers are an Imbued/Enhanced Item. His spider-sense, wall-crawling, enhanced physical capabilities in general, superlative reflexes and impressive luck are a combination of mundane Merits, Life, Mind, Forces, Fate and Time. The costume itself could also be Enhanced for greater flexibility and protection, maybe also Imbued with a Mind Veiling spell to improve the disguise. Spidey also uses Space to conceal his sympathetic connections to his loved ones, and for Scrying both friend and foe. Even without spells, his stats are still very formidable.<br /> <br /> I am not sure how to translate his standard back-story into an Awakening, be it a Mystery Play or Astral Journey. His Nimbus might include webs as a symbol of personal connections, binding promises and karma. Spiders themselves might symbolize Fate: both of them can weave and cut webs in their own way, be it to connect, restrain, protect or harm. The members of Spidey\u2019s Rogue Gallery work well as Deviants, Slashers and the occasional unscrupulous Mage. The symbiotes, though? They definitely work as scarily intimate Abyssals. Madame Web is a Mastigos. Aunt May, Mary Jane and similar characters could be Sleepwalkers, depending on how much they know about Peter.<br /> <br /> Feedback is appreciated! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Virtue:</b> Responsible/Inventive<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Short-Tempered<br /> <b>Concept:</b> Genius Superhero<br /> <br /> <b>Path:</b> Acanthus<br /> <b>Order:</b> Free Council<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 5, Wits 6, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 5, Dexterity 6, Stamina 5<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 2, Manipulation 2, Composure 4<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics (Journalism) 3, Crafts (Engineering) 4, Computer 3, Medicine 2, Occult 2, Politics 1, Investigation (Scoops) 3, Science (Biology) 4<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics (Climbing, Gymnastics) 6, Brawl 4, Drive 1, Firearms (Web-Slingers) 2, Larceny 2, Stealth (Ambush) 3, Survival 2, Weaponry (Improvised) 4<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken 1, Empathy 3, Expression (Humor) 3, Intimidation (Bluff) 3, Persuasion (Diplomacy) 3, Socialize (Office) 2, Streetwise (New York City) 3, Subterfuge (Excuses) 3<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Virtuous, Ambidextrous, Encyclopedic Knowledge (Crafts, Science, Expression), Area Of Expertise (Scoops, Engineering), Interdisciplinary Specialty (Humor, Gymnastics, Engineering), Patient, Common Sense, Indomitable, Professional Training 3 (Journalist: Empathy, Investigation, Persuasion), Trained Observer 3, Danger Sense, Direction Sense, Tolerance For Biology, Demolisher 3, Double Jointed, Disarm*, Iron Stamina 3, Fleet Of Foot 3, Fast Reflexes 3, Hardy 3, Parkour 5, Improvised Weapons 3, Martial Arts 3, Firefight 3 (Web-Slingers), Unarmed Defense 5, Quick Healer, Allies 3/Status 1 (Daily Bugle), Allies 3/Status 2 (Free Council), Contacts 6 (Journalists, Researchers, Law Enforcers, Free Council, Guardians Of The Veil, Adamantine Arrow), Resources 2, Striking Looks +1, Alternate Identity 1 (Spider-Man), Fame 2 (Spider-Man), Fixer, Iron Will, Inspiring, Pusher, Sympathetic, True Friend (Mary Jane, Aunt May), Web-Slinger Style 5**<br /> <br /> *Spidey normally disarms opponents with his webs, or fists hardened with Life spells. He can do it with Weaponry too.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>**<i>Web-Slinger Style</i></b></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Eight Eyes (\u2022):</b> Web-Slinging is practically the same as walking for Spidey. Most difficulties that people experience when trying to use the web-slingers never apply to him. Ignore environmental penalties to Perception rolls and Range penalties equal to your dots in Web-Slinger for the purposes of the namesake. Other Perception rolls and Ranges are not affected.<br /> <br /> <b>Multi-Purpose (\u2022\u2022):</b> Spidey knows very well that the web-slingers aren\u2019t just for swinging around and tying people up. They\u2019re also useful for keeping ramshackle repairs together, making traps, quick patch-ups for wounds and creative expression. He is considered to have an Interdisciplinary Specialty of Web-Slinging with Area Of Expertise built-in, even if the Skill in question is not Mental, lower than 3, or lowered from 3 through whatever means.<br /> <br /> <b>Pin-Point (\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> Spidey can calculate angles and distance with lightning speed and amazing precision, especially for disarming and stunning. Every 2 dice he subtracts from his Dexterity + Firearms pool becomes a +1B for attacks with webs. An Exceptional Success on this roll also inflicts a fitting Tilt, usually Arm Wrack, Leg Wrack, Knocked Down or Immobilized. Inflicting the Blinded Tilt doesn\u2019t stand to gain with a reduced dice pool, as it only requires Spidey to roll Dexterity + Firearms \u2013 3 for targeting the opponent\u2019s head.<br /> <br /> <b>Arachnid Focus (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> If he completely concentrates on a target, Spidey is virtually guaranteed to hit as intended. Instead of gaining +2 or more when making an All-Out Attack with the web-slingers, he may receive the Rote Quality. He may use this maneuver at the same time as the previous one, but doing so requires 1 willpower point.<br /> <br /> <b>Ultimate Web-Spinning (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> It is often when a split second can mean the difference between life and death that Spidey makes the most of his web fluid/Mana. He spends 1 willpower point, and all Mana costs for Reach and mitigation of Paradox are halved, round down. This maneuver may be combined with Arachnid Focus OR Pin-Point. The situation does need to be so drastic for him to use this maneuver.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Health:</b> 10<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 9<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 6 + Athletics/Brawl/Weaponry<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 12<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 20<br /> <b>Gnosis:</b> 6<br /> <b>Wisdom:</b> 8<br /> <b>Arcana:</b> Life 3, Matter 3, Forces 2, Fate 2, Time 2, Space 2, Mind 2</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I actually once came up with a concept for Spider-Man as a changeling: dual-kith Skitterskulk/Steepscrambler. The &quot;thief&quot; who he ignored in the course of his durance and later shot his Uncle Ben was actually his own imperfect fetch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T00:01:30-07:00","id":671696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowbody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=670955#post670955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually once came up with a concept for Spider-Man as a changeling: dual-kith Skitterskulk/Steepscrambler. The &quot;thief&quot; who he ignored in the course of his durance and later shot his Uncle Ben was actually his own imperfect fetch.</div> </div> </div> </div> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=166128#post166128\"><b>Yeah, I saw that post, it was pretty good!</b></a> I think Peter works better as a Fairest, if we go by the 2ED Seemings. He doesn't actually have an overtly spider-like Mien: it his Hedgespun costume, Token web-shooters and Contracts that form the Spider-Man persona. What his kiths in 2ED would be is up for debate, but Skitterskulk + Maker sounds good. Whatever his Durance was, he escaped by being responsible and serving as an example to someone. That method of escape (and Uncle Ben's death) stuck with him enough to not only make him a Fairest, but a superhero.<br /> <br /> Besides, it's been made clear that seeing Supernal magic is invariably an Integrity Breaking Point for Sleepers, not to mention Paradox. An Awakened Spidey wouldn't work.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T19:32:16-07:00","id":672781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=671696#post671696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=166128#post166128\"><b>Yeah, I saw that post, it was pretty good!</b></a> I think Peter works better as a Fairest, if we go by the 2ED Seemings. He doesn't actually have an overtly spider-like Mien: it his Hedgespun costume, Token web-shooters and Contracts that form the Spider-Man persona. What his kiths in 2ED would be is up for debate, but Skitterskulk + Maker sounds good. Whatever his Durance was, he escaped by being responsible and serving as an example to someone. That method of escape (and Uncle Ben's death) stuck with him enough to not only make him a Fairest, but a superhero.<br /> <br /> Besides, it's been made clear that seeing Supernal magic is invariably an Integrity Breaking Point for Sleepers, not to mention Paradox. An Awakened Spidey wouldn't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad you liked. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Yeah, Fairest seeming does work for 2E. Say that he spent his durance as a spider-ling, spinning webs, losing himself in the animal power he never had as &quot;puny Parker&quot; until he finally remembered his family and responsibilities?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T03:57:26-07:00","id":673048,"title":"","content":"Here's my take on a few Grand Theft Auto characters.....<br /> <br /> Salvatore Leone would be a Ventrue elder wracked with paranoia<br /> Toni Cipriani could work as either Sal's ghoul or as a Gangrel who works directly beneath him<br /> Trevor Philips is definitely a Slasher, most likely a Maniac<br /> Michael DeSanta could work as an independent hunter at the Tier 1 level who steals from other supernaturals<br /> Claude Speed could work as a Changeling or Sin-Eater, though in all honesty, a standard mortal works best.<br /> Edward T. Fortune (the United Liberty Paper guy from GTA IV) is definitely with Task Force Valkyrie, and United Liberty Paper is a front for TFV","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T04:54:55-07:00","id":673066,"title":"","content":"MGS5 &quot;Boss&quot; is a Former Hunter/Slasher that has Legend as his Purpose.<br /> The Skulls are a unit of Supernaturals that have been Lobotomised and are fielded against the Enemies of Cipher.<br /> Cipher is a Tier 3 conspiracy dedicated to stopping &quot;Boss&quot; and those he attracts to his banner.<br /> Huey is a Genius.. Complete with his total lack of responsibility even though he knows he's wrong.<br /> The Parasite's (Vocal cord) are err... Bugs Warped by Spirits, twisted into destroying &quot;Language&quot; as the root of evil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T08:07:17-07:00","id":673183,"title":"","content":"<b>Rick</b> from <b>Rick and Morty</b> is probably a Hoffnung <b>Genius</b>, possibly Unmada and definitely low-Obligation. Rick is his Beholden, but he might be on the path to becoming Inspired. Some of his more memorable Wonders:<br /> <br /> <b>Portal Gun:</b> Skafoi 4, Katastrofi 1. Travels between realities and through space by shooting a portal that persists for a scene, or until he closes it. (Skafoi Ray, Fragile)<br /> <b>Space Car:</b> Skafoi 4, Prostasia 3, Automata 5, Apokalypsi 3, Katastrofi 2, Metaptropi 3. Capable of atmospheric and space flight, equipped with lethal weapons including but not limited to a raygun and a person dicer, high-powered AI, and basically enything else you could need or want. Runs on a pocket dimension battery. (Dexterous limbs, Limited Battery Life, Low-Light Vision, Variable damage, Bulletproof, Lockbox)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T15:20:01-07:00","id":674610,"title":"","content":"The Payday gang from the Payday games are a pack of criminal Iron Masters (I will let you guys figure out the auspices of the DLC characters, since Payday two has way too many playable characters, but of the core five, Dallas is the Elodoth, Chains is the Rahu, Wolf is the Ithaeur, Houston is the Irraka and Hoxton is the Cahalith) with Crime.net being the modern incarnation of an ancient lodge dedicated to criminal activity whose totem, Bain, is also the pack totem to the Payday gang. Bain is an ancient Iron master thief who has reached a level of primal urge where he is starting to become more of a spirit and can thus act as the lodge/pack's totem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T15:39:56-07:00","id":674649,"title":"","content":"I've always pondered getting into Payday, you've pretty much sold me on the matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T07:28:49-07:00","id":677586,"title":"","content":"The entirety of the surrealist and nightmarish visuals of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eraserhead\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Eraserhead</b></a> could be seen as the slow Awakening of a feeble and tormented Sleeper who feels oppressed by his growing obligations in a mechanical and uncaring world. The strange blending of reality and dream intrinsic to the movie makes it hard to say if Henry's Awakening is a Mystery Play or Astral Journey. His Path is likely Mastigos, or perhaps he is going through a False Awakening as he gazes far too much into the Abyss (see Night Horrors - The Unbidden, page 128). The whole movie is excellent inspiration for creepy Awakenings and stories focused on the Astral, particularly on crushed hope and repressed urges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T09:55:50-07:00","id":677727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=673183#post673183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Rick</b> from <b>Rick and Morty</b> is probably a Hoffnung <b>Genius</b>, possibly Unmada and definitely low-Obligation. Rick is his Beholden, but he might be on the path to becoming Inspired. Some of his more memorable Wonders:<br /> <br /> <b>Portal Gun:</b> Skafoi 4, Katastrofi 1. Travels between realities and through space by shooting a portal that persists for a scene, or until he closes it. (Skafoi Ray, Fragile)<br /> <b>Space Car:</b> Skafoi 4, Prostasia 3, Automata 5, Apokalypsi 3, Katastrofi 2, Metaptropi 3. Capable of atmospheric and space flight, equipped with lethal weapons including but not limited to a raygun and a person dicer, high-powered AI, and basically enything else you could need or want. Runs on a pocket dimension battery. (Dexterous limbs, Limited Battery Life, Low-Light Vision, Variable damage, Bulletproof, Lockbox)</div> </div> </div> </div> He seems a lot more like a Neid, because of all that spite, cynicism and hidden loneliness. Hoffnungs tend to be optimistic visionaries, which is the sort of attitude Rick would dismiss as ridiculous in practically any situation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T10:29:16-07:00","id":677765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=677727#post677727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> He seems a lot more like a Neid, because of all that spite, cynicism and hidden loneliness. Hoffnungs tend to be optimistic visionaries, which is the sort of attitude Rick would dismiss as ridiculous in practically any situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you're probably right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T17:28:37-07:00","id":678333,"title":"","content":"James Bond is, obviously, a Demon-blooded agent working for an Agency masquerading as a branch of British intelligence. His Stigmata would be giving his full name, if asked. In addition to various Gadgets, he makes personal use of Knockout Punch, Check Backdrop, Merciless Gunman, and other Embeds.<br /> <br /> (And if you want to explain why the movie actors keep changing, you could say his parentage keeps getting passed around amongst different demons, thus retroactively changing his appearance)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T13:07:30-07:00","id":679286,"title":"","content":"In honor of a certain game, here's human varieties of their characters:<br /> <br /> <b>The House of Dreamurr: </b>All of them are powerful Obrimos, with one being quite skilled in Death, Life, and Time magic as well. Asgore is what happens when their moral tendencies snuff out their inner fire.<br /> <br /> <b>Sans and Papyrus: </b>Sin-Eaters, though one is a lot better at this gig than the other.<br /> <br /> <b>Undyne: </b>Anakim with a Hunger for Predation-she mostly feeds on people she's after when they realize how implacable she is.<br /> <br /> <b>Alphys: </b>Relatively non-malignant Promethean alchemist.<br /> <br /> <b>Mettaton: </b>The homunculus made by Alphys. Not actually a Promethean, or even entirely artificial.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Flowey: </b>Lich, and pretty pissed off about it.<br /> <br /> <b>The Fallen Child: </b>Unknown, possibly an angel of the God-Machine meant to eradicate humans. Maybe a True Fae.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 09-26-2015, 07:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T01:04:28-07:00","id":695846,"title":"","content":"I was watching some Bayonetta videos, and thought about what splat she would belong to. The fact that she would be a walking breach of any splat's masquerade if she acted like in the games notwithstanding, my first hunch was a Destroyer Saboteur/Tempter. However, the things she does would be out of character for just about any Cover. Maybe her main Cover is custom made or hi-jacked from an Angel. Furthermore, what power could a Demon have that would mimic her ability to summon those monsters out of her own hair? I'd say that she creates Hellhounds with the Twilight Entity and Essence Eater Adaptations, allowing them to follow her unnoticed and feed from Angels. Her animal forms could be a result of Show Of Power, or a homebrewed Exploit that lets Demons become animals.<br /> <br /> Another option that came to mind would be an Elder Daeva. Her ability to summon demons could be mimicked with something like this Devotion I wrote once (Beast Made Flesh), which lets the user combine Protean, Vigor and Resilience to use his own flesh and Vitae as conduits for monstrous servants. My write up of this Devotion was poorly thought out, so I'd have to overhaul it. Her other powers can be represented just fine with the normal Disciplines. The Scarborough Fair and Love Is Blue (her quadruple guns in the first and second games, respectively) are <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/477337-falco-s-nwod-homebrew\"><b>Sanguine Objects</b></a>. At first I considered her to be a member of the Circle Of The Crone, but she interacts with humans in a way that suggests a decent Humanity rating, and Cruac places a steep limit on Humanity.She's probably Unaligned. I don't know what equivalent to angels this version of Bayonetta would fight, though. She could be an ally of a Ring of Unchained and fight GM Angels as if she was a Saboteur herself.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T16:13:52-07:00","id":696604,"title":"","content":"Solomon Grundy is some kind of Extempore Promethean, or possibly a Frankenstein that bought the Nepri's Bestowment as a Transmutation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T18:29:57-07:00","id":698264,"title":"","content":"Come to think of it, Jackie Estacado from &quot;The Darkness&quot; works well as a Beast. The Darkness is an especially sadistic Horror, Jackie is an Eshmaki and his Hungers are Punishment and Power. When he attacks with the tendrils and serpent heads of the Darkness, he is using the <i>Limb From Limb</i>, <i>Monster Of The Deep</i>, <i>Cyclopean Strength </i>and<i> Titanic Blow</i> Atavisms. His affinity for shadows and stealth are a result of the <i>Shadowed Soul</i> and <i>From The Shadows</i> Atavisms. The terrorizing presence of the Darkness is likewise caused by the <i>Looming Presence</i> Atavism, and Jackie's abnormal endurance and healing speed are granted by <i>Unbreakable</i> and <i>Relentless Hunter</i>. The Otherworld levels could be Chambers in Jackie's Lair.<br /> <br /> All in all, Jackie could also be a Sin-Eater with a really messed up Geist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 10-12-2015, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T14:48:19-07:00","id":709315,"title":"","content":"Uncle Grandpa seems to be an Abyssal Incursion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T15:35:23-07:00","id":709376,"title":"","content":"the Avatar Spirit is a Guardian/Tempter who reached Hell a long time ago. with a gadget made from Like In The Movies embed that activates when ever the wearer gets board. Her virtue is In-character and her vice is change. she is afraid that Azula is a new demon who found her hell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7525-quinn-h","name":"Quinn H.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T22:46:51-07:00","id":709975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=709315#post709315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uncle Grandpa seems to be an Abyssal Incursion.</div> </div> </div> </div>More like Abysmal, if you ask me.\u200b<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T00:28:35-07:00","id":710102,"title":"","content":"I've always been a fan of giant monsters/kaiju. The problem with including them in the NWOD is that they could easily break the masquerade, which is pretty intrinsic to the setting. <br /> <br /> That being said, I think the most straightforward way to include kaiju would be to make them Rank 6+ Cryptids (the ones mutated by Infrastructure). They could also be animals or objects who were Claimed by the Royal Avatars of the Gods Of The Shadow, legendary hobgoblins or especially monstrous True Fae, devastating Abyssal Incursions, ancient Pandorans, something that crawled out of the Dark Places opened by a Strix, an unusual Cthonian, or a Beast who achieved any of the three types of Inheritance. As for fan splats, I know that Geniuses with enough Inspiration, Axioms, resources and assistants can build kaiju-like Wonders. Some Conspiracies might create mecha-like Endowments to fight kaiju, Pacific Rim style.<br /> <br /> I believe that Godzilla himself could be the Horror of an Anakim Tyrant/Ravager who has Lair 9 or even 10. His Atavisms are Dragonfire, Cyclopean Strength, Titanic Blow, Looming Presence, Limb From Limb, Unbreakable, Relentless Hunter and Heart Of The Ocean. He probably reached the Incarnate Inheritance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 10-20-2015, 03:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T05:10:43-07:00","id":710400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=709975#post709975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More like Abysmal, if you ask me.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Abis Mal would be a rogue Aegis Kai Doru agent.","signatu