post710400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Abis Mal would be a rogue Aegis Kai Doru agent.</div> </div> </div> </div> I meant that Uncle Grampa is abysmal, as in abysmally stupid. But I think you knew that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T17:59:45-07:00","id":736402,"title":"","content":"I would love to have Amaterasu from Okami as an epic Uratha in a Dark Era based on feudal Japan. Her Fetishes and Talens are powered by Royal Avatars of Rank 6 Spirits of the Sun (not Helios, he's Rank 8 and doesn't even bother with Royal Avatars). Instead of the Brush, she has all the Gifts and Rites that control the elements and forces of nature, and a Merit that gives her 8 Again on the rolls to use those powers. Issun does not command the sort of respect and power that a Totem spirit does, but he knows his stuff and is helpful in his own way. He probably works better as a hobgoblin, though. Spoilers for the plot below:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The true final boss, Yami, is definitely an Idigam, and one with Rank 6.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T02:08:18-07:00","id":737397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=736402#post736402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would love to have Amaterasu from Okami as an epic Uratha in a Dark Era based on feudal Japan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Should not Ametrasu being just local Helios varation, maybe his Royal Avatar? With <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tsukuyomi-no-Mikoto\" target=\"_blank\">Tsukuyomi/Tsukiyomo</a> as the Father Moon/ Mother Luna figure. Interesting would be that Okami is local Wolf variant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T09:59:30-07:00","id":738693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=737397#post737397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should not Ametrasu being just local Helios varation, maybe his Royal Avatar?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the second time you've suggested that characters be Royal Avatars of beings that explicitly do not create Royal Avatars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T10:49:34-07:00","id":744700,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-106\" target=\"_blank\"><b>SCP-106 (AKA The Old Man)</b></a> [scary images] is a prime example of a Beast who does not care about acting like a human. More specifically, he's an Anakim with a Hunger for Prey. Even <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vjRlLvai_EU\" target=\"_blank\"><b>his theme tune from the video game adaptation</b></a> sounds like something from a slasher flick. That pocket dimension he drags people to is one of the main Chambers in his Lair. He may have even based that Chamber on the Site the Foundation contained him in, as a sort of game or payback. The way he passes through walls made of the toughest materials is just like the Anakim Birthright. He could also be imposing the Corrosive and Decayed Lair Traits, and using the Titanic Blow Atavism. His other Atavisms are Limb From Limb, Cyclopean Strength, Looming Presence, Basilisk's Touch, From The Shadows, Unbreakable, Needs Must and Relentless Hunter. His Nightmares are probably All Your Teeth Are Falling Out, Behold My True Form, You Cannot Kill It and Run Away. The <a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/the-young-man\" target=\"_blank\"><b>story that explores what he was like before becoming a Beast</b></a> (scary image at the end) is terrifying, as is <a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/treats\" target=\"_blank\"><b>the one where he celebrates Halloween</b></a>. Warning: all three articles contain vivid descriptions of extreme violence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 10-31-2015, 10:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T05:15:03-08:00","id":746399,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Dracula</span></b><br /> <br /> When it comes to a fictional character such a Dracula, there are a staggering number of adaptions, interpretations and re-inventions. For this write up, I am presenting Vlad Dracul as I believe he would appear in <i>Vampire the Requiem. </i><br /> Using the Dracula, Prince of Paris plot hook from the <i>Chroniclers Guide</i>, this version has ruled the City of Lights for over 100 years under an alias. His use of the coils has allowed him to transcend clan (although as the Prince of Paris he poses as a Gangrel). He is careful not to expose the true extent for his power, lest others discover who he truly is. <hr /><br /> <b>Vlad Dracul \u2013 Dracula</b><br /> <b>Mask: </b>Master; <b>Dirge: </b>Philosopher<br /> <b>Clan</b>: Unknown<br /> <b>Covenant:</b> Unaligned<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 6, Wits 5, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 6, Dexterity 4, Stamina 6<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 6, Manipulation 4, Composure 6<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 5(History, Religion), Animal Ken 5 (Children of the Night), Athletics 4, Brawl 4, Crafts 2, Expression 3 (Writing), Firearms 3 (Crossbow), Intimidation 6(Terror), Investigation 5 (Supernatural Mysteries), Medicine 3, Persuasion 5, Occult 6 (Transcendence), Politics 5 (Ordo Dracul), Ride 4, Science 3 (Experimentation), Socialize 5, Survival 4(Wallachia), Stealth 5, Subterfuge 5(Occult Secrets), Warfare 4, Weaponry 5(Halberd, Sword)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Acute Senses, Allies (Many), Area of Expertise (Ordo Dracul, Transcendence), Claws of the Unholy, Contacts (Many), Cutthroat, Defensive Combat (Weaponry), Eidetic Memory, Etiquette 5, Encyclopedic Knowledge (Occult), Eye for the Strange, Fame 3, Haven 5, Herd 5, Indomitable, Inspiring, Iron Will, Language (Many), Meditative Mind 4, Professional Training 4 (Voivode; Persuasion, Politics, Warfare), Resources 5, Retainer 5,Safe Place 5, Status 5 (Prince of Paris), Striking Looks 1, Style: Armed Defense 3, Style: Armored Combat 1*, Style: Heavy Weapons 4, Style: Kindred Dueling 4, Style: Mounted Combat 2*, Style: Riding the Wave 5, Style: Weapon and Shield 2*, Swarm Form, Taste, Tolerance for Biology, Trained Observer 1<br /> <i>Merits marked with an asterisk (*) are from the Hurt Locker playtest document.</i><br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Animalism 5, Auspex 6, Celerity 3, Dominate 4, Majesty 5, Nightmare 4, Obfuscate 4, Protean 6, Resilience 4, Vigor 3<br /> <b>Blood Magic: </b>Cruac 3 (Cheval, Deflection of Wooden Doom, Drops of Destiny, Touch of the Morrigan), Theban 3 (Damned Radiance, Malediction of Despair, Sanctity, Vitae Reliquary)<br /> <b>Devotions: </b>Force of Nature, Quicken Sight, Shared Sight, Summoning, Vermin Flood<br /> <b>Coils: </b>Ascendant 6, Voivode 5, Wyrm 5, and likely more<br /> <b>Humanity:</b> 5<br /> <b>Blood Potency</b>: 6 (this number fluctuates depending on how recent Dracula's last extended torpor was)<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 10<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 9<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 15<br /> <b>Health:</b> 11","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 11-01-2015, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T20:39:50-08:00","id":748307,"title":"","content":"The Nameless One from &quot;Planescape: Torment&quot; would work well as inspiration for a Mummy PC, and the whole game is rich with ideas for characters of other splats and personalities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T22:44:55-08:00","id":748514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=748307#post748307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Nameless One from &amp;quot;Planescape: Torment&amp;quot; would work well as inspiration for a Mummy PC, and the whole game is rich with ideas for characters of other splats and personalities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, which cRPG did Paradox just produce? Which team was producing it? What game was it a throwback too?<br /> <br /> Yeah, I want my Torment-style Mummy video game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T16:34:14-08:00","id":750262,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>The Wolfman</b></span><br /> <br /> For this write up, I am presenting Lawrence Talbot, the titular character from the 1941 version of \u201cThe Wolfman\u201d as I believe he would appear in <i>Werewolf the Forsaken. </i>This version of Lawrence Talbot was a talented and popular student, gifted in both athletics and having a keen scientific mind, destined for a productive and successful life until he inherited the \u201cfamily curse\u201d. At least one member of the Talbot family is born wolf-blooded every few generations. Lawrence is the first full Uratha of his family line for over 100 years. The legend passed to him from his family lore is that he is fated to die at the hands of someone who loves him, so he walks the path of a lone wolf. After years on the road learning about his abilities, he has returned home to investigate the mysterious death of his older brother.<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Lawrence Talbot \u2013 The Wolfman</b><br /> <b>Blood: </b>Destroyer; <b>Bone: </b>Rationalist<br /> <b>Auspice: </b>Rahu<br /> <b>Tribe</b>: Ghost Wolf<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 3, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 4, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 2(Research), Athletics 3, Brawl 3(Claws), Computers 2, Crafts 2, Drive 1, Empathy 2, Investigation 3, Intimidation 3, Medicine 1, Occult 2 (Folklore), Science 3, Socialize 2, Stealth 2, Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 2, Survival 2, Weaponry 1 (Clubs)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Allies 3 (Talbot Family), Anonymity 2, Blood Affinity, Common Sense, Danger Sense, Favored Form 2(Gauru),Fortified Form 4 (Gauru), Fleet of Foot 1, Hardy 1, Mentor 3, Patient, Striking Looks 1, Style: Relentless Assault 3, Style: Street Fighting 2<br /> <b>Gifts:</b> Change (Purity), Evasion (Purity), Full Moon 2, Knowledge (Wisdom), Rage (Purity), Strength (Honor, Purity)<br /> <b>Rites:</b> Chain Rage, Sacred Hunt<br /> <b>Harmony:</b> 7<br /> <b>Renown:</b> Honor 1, Purity 2, Wisdom 2<br /> <b>Primal Urge</b>: 3<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 6<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 13<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T10:34:46-08:00","id":754414,"title":"","content":"Guys, I figured out why Wile E. Coyote always uses ACME products to catch the Road Runner instead of going to a restaurant. He is a Huntsman, the ACME products are the Arcadian weapons his employer gave him, and the whole cartoon chase is an Approach. Road Runner is a Beast Runnerswift who gets his kicks from outsmarting Huntsmen.<br /> <br /> I can't help but imagine a Looney Tunes Freehold now. If escaping capture is what changelings are best at, then Bugs Bunny is the ultimate changeling. Also, you know that episode of the Looney Tunes Show where Bugs calls Daffy a narcissist, a sociopath and a psychopath? He's not far off the mark. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Xi_hcwB8i64\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Daffy has some very low Clarity.</b></a> He may or may not be a Charlatan Gentry.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T12:25:50-08:00","id":754755,"title":"","content":"I'd like to share a small headcanon I have about the NWOD, related to the above post. Firstly, ask yourself, what are many cartoon characters to a fair degree, especially the more Max Fleischer ones? Sociopaths. They are deceptive, remorseless, unpredictable, vice-ridden creatures, and they have very twisted notions of humor. Just look at what <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tLeH2Qbzdhc\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Big Head/The Mask was like in the original Dark Horse comics</b></a>, or <b><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kum1Z78mgzI\" target=\"_blank\">Peacock from Skullgirls</a> </b>(the latter is not so bad, though).<br /> <br /> Once upon a time, there was a True Fae with some level of self-awareness about what it was. It knew the Gentry scared humans, and that they told stories involving beings like it called &quot;fairy tales&quot;. The monster had a mangled understanding of the entire concept, as Gentry are wont to do. It liked the talking animals, the games its siblings played with mortals and the violent bits, but not much beyond that. It wanted to spread fairy tales about itself, but was outclassed by more experienced and powerful Strangers. Then there was a day where it discovered a human invention called television. Unable to build one itself or order one it liked in any goblin market at the time, it tried recreating the shows and fairy tales inside its Realm. The escaped changelings told others about what they had been through, and these stories found their way into the ears of those who controlled what was shown on television.<br /> <br /> The damn creature got a success on the chance die. It created the idea that grew into the first cartoons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 11-05-2015, 10:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T01:27:51-08:00","id":756018,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;Remember, remember the fifth of November</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Gunpowder Treason and Plot</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">I see of no reason,</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Why Gunpowder Treason</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Should ever be forgot...&quot;<br /> <br /> To day is Gunpoweder Treason day - and <b>V for Vendetta</b> one. Pitty we do not have <b>Promethean: The Created</b> 2ED </span></span></span>as I would stat V from is as from <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/alchemical-recipes/\" target=\"_blank\">Extempore Linage</a>, born in the fire of Larkhill. Question would still be his Refinement - he wants to teach humans, especially govermnet, that freedom is most important. So maybe Aurum? Or new Phosphorum? Here is from the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/its-complicated/\" target=\"_blank\">spoiler on Refinements</a>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>It's Complicated</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li><b>Phosphorum, the Refinement of Phosphorus:</b> The candle that burns twice as bright, burns half as long. The <i>Light-Bringers</i> reject the cautionary aspect to that philosophy and burning dazzingly, brilliantly. They take risks that no human would consider, they abuse their bodies and minds, and they risk their own existences to follow other Prometheans to the River of Death. Why? Many Light-Bringers have tasted defeat. They tried to create a new Promethean, but raised Pandorans instead. They attempted the New Dawn, but something went wrong and sent them stumbling backwards on the path. And now that they know how tenuous it all really is, instead of becoming fearful and cautious, they stand, bloody but unbowed, burning bright. Alex loves it when they see others trying in vain to gender them. They personally gave up trying to decide between the two long ago, perfectly happy with that nebulous nonbinary space. They\u2019ve been at this for a while, long enough to have been through half a dozen Refinements trying to find one that fits, but like their gender it always seemed to be one big question mark\u2026 until they discovered the path of the Light-Bringer.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-05-2015, 04:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T10:44:41-08:00","id":756888,"title":"","content":"He kinda makes me think of a Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T10:59:37-08:00","id":756934,"title":"","content":"He would fit pretty well in Deviant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T11:19:10-08:00","id":756958,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt1446192/\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Guardians</a>: The Guardians are strange, high Ranked ghosts, apparently able to dwell outside the Underworld as long as they defend children. They seem to have greater difficulty than normal using their Manifestations around those who don't believe in them, and their overall power (Rank, Numina, Influences) is tied to the degree of children's belief. Their personal realms are similar to Dead Dominions, but largely not subterranean-themed. The Man in the Moon, is likely a Deathlord or potent Kerberos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T12:49:41-08:00","id":757130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=756958#post756958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt1446192/\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Guardians</a>: The Guardians are strange, high Ranked ghosts, apparently able to dwell outside the Underworld as long as they defend children. They seem to have greater difficulty than normal using their Manifestations around those who don't believe in them, and their overall power (Rank, Numina, Influences) is tied to the degree of children's belief. Their personal realms are similar to Dead Dominions, but largely not subterranean-themed. The Man in the Moon, is likely a Deathlord or potent Kerberos.</div> </div> </div> </div> The whole movie feels more like something out of Changeling: The Dreaming. But then again, <a href=\"http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.br/2013/05/london-fae-spotlight-jack-frost.html\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Jack Frost himself could be something else.</b></a><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T13:13:13-08:00","id":757159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=757130#post757130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The whole movie feels more like something out of Changeling: The Dreaming. But then again, <a href=\"http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.br/2013/05/london-fae-spotlight-jack-frost.html\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Jack Frost himself could be something else.</b></a><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we are dealing with the New World of Darkness, here. And Changeling: the Lost it ain't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T09:30:20-08:00","id":760032,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Creature from the Black Lagoon</b></span><br /> <br /> For this write up, I am presenting the Gill Man, the titular character from the 1954 film \u201cThe Creature from the Black Lagoon\u201d as I believe he would appear in <i>Beast the Primordial.</i><br /> Dr. Carl Maia is a respected marine biologist and paleontologist. A native on Brazil, he has researched and cataloged dozens of prehistoric life forms that once roamed the coasts and interior of what is now South America. While on an expedition to a region known as \u201cthe Black Lagoon\u201d, he was plagued by nightmares of being stalked by \u201cThe Gill Man\u201d; a bizarre piscine-humanoid creature. He soon became one with the Horror. Now he travels the world, chasing rumors of paranormal animals and other strange beings, and protecting them from the depredations of civilization if necessary. <hr /><br /> <b>Dr. Carl Maia\u2013 The Creature from the Black Lagoon</b><br /> <b>Legend: </b>Stalker; <b>Life: </b>Explorer<br /> <b>Family: </b>Makara <br /> <b>Hunger</b>: Prey<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 3, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 4, Dexterity 4, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 3(Anthropology, Research), Animal Ken 2(Aquatic), Athletics 3(Swimming), Brawl 3, Crafts 2, Drive 2(Boats), Expression 2(Lecture), Firearms 2(Rifle), Investigation 3, Intimidation 2, Medicine 2, Persuasion 2, Occult 2(Parazoology), Science 4(Marine Biology, Paleontology), Socialize 2, Stealth 3(Water), Subterfuge 2, Survival 3(Jungle, Ocean), Weaponry 1 (Knives)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Allies 3(Academic), Area of Expertise (Boats, Jungle, Parazoology, Swimming), Direction Sense (Advanced), Double Jointed, Hunger Management 2, Iron Skin 2, Killer Instinct 2, Language (Portuguese; English, Spanish), Patient, Professional Training 4 (Marine Biologist; Academics, Athletics, Science), Resources 3, Trained Observer<br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> Heart of the Ocean, Monster from the Deep, Needs Must, Relentless Hunter<br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> Behold My True Form, Fear is Contagious, Run Away, You Are Not Alone<br /> <b>Satiety:</b> 4<br /> <b>Lair</b>: 4<br /> <b>Lair Traits:</b> Flooded, Maze, Sealed Exits, Suffocating<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 7<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 13<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T11:23:40-08:00","id":760100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=756888#post756888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He kinda makes me think of a Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div> He'd be an Eshmaki Ravager, yes? He does operate on the outskirts of society, he is very stealthy, and fights more like an assassin than a brawler. However, he does make the government feel powerless as the plot progresses, and he's larger than life in general. I'd say he shares some Atavisms with the Anakim and Ugallu, including Mimir's Wisdom, Looming Presence, Needs Must and Eye Of Heaven. The Hunger For Ruin fits nicely with the whole bomb throwing anarchist schtick. As nofather pointed out, a Deviant version of V would fit like a glove. The comic and its movie adaptation are even cited as inspirational material for Deviant.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T23:38:06-08:00","id":760531,"title":"","content":"What would Ash from the evil dead series stats be ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T01:06:31-08:00","id":760562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=760531#post760531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would Ash from the evil dead series stats be ?</div> </div> </div> </div>A really sad tier 1 Hunter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-d