5-08:00","id":760720,"title":"","content":"Very well done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T11:20:51-08:00","id":760779,"title":"","content":"I've kinda made Changeling AUs for pretty much everything I'm into, and I just started one for Undertale (SPOILERS IF YOU HAVEN'T PLAYED IT PLAY IT NOW):<br /> <br /> Frisk: Kithless or Fairest Playmate<br /> Chara: Fetchspawn<br /> Papyrus: Wizened Soldier<br /> Sans: Darkling Palewraith<br /> Toriel: Beast Broadback<br /> Alphys: Wizened or Beast Inventor<br /> Undyne: Ogre Water-Dweller<br /> Metatton: Elemental Manikin<br /> Grillby: Elemental Fireheart<br /> The dogs: Beast Truefriends<br /> Asgore: Beast Broadback, also the Autumn King<br /> Muffet: Beast Venombite<br /> Flowey: ???<br /> Gaster: Wizened Inventor","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 11-08-2015, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T11:41:36-08:00","id":760799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=760675#post760675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would give him more credit than that. Ash may be a fool, but he is an <i>exceptionally good at killing deadites</i> fool.<br /> <br /> The below reflects Ash as he was presented in <i>Evil Dead 2</i> and <i>Army of Darkness, </i>with additional notes from the <i>Army of Darkness RPG.</i><br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Ash Williams- The Promised One</b><br /> <b>Virtue: </b>Steely; Ash confronts mind-bending horrors with determination and a wry sense of humor.<br /> <b>Vice: </b>Over Confidence; Ash believes he can handle anyone or anything. This gets him into trouble.<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 4, Dexterity 4, Stamina 5<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 1, Athletics 3, Brawl 4(Deadites), Crafts 3, Drive 3, Firearms 4(Rifle, Shotgun), Intimidation 3, Occult 1(Deadites), Persuasion 3, Science 1(Chemistry), Subterfuge 2, Survival 2, Weaponry 4 (Chainsaw)<br /> <b>Skill Tricks: </b>Crafts (Improvised Tools, Weaponsmith), Brawl (Killer Instinct), Firearms (Gun Catalog), Persuasion (On the Prowl)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area of Expertise (Deadites), Cheap Shot, Danger Sense, Defensive Combat (Brawl, Weaponry), Eye for the Strange, Fast Reflexes 2, Hardy 2, Indomitable, Inspiring, Interdisciplinary Specialty (Deadites), Iron Skin 4, Iron Stamina 3, Iron Will, Quick Draw (Shotgun), Striking Looks 1, Style: Firefight 1, Style: Heavy Weapons 4, Style: Improvised Weapons 3, Style: Street Fighting 5, Tolerance for Biology, Unseen Sense (Deadites)<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 5<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 7 [Risk Willpower]<br /> <b>Conviction:</b> 3 [Mirrors, pg.32-33]<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 7<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 7<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 13<br /> <b>Health:</b> 10<br /> <b>Conditions: </b>Cursed, Forgetful</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesomesauce! My only nitpick is that you noted how strong his will is, but only gave him a Conviction of 3. He deserves a 5. You gave Solid Snake a Conviction of 6, remember? Ash fights eldritch horrors big and small, and doesn't go completely mad. You could even go ahead and give him the same Conviction as Snake. I haven't seen the Evil Dead movies yet, so I could be exaggerating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T11:54:18-08:00","id":760811,"title":"","content":"I remember classifying the Doctor as either a one-of-a-kind True Fae or a Genius. ArcaneArts and Basic convinced me he could also be an Unchained Demon.<br /> <br /> However, I think an Inspired Mane is closer to the spirit of the show. Gallifrey would be a Bardo with an abnormally high concentration of Inspired Manes. What the connection between Gallifreyans and Guardians Of Forever might be remains debatable, but I can see them helping each other out in a pinch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T13:21:41-08:00","id":765752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=460384#post460384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><i>Notes</i></b><br /> These traits represent Sam and Dean during the third season of <i>Supernatural</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Dean Winchester</b><br /> <b>Virtue: </b>Loyalty \u2013 Dean is intensely loyal; he is willing to go to hell and back (literally) for his allies.<br /> <b>Vice: </b>Impulsive \u2013 Dean often makes decisions with little forethought or consideration of consequence.<br /> <br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Sam Winchester</b><br /> <b>Virtue: </b>Empathy \u2013 Sam connects with people easily, and seeks to understand people before making any judgments.<br /> <b>Vice: </b>Stubborn \u2013 Once Sam has decided on a course of action, he is loath to change it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Myself, I would add for Dean a <i>Vice-Ridden</i> Merit connected to second Vice - <b>Hedonism</b> - to encapsulate his dedication to all drinking, casual sex and eating habits in one <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T07:24:53-08:00","id":766237,"title":"","content":"Balder (Bayonetta 2 Version) (done in 1E, though once we get 2E he should mostly be adaptable)<br /> <br /> Obrimos Mage, Exiled from Silver Ladder; Scion of God Legacy (3rd Attainment), Gnosis 7<br /> <br /> Virtue: Fortitude; Vice: Lust<br /> Strength 4, Dexterity 7, Stamina 5<br /> Intelligence 4, Wits 5, Resolve 6<br /> Presence 4, Manipulation 2, Composure 2<br /> <br /> Skills (note: Balder is 500 years old, and uses certain variant skills): Academics 3, Occult (Paradiso, the Aether, Angels) 6, Politics 1, Investigation 2, Athletics 6 (Throwing Spears), Brawl 5, Survival 4, Weaponry 7 (Holy Glaive), Animal Ken 3 (Peacocks, Wolves), Intimidation 5, Subterfuge 2<br /> <br /> Arcana: Prime 5, Forces 5, Spirit 5, Time 5, Space 4, Life 4<br /> <br /> Rotes: Among his rotes are forces spells that attack with fire and electricity, a rote which allows him to thrust his spear into one portal and have a larger version come out the other end, and the ability to turn into a wolf<br /> <br /> Merits: Combat Awareness, Language (likely several; is known to possess English and Enochian, and likely possesses Latin and Italian), Tolerance for Biology, Ambidextrous, Demolisher 1, Fast Reflexes 3, Fleet of Foot 1, Fighting Finesse, Weaponry Dodge, Law of Embodiment, Destiny 5, Otherworldly Eyes, Slayer, Summoner's Soul (Aether), Artifact Weapon (Holy Glaive)<br /> <br /> Fighting/Movement Styles: Aggressive Striking 2, Evasive Striking 5, Sojutsu 4, Parkour 5<br /> <br /> Flaws: Anachronistic (if set in a modern game; remember, he's from the 1300-1500s), True Love (will do anything for his true love)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T08:13:26-08:00","id":766265,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>The Mummy</b></span><br /> <br /> For this write up, I am presenting Imhotep, the titular character both the 1932 and 1999 version of \u201cThe Mummy\u201d as I believe he would appear in <i>Mummy the Curse.</i><br /> <br /> This version of Imhotep was an Iremite priest and member of the Su-Menent Guild, who was respected for his wisdom and scholarship. In his life prior to the Rite of Return, he was involved in a secretive affair with a woman named Anck-su-Namun, who was a member of the Mesen-Nebu Guild (and betrothed to an Iremite noble). He believes now that he was chosen for the Rite to separate him from his beloved. Over the centuries he has learned that Anck su Namun was also given the Rite of Return, and they were briefly re-united during the 1rst Sothic turn, and again during the 3<sup>rd</sup>.<br /> <br /> Imhotep has currently been active since 2012. He uses the alias of \u201cArdath Bey\u201d and is a wealthy and influential art and antiquities dealer. He strives to balance his duties as Arisen against his desire to locate Anck su Namun. His considerable resources indicate that she has not yet awaken in the current Sothic turn, and he fears some terrible fate may have befallen her. <hr /><b>Ardath Bey\u2013 The Mummy Imhotep</b><br /> <b>Virtue: </b>Passionate; <b>Vice: </b>Vengeful<br /> <b>Decree</b>: Name (Ren) <b>Judge: </b>The First Judge<br /> <b>Guild:</b> Shepard (Su\u2013Menent)<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 5(7), Wits 4, Resolve 5(6)<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 5(6), Dexterity 4, Stamina 5(6)<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 5(6), Manipulation 4, Composure 5<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 6(Relics), Athletics 3, Brawl 4(Grapple), Crafts 3, Empathy 2, Intimidation 3, Investigation 5, Larceny 2, Medicine 2 (Anatomy), Occult 6, Persuasion 4, Politics 4(Guild), Ride 2, Science 3(Alchemy), Stealth 3, Subterfuge 3, Survival 3 (Desert), Weaponry 3<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Allies (Many), Area of Expertise (Anatomy, Relics), At Any Cost*, Choke Hold, Clinch Strike *, Contacts (Many), Cult (Reach 4, Grasp 4; Blas\u00e9, Obedient, Ritualistic), Enigma 4, Defensive Combat (Brawl), Guild Status 5, Indomitable, Interdisciplinary Specialty (Anatomy, Relics), Inspiring, Iron Skin 2, Iron Will, Library 3 (Occult), Linguistics (Many), Meditative Mind 4, Resources 5, Professional Training 5 (Priest; Academics, Politics, Occult), Style: Grappling 2, Style: Martial Arts 2, Style: Unarmed Defense 3, Tomb (Geometry 4. Peril 4, Obscure, Prime Location), Trained Observer 3, Witness 3(Retainer-Benny), True Friend<br /> <i>Merits marked with an asterisk (*) are from the Hurt Locker playtest document.</i><br /> <b>Pillars:</b> Name 5; Essence 4, Heart 3, Shadow 4, Spirit 2<br /> <b>Affinities: </b>Ancient Horror Unveiling, Auspicious Mastery, Blessed Panoply, Blessed Soul, Charmed Lives, Death Sight, Entombed Glory, Epic Heart, Eternal Legend, <i>Fated Soul</i>, Gift of Truth, Glorious Mien, God Sight, Grip of Death, Guardian Wrath, Living Monolith, Retributive Curse, Shrouding Aura<br /> <b>Utterances: </b>Awaken the Dead (I,II,III), Doom Affliction (I,II), Jar of Teeth (I,II), Kiss of Apep (I,II), Rebuke the Vizier (I,III), Secrets Ripped from Skies (I,II,III), Words of Dead Glory (I,II,III), Wrathful Desert Power (I)<br /> <b>Relics:</b> The Book of the Dead (Text 4), Bracelet of Anubis (Uter 3)<br /> <b>Memory:</b> 6<br /> <b>Sekhem</b>: 5<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 9<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 8<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 14<br /> <b>Health:</b> 10","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 11-15-2015, 06:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T23:48:52-08:00","id":766881,"title":"","content":"This might be a bit of a cheat, but Mur Lafferty (a former White Wolf writer) is working on a series that feels a lot like a variant nWoD setting. In search of a new job, a black-listed author returns to New York City . . . where she continues to strike out. But a small, &quot;oddly&quot; obscure ( <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) startup is willing to take a risk on her . . . and she promptly finds herself the new managing editor on the Shambling Guide series. The world's <i>premiere</i> travel guide series for the monsters of the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because of the disaster that was her last job, Zoe is searching for a fresh start as a travel book editor in the tourist-centric New York City. After stumbling across a seemingly perfect position though, Zoe is blocked at every turn because of the one thing she can't take off her resume \u2014- human.<br /> <br /> Not to be put off by anything \u2014 especially not her blood drinking boss or death goddess coworker \u2014 Zoe delves deep into the monster world. But her job turns deadly when the careful balance between human and monsters starts to crumble \u2014 with Zoe right in the middle. </div> </div> </div>Off-hand, I see elements of <i>Requiem</i>, <i>Promethean</i>, and <i>Mage</i> (particularly the &quot;House of Ariadne&quot; Legacy) in the series. There's also a nice shout out to the <i>Wraith Player's Guide</i> from the classic World of Darkness series.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T10:09:06-08:00","id":769363,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b> The Phantom of the Opera</b></span><br /> <br /> The Phantom of the Opera, as seen many different incarnations over the years, from the original serial novels published in 1909, to the Lon Chaney silent film in 1925, to the popular musical in 1986. This version of the Phantom blends elements from the sources above. I considered a view different variations (including a Freak Slasher and a Sin Eater), but ultimately went with a Ghost.<br /> <br /> This version of the Phantom is a legend that stalks the hallways and hidden passages of the Palais Garnier opera House in Paris, France. The details of his life are jumble of conflicting rumors, some describing a violent, malformed madman, others describing a brilliant artist scarred by the cruelties of his peers. The stories agree that his obsession with a beautiful soprano in the year 1881 led to a series of accidents and murders, all of which culminated in the death of the Phantom at the hands of an angry mob.<br /> His forlorn spirit lingers on to this day. He considers the opera house his domain, but on rarely makes his presence known (typically if he disagrees with a casting choice or music selection). He is searching for the one that has the voice, pure and sublime, that can sooth his spirit and allow him to move on. Until then, he will haunt the Opera House, a phantom in name and in truth. <hr /><br /> <b>Erik\u2013 The Phantom of the Opera</b><br /> <b>Virtue: </b>Romantic <b>Vice: </b>Obsessive<br /> <b>Rank: </b>2<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 5, Finesse 5, Resistance 4, Willpower 9, Essence 15<br /> <b>Integrity: </b>4<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 9<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 4<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 15<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 9<br /> <b>Influences:</b> Opera House 2<br /> <b>Ban: </b>The Phantom is transfixed by the sound of a woman singing opera in soprano<br /> <b>Bane: </b>Crystal from the Opera House Chandelier<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Fetter, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Awe, Emotional Aura, Firestarter, Mortal Mask, Telekinesis<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T12:15:50-08:00","id":770191,"title":"","content":"Something I preparing for mine newest RPG club game to run. Behold father of modern Alchemy! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Nicolas Flamel</b></span><br /> <br /> This version of Flamel is Archmaster, previous Moros mage. Living once as Parisian member of Silver Ladder in XIV century, working with poor and Jews of from \u00cele-de-France, he dedicated his life to unlocking Mystery of immortality to give it back to people. His Sleepwalker wife Perenelle helped him in his research for decades. Finally, he unlocked secrets of Philosophical Stone, change of base Matter in to everlasting Life - and become Archmage by this very act. But the price for this was the life of his wife. When he became immortal, she died from the old age, now and forever written in reality. Flamel then understand the principle of Stone \u2013 it can grant you life, only it costs the life of others. This Quintessence is simple \u2013 a life for the life.<br /> <br /> Flamel know he could not continue his works in open, especially after departure of wife, but as once a Ladder mage, he tried to stir some possible alchemist in their studies. He faked his death with her, change identities and traveled world, bringing his own legend with him as stranger talking about himself. Once or twice in generation he proposed the Elixir of Life to those he thought are worthy \u2013 only to made them aware that it would take someone others life to do it. If they agree, he would made the Elixir, but then left the prospect suddenly \u2013 they would have only one more life time to uncover secrets of Alchemy, or they would parish. But he taught some time those that declined his offer, marking a true Wisdom.<br /> <br /> As to his whereabouts, nothing is sure now. Some said he omits Ascension War to continue his research, even after over half millennium of it. Others say he went to New World the first time Europeans sailed to Americas and there is somewhere, hiding in the middle of nowhere from the Orders and their brutal politics over Mysteries. And others say that Flamel finally get to Ascension, reconnecting with his wife in Supernal \u2013 but he left a body made of red crystal that is whole made of Philosophical Stone. <hr /><br /> <b>Nicolas Flamel</b><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Dedicated; <b>Vice:</b> Judgmental<br /> <b>( Ex-Path:</b> Moros <b>)</b><br /> <b>Noumenon:</b> Becoming the Alchemy itself<br /> <b>Entente:</b> None ( closest is Siddha )<br /> <b>Legacy:</b> Uncrowned Kings?<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 7, Wits 4, Resolve 7<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 4, Stamina 5<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 5, Manipulation 6, Composure 5<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 7(Alchemy), Athletics 2, Brawl 2, Crafts 5, Empathy 3, Intimidation 2, Investigation 5, Medicine 4 (Anatomy), Occult 7(Alchemy) , Persuasion 4, Politics 4(Alchemists), Ride 2, Science 3(Chemistry), Stealth 3, Subterfuge 3, Survival 2(Travel), Weaponry 3(Tools)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Eidetic Memory, Holistic Awareness, Indomitable, Patient, Hardy, 3 X Alternate Identity 3, Anonymity 5, Inspiring<br /> <b>Arcana: </b>Matter 8, Life 7, Prime 6, Mind 5, Fate 4, Forces 4, Death 3, Time 2, Space 2<br /> <b>Wisdom:</b> 8<br /> <b>Gnosis</b>: 9<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 12<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 9<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 12<br /> <b>Health:</b> 10","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-21-2015, 03:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T19:41:43-08:00","id":771156,"title":"","content":"While discovering that the newest mystery was actually caused by supernatural phenomena pretty much goes against the spirit of almost every Scooby-Doo episode, I can't help but chuckle at the idea of Shaggy as a Sin-Eater, with Scooby as his Geist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T22:58:53-08:00","id":771250,"title":"","content":"I don't suppose Lord Havelock Vetinari of Ankh-Morpork has been raised yet? He said hopefully?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T02:08:16-08:00","id":771333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=771250#post771250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't suppose Lord Havelock Vetinari of Ankh-Morpork has been raised yet? He said hopefully?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well Respected and equally Feared Tyrant Beast.... Most likely Apex, Probably a Eshmaki.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T03:03:28-08:00","id":771348,"title":"","content":"Havelock doesn't strike me as particularly Beastly. His talents are more towards being a master of politics and manipulation, which lends more towards Vampire, Demon, Mummy or Changeling.<br /> There have been rumours in-universe of him being a Vampire, and he is dating bona-fide black ribboner Lady Margolotta (probably), but it still seems unlikely to me simply for the reason of it being too obvious. <br /> <br /> Mummy doesn't seem likely either. He's been around too consistently and seems genuinely concerned about dying on occasion. If he is though, he's probably either Tef-Aabi or Maa-Kep.<br /> <br /> Demon fits rather well, possibly a Tempter residing in an alternate reality he is attempting to turn into Hell, although there is a possibility of him being an Inquisitor as well. Either a Messenger or a Psychopomp from his habit of manipulating people. Has various embeds targeted around being unseen and buffing his social aspects. The Gonne was a rifle embedded with Merciless Gunman.<br /> <br /> As a Changeling, he's gotta be a Darkling, probably of either Shadowsoul or Chatelane Kiths, definitely Autumn Court.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T05:58:56-08:00","id":771429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrBreaksIt</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a Changeling, he's gotta be a Darkling, probably of either Shadowsoul or Chatelane Kiths, definitely Autumn Court.</div> </div> </div> </div> ...The first book Patrician was his Fetch! It explains so much!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T09:50:07-08:00","id":771552,"title":"","content":"I'm leaning toward Mekhet Golcondan with utterly crazy Attributes and almost no Disciplines, myself, but I needed a Prince in my setting anyway. <br /> <br /> ...Incidentally he keeps an extremely clever Architect of the Monolith named Leonard locked up in secret.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T11:04:32-08:00","id":771606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=771552#post771552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Incidentally he keeps an extremely clever Architect of the Monolith named Leonard locked up in secret.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who happens to have no Clue about what the &quot;Masquerade&quot; is and would need to be Blood hunted otherwise? Who's Invented MANY &quot;New&quot; Rituals that are literally Spells from Mages that he has no idea about other then them popping them into his head?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T02:06:01-08:00","id":772884,"title":"","content":"It's obvious to the point of redundancy, but Dorian Grey would be the prettiest Daeva","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","name":"someguywithakatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T03:17:37-08:00","id":772898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>someguywithakatana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=772884#post772884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's obvious to the point of redundancy, but Dorian Grey would be the prettiest Daeva</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they used him as the inspirational material for Eternals (from WoD: Immortals), though, which (as he was a/the inspiration), he'd fit better.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T06:14:20-08:00","id":773039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=772898#post772898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think they used him as the inspirational material for Eternals (from WoD: Immortals), though, which (as he was a/the inspiration), he'd fit better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haven't read that book, so I'll take your word for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","name":"someguywithakatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T07:46:34-08:00","id":773104,"title":"","content":"The short version: Immortals who have an object that prevents them from dying. But they also take damage as the object does. Pretty much it aside from some minor Taste-like side ability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T06:11:04-08:00","id":775421,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Frankenstein's Monster</b></span><br /> <br /> Frankenstein\u2019s Monster is a fictional creature that has seen as many adaptions, re-interpretations, and re-telling\u2019s as Dracula (possibly more). He has been depicted as everything from a remorseless monster to a sympathetic creature longing to belong. For this write up, I am presenting The Monster as I believe he would appear in <i>Promethean the Created.</i><br /> The version of the Monster is the progenitor of the Frankenstein lineage, last seen in the opening fiction under the alias \u201cMr. Verney\u201d. After a climactic encounter with the Pandoran known as \u201cThe Bride\u201d, the Monster had finally destroyed the creature, but was left shaken by the battle. After retreating to the arctic for several years, he has returned to the place of his creation, to the ruins of a manor house only a few miles from Castle Frankenstein in Hesse, Germany. Reclaiming the name \u201cAdam\u201d, it is here he has chosen to begin his Pilgrimage anew, and complete the journey started over 200 years ago. <hr /><br /> <b>Adam\u2013 Frankenstein\u2019s Monster</b><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Love; <b>Vice: </b>Rage<br /> <b>Lineage</b>: Frankenstein; <b>Refinement: </b>Plumbum (Lead)<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 4, Resolve 5(6)<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 7, Dexterity 4, Stamina 7<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 4, Manipulation 3, Composure 4<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 4 (Music, Philosophy), Athletics 5, Brawl 5, Crafts 3, Empathy 3(Detect Lies), Expression 3 (Eloquence), Intimidation 5(Threats), Larceny 2, Medicine 2 (Anatomy), Occult 4 (Alchemy), Persuasion 2 (Pathos),Science 3 (Chemistry, Electricity), Stealth 4(Stalking), Subterfuge 3, Survival 5 (Arctic), Streetwise 2, Weaponry 2 (Improvised)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Air of Menace*, Alternate Identity 2, Area of Expertise (Alchemy, Music), At Any Cost*, Choke Hold, Danger Sense, Direction Sense, Elpis 2, Fame 3, Fast Reflexes 2, Fleet of Foot 2, Giant, Indomitable, Iron Will, Language (German, many others), Repute 3, Style: Improvised Weaponry 3, Iron Skin 4, Style: Relentless Assault 5, Style: Street Fighting 3, Striking Looks 2 (Frightening)<br /> <i>Merits marked with an asterisk (*) are from the Hurt Locker playtest document.</i><br /> <b>Bestowment:</b> Unholy Stamina, Unholy Strength<br /> <b>Transmutations: </b>Corporeum (<i>Autonomic Control, Hard Body, Human Flesh, Regeneration, Swift Feet</i>), Deception (<i>Incognito, Leave no Trace, Silent Steps</i>), Disquietism (<i>Alembic 3, Nameless Dread, Quell Disquiet, Soothe Disquiet 5</i>), Electrification (<i>Black Out, Divine Lightning, Feel the Spark, Generator, Jolt, Shock</i>), Mesmerism (<i>Atavistic Instinct, Firebringer, Fixed Stare, Flight, Logos</i>), Sensorium (<i>Translators Eye, Night Sight</i>), Saturninus (<i>Cleansing Ritual, Refined Masquerade</i>), Vitality (<i>Battering Ram, Bludgeon, Defenestrating Blow, Fist of Talos, Hyperion\u2019s Flight, Might 5, Pulverizing Blow, Shoulders of Atlas, Stupefying Blow, Thunderclap Blow, Titanic Vigor, Titan\u2019s Throw, Vault</i>), Vulcanus (<i>Electroshock Recharge, Sense Flux, Sense Pyros</i>)<br /> <b>Pilgrimage:</b> 6<br /> <b>Azoth</b>: 5 (Reduced by going to the Wastes)<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 9<br /> <b>Size:</b> 6<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 10<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 9<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 18<br /> <b>Health:</b> 13","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 12-05-2015, 08:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T19:04:16-08:00","id":780308,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Dr.Jekyll &amp; Mr.Hyde</b></span><br /> <br /> For this write up, I am presenting Dr. Henry Jekyll (and his alter-ego, Edward Hyde), the titular character of Robert Louis Stevenson\u2019s 1886 novel <i>The Strange Case of Dr Jekyll and Mr Hyde</i>, as a member of the Cheiron Group conspiracy from <i>Hunter: The Vigil.</i><br /> This version of Dr. Henry Jekyll is a chemist employed by the Cheiron group, developing new, cutting edge combat and performance enhancing drugs. While presenting the image of a clean cut and morally upright person, Jekyll\u2019s darker impulses led him to create an implant that stores an experimental steroid that increases his physical strength and prowess. While the steroid does grant a boost to such traits, it also led to a psychotic break. Now whenever he triggers the implant, his alternate persona \u201cMr Hyde\u201d takes over. Hyde is an amoral sociopath who acts out the impulses that Jekyll represses, and utilizes all the physical benefits of Jekyll\u2019s steroid. Even more disturbing is that the implant has triggered by its self on more than a few occasions. Dr. Jekyll is currently working on a way to revise the formula that lets him enjoy its benefits without unleashing the \u201cHyde\u201d persona. Likewise, Hyde is seeking a way to rid himself of Jekyll\u2019s moralizing and hypocrisy permanently. <hr /><br /> <b>Henry Jekyll/Edward Hyde</b><br /> <b>Virtue (Jekyll):</b> Prudent; <b>Vice (Jekyll): </b>Hypocrite <b>/ Virtue(Hyde):</b> Determined; <b>Vice (Hyde): </b>Amoral <b>; Vice-Ridden (Hyde):</b> Violent<br /> <b>Conspiracy:</b> Cheiron Group<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4 (Hyde 3), Wits 3, Resolve 3 (Hyde 4)<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3(Hyde 5), Dexterity 3, Stamina 3(Hyde 5)<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3(Hyde 4), Manipulation 3, Composure 4(Hyde 3)<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 3/2(Psychology), Athletics 2/3 (Running), Brawl 2/4, Computers 2/0, Crafts 2, Intimidation 1/3, Larceny 1/3, Medicine 3/0, Politics 2/0 (Corporate), Science 4 (Bio-Chemistry), Socialize 2(Etiquette), Stealth 2, Streetwise 1/3(Vice), Subterfuge 3, Weaponry 1/2 (Clubs)<br /> *The ratings after the slash are used while in the \u201cHyde\u201d persona.<br /> <b>Merits (Jekyll):</b> Allies 3 (Lawyer Gabriel Utterson), Alternate Identity 2 (Hyde), Area of Expertise (Etiquette, Psychology, Bio-Chemistry), Interdisciplinary Specialty (Bio-Chemistry), Professional Training 4 (Academics, Medicine, Science), Resources 4, Status 3 (Cheiron Group), Striking Looks 1(Stylish)<br /> <b>Merits (Hyde):</b> Area of Expertise (Vice), Danger Sense, Defensive Combat (Brawl), Fast Reflexes 2, Hardy 2, Iron Skin 2, Style: Improvised Weaponry 1, Style: Parkour 2, Style: Street Fighting 3, Tolerance for Biology, Vice-Ridden (Violent), Striking Looks 1(Cruel)<br /> <b>Endowment: </b>Thaumatechnology (Strange Form 5; Jekyll/Hyde have the Strange Form Dread power as an Endowment. When activated, it triggers the \u201cHyde\u201d persona and grants +2 to Strength, +2 Stamina, +1 Armor, and alters Intelligence, Presence, Resolve and Composure)<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 5<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 7<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> Jekyll 7, Hyde 8<br /> <b>Defense:</b> Jekyll 5, Hyde 7<br /> <b>Armor:</b> Jekyll 0, Hyde 1<br /> <b>Speed:</b> Jekyll 11, Hyde 13<br /> <b>Health:</b> Jekyll 8, Hyde 10<br /> <b>Condition:</b> Dissociative Identity Disorder, Malefactor<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <b>Dissociative Identity Disorder </b><b>[Persistent]</b><br /> You have suffered a trauma severe enough that it fractures your character personality into one or more additional personas, allowing you to deny your trauma or any actions the trauma causes by placing the blame on \u201csomeone else.\u201d An abused person might develop a tough-as-nails survivor personality, create a \u201cprotector\u201d or even become a murderer to deny the abuse she suffers. The personalities may or may not be aware of each other, and they come and go through your character\u2019s mind in response to specific situations or conditions.<br /> The character selects a specific breaking point. If a Breaking Point roll involving this specific breaking point is failed, the alternate persona takes over for the rest of the scene. On a dramatic failure the alternate personality remains in control until another roll for a specific breaking point is failed (this could be the same breaking point or a different one). This alternate personality usually has its own virtue, vice, aspirations and Breaking Points. The persona may also manifest different Skills (all skills are purchased normally, but certain personalities might not be aware they have such skills or may use them to different degrees of proficiency).<br /> <b>Possible Sources: </b>Neurological conditions, Psychological trauma, encountering a breaking point<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>Regain a dot of Integrity, or achieve an exceptional success on a breaking point. Long term psychological treatment can also re-integrate the personalities.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> When this the actions of one of the characters alternate persona causes severe complications in the life of the primary personality.<br /> <br /> <b>Malefactor [Persistent]</b><br /> Your darkest nature and most venial impulses are forced to the surface. While this condition is active, you no longer gain willpower from your Virtue. You continue to gain willpower from your vice as normal, but you may also fully recover all of your willpower by acting out for vice in a more extreme manner.<br /> <b>Resolution: </b> Increasing your Integrity<b>; </b>suffering a breaking point when acting out of Virtue.<br /> <b>Beat: </b>Whenever acting out your Vice damages a relationship or causes long term trouble.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 12-04-2015, 10:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T04:37:59-08:00","id":780499,"title":"","content":"I'm not stopping to analyse completely each sheet right now, but I would make the Frankenstein Monster even more bright. Maybe he isn't the most successful promethean around in his Pilgrimage, but he is described in the novel as not just a mockery of human life, but actually of its highest state. He's as much a genius as the doctor himself, if not even smarter.<br /> <br /> For Jeckyll and Hyde I would go far from this, assuming I'm trying to be honest with the original character, and not with the great number of bad adaptations of it. The concoction created by Dr Jekyll could be meant as a mental weapon to control the creatures, something to subsume their inhuman urges and give the imbiber more clarity of mind. Imagine a potion able to convert all the Alternate Integrities back into just Integrity, and put some common Breaking-Points, like killing, back into place? It could cure even Slashers! For the sound mind, maybe a greater capacity to resist loss of Integrity and to comprehend those who don't have it.<br /> <br /> But something went wrong, as you could expect, and Hyde is <u>devoid</u> of Integrity instead. Maybe it is a state similar to terminal Soulessness, but more stable, or maybe it is something else. But as evil as he is, Hyde never was more physically able or less smart than Jekyll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T06:06:17-08:00","id":780525,"title":"","content":"Re: Frankenstein's Monster<br /> <br /> You mage a good point for the Creature's Intelligence. I re-read a bit of the novel and agree that his intelligence is much greater than much of pop culture gives him credit for (seriously, He learns a sophisticated degree of language and reading after several months of pure observation). I updated his intelligence to a 4, learning at least some room for even more improvement.<br /> <br /> Re: Jekyll/ Hyde<br /> <br /> I mulled over a few different ways to present a modern World of Darkness Jekyll/Hyde. From my reading of the novel. Jekyll played the part of a upstanding citizen, but had urges that were contrary to his self image. His formula was conceived as a way to exorcise these urges, but instead gave him a way to indulge them without tarnishing his reputation. Jekyll <i>enjoyed</i> being Hyde..until he lost control of him.<br /> <br /> As far as the actual mechanics, I almost went with making the Hyde personae a slasher but with no real change of capabilities from Jekyll, but decided that the pop-culture spin where Hyde is more physically powerful was more interesting (as always, your mileage may vary).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T19:33:25-08:00","id":781490,"title":"","content":"Since Reighnhell has already posted his write-up for the Xenomorph, I figured there was no harm in mentioning that he also did a write-up for the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/277408-the-alien-xenomorph-in-wod-rulesset?p=277696#post277696\"><b>Predator.</b></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T18:06:27-08:00","id":782568,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>The Invisible Man</b></span><br /> <br /> For this write up, I am presenting the Invisible Man, combining elements from the 1997 novel by HG Wells, and the 1933 film, as a Genius from <i>World of Darkness: Slasher</i> (further augmented by a Dread power to represent his unique condition).<br /> This version of the Invisible Man is Dr. Jack Griffin, and independent chemist who spent years attempting to devise a compound that could render materials invisible. After having squandered his resources, alienated his associates and been laughed out of academia, Dr. Griffin was reduced to living on the streets while he still worked desperately to perfect the formula that would give him the wealth and fame he desperately desired. He eventually created a formula and experimented upon himself. The formula was successful, but unstable, making Dr.Griffin permanently transparent and unhinging his mind. Now he indulges in theft, arson, and occasionally murder while his delusions become increasingly grandiose and megalomaniacal. <hr /><br /> <b>Dr. Jack Griffin \u2013 The Invisible Man</b><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Ambition; <b>Vice: </b>Reckless <b>Vice-Ridden:</b> Greed<br /> <b>Undertaking: </b>Genius<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 4, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 4, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 2 Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 2(Research), Athletics 2, Brawl 2, Computer 2, Crafts 3(Jury Rig, Traps), Intimidation 2(Coercion), Investigation 2 (Scrounging), Larceny 4(Arson, Burglary), Medicine 3, Science 4(Chemistry, Optics), Stealth 4(Invisibility), Streetwise 2(Homeless), Subterfuge 2(Disguise), Survival 2(Urban)<br /> <b>Merits: </b>Anonymity 3, Area of Expertise (Chemistry), Eidetic Memory, Fast Reflexes 1, Fleet of Foot 2, Interdisciplinary Specialty (Chemistry), Murder Expert, Professional Training (Scientist; Academics, Medicine, Science), Tolerance for Biology, Vice Ridden<br /> <b>Talent: </b>Profiling <b>Frailty:</b> Intolerance for Chaos<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 4<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 8<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed: </b>14<br /> <b>Health: </b>7<br /> <b>Condition: </b>Madness<br /> <br /> <b><i>Dread Powers</i></b><br /> <br /> <b>Invisibility: </b>Griffin\u2019s flesh and blood do not register to sight, even under infrared or ultraviolet light. This ability does not extend to items worn or carried and even items swallowed will be visible for several minutes. Once Griffin sheds his clothing he becomes nearly imperceptible to the naked eye. Perception rolls to spot him suffer a \u20135 penalty, except those based strictly on smell, sound or motion. Opponents fight blindly and must rely on cunning and their other senses to hit. (See \u201cFighting Blind,\u201d World of Darkness Rulebook, p. 166.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 12-08-2015, 09:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T22:34:51-08:00","id":785189,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Dorian Gray</b></span><br /> <br /> For this write up, I am presenting Dorian Gray, the titular character of Oscar Wilde\u2019s 1890 novel <i>The Picture of Dorian Gray</i>, as an Eternal from <i>World of Darkness: Immortals.</i><br /> This version of Dorian did not die as the original tale would have people believe. Instead, he faked his demise will leaving a will bequeathing his considerable fortune, to previously-unknown illegitimate son, legitimized posthumously in the will. Of course, this was Dorian posing as his own descendant. He has repeated this ruse several times. Most recently he has returned to London after spending several decades abroad. He is currently posing as his latest descendant and operating as a club promoter, patron of the arts, and information broker. <hr /><br /> <b>Dorian Gray</b><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Repentant; <b>Vice: </b>Hedonist <b>Vice-Ridden:</b> Romantic<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 4, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 4 Manipulation 4, Composure 4<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 3 (Art, Literature), Athletics 1, Brawl 2, Crafts 2 (Art), Empathy 4, Expression 2(Eloquence), Firearms 2, Intimidation 2, Medicine 1, Investigation 3(Blackmail Material), Larceny 2, Occult 1, Persuasion 5 (Seduction), Politics 2(British), Socialize 5 (Aristocracy, Carousing), Stealth 2, Streetwise 4 (Vice), Subterfuge 4, Weaponry 2(Clubs, Knives)<br /> <b>Merits: </b>Alternate Identity 3, Area of Expertise (Art, Seduction, Vice), Barfly, Contacts 4 (Artists, Aristocracy, Drug Dealers, Prostitutes), Etiquette 4, Fixer, Inspiring, Language (Many), Professional Training 5 (Socialite; Academics, Politics, Socialize), Pusher, Resources 5, Staff 3, Striking Looks 2, Taste, Vice Ridden<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 6<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 7<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 7<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 4<br /> <b>Speed: </b>11<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <br /> <b><i>Dread Powers</i></b><br /> <br /> <b><i>Anchor:</i> </b>Dorian\u2019s immortality is anchored to his Portrait. Any damage inflicted to it is also inflicted to Dorian. This damage cannot be healed unless the Portrait is likewise repaired. Destroying the Portrait will destroy Dorian Gray. The Portrait has a Size of 4 and a Durability of 2.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Immortality:</i> </b>Dorian does not age as is immune to natural poisons and diseases (but can still indulge in drug use with no risk of overdose). He regenerates damage at a rate of 1 bashing every 2 minutes, 1 lethal every 8 hours and 1 aggravated each day. He can also regrow lost limbs within a month and damaged organs within a few weeks. Even if killed He will return to life within a day.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T23:12:19-08:00","id":785202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=785189#post785189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Dorian Gray</b></span><br /> <br /> For this write up, I am presenting Dorian Gray, the titular character of Oscar Wilde\u2019s 1890 novel <i>The Picture of Dorian Gray</i>, as an Eternal from <i>World of Darkness: Immortals.</i>...<br /> <br /> He is currently posing as his latest descendant and operating as a club promoter, patron of the arts, and information broker.</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone has watching <b>Librarians</b> lately, yes? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T23:22:37-08:00","id":785209,"title":"","content":"I have actually not seen it yet!<br /> <br /> I am just between games so stating out CofD (liking the new name!) versions of classic villains, monsters and the occasional hero keep my Storytelling system muscles strong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T07:17:56-08:00","id":785376,"title":"","content":"Seeing your write ups is always a joy. They're each interesting in their own right and insightful for creating similar characters for use in games. I hope you keep sharing them!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T22:44:47-08:00","id":787167,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Santa Claus</span></b><br /> <br /> For this write up, I am using the Horror rules from Chronicles of Darkness to present a version of Santa Claus.<br /> <br /> No one is really certain who or what Mr. Christopher Nicholas is. While it seems unlikely that he is the true mythological Santa Claus, he wields a large degree of otherworldly power that even master occultists are at a loss to explain. He even looks the part of a distinguished older gentleman a stocky build, snowy white beard, warm smile and twinkling eyes. To mortal society, he is a reclusive philanthropist who gives vast sums of money to a large number of humanitarian causes each year. To others he is a mysterious figure that is most active around the time of the solstice. For those that are charitable, honest, and kind; he leaves gifts and offers encouragement. For those that are selfish, wicked and naughty; he leaves a gentle warning, typically a lump of coal. The worst offenders he leaves for <i>something</i> else to deal with.. <hr /><br /> <b>Mr. Nicholas</b><br /> <b>Virtuous: </b>Jovial<b> Virtue: </b>Generous; <b>Vice: </b>Gluttony<br /> <b>Aspiration: </b>Reward the Virtuous, Spread Cheer, Inspire Hope<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 6, Wits 5, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 5, Dexterity 4, Stamina 5<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 7, Manipulation 4, Composure 5<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 4(Religion), Animal Ken 4, Athletics 2, Crafts 5(Toys), Drive 3(Sleigh), Empathy 5(Children), Expression 3, Occult 4(Folklore), Persuasion 5, Survival 3, Stealth 5, Weaponry 2<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area of Expertise (Children, Religion, Toys), Danger Sense, Eidetic Memory, Indomitable, Inspiring, Language (All), Resources 5, Safe Place 3 (Workshop), Staff 3, Striking Looks 1, Virtuous<br /> <b>Integrity: </b>10<br /> <b>Potency: </b>8<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 18<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 9<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 14 (Flight 19)<br /> <b>Health:</b> 10<br /> <b>Powers of Santa: </b>Eye Spy, Holiday Miracle*, Immortal, Influence 1 (Hope), Know Soul, Surprise Entrance, Vanish*<br /> <br /> <i>Holiday Miracle:</i> This functions as the <i>Miracle</i> dread power, but Mr. Nicolas may use it freely as long as it benefits others. This ability has no effect on the subjects Aspirations, but anytime they would regain Willpower from their vice they also gain the <i>Guilty</i> condition.<br /> <br /> <i>Vanish:</i> When Mr. Nicholas is in a situation that might turn violent, or if he simply wants to leave, he may disappear into thin air. He will reappear sometime later (as little as a few minutes, or as long as several months) at one of his Workshops or any place with a high concentration of cheer and goodwill.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 12-17-2015, 10:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T03:29:13-08:00","id":787253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The worst offenders he leaves for <i>something</i> else to deal with.. </div> </div> </div>Someone needs to do the Krampus next.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T19:25:09-08:00","id":787777,"title":"","content":"I would like to see the Team Fortress gang as Mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T19:31:50-08:00","id":787782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=787777#post787777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to see the Team Fortress gang as Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div> The lovely thing about the TF Team is that you can write them into almost any RPG (seriously, I have about 3 versions of each character in Dark Heresy).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T20:10:21-08:00","id":788492,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>The Krampus</b></span><br /> <br /> For this write up, I am using the Horror rules from Chronicles of Darkness to present a version of the Krampus.<br /> The creature known as \u201cThe Krampus\u201d is the shadow of St. Nicholas, inspiring dread and dealing punishment to the wicked. To most, he takes the form of Mr. Peter Black, the esteemed business partner of Mr. Nicholas. But during the dark weeks surrounding the winter solstice, he takes his true form; a shaggy, horned, goat legged horror. As the Krampus he leaves cryptic warnings and bizarre \u201cgifts\u201d as a reminder that misbehavior will be punished. For the worst offenders, he claims their souls, dragging them in chains to a place that can only be called \u201cHell\u201d.<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>The Krampus</b><br /> <b>Virtue: </b>Just; <b>Vice: </b>Cruel<br /> <b>Aspiration: </b>Punish the Wicked, Inspire Virtue through Terror<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 5, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 7, Dexterity 5, Stamina 5<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 6, Manipulation 4, Composure 5<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 4, Brawl 4, Crafts 2 (Gifts), Empathy 4(Guilt), Intimidation 6, Larceny 4, Occult 4(Folklore), Stealth 5, Subterfuge 4, Survival 4, Weaponry 4 (Chains)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Danger Sense, Eidetic Memory, Indomitable, Language (All), Lightning Reflexes 2, Style: Parkour 5, Striking Looks 2(Nightmarish)<br /> <b>Potency: </b>8<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 18<br /> <b>Size:</b> 6<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 12<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 9<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 18 (Flight 23)<br /> <b>Health:</b> 11<br /> <b>Powers of the Krampus: </b>Hunters Senses (Wickedness), Immortal, Madness and Terror, Know Soul, Soul Thief, Surprise Entrance, Vanish*<br /> <br /> <i>Vanish:</i> The Krampus can disappear in the blink of an eye, leaving behind bitter memories and harsh lessons.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T17:41:05-08:00","id":789998,"title":"","content":"<b>Stiles Stilinski</b><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Loyal <b>Vice:</b> Suspicious<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b> Survive High School, Protect his father and his friends, Solve the mystery of the week<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 4, Resolve 2<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 2, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 2, Manipulation 3, Composure 2<br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics 2 (Research), Computer 1, Crafts 1, Investigation 3 (Identifying Patterns), Medicine 1, Occult 1 (Werewolves, Research), Politics 1, Science 1<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 1, Drive 1, Larceny 2<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Empathy 2, Expression 1, Persuasion 2, Subterfuge 3 (Misdirection)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area of Expertise (Research), Good Time Management, Eye for the Strange, Fast Talking 3, Status - Police 1 (Son of the Sheriff), True Friend (Scott McCall), <br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 4<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 4<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 3<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 9<br /> <b>Health:</b> 7","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T12:54:27-08:00","id":790436,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Music/DoctorSteel\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Doctor Steel</b></a> is prime inspirational material for Genius: The Transgression. He started out as a Grimm, but soon became much more like a Hoffnung. What is interesting is that he's not truly crazy: he feigns an over the top insanity as part of his persona. Despite this, he really despises the current state of the world and wants to take over it to build an utopia. And his songs are damn catchy, to boot. He makes me want to run a Genius game where the PCs and NPCs are Internet celebrities who fight each other for both funding and viewership, all while presenting their more direct conflicts as part of a show.<br /> <br /> On a much darker note, we have <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=M3iOROuTuMA\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Salad Fingers</b></a> (warning: disturbing content). He's probably a changeling with Clarity 0 who lives deep inside a mostly deserted part of the Hedge. Or maybe he's a mage with Wisdom 0, and some or all of those random, creepy things that happen around him are actually caused by his out of control spellcasting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T16:11:54-08:00","id":791839,"title":"","content":"Going back to my Payday Gang as Werewolves bit, The Dentist and the Elephant are totally Demons. Specifically they are a pair of Messenger Saboteurs who use the promise of freeing Hoxton (the pack's Cahalith) from prison as a means of manipulating the Payday pack into getting their mortal pawns into political positions (the elephant's first two jobs) and stealing the valuable linchpins of various infrastructure (the Dentist's loot from the golden grin casino heist is definitely a linchpin, especially since the FBI files log on the heist has a casino spokesman saying that the pack &quot;ripped the heart out of this place&quot;, as is the cursed diamond). The Big Bank was merely a test of the pack's abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T21:04:01-08:00","id":792529,"title":"","content":"I am trying out the new Horror rules from CofD, so I did a quick write up of &quot;The Blob&quot; from the 1958 classic of the same name. <hr /><br /> <b>The Blob</b><br /> <br /> <b>Best At: </b>10 (Consuming Flesh, Oozing through Obstacles)<br /> <b>Worst At: </b>2 (Moving Quickly, Thinking)<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Consume all Flesh<br /> <b>Willpower/Scene:</b> 6<br /> <b>Initiative: </b>5<br /> <b>Defense: </b>2<br /> <b>Speed: </b>7<br /> <b>Size: </b>5<br /> <b>Health: </b>12<br /> <b>Banes: </b>Cold<br /> <b>Dread Powers: </b>Consume*, Fluid Form*, Natural Weapons (Digestive Ooze 1), Regenerate 1, Surprise Entrance, Unbreakable, Wall Climb<br /> <br /> <i><b>Consume:</b></i> The Blob receives a +3 modifier to grapple checks, flowing over its target in a wave of acidic ooze. If the Blob is successful, it assaults its captive with digestive acids, applying successes on its roll to establish a grapple as lethal damage. It also applies its natural weapon when using the Damage maneuver while in a Grapple.The Blob may regain 1 point of Willpower per point of damage inflicted, heal one point of Health or gain 1 point of Size.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Fluid Form:</b></i> The Blob can liquefy itself into a fluid by spending 1Willpower. This lasts until the end of the scene, during which time it can flow down drains, under doors, or immerse itself into another body of liquid and swim through it at twice its normal Speed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":".  adding suggested updates 12-25-2015, 10:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T21:12:36-08:00","id":792535,"title":"","content":"I think there should be a note in consume that it can use the Damage Move in the first turn of grapple, or that it can inflict damage that way. Kind of like the mechanic for a vampire in frenzy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T06:13:54-08:00","id":792718,"ti