ide 1, Natural Weapons (Bite +2), Snare<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T21:20:34-08:00","id":792937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=792918#post792918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Bane:</b> Electricity</div> </div> </div> </div>So I see we're going with the changed ending, then? The one where humanity wins?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T21:41:35-08:00","id":792939,"title":"","content":"Yep. While my brain appreciates the original &quot;Don't Feed the Plants&quot; ending, my heart prefers the &quot;Hollywood&quot; ending.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T09:40:52-08:00","id":793151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=788492#post788492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>The Krampus</b></span><br /> <br /> For this write up, I am using the Horror rules from Chronicles of Darkness to present a version of the Krampus.<br /> The creature known as \u201cThe Krampus\u201d is the shadow of St. Nicholas, inspiring dread and dealing punishment to the wicked. To most, he takes the form of Mr. Peter Black, the esteemed business partner of Mr. Nicholas. But during the dark weeks surrounding the winter solstice, he takes his true form; a shaggy, horned, goat legged horror. As the Krampus he leaves cryptic warnings and bizarre \u201cgifts\u201d as a reminder that misbehavior will be punished. For the worst offenders, he claims their souls, dragging them in chains to a place that can only be called \u201cHell\u201d.<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>The Krampus</b><br /> <b>Virtue: </b>Just; <b>Vice: </b>Cruel<br /> <b>Aspiration: </b>Punish the Wicked, Inspire Virtue through Terror<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 5, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 7, Dexterity 5, Stamina 5<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 6, Manipulation 4, Composure 5<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 4, Brawl 4, Crafts 2 (Gifts), Empathy 4(Guilt), Intimidation 6, Larceny 4, Occult 4(Folklore), Stealth 5, Subterfuge 4, Survival 4, Weaponry 4 (Chains)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Danger Sense, Eidetic Memory, Indomitable, Language (All), Lightning Reflexes 2, Style: Parkour 5, Striking Looks 2(Nightmarish)<br /> <b>Potency: </b>8<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 18<br /> <b>Size:</b> 6<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 12<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 9<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 18 (Flight 23)<br /> <b>Health:</b> 11<br /> <b>Powers of the Krampus: </b>Hunters Senses (Wickedness), Immortal, Madness and Terror, Know Soul, Soul Thief, Surprise Entrance, Vanish*<br /> <br /> <i>Vanish:</i> The Krampus can disappear in the blink of an eye, leaving behind bitter memories and harsh lessons.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Me and my friends were just talking about this. we thought he would be a true fae","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T14:11:33-08:00","id":793262,"title":"","content":"Stephen King's IT as a very, very old Dalga with a single subsistence-level Servitor whose theme is Clowns instead of Clocks?<br /> <br /> I feel as though this is either obliviously obvious or all I'm doing is explicitly demonstrating exactly how oblivious I am :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1289,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","user":"Hastur00","date":". 12-26-2015, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T16:45:52-08:00","id":793314,"title":"","content":"Earlier in this thread, someone mentioned that the G-Man from Half-Life is a God-Machine Angel, because he's a human-looking, mysterious entity with space-time bending powers who serves nebulous masters whose true nature is unknown. Basic also started a thread on the Demon forum where they said that the Lutece Twins from Bioshock Infinite are also God-Machine Angels, since they act similarly and show the same kind of powers.<br /> <br /> Following that while staying on the topic of video games, I believe the Happy Mask Salesman from the Legend Of Zelda series could also be a God-Machine Angel, given his odd mannerisms, suspicious levels of knowledge about the game's events and his ability to appear and disappear as he pleases, among other things.<br /> <br /> I wonder how many enigmatic video game characters could be interpreted as Angels?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-27-2015, 08:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T17:29:28-08:00","id":793330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=793314#post793314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Earlier in this thread, someone mentioned that the G-Man from Half-Life is a God-Machine Angel, because he's a human-looking, mysterious entity with space-time bending powers who serves nebulous masters whose true nature is unknown. Basic also started a thread on the Demon forum where they said that the Lutece Twins from Bioshock Infinite are also God-Machine Angels, since they act similarly and show the same kind of powers.<br /> <br /> Following that while staying on the topic of video games, I believe the Happy Mask Salesman from the Legend Of Zelda series could also be a God-Machine Angel, given his odd mannerisms, suspicous levels of knowledge about the game's events and his ability to appear and disappear as he pleases, among other things.<br /> <br /> I wonder how many enigmatic video game characters could be interpreted as Angels?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooo... I like that! I would have pegged the Happy Mask Salesman as a powerful Spirit or True Fae, but an Angel works too! It could also be possible that he's an Exile too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T14:02:24-08:00","id":793771,"title":"","content":"Speaking of the God-Machine and video games, it seems possible that the Markers from the Dead Space series were at one point part of Infrastructure, but something worse than the God-Machine overtook them and transformed them for its own purposes. Perhaps it was an Abyssal, or maybe it was one of the eldritch horrors from Second Sight. Isaac and other characters affected by the Markers suffer from symptoms similar to those of Stigmatics, as well.<br /> <br /> On an unrelated note, Majin Buu from Dragon Ball is an Idigam, as I pointed out in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/644946-dragon-ball-z-celestial-masters?p=645013#post645013\"><b>this post.</b></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T12:22:58-08:00","id":794320,"title":"","content":"I just finished watching the first season of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Bletchley_Circle\" target=\"_blank\">The Bletchley Circle</a>, and I can't help but see it as four Hunters tracking down a Slasher. So I figured I'd stat out the main four characters of the show.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Susan Gray</i></b><br /> <br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Determined. <b>Vice:</b> Curious.<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b> Make A Difference, Solve A Grand Mystery.<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 3, Resolve 3.<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 2, Stamina 2.<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 1, Manipulation 2, Composure 4.<br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics 3, Computer 1, Investigation 4 (Patterns), Science 3 (Mathematics, Cryptography).<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Firearms 1, Larceny 1, Stealth 2.<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Empathy 2, Persuasion 1, Socialise 2, Subterfuge 2.<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area of Expertise (Patterns), Good Time Management, Interdisciplinary Specialty (Patterns), Investigative Aide (Science), Investigative Prodigy 5, Hobbyist Clique (Science), Resources 3.<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 7.<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5.<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> +5.<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 2.<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 9.<br /> <b>Health:</b> 7.<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 7.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Millie</b></i><br /> <br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Passionate. <b>Vice:</b> Blunt.<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b> Be Extraordinary, Have A Grand Adventure.<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 4, Resolve 3.<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 2, Stamina 2.<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 3.<br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics 1, Computer 1, Investigation 2, Science 3 (Mathematics, Cryptography).<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Firearms 2 (Pistols), Larceny 1, Stealth 1.<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Empathy 1, Persuasion 2, Socialise 2, Streetwise 3, Subterfuge 3.<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Good Time Management, Investigative Aide (Science), Language (German), Language (Russian), Multilingual 4 (Diverse European Languages), Barfly, Closed Book, Contacts 2 (Black Market, Criminals), Style: Fast-Taking 5, Fixer, Hobbyist Clique (Science), Resources 2, Spin Doctor, Striking Looks 1, Table Turner, Taste.<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 6.<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5.<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> +5.<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 2.<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 9.<br /> <b>Health:</b> 7.<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 6.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Lucy</i></b><br /> <br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Innocent. <b>Vice:</b> Reluctant.<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b> Help Her Friends Succeed, Use Her Talents For Good.<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 2, Resolve 2.<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 2, Stamina 2.<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 2, Manipulation 2, Composure 3.<br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics 3 (Research), Computer 1, Investigation 3, Science 3 (Mathematics, Cryptography).<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 1, Larceny 2, Stealth 1.<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Empathy 2, Persuasion 2, Socialise 2, Subterfuge 1.<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area of Expertise (Research), Eidetic Memory, Good Time Management, Interdisciplinary Specialty (Research), Investigative Aide (Science), Patient, Trained Observer, Hobbyist Clique (Science), Resources 2, Striking Looks 1.<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 5.<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5.<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> +5.<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 2.<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 9.<br /> <b>Health:</b> 7.<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 8.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Jean</b></i><br /> <br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Righteous, Protective. <b>Vice:</b> Harsh.<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b> Protect An Innocent From Harm or Injustice, Stand For What She Believes In.<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 2, Resolve 4.<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 2, Stamina 2.<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 2, Composure 3.<br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics 3 (Research), Computer 1, Investigation 1, Science 3 (Mathematics, Cryptography).<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 1, Firearms 1, Stealth 2.<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Persuasion 1, Intimidation 3 (Authority), Socialise 2, Subterfuge 1 (State Secrets).<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area of Expertise (Authority), Good Time Management, Interdisciplinary Specialty (Authority). Investigative Aide (Science), Library (Investigation) 3, Professional Training (Academics, Investigation, Science) 5, Contacts 2 (Government Clerks, SOE Agents), Tolerance For Biology, Virtuous, Hobbyist Clique (Science), Iron Will, Resources 2, Small Unit Tactics.<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 7.<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5.<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> +5.<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 2.<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 9.<br /> <b>Health:</b> 7.<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 7.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Alice Lancaster (n\u00e9e Merren)</b></i><br /> <br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Stoic. <b>Vice:</b> Martyr.<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b> Be A Good Mother.<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 3, Resolve 3.<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 2, Stamina 2.<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 2, Manipulation 2, Composure 3.<br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics 1, Computer 3 (Code Machines), Crafts 3 (Code Machines), Investigation 1, Science 3 (Mathematics).<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 2, Firearms 1, Stealth 1.<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Empathy 1, Persuasion 1, Intimidation 1, Socialise 1, Subterfuge 3.<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area of Expertise (Code Machines), Good Time Management, Interdisciplinary Specialty (Mathematics). Investigative Aide (Science), Ally (Elizabeth Lancaster) 1, Alternate Identity 1, Fame 1, Hobbyist Clique (Science), Resources 2.<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 6.<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5.<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> +5.<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 2.<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 9.<br /> <b>Health:</b> 7.<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 6.<br /> <br /> I have also mentally headcanoned that after these women's victories, The Bletchley Circle grew from a cell to a proper Compact, and now boasts almost a hundred Hunters spread out throughout Europe and America, using mathematics and cryptography to find the hidden truths in the CofD.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Reviewing some stuff after finishing S2, and adding in Alice Merren.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":10056,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","user":"ShadowKnight1224","date":". 12-28-2015, 07:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T14:51:09-08:00","id":795102,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m rewatching <b>X-Files</b> before 2016 revival and with all the talk about <b>Hunter: The Vigil</b> 2ED, I thought I get you iconic pair of hunters. In this version they both run Tier 1 cell amidst of FBI that is, technically, part of VASCU Conspiracy, but in reality is seperated from it, being dedicated to more \u2018otherworldly\u2019 matters than most of VASCU dedicated to catching serial killers. The so called \u201cX-Files\u201d are denomination on the cases normal FBI do not have rational resolution. Write up is based on the time of series first season.<br /> <br /> <b><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Fox \u201cSpooky\u201d Mulder</span></i></b><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Believer<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Naive<br /> <b>Profession:</b> Detective ( FBI Agent)<br /> <b>Organization:</b> Vanguard Serial Crimes Unit ( Cell called \u2018X-Files\u2019 )<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 4, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 3, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics 3, Investigation 4 (Crimes Scens), Medicine 1, Politics 2, Occult 4 (UFO, Conspiracy Theories), Science 1<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 2 (Running), Brawl 2, Drive 1, Firearms 3 (Pistols), Stealth 2, Survival 1, Weaponry 2<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Empathy 3 (Motives), Intimidation 1, Socialize 1, Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 2<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Eye for the Strange, Danger Sense, Indomitable, Investigative Aide (Occult), Library 1 (Occult \u2013 Basement Office in FBI HQ ), Professional Training 3 ( Detective; Empathy, Investigation &amp; Occult ), Tolerance for Biology, Trained Observer 3, Contacts ( FBI Agents, Science Experts, Conspiracy Theorists, Government Informants )<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 7<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 6 ( He <i>is</i> a bit Spooky )<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 6<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 5<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 11<br /> <b>Health:</b> 7<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Obsession ( Samantha, Often )<br /> <b>Aspirations: </b>Find Samantha, Uncover Government Conspiracy<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i>Dana Scully</i></b></span><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Rational<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Doubting<br /> <b>Profession:</b> Doctor ( FBI Agent)<br /> <b>Organization:</b> Vanguard Serial Crimes Unit ( Cell called \u2018X-Files\u2019 )<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 3, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 4<br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics 3, Investigation 3 (Crime Scenes), Medicine 3 (Autopsies), Politics 1, Science 3<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 2, Brawl 2, Drive 1, Firearms 3 (Pistols), Stealth 2, Survival 1, Weaponry 2<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Empathy 2 (Motives, Mental Health), Persuasion 2, Intimidation 1, Socialize 2, Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 2<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Common Sense, Danger Sense, Indomitable, Patient, Professional Training 3 ( Doctor; Empathy, Investigation &amp; Medicine ), Tolerance for Biology, Trained Observer 1, Small-Framed, Contacts ( FBI Agents, Science Experts, Medical Community )<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 7<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 8 ( She <i>is</i> a bit hard standing )<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 7<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 5<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 10<br /> <b>Size:</b> 4<br /> <b>Health:</b> 6<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Spooked ( Often )<br /> <b>Aspirations: </b>Helping Mulder be objective, Write rational rapports<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-03-2016, 06:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T17:23:26-08:00","id":798500,"title":"","content":"So going through and skimming the thread, I just realized that there's only been two mentions of Bayonetta that I saw, and one of them was just a statblock I wrote for Balder.<br /> <br /> I've had this discussion on the RPG.net forum, but Bayonetta (all Umbra Witches, really) are clearly Mages following a Legacy. They are masters of Time, Spirit, Life, and Matter, (the last to account for the hair becoming... well, everything), though Bayonetta also wields some Fate and light Forces combinations (to make sure her shots stick) and Space (some of her moves involve moving into another area for a strike). Possibly also aligned with the Arrows (though possibly as a secretive, Left-Handed Legacy); this is a call I make due to the combination of magic and attacks she uses (she's probably got Adamantine Hand). I'm going to say she's a Thyrsus, as well, and that the Legacy gives her Time as an extra Arcana. They are NOT Mastigos, even though they use Demons; Bayonetta is never seen using a single Mind spell that I can see (thogh she may use a few more subtle spells, to improve her Wits or Social stats, I'd never peg her a Master of Mind, or of space for that matter).<br /> <br /> As shown in my drawing-up of Balder, I see the Lumen Sages as Obrimos who follow the Scion of God Legacy (they even have masks, and their powers involve summoning and using Angels).<br /> <br /> We don't see much of him, but I could stat Rodin as either a Mage or a Demon. He's a demon in-game, but it's pretty subtle that that's what he really is (he's got a very strong Cover, to be sure, and Angels who know who he is stay away from him). But, his role is really much closer to being a Forge-master - he's got a massive array of crafted items, most of which are made from demonic materials (both in terms of &quot;ores from hell&quot; and actual demons made into weapons). He's also got a faculty for Spirit magic (especially impressive since he's likely a Moros, though one far more focused on Matter than Death), enough that he can go into Inferno and come out again. Obviously, the Gates of Hell bar and armory is his &quot;safe place,&quot; probably with a size of 3 and Security of 5. If you use alternative paths, I'd give him a path of Spirit and Matter, with anything other than Prime or Forces being an inferior arcana (Mind works, as does Time).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T20:12:57-08:00","id":798767,"title":"","content":"While Deadpool is closer to a Deviant from what we've been shown, does anyone else think he could be a Charlatan Gentry? His regeneration is like Immortal Flesh, his hedonism is like Ruled By Passion, his equipment could be stolen Hedgespun and some of his stunts might be aided by Contracts. Insanity goes without saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T14:44:28-08:00","id":799808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=798767#post798767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While Deadpool is closer to a Deviant from what we've been shown, does anyone else think he could be a Charlatan Gentry? His regeneration is like Immortal Flesh, his hedonism is like Ruled By Passion, his equipment could be stolen Hedgespun and some of his stunts might be aided by Contracts. Insanity goes without saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, considering the revelation about Wade's possible connection to T-Ray at the end of Joe Kelly's run...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T10:21:56-08:00","id":815552,"title":"","content":"I think Gazelle from The Kings Man is a demon <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://vignette3.wikia.nocookie.net/villains/images/5/52/B7bzFBoCAAM-vUX.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/576?cb=20150221234932\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Name:Gazelle<br /> Incraction: Destroyer<br /> Agenda: Saboteur<br /> Catalyst:<br /> Age:Unknown<br /> Concept: Right Hand Henchmen<br /> Virtue: Loyal<br /> Vice: Sadistic<br /> Mental Attributes: Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 3 <br /> Physical Attributes: Strength 3, Dexterity 5, Stamina 3<br /> Social Attributes: Presence 3, Manipulation 2, Composure 3 <br /> Mental Skills: Computer 1, Medicine 1<br /> Physical Skills: Athletics 4, Brawl 3, Firearms 2, Weaponry 5 (Blades)<br /> Social Skills: Expression 2 (Killing), Intimidation 3, Socialize 2<br /> Merits: Terrible Form 2, Versatile Transformation, High Tolerance 1, Fast Reflexes 3, Perfessional Training 4, Ambidextrious 2, Double Jointed 2, Fleet of Foot 3, Fighting Finesse, Quick Draw, Armed Defese 5, Defensive Combat, Light Weapons 5<br /> Health: 8<br /> Willpower: 6<br /> Cover: 9<br /> Primum:3<br /> Aether: 13 <br /> Size:5 <br /> Speed:16 <br /> Defense: 8 <br /> Initiative Mod: 8<br /> Armor: <br /> Beats:<br /> Cover Beats:<br /> Experiences:<br /> Cover Experiences:<br /> Demonic Form: Blade Hands (Blade Legs), Inhuman Reflexes, Inhuman Strength, Fast Attack, Abruption Jets, Blind Sense, Plasma Drive, Wound Healing<br /> Embeds:Bystander Effect, Hesitation, Hush, Just Bruised, Merciless Swordsman (Leg Swords), Shatter, Turn Blade<br /> Exploits: Newton's Nightmares<br /> Interlocks: ????<br /> Weapons &amp; Equipment:<br /> Conditions:<br /> Short Term Aspirations:<br /> Long Term Aspiration:<br /> Bio:<br /> Covers:","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T15:06:07-08:00","id":828450,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking that Chuck, from the series of the same name, is a Stigmatic with the Download Knowledge and Trivia Embeds, although a case might be made for a Deviant, seeing as he had a computer jammed in his brain against his will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T05:53:18-08:00","id":829216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=828450#post828450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking that Chuck, from the series of the same name, is a Stigmatic with the Download Knowledge and Trivia Embeds, although a case might be made for a Deviant, seeing as he had a computer jammed in his brain against his will.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Until we see more of Deviant, I'd go with the first one, honestly. Being a Deviant may imply other powers that he simply doesn't possess, and one can become a Stigmatic without one's permission just as easily.<br /> <br /> That said, I definitely think your Stigmatic example is spot on, from what little I know of the show (honestly didn't catch my attention when it was on).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T06:52:16-08:00","id":829224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=828450#post828450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking that Chuck, from the series of the same name, is a Stigmatic with the Download Knowledge and Trivia Embeds, although a case might be made for a Deviant, seeing as he had a computer jammed in his brain against his will.</div> </div> </div> </div>Phh, please - with all the knowlegde and Skills he got with Intersect? He is clearly the Mind mage. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T12:38:22-08:00","id":829373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=829224#post829224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Phh, please - with all the knowlegde and Skills he got with Intersect? He is clearly the Mind mage. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>He doesn't really have nay control over it. Maybe an unlucky Sleepwalker on the receiving end of a Mind Spell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T05:39:58-08:00","id":833185,"title":"","content":"Frank Castle, aka Punisher, Eshmaki Nemesis. Relentless Hunter and Unbreakable Atavisms, Run Away and You Deserve This Nightmares, tons of dots in Physical Skills, more than one could think in Mental, few in Social (but strong Intimidation). Add some Merits and stuff from Hurt Locker and you're there. The Horror is a Grim Reaper in military clothes, the Lair an urban battlefield.<br /> <br /> Feeds a lot. Heroes tend to bother him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 02-19-2016, 08:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T07:54:10-08:00","id":833263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=833185#post833185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frank Castle, aka Punisher, Eshmaki Nemesis. Relentless Hunter and Unbreakable Atavisms, Run Away and You Deserve This Nightmares, tons of dots in Physical Skills, more than one could think in Mental, few in Social (but strong Intimidation). Add some Merits and stuff from Hurt Locker and you're there. The Horror is a Grim Reaper in military clothes, the Lair an urban battlefield.<br /> <br /> Feeds a lot. Heroes tend to bother him.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd actually go with Anakim, since he's quite a bit more brutish than say, Daredevil. Frank Castle doesn't stalk his foes, he chases them. He comes in, leaves, and in between is a storm of bullets, beatings, and grease stains that used to be his enemies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T08:05:17-08:00","id":833273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=833263#post833263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd actually go with Anakim, since he's quite a bit more brutish than say, Daredevil. Frank Castle doesn't stalk his foes, he chases them. He comes in, leaves, and in between is a storm of bullets, beatings, and grease stains that used to be his enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that as well and it was not an easy choice, but I ultimately went for Eshmaki because of the Fear behind the Family. I think he's slightly more about Destruction than Hopelessness, since he cares more about killing criminals than scaring them in the first place.<br /> <br /> Might be wrong, though. It's the sort of choice you're never 100% sure and needs little to make yourself change mind. I'm the first to admit that he'd do wonders with the Anakim's Birthright.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T06:01:35-08:00","id":839094,"title":"","content":"Is it just me, or would the Midnight Crew from Homestuck be good inspiration for a Ring of Saboteurs? The <b><a href=\"https://youtu.be/ll3gOluKb5Y\" target=\"_blank\"> Intermission where they invade the Felt Mansion</a></b> is like a comical spin on missions to bring down timey-wimey Infrastructure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T12:08:22-08:00","id":839344,"title":"","content":"I could totally see Walter White as a Moros Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T16:00:43-08:00","id":839492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=839344#post839344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could totally see Walter White as a Moros Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-the-nwod?p=460394#post460394\"><b>Reighnhell wrote stats for him and Jesse as mortals.</b></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T23:39:48-08:00","id":840447,"title":"","content":"Ok yesterday i finished Life is Strange and was quite amazed how the whole thing could be seen as an Acanthus Awakening. So here's Maxine Caulfield, as a mage after the events of the game.<br /> <br /> Name: Maxine Caulfield<br /> Shadowname: Supermax<br /> Order: Orderless, as she hasn't come in contact with the Orders yet, if she does, she'll propably join the Free Council<br /> Legacy: None<br /> Virtue: Charity<br /> Vice: Nosyness<br /> Obsessions: Though Max has largely gone over what happened with Arcadia, there's a thought in her head that it might be possible to change the past without making the necessary sacrifice. There has to be something she missed. <br /> <br /> Gnosis: 2<br /> Wisdom: 7<br /> Dedicated magical tool: Camera<br /> <br /> <br /> Attributes:<br /> Physical: Strenght 2, Dextrerity 3, Stamina 1<br /> Mental: Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 4<br /> Social: Presence 2, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <br /> Skills:<br /> Physical: Stealth 2, Drive 2, Firearms 1 Athletics 1 Larcery 1<br /> Mental: Investigation 2, Crafts 1, Computer 1,<br /> Social: Empathy 2, Persuassion 2, Socialize 1, Subtefuge 2, Expression (Photographs) 3, Animal Ken 1<br /> <br /> Merits:<br /> Sleepwalker Retainer (Chloe Price)<br /> True friend (Chloe Price)<br /> Taste<br /> <br /> Arcana:<br /> Time 3<br /> Fate 2<br /> Space 1<br /> <br /> Rotes:<br /> None as she yet has to come in contact with the Orders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","user":"Menace","date":". 03-02-2016, 02:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T23:53:19-08:00","id":840450,"title":"","content":"Only small nitpicking - <b>Mages without Order are called Solitaires.</b> Those that are part of lesser magical organizations are called Nameless. Free Council is coalition of previous Nameless traditions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Those that deliberate <i>left</i> or were <i>exiled </i>from Orders are called Apostates.<br /> <br /> So Max is Solitaire as far as Orders are. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T00:31:35-08:00","id":840465,"title":"","content":"I wonder what Agent Peggy Carter would look like in the Chronicles of Darkness... Or Howard Stark for that matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T00:40:14-08:00","id":840472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=840465#post840465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder what Agent Peggy Carter would look like in the Chronicles of Darkness... Or Howard Stark for that matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, this is sort-of-timely \u2014 finally saw Age of Ultron last weekend and picked up a useful addition to my comprehension of Promethean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T02:03:43-08:00","id":840491,"title":"","content":"What merits would you give her for the, well, the other ending?<br /> EDIT<br /> I personally think that Wisdom 7 is waaaaaaaaaaay to high for what she did in *that* ending. Her choice was extreme, monstrous act of hubris.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 03-02-2016, 05:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T02:43:59-08:00","id":840504,"title":"","content":"About that, he're my theory in the spoiler.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Until the &quot;important choice&quot; Max wasn't a mage, so no lower Wisdom. As for the choice, Max denies that fate and destiny cannot be changed and that her choices don't, which is a very Acanthus point of view. Sacrificing Cloe would mean that she accepts that she can't change anything and that would be digging into the Lie once again, going into conformity, failing her Awakening. An Act of Hubris would be still trying to save both Cloe and the town. She still might try to do it later.<br /> <br /> Off course it could be seen in a different way, but that's my interpretation.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Also I like how the whole climbing to the Lighthouse sequence (especially in the nightmare) was pretty pararel to climbing the watchtower of the Lunargent thorn","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","user":"Menace","date":". 03-02-2016, 05:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T03:53:45-08:00","id":840535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=840450#post840450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only small nitpicking - <b>Mages without Order are called Solitaires.</b> Those that are part of lesser magical organizations are called Nameless. Free Council is coalition of previous Nameless traditions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Those that deliberate <i>left</i> or were <i>exiled </i>from Orders are called Apostates.<br /> <br /> So Max is Solitaire as far as Orders are. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Solitares are mages without Cabals. Apostates are mages without orders, and it's usually used to refer to someone who at least had the opportunity to join an order and refused, not to someone who may not even know that orders exists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T17:50:56-08:00","id":841034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=840465#post840465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder what Agent Peggy Carter would look like in the Chronicles of Darkness... Or Howard Stark for that matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither Stark, father or son, could be anything other than a Genius; Howard's a Staunen, Tony a Grimm. Peggy's a mortal, or rather, a Hunter without a Conspiracy, though she's going to help found one soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T18:00:57-08:00","id":841036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WarDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=841034#post841034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Neither Stark, father or son, could be anything other than a Genius; Howard's a Staunen, Tony a Grimm. Peggy's a mortal, or rather, a Hunter without a Conspiracy, though she's going to help found one soon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could we do it in something besides a fan line?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T18:08:32-08:00","id":841040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=841036#post841036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could we do it in something besides a fan line?</div> </div> </div> </div> Perhaps Tony could be treated as a Hunter who confronts the supernatural mostly through political and economical influence. His Suits would be top-of-the-line Endowments, even by the standards of all the hyper-tech in H:tV. Also, wouldn't Genius!Tony be a Klagen? He Catalyzed by rejecting the use of his amazing intellect solely for personal gain, and the Klagen favor the Exelixi Axiom, which is necessary for powered exoskeletons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 03-02-2016, 09:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T21:50:50-08:00","id":841122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=841036#post841036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could we do it in something besides a fan line?</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't realize there was a rule about fan lines not being good enough for importing characters from from other media. Nothing else fits them half as well, but I guess they could also be mages who cast through instruments disguised as high technology.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>[B</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gottagofeast\">GottaGoFeast</a>[/B]<br /> ] Perhaps Tony could be treated as a Hunter who confronts the supernatural mostly through political and economical influence. His Suits would be top-of-the-line Endowments, even by the standards of all the hyper-tech in H:tV. Also, wouldn't Genius!Tony be a Klagen? He Catalyzed by rejecting the use of his amazing intellect solely for personal gain, and the Klagen favor the Exelixi Axiom, which is necessary for powered exoskeletons.</div> </div> </div> </div>In comics, maybe. Movie-Tony catalyzed because he was <i>angry </i>at the people who were using his inventions, his property, for evil and terrorism. There was also a good bit of guilt and self-loathing in there, but even that was outwardly expressed as rage. The fact that his friend died in the process didn't help either. You can see it on his face both while he's piloting the first suit to escape, and when he goes on his first &quot;mission&quot; after seeing the news broadcast. <br /> <br /> As for Axioms, he's full of crap when he says the suit isn't a weapon. Everything about it can be used as a weapon, meaning it's dripping with Katastrofi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T21:57:06-08:00","id":841126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WarDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=841122#post841122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't realize there was a rule about fan lines not being good enough for importing characters from from other media.</div> </div> </div> </div>Take the oral word-proboscis away from Leet's face and keep it away from anybody else's while you're at it, <i>por favor</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T22:03:11-08:00","id":841128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WarDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=841122#post841122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Didn't realize there was a rule about fan lines not being good enough for importing characters from from other media. </div> </div> </div> </div>There isn't, I just asked for thoughts on what they'd be like without using a fan line.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T22:52:59-08:00","id":841146,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlueBiscuit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=840535#post840535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Solitares are mages without Cabals. Apostates are mages without orders, and it's usually used to refer to someone who at least had the opportunity to join an order and refused, not to someone who may not even know that orders exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Read <b>Left Hand Path </b>and <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/a-well-armed-society/\" target=\"_blank\">Mage Society spoiler</a> - Solitares and Apostates definition have changed and those that I wrote will be used in 2ED.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage Society spoiler</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">A </span></span></span><b>solitary</b><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> is a mage who does not belong to any cabal or Order. Some hail from remote regions with few or no other resident Awakened or haven\u2019t attracted the attention of an Order yet. Most of these join an Order once the opportunity presents itself.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">An <b>apostate</b> rejected membership in all the Orders for whatever reason. This is a daunting prospect when even casual membership in an Order grants access to so many resources \u2013 thousands of years\u2019 worth of accumulated knowledge, grimoires, rotes, Legacies, artifacts, Imbued items, and secrets. Some apostates were once part of an Order and left (voluntarily or not), taking some its secrets with them. These latter apostates are distrusted by all the other Orders, who see them potential traitors or enemy spies.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Solitary is <i>not</i> mage without Cabal - it's a Awakened that was &quot;not touched&quot; by Orders culture.<br /> (Yeah, I also liked more that they meant solo mages)<br /> <br /> <i>Max</i> from <b>Life is Strange</b> is clearly Solitary Acnathus. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span></span></span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-03-2016, 03:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T05:06:19-08:00","id":841230,"title":"","content":"If Genius is no good for Tony, then there's also something to be said for him being an Obrimos with some Matter and Mind Magic at his disposal, especially with his more advanced armor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T08:19:49-08:00","id":841303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=841230#post841230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Genius is no good for Tony, then there's also something to be said for him being an Obrimos with some Matter and Mind Magic at his disposal, especially with his more advanced armor.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only problem is he's clearly needing his devices to operate. That's either extreme Yantra focus, or something else. Relic-crafting maybe?<br /> <br /> Genius is really the best option. A 1-person Conspiracy that makes his own Endowments is the closest other fit, I think.<br /> <hr /><br /> What do people think of some of the villains and side characters of the show?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-03-2016, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T05:24:35-08:00","id":841839,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the &quot;Vampires&quot; in Dusk till Dawn the series are still best represented by Vampire... thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T05:31:11-08:00","id":841840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=841839#post841839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if the &quot;Vampires&quot; in Dusk till Dawn the series are still best represented by Vampire... thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably Strix Possessed Or... Err Belials Brood best represent them. (In my Opinion anyway)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T16:45:36-08:00","id":842241,"title":"","content":"I tried making character sheets for SCP-076-2 and SCP-682, but I messed them up. Here's my second attempt.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><b>Able</b></i></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Virtue:</b> Valorous<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Furious<br /> <br /> <b>Aspirations:</b> Fight Worthy Opponents, Engage In Wanton Violence, Find SCP-073<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 5, Wits 7, Resolve 10<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 10, Dexterity 7, Stamina 10<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 5, Manipulation 1, Composure 5<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics (Ancient Warfare) 4, Crafts (Blacksmithing) 3, Investigation 2, Medicine 2, Occult 4, Science (Metallurgy) 3, Athletics 5, Brawl 5, Survival 3, Weaponry (Great Blades) 6, Animal Ken (Livestock) 2, Empathy 1, Expression 2, Intimidation (Violence) 5, Persuasion 1, Subterfuge 2<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area Of Expertise 1 (Ancient Warfare), Eidetic Memory 2, Encyclopedic Knowledge 2 (Academics, Occult), Indomitable (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration\"><b>Epic</b></a>), Interdisciplinary Specialty 1 (Ancient Warfare), Language (Many), Ambidextrous 3, Demolisher 3, Iron Stamina 3, Parkour 4, Air Of Menace 2, Closed Book 4, Iron Will 2, Heavy Weapons 5, Iron Skin 2 (Advanced 2), Martial Arts 5, Relentless Assault 5<br /> <br /> <b>Health:</b> 16 (Size 6)<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 25<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 13<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 12<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 35 (Species Factor 18)<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 5/5<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 10<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Armored Hide 3, Fabricate (Obsidian Weapons)*, Hideous Strength*, Immortal, Monstrous Resilience, Reality Stutter, Regenerate 3, Unbreakable<br /> <br /> <b><i>*Fabricate:</i></b> The creature can conjure objects from nowhere. By spending a point of Willpower and making a roll of an appropriate dice pool (minus the highest of the objects Availability, Size, or Weapon Bonus), the creature can produce equipment, items or weapons from thin air. The object is considered a typical item of its type and provides its standard equipment or weapon bonuses if applicable. Fabricated objects last until the end of the scene, at which point they vanish. Objects created with Fabricate typically have \u201cflaw\u201d (the objects might be fragile, deal less damage etc.)<br /> <br /> <i><b>*Hideous Strength:</b></i> Able\u2019s might is truly formidable; by spending a point of Willpower, he can increase his Strength by his Potency until the end of the scene. Furthermore, he adds his Potency as automatic successes on Strength + Stamina rolls made to perform a feat of strength, such as lifting a massive object or breaking free of restraints.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><b>The Hard To Destroy Reptile</b></i></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Virtue:</b> Adaptive<br /> <b>Vice: </b>Hateful<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b> Escape Containment, Lash Out Violently At All Life Forms, Survive Any Attempt At Killing It<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 6, Wits 8, Resolve 8<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 8, Dexterity 6, Stamina 10<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 5, Manipulation 3, Composure 6<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 2, Computer 1, Crafts (Sabotage Technology) 1, Investigation (Traps) 3, Medicine 1, Occult 3, Science 2, Athletics (Escaping) 4, Brawl (Natural Weapons) 5, Stealth (Ambush) 3, Survival 4, Empathy (Hostility) 1, Expression (Insults) 1, Intimidation (God-Awful Roar) 5, Subterfuge (Play Possum) 4<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area Of Expertise (Escaping), Common Sense, Danger Sense (Advanced), Direction Sense, Indomitable (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration\"><b>Epic</b></a>), Interdisciplinary Specialty (Escaping), Eidetic Memory, Trained Observer 3, Demolisher 3, Double Jointed (Advanced), Iron Stamina 3, Air Of Menace, Closed Book 5, Iron Will, Iron Skin 2 (Advanced 2), Killer Instinct 3 (Advanced 2), Relentless Assault 3<br /> <br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 24<br /> <b>Initiative: </b>12<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 10<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 26 (Species Factor 12)<br /> <b>Health:</b> 22 (Size 12)<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 4/4<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 10<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Hydrochloric Acid<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Armored Hide 2, <b>Devourer*</b>, Immortal, Jump Scare, Monstrous Resilience, Natural Weapons 2, Regenerate 4, <b>Shifting*</b>, Wall Climb<br /> <br /> <i><b>*Devourer </b></i>and <i><b>*Shifting</b></i>: These work as the ones used by the Idigam, but 682 usually has to receive a fair amount of damage before adapting to a threat. Adaptations are normally gone within a scene or two.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-10-2017, 08:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T14:22:11-08:00","id":844147,"title":"","content":"I might as well post this one too. This version of Ukulele/Alto Clef is from <a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/able-baker-charlie\" target=\"_blank\"><b>this Foundation Tale.</b></a><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><b>Agent Ukulele</b></i></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Virtue:</b> Destructive <br /> <b>Vice:</b> Mischievous<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 8, Resolve 10<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 9, Dexterity 7, Stamina 10<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 6, Manipulation 4, Composure 5<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 1, Crafts (Explosives) 3, Investigation 2, Medicine 1, Occult 2, Athletics 7, Brawl 4, Drive 2, Firearms 7, Larceny 3, Stealth 2, Weaponry (Cartoonish) 7, Expression (Humor) 3, Intimidation (Batshit Crazy) 4, Persuasion (Taunting) 3, Subterfuge (Lethal Pranks) 4<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area Of Expertise (Cartoonish), Danger Sense (Advanced), Indomitable (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration\"><b>Epic</b></a>), Interdisciplinary Specialty (Cartoonish), Double Jointed (Advanced), Parkour 4, Iron Will, Table Turner, Heavy Weapons 4, Iron Skin 2 (Advanced 2), Killer Instinct 3 (Advanced 3), Relentless Assault 3<br /> <br /> <b>Health:</b> 10 (Size 5)<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 25<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 14<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 12<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 50 (Species Factor 34)<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 5/5<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 10<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Must obey the mission given to it by the one who holds the device that activates its transformation.<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Armored Hide 3, Fabricate* (Cartoonish Weapons), Influence (Destruction 5), Monstrous Resilience, Numen (Seek, Teleportation*), Surprise Entrance, Unbreakable, Uncanny Regeneration*<br /> <br /> <b><i>*Fabricate:</i></b> The creature can conjure objects from nowhere. By spending a point of Willpower and making a roll of an appropriate dice pool (minus the highest of the objects Availability, Size, or Weapon Bonus), the creature can produce equipment, items or weapons from thin air. The object is considered a typical item of its type and provides its standard equipment or weapon bonuses if applicable. Fabricated objects last until the end of the scene, at which point they vanish. Objects created with Fabricate typically have \u201cflaw\u201d (the objects might be fragile, deal less damage etc.)<br /> <br /> *<b>Teleportation:</b> When the entity moves, it may reflexively spend 1 Essence to vanish and reappear at another location within its line of sight up to its (Rank x Speed) in yards away. Doing so adds +2 to its Defense for the turn. If the entity has the Seek Numen, it may teleport to the nearest location with a suitable Condition by spending 3 Essence. The entity can spend an additional 2 points of Essence to take a passenger with them (an unwilling passage may resist with a roll of Resolve + Composure + Supernatural Tolerance).<br /> <br /> <i><b>*Uncanny Regeneration:</b></i> Ukulele adds its Potency to his Health, and heals all bashing and lethal damage at the start of each turn. He downgrades a number of aggravated damage from mundande and supernatural sources euqal to Stamina into lethal.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-10-2017, 09:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T23:23:50-08:00","id":844362,"title":"","content":"I find myself picturing Frisk from Undertale as a sin-eater with Chara as the Geist. A genocide route involves Frisk loosing all their synergy and getting puppeted by Chara.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T13:54:48-08:00","id":844716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cmwatford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=844362#post844362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find myself picturing Frisk from Undertale as a sin-eater with Chara as the Geist. A genocide route involves Frisk loosing all their synergy and getting puppeted by Chara.</div> </div> </div> </div> I had the same thought <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=835070#post835070\">a while ago.</a></b> If you interpret the game through the lens of Changeling, the Underground could be a Hedge Kingdom (not to be confused with an Arcadian Realm, as Toriel and Asgore can't be True Fae). Chara doesn't fall neatly into any fae category. He/she acts like a Fetchspawn or True Fae, but he/she is still technically a human, albeit a completely heartless one. That makes me think of him/her as a Slasher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":""