Oh, right. I had forgotten about that, sorry. He was really bored with all that power, IIRC. If he's not a cursed hobgoblin or changeling, he might be a True Fae that is Dwindling from the lack of genuine conflict.<br /> <br /> Speaking of indie RPGs, what does everyone think the Batter from Mortis Ghost's OFF would be? A Cthonian? G-M or Principle Angel gone wrong? Abyssal? A Legend Slasher who's lost all but a few scraps of his humanity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 03-09-2016, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T07:46:41-08:00","id":845073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=844810#post844810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ...<br /> <br /> Speaking of indie RPGs, what does everyone think the Batter from Mortis Ghost's OFF would be? A Cthonian? G-M or Principle Angel gone wrong? Abyssal? A Legend Slasher who's lost all but a few scraps of his humanity?</div> </div> </div> </div>I always thought OFF was set in Arcadia, with the Batter as a low-Clarity, high-Wyrd Changeling who had returned to destroy the realm that tortured him. Of course, the Batter fails to care that he's destroying Changelings that haven't escaped yet...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T08:23:47-08:00","id":845094,"title":"","content":"Bo from Lost Girl, Changeling Fairest Deartheart/Leechfinger.<br /> <br /> Hades her Father- True Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T08:33:53-08:00","id":845097,"title":"","content":"Jesus: Sin Eater, Torn Necromancer, Giest the Holy Ghost.<br /> <br /> Moses: Mage, Obrimos<br /> <br /> Santa Claws: Changeling Wizened Maker/Snowskin.<br /> <br /> The Wraith from Stargate Atlantis, Beasts Namtaru.<br /> <br /> Jadzia Dax: This ones hard. Sin-Eater?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T08:43:51-08:00","id":845101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=845073#post845073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I always thought OFF was set in Arcadia, with the Batter as a low-Clarity, high-Wyrd Changeling who had returned to destroy the realm that tortured him. Of course, the Batter fails to care that he's destroying Changelings that haven't escaped yet...</div> </div> </div> </div> I can sorta buy the Batter as a changeling, but his Clarity is up for debate, as so much of the game is dependant on symbolism and the player's interpretation. The Batter is supremely single-minded and determined, so maybe he has Clarity 10. Even so, I don't think he's returning to Arcadia for revenge. He seems to be motivated by a twisted and grim compassion with a side of holier-than-thou.<br /> <br /> Or maybe the Batter and the Queen are changelings-turned-Gentry who used to know each other. The story is a Feud pieced together from the distant and fragmented memories of their mortal lives. Zacharie just plays his role in the story because he's a changeling with high Clarity. He's seen this song and dance before. The destruction of the Guardians, the purification of the Zones and finally the end of the Queen are a Wisp, Realm and Actor being claimed by the Batter, respectively. The Batter then Devours the True Name of the Queen, allowing him to kill Hugo and achieve total purification/Wyrd Transcendence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T08:50:52-08:00","id":845104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=845101#post845101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I can sorta buy the Batter as a changeling, but his Clarity is up for debate, as so much of the game is dependant on symbolism and the player's interpretation. The Batter is supremely single-minded and determined, so maybe he has Clarity 10. Even so, I don't think he's returning to Arcadia for revenge. He seems to be motivated by a twisted and grim compassion with a side of holier-than-thou.<br /> <br /> Or maybe the Batter and the Queen are changelings-turned-Gentry who used to know each other. The story is a Feud pieced together from the distant and fragmented memories of their mortal lives. Zacharie just plays his role in the story because he's a changeling with high Clarity. He's seen this song and dance before. The destruction of the Guardians, the purification of the Zones and finally the end of the Queen are a Wisp, Realm and Actor being claimed by the Batter, respectively. The Batter then Devours the True Name of the Queen, allowing him to kill Hugo and achieve total purification/Wyrd Transcendence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Either way, I'd imagine the Judge as a Changeling who wants everyone to be freed, and at first thinks the Batter will do that, but is appalled when he finds out it's the opposite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T09:00:04-08:00","id":845109,"title":"","content":"Spoilers for a 30-year-old show? Spoilers for a 30-year-old-show! (These are just the ones I thought of; I like the idea that much of the town is mundane.)<br /> <br /> Twin Peaks<br /> <br /> Special Agent Dale Cooper: Demon, Messenger/Investigator. Fell when he failed to arrest Leo Johnson for the murder of Laura Palmer, as he wanted to find the true killer. Pacted to add to his backstory, since the has multiple DB Coopers running around as covers. Definitely has Embeds to make people like/trust him. <br /> <br /> Laura Palmer: Fetch. Until her Changeling's return, she didn't know she wasn't real; that revelation helped prompt her downward spiral. Had a friendly relationship with her Changeling, who now goes by Maddy Ferguson. Has the Echo that lets her use Maddy's powers, hence how she showed up in dreams.<br /> <br /> Maddy Ferguson: Changeling, Darkling Dearheart. Formerly Laura Palmer. Got taken when fleeing from BOB. Escaped; created a fictional life as a long-lost cousin rather than trying to take her old life back. Somewhat horrified at what her Fetch got up to, but still grieving that death. <br /> <br /> Audrey Horne: Mage, Mastigos. Only recently Awakened, and there's not currently any other Mages in town to bring her into the fold. <br /> <br /> Sheriff Truman and the Bookhouse Boys: Hunters. Currently only local, they work on both mundane crimes and those with a supernatural bent.<br /> <br /> Harold Smith: Promethean, Osiran on the Cuprim Refinement. Liked Laura because she didn't suffer from Disquiet. When Donna and Maddy did, it broke him, hence his suicide.<br /> <br /> BOB: Strix. Alien mindset, possesses people, no real agenda, has a thing with owls. Strix.<br /> <br /> MIKE: Goetic demon of a dead Mage, or some kind of ghost-Mage. Strix were the last mystery he was investigating; sadly, his hubris lead to a whole lot of them in Twin Peaks. He's trying to make up for it now that he's super dead.<br /> <br /> Windom Earle: Angel, Destroyer. Possibly an Exile, possibly close to Falling, possibly Fell already but doesn't care. Mission may be to destroy Cooper.<br /> <br /> Log Lady: Purified. Spirit of Pines and the Forest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T09:12:50-08:00","id":845116,"title":"","content":"I always saw Cooper as mid-Awakening Acanthus rather than anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T02:45:11-08:00","id":845539,"title":"","content":"Just gonna put this here...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0AvWV6Mk374&amp;feature=iv&amp;src_vid=zGCictw_TgM &amp;annotation_id=annotation_4027965417\" data-code=\"0AvWV6Mk374\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/0AvWV6Mk374/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> And say Promethean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T03:42:46-08:00","id":845547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=845539#post845539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just gonna put this here...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0AvWV6Mk374&amp;feature=iv&amp;src_vid=zGCictw_TgM &amp;annotation_id=annotation_4027965417\" data-code=\"0AvWV6Mk374\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/0AvWV6Mk374/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> And say Promethean.</div> </div> </div> </div>After all the hours wasted on League, one could think I would have made the connection. Now I feel stupid.<br /> <br /> But yeah, Promethean is spot on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T13:21:46-08:00","id":846249,"title":"","content":"Ok, what do you all think about these:<br /> <br /> Spider-Man: Changeling or Deviant?<br /> Ghost Rider: Sin-Eater or Beast?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 03-12-2016, 10:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T18:50:26-08:00","id":846374,"title":"","content":"Deviant and Sin-Eater, respectively, going by their flavor text. Amusingly, I think Spider-Man works as a Beast, too; he uses arachnid-like powers while still being totally human in appearance, and feeds by bringing supernatural criminals to justice. The other superheroes are his kinship bonds, and see him as one of them, while Jameson is distrusts him because he can somehow get glimpses of his Horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T19:13:53-08:00","id":846378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WarDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=846374#post846374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deviant and Sin-Eater, respectively, going by their flavor text. Amusingly, I think Spider-Man works as a Beast, too; he uses arachnid-like powers while still being totally human in appearance, and feeds by bringing supernatural criminals to justice. The other superheroes are his kinship bonds, and see him as one of them, while Jameson is distrusts him because he can somehow get glimpses of his Horror.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hmmm... now that I think about it, Beast!Spidey sounds pretty cool. His super senses and agility, combined with his creative and non-lethal uses for the web-shooters make me think of him as Ugallu Nemesis, rather than Eshmaki. The latter Family is a lot more fitting for Venom, Carnage and other symbiote hosts. Venom can even fool the Spider-Sense, remember? You could also make a case for Namtaru, what with all those slimy and toothy bits. Venom is more of a Predator, while Carnage is a Ravager.<br /> <br /> But what would Beast!Spidey's Lair be like? A darker version of NY with lots of traps, spying spots and web cocoons that release muffled screams? (Those would be illusory, of course)<br /> <br /> Jameson might become a Hero. Wasn't there an old comic issue where he used a Doctor Octopus-like mech to fight Spidey?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, if you want to explain why people see actual webs instead of ropes or wire when Spidey uses his restraining Atavism, you could say he has a Merit tied to it. The Atavism becomes more visually obvious in exchange for a +1 or +2 bonus to the dice pool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 03-12-2016, 10:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T15:13:54-07:00","id":847888,"title":"","content":"How about <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Mask\" target=\"_blank\"><b>The Mask</b></a>? A True Fae's Prop that turns the wearer into a pseudo-Actor, including Immortal Flesh and Ruled By Passion? A Relic containing a Rank 5 mischief spirit that Claims the wearer, turning them into a Horror?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T16:11:04-07:00","id":847903,"title":"","content":"I thought the Mask was a Demon Gadget of some kind, that gave you the Deep Pockets Exploit. Maybe the Mask was designed to allow you to swap covers to anything you can imagine, but the Mask itself is a cover, so all compromise goes to it. Meaning that whilst you're wearing the Mask you will certainly be actively pursued by angels.<br /> <br /> as seen in Supernatural Loki is obviously a fallen angel","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":4046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","user":"xenoterracide","date":". 03-15-2016, 07:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T21:27:42-07:00","id":848001,"title":"","content":"Way too overt to be a Gadget. Probably more along the lines of &quot;Relic with Mischief Spirit,&quot; considering that &quot;Mass Create Mischief&quot; is probably about the best way you could describe Big Head's abilities, even moreso since &quot;bound spirit&quot; is literally the item's origin in the comic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T00:33:43-07:00","id":848034,"title":"","content":"This may not be a good theory given how I know little about Mummy, but could the Doctor be a Mummy who has achieved aptheosis? His TARDIS could be a potent relic, or even a form of a Mage from the future that is allowing others to direct its awesome powers.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, the Doctor and TARDIS are a Demon who has developed a mobile safehouse it is connected to, either creating a new cover from aspects of other people or, somehow, manufacturing them for himself. Demon I am likewise not too familiar with, so I could be off here. If nothing else, the Doctor is very advanced, even if by his own peoples' view he is behind the times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T10:31:50-07:00","id":848258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=848034#post848034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This may not be a good theory given how I know little about Mummy, but could the Doctor be a Mummy who has achieved aptheosis? His TARDIS could be a potent relic, or even a form of a Mage from the future that is allowing others to direct its awesome powers.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, the Doctor and TARDIS are a Demon who has developed a mobile safehouse it is connected to, either creating a new cover from aspects of other people or, somehow, manufacturing them for himself. Demon I am likewise not too familiar with, so I could be off here. If nothing else, the Doctor is very advanced, even if by his own peoples' view he is behind the times.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think the Doctor is probably one of three things:<br /> <br /> 1) A one-of-a-kind True Fae. He no longer participates in Feuds with other True Fae over Titles, so he isn't an Actor and the TARDIS is not a Realm. He is manifesting as his True Name, making him less powerful than the Gentry who still hold at least one Title. The TARDIS could be represented mechanically as an epic Mobile Hollow, but it is a thinking being that might not be completely fae. This version of the Doctor can't use Dream Warping, but he can build Hedgespun instead, such as the Sonic Screwdriver and K-9. He understands humans better than other True Fae, but doesn't have Clarity and can still be fickle and proud jerk.<br /> <br /> 2) A Demon, like you said. The TARDIS would be a Lares (i.e. Exiled Angel with a building as a Cover).<br /> <br /> 3) An Inspired Mane, as described in Genius: The Transgression. Gallifrey might be a Bardo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T10:59:07-07:00","id":848285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=848258#post848258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think the Doctor is probably one of three things:</div> </div> </div> </div>And do not forget and exAcanthus Free Council Archmaster. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T14:58:22-07:00","id":848431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=848285#post848285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And do not forget and exAcanthus Free Council Archmaster. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> I always had trouble imagining him as a Mage, yet alone an Archmage. His focus on technology does resonate with the Free Council, but Mages can do a whole lot with just improvised spellcasting. The Doctor would have high Gnosis and Wisdom, but few dots in Arcana. Any world-changing power he has is due to the TARDIS, which is above the scope of even an Artifact. It's more likely that the TARDIS is some Sanctum improved with Matter, Mind and Prime, as well as Imperial spells of Time and Space. It used to belong to an Archmage, but it became obsolete and the Doctor adopted it. He can't build TARDISes, remember? That's a Gallifreyan/Archmage feat.<br /> <br /> There's also the issue of Quiescence, Dissonance and Paradox. How does he protect his Companions and himself from all of that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 03-16-2016, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T15:34:48-07:00","id":848443,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Doctor would be a fledgling Mage, with some Knowing spells, stolen Artifact and really powerful permanent spell cast on him on charge system. His adventures and general themes *fit* Mage, but he is not a good example of Mage powers, other than really newbie spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T01:32:25-07:00","id":851023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=848443#post848443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Doctor would be a fledgling Mage, with some Knowing spells, stolen Artifact and really powerful permanent spell cast on him on charge system. His adventures and general themes *fit* Mage, but he is not a good example of Mage powers, other than really newbie spells.</div> </div> </div> </div> There are some exceptions, like when the Ninth Doctor slowed down time to pass through a whirling fan. It was in that episode where he takes Rose to the very distant future inside a spaceship where lots of different aliens were watching the Earth being engulfed by the Sun going supernova. <br /> <br /> There are also the many times the different Doctors use telepathy or another psychic power.<br /> <br /> By the way, I forgot to mention five things about Gentry!Doctor. His Regeneration is a modified version of Immortal Flesh, he is not Ruled By Passion (i.e. he gains willpower from Virtue and Vice like a mortal), he naturally doesn't have the limits on Expression, Empathy and Computers that other Gentry have, he has the Manifest Mien Condition that makes his two hearts perceptible through the Mask and he can't create Huntsmen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 03-22-2016, 04:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T16:05:04-07:00","id":852643,"title":"","content":"I was going to post a full write-up for Saitama from One Punch Man as a Horror with Potency 10, but the more I thought about it, the more I realized that was just plain unnecessary. Instead, I'll use the Brief Nightmare system, but he'll be a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/830824-silly-fun-time-i-am-the-mastah\"><b>Cheater</b></a> (or &quot;Arch-Cheater&quot;, rather) instead of a Horror.<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue: </b>Humble/Determined<br /> <b>Vice: </b>Ennui<br /> <br /> <b>Hack: </b>Punching 15<br /> <b>Best At: </b>Super-Heroics 25 (Increased by Hack)<br /> <b>Worst At: </b>2 (Being Proactive, Academic Pursuits, Not Looking Like A Stick Figure)<br /> <b>All Other Pools: </b>5 or 20 (If combined with Hack)<br /> <b>Aspirations: </b>Be A Hero For Fun, Do The Right Thing<br /> <b>Willpower/Scene:</b> 25 (Resolve 6 + Composure 4 + Hack)<br /> <b>Initiative: </b>15<br /> <b>Defense: </b>20<br /> <b>Speed: </b>Effectively Limitless<br /> <b>Size: </b>5<br /> <b>Health: </b>35<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 9<br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Punching [Counts as supernatural damage and forces lesser opponents to use Down &amp; Dirty Combat, 25 Dice with 8 Again, Bashing or Lethal]<br /> Serious Series [Special: See Below]<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers: </b><b><i>Colossus*</i></b>, <i><b>Hideous Strength*</b></i>, <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/278509-spooky-ghosts-and-nice-spirits-what-are-your-custom-numina\">Numen (Stutter Step)</a></b>, Prodigious Leap, Reality Stutter, Swift, Unbreakable, <b><i>Unnatural Healing*</i><br /> <br /> Colossus: </b>As per the Idigam version. Saitama gains a General Armor equal to his Best Dice Pool, counts his Size twice for his Health and his Punching receives 8 Again against lesser opponents. Should an opponent get 5+ Successes against Saitama, he receives the full damage, but reduces it by his General Armor. Should the opponent get 4 Successes or less, Saitama only receives one damage of the appropriate type due to being Unbreakable.<br /> <br /> <b>Hideous Strength:</b> By spending a point of Willpower, Saitama can increase his Strength by his Hack until the end of the scene. Furthermore, he adds his Hack as automatic successes on Strength + Stamina rolls made to perform a feat of strength, such as lifting a massive object or breaking free of restraints.<br /> <br /> <b>Unnatural Healing:</b> Saitama heals all bashing and lethal damage at the start of each turn. Downgrade a number of damage from any aggravated attack into lethal equal to his Best Dice Pool (this stacks with Colossal and Unbreakable), be the source mundane or supernatural.<br /> <br /> <i><u><b>Serious Series:</b></u></i> The stats above are for when Saitama isn't making any effort. When he does, he is considered to have a Supernal Scaling (Mage Chronicler's Guide, page 218). That is, add 16 dice to his Best Dice Pool for a total of 41 with 8 Again. Take the total amount of Successes and multiply them by whatever arbitrarily gigantic number you want, and go full anime with your descriptions of the ensuing destruction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 05-24-2017, 11:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T10:12:47-07:00","id":853547,"title":"","content":"Ok, serious question: would the Doctor work as an antagonist in a Demon game? Not necessarily out to harm anyone, mind you. I mean something closer to a mobile natural disaster that you have to contain somehow. He mostly uses Lares!TARDIS to go on adventures, and even then he causes a lot of collateral damage. What if he had goals in mind for his Hell and made little effort to clean up his temporal messes? You'd have Demons and Angels alike trying to predict his next appearance and sabotage his plans, perhaps stealing the TARDIS and/or sending him to be reprogrammed into an Angel (or more likely just recycled). <br /> <br /> Some of the beings that look for the Doctor could be time-traveling Angels, outer space Cryptids and weirder things still, like Bardos, free-roaming Idigam and Supernal/Abyssal Verges. This more proactive but ruthless Doctor would have good reason to keep hidden and on the move. Heck, you might need a multi-splat team of experts in wibbly-wobbly matters to track him down, and that's without going into all the contingencies and backup plans he definitely has. All the while trying not to make the time-line worse, and being tempted to explore.<br /> <br /> Does that sound fun?<br /> <br /> By the way, did anyone else think of the Cybermen when they saw the Dalga in GMC? As for the Daleks, I don't think they are Angels, or even created by the G-M. Maintaining the status quo is obviously not compatible with the extinction of all non-Daleks.<br /> <br /> EDIT: On second thought, I was probably thinking of the Master. I still think it would be interesting to tell the story from the point of view of those who are caught in the Doctor's mishaps and try to stop him from causing more trouble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 03-26-2016, 01:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T14:37:48-07:00","id":853684,"title":"","content":"Holy God-Machine, it just occured to me!<br /> The House of Black and White from Game of Thrones/A Song of Ice and Fire are a group of (Legion) mages!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T13:14:17-07:00","id":854179,"title":"","content":"How would you port five prodigies of Kiseki no Sedai from Kuroko no Basket?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T19:05:35-07:00","id":854803,"title":"","content":"I've been thinking of ways to port GARO.<br /> <br /> For those who aren't familiar with the series, it centers around an order of magic using knights hunting down demons and the possessed in a modern day setting.<br /> <br /> My first and most obvious idea is would be that the Makai Knights are a Hunter Conspiracy, focusing on dealing with spirits and the claimed.<br /> <br /> Let's see what other ways it could be done...<br /> <br /> A Werewolf lodge might work. There <i>is</i> a distinct wolf theme to the Makai Knights, most prominently in the design of their armor. Which combined with their focus on banishing demons, killing the possessed, and sealing gates to the demon realm, lends itself rather well to a Werewolf adaption.<br /> <br /> Mage could also work? The magic most of the characters use is very dependent on items and rituals, but the movies and second season had a more Mage-like vibe to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":2598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","user":"Gryphon's Feather","date":". 02-19-2017, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T22:56:18-07:00","id":858172,"title":"","content":"The Autobots might be a Ring of Integrators/Saboteurs who fight against a rival militant Ring known as the Decepticons. The Autobots want to fix the God-Machine so It can be directed toward protecting the freedom of all sentient beings, instead of only using them as resources in plans that don't go anywhere. Optimus Prime would be a Guardian. The vehicle forms could be special Covers that are upgraded with Gadgets and the Demon Car Exploit.<br /> <br /> By the way, the Powerpuff Girls? They're totally Deviants. They were created because of an accident in a scientific experiment, they only have a few powers that can be amplified to extremely devastating levels, they fight bizarre monsters routinely and they struggle to get along with normal people. If you watch their movie, you might see tones of an Innocents Deviant game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-03-2016, 02:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T23:21:38-07:00","id":858183,"title":"","content":"Talking about the Doctor, I really do think he fits as a Mage...however I know we are talking New World of Darkness here but the Doctor almost fits OLD World of Darkness mage, specifically Technocracy, a little bit to well. Remember the Time Lords 'Removed Magic from the World' at the daawn of creation. They imposed linear time on the universe. The Time Lords being oWoD Mage's could definitely work. Not sure what KIND of mage he would be in there but....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11535-furoan","name":"Furoan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T00:01:26-07:00","id":858192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=846249#post846249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, what do you all think about these:<br /> <br /> <br /> Ghost Rider: Sin-Eater or Beast?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghost Rider is a Baykosh or a sin eater <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T00:43:19-07:00","id":858200,"title":"","content":"Do you think the shadow might be a Mage, Demon or a Kindred maybe. <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://static2.comicvine.com/uploads/original/1/15776/2598390-shadow1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T01:07:31-07:00","id":858208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=858200#post858200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think the shadow might be a Mage, Demon or a Kindred maybe.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://static2.comicvine.com/uploads/original/1/15776/2598390-shadow1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd peg him as a Vampire myself. I have a guy in my Vampire chronicle based slightly on him. A hunter from WW2 that was turned and faked his death. He found his way to the States after the war where he continued his hunting from the shadows using his sprinkling of Dominate and Vigor to fight crime.<br /> <br /> Used his background from the comics/radio dramas as a starter. His power of &quot;to cloud men's minds&quot; pegged me as Dominate to me. Plus the later information begs Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/213-darkhunter","name":"Darkhunter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar213_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T14:09:10-07:00","id":858515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=858192#post858192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ghost Rider is a Baykosh or a sin eater<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Which splat are the Baykosh from? Also, could you please put images like that inside a spoiler next time? I was startled. You create a spoiler box by typing [&quot;SPOILER&quot;]yourimagehere[&quot;/SPOILER&quot;], but without the quote marks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T15:02:07-07:00","id":858545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=858515#post858515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which splat are the Baykosh from?</div> </div> </div> </div>Night Horrors: Wicked Dead. It's a particularly ancient ghost who goes after people who've survived places of violence unharmed and tears out their organs and the time they thought they still had. Notably looks like a modern Grim Reaper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T21:46:33-07:00","id":858766,"title":"","content":"Do you think max payne would be a hunter. I mean he does have the whole bullet time thing. So maybe a demon ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T21:51:18-07:00","id":858770,"title":"","content":"Not sure if this was tackled yet, but here goes...<br /> <br /> Sans the Skeleton from Undertale.<br /> <br /> The closest I can actually imagine him being would be as a Changeling with the Dual Kith Merit. What his kiths could be, though, would be the tricky part. So far, I'd mention Oracle (to reflect his knowledge of multiple timelines), Maker (to reflect his possible scientific background), and Weisse Frau (to reflect his telekinetic attacks when he's fought as a boss).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T22:20:55-07:00","id":858778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=858770#post858770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if this was tackled yet, but here goes...<br /> <br /> Sans the Skeleton from Undertale.<br /> <br /> The closest I can actually imagine him being would be as a Changeling with the Dual Kith Merit. What his kiths could be, though, would be the tricky part. So far, I'd mention Oracle (to reflect his knowledge of multiple timelines), Maker (to reflect his possible scientific background), and Weisse Frau (to reflect his telekinetic attacks when he's fought as a boss).</div> </div> </div> </div> If he's a Changeling, he doesn't need the Oracle, Maker or Weisse Frau Kiths. Instead, he'd have high Clarity, be skilled with Talecrafting, use some Contracts of Hours and Omen, and have Merits that improve Hedgespinning. His Kith would be Palewraith, perhaps with Trickster as a secondary Kith. His Seeming is probably Darkling. The telekinesis might be a Goblin Vow or Goblin Contract. The Gaster Blasters could be powerful Tokens he crafted himself (or he might have copied the blueprints/stolen them from Gaster).<br /> <br /> I personally see him as a Sin-Eater, with Gaster as his Geist. Same goes for Papyrus, but who his Geist would be is up for debate. Maybe it would be River Person (who is Gaster's wife in a certain &quot;ask the characters&quot; video series).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-04-2016, 01:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T00:47:23-07:00","id":858817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=858778#post858778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If he's a Changeling, he doesn't need the Oracle, Maker or Weisse Frau Kiths. Instead, he'd have high Clarity, be skilled with Talecrafting, use some Contracts of Hours and Omen, and have Merits that improve Hedgespinning. His Kith would be Palewraith, perhaps with Trickster as a secondary Kith. His Seeming is probably Darkling. The telekinesis might be a Goblin Vow or Goblin Contract. The Gaster Blasters could be powerful Tokens he crafted himself (or he might have copied the blueprints/stolen them from Gaster).<br /> <br /> I personally see him as a Sin-Eater, with Gaster as his Geist. Same goes for Papyrus, but who his Geist would be is up for debate. Maybe it would be River Person (who is Gaster's wife in a certain &amp;quot;ask the characters&amp;quot; video series).</div> </div> </div> </div>Trickster kith? Or did you mean Coyote? That said, I fail to see how Palewraith works for a Changeling interpretation of Sans. On a related note, Weisse Frau might be a good fit when you consider his friendship with Frisk (in a pacifist run). Everything else, though, makes sense. Though I'd have to wait on the stuff for Talecrafting and Tokens, and and any Merits related to Hedgespinning to see if they <i>are</i> applicable.<br /> <br /> On a related note, how about Papyrus? I can see him being a Ridleseeker and/or Slewfoot, with Fairest as his Seeming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T04:30:48-07:00","id":858882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=858817#post858817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Trickster kith? Or did you mean Coyote? That said, I fail to see how Palewraith works for a Changeling interpretation of Sans. On a related note, Weisse Frau might be a good fit when you consider his friendship with Frisk (in a pacifist run). Everything else, though, makes sense. Though I'd have to wait on the stuff for Talecrafting and Tokens, and and any Merits related to Hedgespinning to see if they <i>are</i> applicable.<br /> <br /> On a related note, how about Papyrus? I can see him being a Ridleseeker and/or Slewfoot, with Fairest as his Seeming.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh yeah, I meant Coyote. I say Palewraith to represent how he sneaks up on Frisk in his first scene. His sprite is all black, and you might think he's going to be a scary guy, but then he shakes your hand with a whopee cushion. He also teleports, which the Palewraith Kith can mimic by letting you move very quietly while others are distracted. This can end up looking like teleportation. His shortcuts could also be Trods.<br /> <br /> Papyrus would probably have an easier time joining the Royal Guard if he was a Fairest. He's a very cheerful and encouraging person, no doubt. But he is rather single-minded about defending the Underground. He fancies himself a puzzlemaster and an expert chef, but doesn't really excel at either. However, even Undyne admits he is an excellent fighter. I'd say this passion for a specific craft and perfectionalism make him a Wizened Soldier. He might have Truefriend as a second Kith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T04:36:25-07:00","id":858884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=858882#post858882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Oh yeah, I meant Coyote. I say Palewraith to represent how he sneaks up on Frisk in his first scene. His sprite is all black, and you might think he's going to be a scary guy, but then he shakes your hand with a whopee cushion. He also teleports, which the Palewraith Kith can mimic by letting you move very quietly while others are distracted. This can end up looking like teleportation. His shortcuts could also be Trods.<br /> <br /> Papyrus would probably have an easier time joining the Royal Guard if he was a Fairest. He's a very cheerful and encouraging person, no doubt. But he is rather single-minded about defending the Underground. He fancies himself a puzzlemaster and an expert chef, but doesn't really excel at either. However, even Undyne admits he is an excellent fighter. I'd say this passion for a specific craft and perfectionalism make him a Wizened Soldier. He might have Truefriend as a second Kith.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can just as easily see him pulling that off with a few Contracts. Like the 2E ones for Darkness and Smoke. His speed/teleportation can similarly be emulated by a Contract (Universal or Goblin?), as can his ability to create boneyards for impaling any unfortunate foes.<br /> <br /> Papyrus as a Wizened Soldier/Truefriend is oddly appropriate. And for some reason, I can see him with a two-handed sword based on a game over fanart I saw online.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T20:14:53-07:00","id":859420,"title":"","content":"I was reading the comic Mercy Sparx and got to wondering what how could you