Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=860813#post860813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hmmm what if she is from one court that made a home in an unknown part of the hedge or something and another court wants to collect court runaways. I don't really know that much about changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div> I thought Courts were supposed to help you <i> not</i> get kidnapped again. Sending someone like her to deal with dissidents is just asking to lose members at the very least. It's probably easier to just make her a Loyalist, like I said. She doesn't seem to be on quite the same level as a Huntsman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T00:34:14-07:00","id":860846,"title":"","content":"You know what would be interesting. If Mercy is a changeling but is wrapped up in the heaven and hell thing because she is the daughter of fallen angel (Demon from demon the decent.) The god machine has her tracking down and collecting run away angels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T00:48:30-07:00","id":860849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=860846#post860846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know what would be interesting. If Mercy is a changeling but is wrapped up in the heaven and hell thing because she is the daughter of fallen angel (Demon from demon the decent.) The god machine has her tracking down and collecting run away angels.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't know if a changeling would be the most efficient for that. Why not make it simple and hire an Integrator who really doesn't like other Demons? There's nothing outright preventing you from having a more &quot;pitchfork and pointy tail&quot; sort of Demonic Form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T13:26:09-07:00","id":861253,"title":"","content":"I started watching FOX's <i>Lucifer</i>. Four episodes in and I'm convinced that he's a social Tyrant Anakim. Lux, his night club, is tied to one of his Chambers, his Heart is a Dante-esque Hell, Maze is another Begotten (or perhaps a Spirit of Lust or Violence or something). Detective Decker is actually a Hero: it's why Luci's stuff doesn't work on her and when she shoots him he actually bleeds (because he's got Advanced and Epic Iron Skin, naturally).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T19:45:58-07:00","id":861544,"title":"","content":"<b><a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-2845\" target=\"_blank\"> SCP-2845 (AKA The Stag)</a></b> is an Idigam of Rank 6 or 7. Alternatively, an Alien of the Strange Spheres with the same Rank.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T01:07:52-07:00","id":861676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=861253#post861253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I started watching FOX's <i>Lucifer</i>. Four episodes in and I'm convinced that he's a social Tyrant Anakim. Lux, his night club, is tied to one of his Chambers, his Heart is a Dante-esque Hell, Maze is another Begotten (or perhaps a Spirit of Lust or Violence or something). Detective Decker is actually a Hero: it's why Luci's stuff doesn't work on her and when she shoots him he actually bleeds (because he's got Advanced and Epic Iron Skin, naturally).</div> </div> </div> </div>Decker is too close to him to be Hero - they would, literally, eat one or another. I much more went with Lucifer as Mastigos - Dissonance on Supernal Magic also answer why everyone <i>cannot</i> believe him that he is more than human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T06:33:03-07:00","id":861786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=861544#post861544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-2845\" target=\"_blank\"> SCP-2845 (AKA The Stag)</a></b> is an Idigam of Rank 6 or 7. Alternatively, an Alien of the Strange Spheres with the same Rank.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, when I read it, my first thought was Fae, or Huntsman, particularly with the message from the containment consutlent:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">...Rituals do not work because of some underlying laws, such as those that science operates on. Rituals work because they are rituals. They work because an arbitrary set of criteria has been met with exacting care. Belief that meeting these arbitrary criteria achieves a certain end assigns power to the ritual. The actions that were once meaningless now have been assigned Meaning through their repetition and application.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">This is how one seals away a god, and this is a god. I know that the Foundation does not approve of using the term, but it is still the case. The Stag is a god, and it is not a petty local god. It is not one of the mild gods of Earth, or some weaker spirit that is bound by the strength of man\u2019s belief.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">We have, for the time being, fooled it into thinking that we have overpowered it. It does not understand that we do so falsely: it is a god. For gods, words have Power. Ritual and belief hold greater power over a god than all the laws of science.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">However, it must be kept in mind that the Stag could escape, right now, if it so chose. With a thought, this entire facility could turn into a puff of hydrogen. If at any point the Stag thought to escape, it would, and we would be powerless to stop it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">However, it will not think to escape, or even to change its strategy. The idea will not even pass through its mind. It cannot comprehend the concept. It does not think in the way we think. Truth be told, I would not say that it thinks at all. This is an old god, it does not dabble in decisions. Decisions are for creatures who may act erratically, variably, or out of line. A god of this strength simply Is. It is an absolute. It acts as a force. In building this ritual, we have shifted its being the slightest bit, and now it is locked into a pattern of behavior: it struggles against us, we struggle against it, and we are locked together in an eternal dance so long as the ritual remains intact....</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Then again, it did come from a comet, so maybe Idigam is a better option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","user":"AceOfAlmonds","date":". 04-08-2016, 09:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T06:51:01-07:00","id":861794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=861676#post861676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Decker is too close to him to be Hero - they would, literally, eat one or another. I much more went with Lucifer as Mastigos - Dissonance on Supernal Magic also answer why everyone <i>cannot</i> believe him that he is more than human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mastigos works fine as well, but there's a dearth of good Beast-ly characters on TV so I saw it as an opportunity.<br /> <br /> Heroes and Beasts don't have to have an antagonistic relationship. And people not believing he's literally the devil can be explained as mortals' tendencies to rationalize weirdness away (&quot;Is that your stage name or something?&quot;) and the fact that he's in <i>L.A.</i>I've never lived there, but the Hollywood version of L.A. seems like they'd just assume he's an eccentric (read: insane) rich dude with delusions. Remember that &quot;Preacher&quot; who it turned out was just a street performer?<br /> <br /> I was reading Beast whilst watching it and his methods struck me as Beast-like. He looks human, we only catch glimpses of his Horror when he's doing something obviously supernatural (or he uses <i>Behold, My True Form!</i> on people), and he Hungers for Punishment (and Justice). The first time I made the connection though was when he arranged an ironic punishment for the paparazzi. He didn't do anything overly supernatural like throw them into personal hells, he just gave them both guns and told them about their transgressions against each other and <i>waited</i>. That struck me as Beast-like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T12:35:56-07:00","id":862084,"title":"","content":"Hmmmm, Simon or Kamina as a Demon and Gurren Lagann as their demonic form? There's even a propulsion that gives your demonic form drills all over its body!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T14:12:45-07:00","id":862181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=861786#post861786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, when I read it, my first thought was Fae, or Huntsman, particularly with the message from the containment consutlent.<br /> <br /> Then again, it did come from a comet, so maybe Idigam is a better option.</div> </div> </div> </div> Wouldn't you know it, I quoted that very message in a thread where someone was insisting on applying the scientific method to cold iron and True Fae. <br /> <br /> I might have considered the Stag as a Pangaean, if it wasn't made explicit that It is from another world/realm. I have spoken with the author of that article, and they said that the Saturn/Kronos imagery is not directly related to the rise of Greek Mythology and the Titanomachy therein. They have also said that the phrase &quot;TOWERING KADATH, MY HOME&quot; was thrown in for kicks, but can be directed toward crossover with the Cthulhu Mythos and CoD if you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T17:44:55-07:00","id":862304,"title":"","content":"I don't know if it's been mentioned, but I'm thinking the Beast from Over the Garden Wall is either an Anakim (He's basically despair incarnate) Tyrant, or some kind of dual-Kith Woodblood/Brollachan Gentry, based on his ties to fear and being made of wood.<br /> <br /> Wirt and Greg would have ended up becoming Woodbloods themselves had they failed to escape when they did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T20:13:21-07:00","id":862978,"title":"","content":"Does anyone else see the lore of the God-Emperor Of Mankind from Warhammer 40000 as an awesome inspiration for Archmages? He would definitely be an ex-Obrimos Bodhisattva, with Gnosis 10. His main Arcana and Imperial Practices would be Life (for creating the genetic blueprints of the Primarchs and the following Space Marine Chapters), Mind &amp; Spirit (for dealing with the Warp and the Chaos Gods) and Prime &amp; Forces (to help unite Mankind and for assorted psyker powers). The grimdarkness is a result of the worst sort of Aponoia and Hubris.<br /> <br /> He is also featured in <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLyiDf91_bTEgnBN0jAvzNbqzrlMGID5WA\" target=\"_blank\"><b>a series of videos where he gets a text-to-speech device installed on his Golden Throne so he can deliver witty commentary about the sorry state of the Imperium and try to fix it.</b></a> It's freaking hilarious and faithful to the source material to boot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T02:00:45-07:00","id":863080,"title":"","content":"Do you think any of the splats would fit the 4 horsemen of the apocalypse ?<br /> <br /> what do you think there stats would be. Maybe there just very powerful spirits ?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/736x/92/83/e2/9283e2aa40e2bb5d2354485b267122cc.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T03:05:48-07:00","id":863091,"title":"","content":"Deathlords, man. I mean the Horsemen are *already* Deathlords in Geist mythology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T10:18:30-07:00","id":863211,"title":"","content":"Spirits of Death, Famine, Conflict, Pestilence, I could see the fifth Horseman being a Deathlord, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-10-2016, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T22:02:15-07:00","id":863488,"title":"","content":"While re-watching <b>Gregory Horror Show</b>, I thought it would be a pretty good fit for Changeling, with Gregory House as an Arcadian realm.<br /> <br /> It's a fairly obscure series, so I'll provide a <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?list=PL7F3FFAB27C6EAC08&amp;v=VJJHtAXywk8&amp;ebc=ANyPxKqlLfz2RGuPxz9Nmov4_ASnJ_QPLinenS0ctcrkl-wSuv731QqT4uas5S9wpUP835MuYgEZ&amp;nohtml5=False\" target=\"_blank\">Link</a>, and a short description too.<br /> <br /> The narrator, who's point of view we see from, gets lost in the woods, eventually arriving at the &quot;Gregory House&quot;, a hotel full of strange people with unnatural characteristics. Nobody is as they appear, with most guests taking the form of animals or objects, and typically obsessed with one particular topic. As the narrator stays at the hotel, they gradually break down, losing track of their memory, their sanity, and even pieces of their identity.<br /> <br /> Will they be able to escape in time?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T20:51:21-07:00","id":865303,"title":"","content":"Which of the 2ED Seemings do you think are the most fitting for Batman and the Joker?<br /> <br /> The former sounds like a Wizened. He feels broken by his origin, and attempts to fix himself by becoming one of the greatest detectives of all time. His gadgets could be imitated with 2ED Contracts of Artifice, which was an Affinity Contract for the Wizened in 1ED. Also, the Wizened Blessing negates environmental and circumstantial penalties to the Wizened's chosen craft, which is similar to how he is not affected by fear. As for Kiths, I'd say he is a Slewfoot + Brollachan, for Greatest Detective and I Am The Night, respectively. Instead of having Windwing as his third Kith, he glides with a Token that sprouts mechanical wings attached to his back. As for Contracts, he'd have 2ED versions of Darkness, Smoke, Oath And Punishment, Stone and the aforementioned Artifice.<br /> <br /> The Joker is harder to pin down, naturally. He describes himself as an Agent Of Chaos in &quot;The Dark Knight&quot;, and he tries to prove how close everyone is to his madness in &quot;The Killing Joke&quot;. He almost never explains anything about himself, to the point of preferring a multiple choice past. He loves to rip apart the bonds and rules that people think they can trust, and he has an artistic bent in what he does. And worst of all, he is highly persuasive. All of this makes me think he is a messed up Elemental Muse + Whisperwisp + Maker. Because of this, he has a much higher Wyrd than Batman. His lethal prank items would be Tokens that he summons with the Discrete Conjuration and Hidden Reality Contracts, rather than the Blessings of the Razorhand and Venombite Kiths. His Clarity is up for debate, and also depends on which version you're using as a base.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T03:57:42-07:00","id":865401,"title":"","content":"Genn Graymane: Urthra clan leader that saw most of his people killed by a group of Vampires/Undead just so they could take their territory. (The Undead were Probably corrupted by some spirit or another). Now leads the Remnants of his Wolf-Blooded and Urthra in attacks against the Undead.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T06:58:14-07:00","id":865481,"title":"","content":"I could also see Batman as a Beast, what with his use of Fear as a weapon/tool. (Not knowledgeable of Beast, so no idea what Family/Hunger)<br /> <br /> Which would make his rogues gallery &quot;Heroes&quot;, in an amusing reversal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T07:56:40-07:00","id":865502,"title":"","content":"Depending on what aspects you focus on, Anakim, Eshmaki, and Ugallu are all potential Families; in the end, he's a Nemesis through and through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T12:16:01-07:00","id":865646,"title":"","content":"A one-off conversation with a friend recently got me thinking of Valkyrie Profile characters, and what they'd be in various settings. While I find the games as a whole are a better fit for Exalted, I'd still like to figure out what a Lenneth and Wylfred would be in the WoD, if there's even a fit to begin with, if there is one?<br /> <br /> My current ideas would be Wylfred as a Sin-Eater, rose from the dead after negotiating with an underworld denizen, derives powerful abilities from mementos taken off dead family members and allies.<br /> <br /> And Lenneth would be, I don't know, Death-Heavy Orbrimos Adamantine, maybe? Commands ghosts, hunts immortals and others who go against fate, general angelic motif. Maybe there isn't a way to do this, or there's an obvious one and I'm not seeing it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":2598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","user":"Gryphon's Feather","date":". 04-14-2016, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T16:06:32-07:00","id":865735,"title":"","content":"How about <b><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ImxnwjBsUHU&#91;B\" target=\"_blank\">Danny Phantom</a></b> and <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XaXEo1CiCds\" target=\"_blank\"><b>XJ-9</b></a>? The former has no apparent Geist, so he's probably not a Sin-Eater. The latter is closer to an Automata Wonder in terms of powers, but she goes through the same sort of troubles that an Unfleshed Promethean would face in the Pilgrimage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T16:16:07-07:00","id":865738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=865735#post865735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about <b><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ImxnwjBsUHU&#91;B\" target=\"_blank\">Danny Phantom</a></b> and <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XaXEo1CiCds\" target=\"_blank\"><b>XJ-9</b></a>? The former has no apparent Geist, so he's probably not a Sin-Eater. The latter is closer to an Automata Wonder in terms of powers, but she goes through the same sort of troubles that an Unfleshed Promethean would face in the Pilgrimage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Danny Phantom is closer to err... an <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/TabletopGame/Orpheus\" target=\"_blank\">Orpheus</a> Operative. Although that's OWoD..... Likely a Conspiracy of Hunters in this version of the world.<br /> XJ-9 well.. never seen it but I'd say Unfleshed Promethean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T16:26:38-07:00","id":865745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=865735#post865735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about <b><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ImxnwjBsUHU&#91;B\" target=\"_blank\">Danny Phantom</a></b> and <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XaXEo1CiCds\" target=\"_blank\"><b>XJ-9</b></a>? The former has no apparent Geist, so he's probably not a Sin-Eater. The latter is closer to an Automata Wonder in terms of powers, but she goes through the same sort of troubles that an Unfleshed Promethean would face in the Pilgrimage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Danny is his own Geist. The Ghost Zone Portal blew out a chunk of his soul (much like a Mage creating a Soulstone) which manifested as a ghost that possessed him. Its tenuous grip on ephemeral reality is a result of this, and is also why his powers develop spottily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T16:54:36-07:00","id":865755,"title":"","content":"The phantom from ace attorney 5 dual destines is obviously an integrator demon sabotaging Japan's space program for the GM, what with the whole master of disguise/ living in cover to the point he forgot his real identity bit.<br /> <br /> Also, XJ-9 is definitely an unfleshed Promethean, albeit one with a unusually good relationship with her demiurge. The Cluster are obviously an army of Unfleshed Centimani who seek to either defeat or corrupt her.<br /> <br /> Of course, if we're doing Nickelodeon shows, then one must ask... exactly what kind of changelings Cosmo and Wanda are?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 04-14-2016, 08:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T17:11:19-07:00","id":865759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=865745#post865745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Danny is his own Geist. The Ghost Zone Portal blew out a chunk of his soul (much like a Mage creating a Soulstone) which manifested as a ghost that possessed him. Its tenuous grip on ephemeral reality is a result of this, and is also why his powers develop spottily.</div> </div> </div> </div> Threshold wise, he's probably of the Forgotten, considering how it was an accident. <br /> <br /> Now Vlad, Vlad is more easily resolved. He's Stricken, slowly dying over the course of five years, and a villainous Bonepicker aside. Plasmius would probably be his Geist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T20:39:24-07:00","id":865789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=865755#post865755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The phantom from ace attorney 5 dual destines is obviously an integrator demon sabotaging Japan's space program for the GM, what with the whole master of disguise/ living in cover to the point he forgot his real identity bit.<br /> <br /> Also, XJ-9 is definitely an unfleshed Promethean, albeit one with a unusually good relationship with her demiurge. The Cluster are obviously an army of Unfleshed Centimani who seek to either defeat or corrupt her.<br /> <br /> Of course, if we're doing Nickelodeon shows, then one must ask... exactly what kind of changelings Cosmo and Wanda are?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not changelings. Fairy World is an astral realm that Timmy, an unwitting powerful psychic, was able to access. Cosmo and Wanda are Geotics representing his childishness and responsibility, respectively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T06:29:34-07:00","id":865919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-