path.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T22:31:00-07:00","id":868193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=868181#post868181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gandalf is good Wisdom 10.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ah, well remembered. The 2ED rules for Supernal entities haven't been spoiled, but he is similar to one. He spends a lot more time in Middle Earth than Supernal entities can normally spend in the Fallen World, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-19-2016, 01:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T22:43:11-07:00","id":868198,"title":"","content":"I also guess that Dumbledore is close to Wisdom 10, not due to him being very nice, but due to his almost villainous carefulness patience and planning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T08:31:50-07:00","id":868456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=868154#post868154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> These images look more like Wisdom 5 or 6 to me. I don't know any Green Lanterns that work like the Mad.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's some extreme examples of mass murder and 'creating a constructs that everyone on Earth can see and be affected by,' not to mention the hundreds, if not thousands, of examples of inflicting pain directly with them. They are showy, loud, use their powers to fulfill the slightest whim. The Black and, arguably a couple other rings actually do the equivalent of stealing souls, and of course they've basically sold their souls on a number of occasions. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://i172.photobucket.com/albums/w17/guy222_photos/DestroysUniverse2.jpg~original\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even if these examples of Wisdom 10 are obscure, I'd like to hear them, please. </div> </div> </div>The first two are from the same source, the High and Spartan, who turns to Jack Marlowe. After a period of doing 'superhero' stuff, the High spends decades sitting and thinking about the perfect way to solve the root of the problem rather than work on band-aids, and in the end for the most part abandons his powers in favor of diplomacy and focus. Jack Marlowe did the same, deciding that being a superhero was not solving anything and instead decided to use his money to assist the lives of others. He used his powers but far more subtly and in a more introspective way, I suppose in Awakening you could say he found a Supernal verge and used it to gain unlimited energy, which he then offered to the masses at an incredibly reasonable fee. In the end he decided that sometimes being Bruce Wayne isn't enough so he had to go Batman.<br /> <br /> I had just thought of another one last night. Silent, from the Black Company series. While the Company itself has two loud sorcerers who often pull pranks on one another with their magics, Silent stays out of it for the most part, very sparsely using his magic and seemingly for the most part using it for divination purposes, except at a few memorable scenes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-19-2016, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T19:34:27-07:00","id":874196,"title":"","content":"Sterling Archer of <i>Archer</i> is some kind of Offspring, probably with the Lucky Break, Deafen (God-damned tinnitus), and some other Embeds. Malory is a particularly abusive Tempter Integrator.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T20:02:47-07:00","id":874213,"title":"","content":"The Xiaolin Warriors from Xiaolin Showdown are Proximi with power over the four classic elements. They are members of the Adamantine Arrow who specialize in the retrieval of Artifacts. The titular Showdown involves the super-imposition of an Astral Realm over the immediate reality, similarly to the Lair of a Beast. Jack Spicer is a Genius and Wuya is a Ghost Mage. I am unsure of what Chase Young would be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T09:30:24-07:00","id":874609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=867664#post867664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone know any characters (not necessarily wizards) who could be examples of Wisdom 10 and 0?</div> </div> </div> </div>Voldemort would probably be a good fit for 0. Saruman after betraying Gandalf and creating the Uruk Hai might also be as well. It really depends on just how unforgiving the Wisdom system turns out to be. Gandalf the White might be a 10.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1881-the-cowardly-scion","name":"The Cowardly Scion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1881_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T09:35:53-07:00","id":874613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=867664#post867664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone know any characters (not necessarily wizards) who could be examples of Wisdom 10 and 0?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Wisdom is mostly the restraint of power, right? I think the Unseen University might count - their whole purpose is to teach wizards(mages) how to <i>not</i> use magic, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T19:11:40-07:00","id":875116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=874213#post874213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Xiaolin Warriors from Xiaolin Showdown are Proximi with power over the four classic elements. They are members of the Adamantine Arrow who specialize in the retrieval of Artifacts. The titular Showdown involves the super-imposition of an Astral Realm over the immediate reality, similarly to the Lair of a Beast. Jack Spicer is a Genius and Wuya is a Ghost Mage. I am unsure of what Chase Young would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>He could be a Dragon shifter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/213-darkhunter","name":"Darkhunter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar213_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T20:00:45-07:00","id":875168,"title":"","content":"Haven't seen the whole series, but Jin from World Trigger always looked like really high Wisdom Acanthus.<br /> <br /> Evil Ryu and Akuma from Street Fighter franchise are interesting cases for Wisdom system, because while both are clearly Left-Handed murder machines, Akuma has that certain...tranquility and control in his Rage (high Wisdom, paradoxically), while Ryu is just all like MURDER KILL ROAR while, well, Evil.<br /> <br /> Yoda is definitely Wisdom 10.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 04-26-2016, 11:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T15:22:16-07:00","id":878162,"title":"","content":"The <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Endless_(comics)\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Endless</b></a> are quite similar to the Aeons, since they <i>are</i> broad and wide-reaching concepts, rather than Royal Avatars or something like that. They can be &quot;replaced&quot; in truly exceptional circumstances as well, like the Aeons.<br /> <br /> The <a href=\"http://marvel.wikia.com/wiki/Living_Tribunal_(Multiverse)\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Living Tribunal</b></a> sounds like a Supernal entity of extremely high Rank above even the Aeons. It would have Rank 9, while the One-Above-All would be Rank 10, possibly residing in/being the source of the Empyrean and thus all of the Supernal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T15:35:21-07:00","id":878178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=858766#post858766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think max payne would be a hunter. I mean he does have the whole bullet time thing. So maybe a demon ?</div> </div> </div> </div> I know this answer is late, but you don't need to be a Demon to have Embeds. You can be a Stigmatic, Demon-Blooded or Nephilim. Alternatively, you can use a Gadget and Supernatural Merits. You can also have a non-supernatural bullet time through Trained Observer 3 + Advanced Fast Reflexes + Firearms Skill Tricks from Mirrors.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T16:07:46-07:00","id":878200,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i>SCP-106, AKA The Old Man</i></span><br /> <br /> Best At (10 Dice): </b>Stalking, Hurting And Tormenting Prey<br /> <b>Worst At (2 Dice): </b>Reacting To Surprise, Long-Term Memory, Understanding Anything Besides Fear<br /> <b>All Other Pools: </b>5<br /> <b>Aspirations: </b>Spread Fear, Suffering And Death<br /> <b>Willpower/Scene:</b> 6<br /> <b>Initiative: </b>7<br /> <b>Defense: </b>5<br /> <b>Speed: </b>8<br /> <b>Size: </b>5<br /> <b>Health: </b>12<br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Claws, Fangs And Other Rotting Protrusions [10 Dice, +1L With Armor Piercing 1]<br /> <br /> <b>Ban:</b> Must retreat into the Pocket Realm temporarily if exposed to sudden and very intense lights<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers: </b>Hunter\u2019s Senses (Humans), Immortal, Jump Scare, Natural Weaponry 1, Numen (Pocket Realm*), Regenerate 2, Surprise Entrance, Toxic 2 (Poisoned), Unbreakable, Wall-Climb, Vanish<br /> <br /> <i><b>*Pocket Realm:</b></i> If SCP-106 sneaks up on or cripples a target, it will usually attempt to drag them into a plane of existence where it will prolong their suffering and fear as a game. SCP-106 is considered to have 5 dots in the Safe Place Merit, and Influence 5 (Pocket Realm Environment). While within the Pocket Realm, he also has Gremlin, Home Ground, Eye Spy, Numen (Hallucination, Heal), Madness And Terror and Maze. These stack with the other Dread Powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 07-10-2017, 08:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T16:32:40-07:00","id":878224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=878162#post878162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Endless_(comics)\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Endless</b></a> are quite similar to the Aeons, since they <i>are</i> broad and wide-reaching concepts, rather than Royal Avatars or something like that. They can be &quot;replaced&quot; in truly exceptional circumstances as well, like the Aeons.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are also Dual-Natured... Death is about Life, Destruction is about Creation, Delirium is about Sanity (I Believe... it's been awhile), Despair is about Hope, Destiny is about Free will.... I'm abit of a Fanboy for them.... :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T17:01:12-07:00","id":878244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=878224#post878224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They are also Dual-Natured... Death is about Life, Destruction is about Creation, Delirium is about Sanity (I Believe... it's been awhile), Despair is about Hope, Destiny is about Free will.... I'm abit of a Fanboy for them.... :P</div> </div> </div> </div> Aeons can do that too. Imperial Mysteries says that Space and Mind are governed by one Aeon. The entity called Dahhak, Aeon Syzygy Of Pandemonium on page 106 of Astral Realms has Rank 8 (same as the other Aeons), so I believe they're the same.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T18:14:58-07:00","id":878291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=874613#post874613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Wisdom is mostly the restraint of power, right? I think the Unseen University might count - their whole purpose is to teach wizards(mages) how to <i>not</i> use magic, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excepting that business in the squash court, of course.<br /> <br /> Funny, Stibbons is generally the level-headed one.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T10:59:03-07:00","id":881100,"title":"","content":"I know that Pan's Labyrinth is cited as inspirational material in the 1ED Changeling Core, but the part with the <b><a href=\"https://youtu.be/lSsfuEG4GMA\" target=\"_blank\">Pale Man</a></b> also works as inspiration for a scene in which you break a law of a Dead Dominion and a Kerberos comes after you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T13:40:36-07:00","id":882184,"title":"","content":"The Wizard of Oz is totally a Demon leveraging Show Of Power for all it is worth. <i>There</i> is the reason he doesn't want anyone to pay attention to the man behind the curtain - observation would mess with his knockoff mojo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T20:20:43-07:00","id":884292,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://1d4chan.org/wiki/Old_Man_Henderson\" target=\"_blank\">Old Man Henderson</a> (page itself is SFW, but some pages on the site are NSFW) is the ultimate Saboteur Demon vs. the Game Master/God-Machine. His ever-shifting backstory is just Henderson playing with his Cover to keep hidden despite his increasingly brazen activities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T13:28:56-07:00","id":884854,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a>: In addition to Gandalf, Dumbledore and Yoda, it seems like Granny Weatherwax from Discworld would have high Wisdom, though not necessarily 10. I haven't read the books, so I'm basing this assumption on this part from her page on Wikipedia: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Despite her power, Granny Weatherwax rarely uses magic in any immediately recognizable form. Instead, she prefers to use headology, a sort of folk-psychology which can be summed up as &quot;if people think you're a witch, you might as well be one&quot;. For instance, Granny could, if she wished, curse people. However it is simpler for her tosay she has cursed them, and let them assume that she is responsible for the next bit of bad luck that happens to befall them; given her reputation this tends to cause such people to flee the country entirely. Nanny Ogg has obliquely implied this avoidance of magic prevents Granny from being tempted into becoming a very successful &quot;bad&quot; witch.<br /> <br /> Headology bears some similarities to psychology in that it requires the user to hold a deep seated understanding of the workings of the human mind in order to be used successfully. However, headology tends to differ from psychology in that it usually involves approaching a problem from an entirely different angle.<br /> <br /> It has been said that the difference between headology and psychiatry is that, were you to approach either with a belief that you were being chased by a monster, a psychiatrist will convince you that there are no monsters coming after you, whereas a headologist will hand you a bat and a chair to stand on. The Headology approach is also very similar to Susan Sto Helit's practical approach to children's problems; since the child already believes in Bogeymen, then you may as well go along with it and teach them that they can also very firmly believe in the fireplace poker, too. </div> </div> </div>For contrast, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SAgQ4XSGvoM\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Star Butterfly</b></a> would definitely be low Wisdom. But what about the Doctor? I have a feeling that his Wisdom would be only slightly higher than Star's.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T15:53:18-07:00","id":887568,"title":"","content":"I believe I figured out what the Outer Gods of the Cthulhu Mythos would be.<br /> <br /> Azathoth: Annunnaki (Extremely High Rank Abyssal). It may be responsible for the False Awakenings from the Night Horrors supplement for Mage.<br /> <br /> Yog-Sothoth: either an Annunnaki or an Alien of the Strange Spheres from the Summoners supplement.<br /> <br /> Nyarlathotep: Aswadim (Scelestus Archmage). The pharaoh-like figure with strange devices and terrible prophecies is not the actual Nyarlathotep, but an Ochema (independent sub-soul created with the Practice Of Dynamics). This Ochema shape-shifts with Life, appears in multiple places simultaneously with Space, wields advanced technology with Matter + Forces and can freely traverse the Dreamlands/Astral with Mind. The real Nyarlathotep is even more powerful, and has anywhere from 6 to 9 dots in the <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/603390-homebrew-abyssal-arcanum\">Abyssal Arcanum</a></b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T01:39:05-07:00","id":887985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=884854#post884854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a>it seems like Granny Weatherwax from Discworld would have high Wisdom, though not necessarily 10.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very much. Witchcraft culture focuses on humility through service, since witches are generally solitary, and put emphasis on providing support, guidance, and troubleshooting rather than leadership; witches wield too much more knowledge and power than their charges not to risk hubris. It doesn't hurt that gingerbread cottages and sleeping curses are their secret shameful boogeyman, so they all keep an uncomfortable eye on each other.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Her solutions very often involve turning an adversary's powers, or consequences of their action, against them, which is a very balanced, minimal use of power in crisis. She's big into narrative and mental fixes.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> OTOH, she's risked Breaking Points when sorely pushed or disrespected (often with the justification of &quot;Can't let witches be publicly disrespected&quot;), and is <i>very </i>prone to thinking she knows better. About everything. Only the fact that she almost always <i>does </i>keeps her from being unbearably tyrannical. That and Nanny has a good idea of how to steer her past her pride.<br /> <br /> &lt;.&lt; Was that too much? I don't know much about a lot, but I'm confident of my grasp of Pratchett :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T15:15:09-07:00","id":890191,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.newgrounds.com/collection/brackenwood\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Bitey Of Brackenwood</b></a> can be seen as a Beast Runnerswift with high Wyrd that lives inside the Hedge and doesn't get along with anybody because of abandonment and anger issues. Alternatively, he could be an unusual Promethean who belongs to a Lineage related to the fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T05:25:05-07:00","id":891674,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/VideoGame/TheCatLady\" target=\"_blank\">The Cat Lady</a> from the Game of the same name... Is a Hunter/Immortal/Hero and the Parasites she has to kill/hunt are Goetic Spirits that have possessed people.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T06:03:04-07:00","id":891686,"title":"","content":"Alright, so I used to have Hulk as a Zeky Promethean with Residual Memories, then when Beast came out, I had him as a reluctant Anakim Ravager, but now, I think I might be able to settle on a Deviant, depending on how exactly they work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T06:24:47-07:00","id":891689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=891686#post891686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, so I used to have Hulk as a Zeky Promethean with Residual Memories, then when Beast came out, I had him as a reluctant Anakim Ravager, but now, I think I might be able to settle on a Deviant, depending on how exactly they work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely Deviant (wasn't Hulk listed as an inspiration?) of unusual power. If not that, I could see a Genius (Klagen/Progenitor) whose modded themselves a bit too much. Alternatively, a Stigmatic with <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=848953#post848953\">Cryptid Form</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T21:39:50-07:00","id":894557,"title":"","content":"So, Angels and Demons! <br /> <br /> <b>Person of Interest</b> is already named as an inspirational media in the Demon book, but I actually disagree on their read of <b>John Reese</b>. While he's certainly a Destroyer by nature, I'd actually put him down as a Tempter, no Saboteur. He'll go to extreme lengths to protect his friends, sure, but he actively resists getting pulled back into the games of global stakes and the future of humanity, instead focusing on the 'irrelevant' numbers and protecting his new life and friends. Even in the most recent season, which is by far the closest to an actual Demon game, he's more interested in the numbers than fighting Samaritan. <br /> <br /> (I haven't gotten my hands on them yet, but from what I've heard, <b>Harold Finch </b>seems more an Analyst than a Psychopomp)<br /> <br /> <b>Root </b>is certainly an Integrator, though a somewhat radical one given she wants the God-Machine replaced wholesale by a more benevolent iteration. I'd probably put her as a Psychopmp, given her vast number of connections and excellence at arranging coincidences and moving people and things around in her past life. Messenger could also work though.<br /> <br /> <b>Sameen Shaw</b>, by contrast, is without a shadow of doubt a Destroyer, but her agenda's a bit more unclear. I'd probably go with Saboteur; despite her sharing the same ostensible goals as Root and being willing to take the Machine at her word, recent events have definitely made her goal first and foremost to kill god.<br /> <br /> <b>The Machine</b> is a particular significant bit of subverted infrastructure, and the Subway is a bolthole. <br /> <br /> <b>Greer</b>, meanwhile, is a loyal Trumpet.<br /> <br /> Moving on to different media,<br /> <br /> <b>John Wick </b>was a Destroyer trying so, so hard to be an Antimonian. The <b>Continental </b>is a Temporal Agency<br /> <br /> <b>Phillip and Elizabeth Jennings</b> are loyal Angels of the machine, though they've come close to falling on quite a few occasions. Probably Swords, but the particular matrix keeping them around is both easy to sustain and hard to replicate, so while not quite Exiles (their orders come through loud and clear), they have a long leash and get used as Wheels and occasionally even Trumpets.<br /> <br /> The Man (in the <b>Booth at the End</b>) IS an Exile, and quite a minor one at that (probably rank 1, maybe 2). He desperately clings to the book, the linchpin of his last mission, using basic deal-with-the-devil stuff to get people to complete Occult Matrices and using the excess power to grant their wishes. <b>Doris </b>is a Tempter who tracked him down and would very much like that book, trying to get him to fall on the way there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11821-st-just","name":"St.Just","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T22:34:03-07:00","id":894566,"title":"","content":"I don't know if it's been mentioned, but the whole of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Gate_(1987_film)\" target=\"_blank\">The Gate</a> could be a very young Moros' Awakening.<br /> <br /> Seriously, it's crazy symbolism heavy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T06:57:26-07:00","id":900912,"title":"","content":"I have far too many ideas involving the CoD and RWBY.<br /> <br /> Blake is a Beast Changeling (Dual Kith Truefriend/Runnerswift) with the pseudonym 'Belle' upon return.<br /> Weiss is an Obrimos Mage who's either a GotV or unaligned with the shadow name 'Snow'<br /> Yang is a Bastet Hatara shapechanger under the Sun-chaser accord with the nickname 'Goldilocks'.<br /> <br /> Glynda is an Obrimos GotV under the Votiaries of the Ordained legacy--tasked to keep guard of Ozpin (see below). SN: The Goodwitch.<br /> Ozpin is a high-wyrd Changeling (Probably Wizened Oracle/Fatemaker) and the Monarch of the Winter Court. Psuedonym: The Wizard<br /> James Ironwood is also a Changeling, Elemental Manikin/Soldier and the King of the Summer Court. Pseudonym: The General<br /> Qrow and Raven are Wind-folk Corvian Shapechangers under the Sun-chaser and Wind-Dancer accords. <br /> Taiyang is a retired Hunter (albeit one with supernatural sympathies) (No details because I don't really know anything about Hunter)<br /> Summer Rose was a Flowering Fairest who made a deal with her keeper so she could have a child.<br /> <br /> Ruby is a standard mortal with more experience than many adults, let alone kids her age. Her main feature would probably be the Biokinesis merit (allowing for the classic heroic stunts that protagonists have).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10141-solaris","name":"Solaris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T07:49:05-07:00","id":900961,"title":"","content":"The Various Mutants from TMNT are all likely Deviants.. not sure if Animal to &quot;Other&quot; is going to be a thing in it but i can see Animals used as a basis for something to use on Humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T08:40:57-07:00","id":901014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=900961#post900961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Various Mutants from TMNT are all likely Deviants.. not sure if Animal to &quot;Other&quot; is going to be a thing in it but i can see Animals used as a basis for something to use on Humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rocket Raccoon as a Deviant?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T17:00:55-07:00","id":903111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=900961#post900961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Various Mutants from TMNT are all likely Deviants.. not sure if Animal to &amp;quot;Other&amp;quot; is going to be a thing in it but i can see Animals used as a basis for something to use on Humans.</div> </div> </div> </div> We had Prometheans made from animal corpses in a supplement, so animal Deviants aren't a stretch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T19:13:36-07:00","id":903902,"title":"","content":"How might the Chaos Gods from Warhammer 40000 fit into the CoD? We already have the Maeljin, but their purviews don't map up neatly to the concepts embodied by the Chaos Gods. Furthermore, the latter are easily Rank 8 in WH40K, which would put them on the same level as the Aeons from Mage if not scaled down. I'm thinking about making them Rank 7 Idigam. <br /> <br /> The constant give and take of power between them, and the Warp's similarities to the Hedge makes me think they could also be True Fae in an endless Feud. This option has less cosmological impact than suddenly putting four entities of Rank 7 on Earth. Also, you could create some awesome Huntsmen based on Warp Daemons to instigate paranoia among changelings, just like the stories where the Inquisition hunts down anything they perceive as heresy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T19:47:52-07:00","id":903912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=903902#post903902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How might the Chaos Gods from Warhammer 40000 fit into the CoD? We already have the Maeljin, but their purviews don't map up neatly to the concepts embodied by the Chaos Gods. Furthermore, the latter are easily Rank 8 in WH40K, which would put them on the same level as the Aeons from Mage if not scaled down. I'm thinking about making them Rank 7 Idigam.<br /> <br /> The constant give and take of power between them, and the Warp's similarities to the Hedge makes me think they could also be True Fae in an endless Feud. This option has less cosmological impact than suddenly putting four entities of Rank 7 on Earth. Also, you could create some awesome Huntsmen based on Warp Daemons to instigate paranoia among changelings, just like the stories where the Inquisition hunts down anything they perceive as heresy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not an expert on 40K lore by any means, but, yeah, the best fit would probably be as high Titled True Fae. Their weird natures, powers of mutation, the disjointed time/space nature of their &quot;realm&quot; seems to perfectly fit with the True Fae.<br /> <br /> What about the C'tan?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T20:48:08-07:00","id":903929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=903912#post903912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not an expert on 40K lore by any means, but, yeah, the best fit would probably be as high Titled True Fae. Their weird natures, powers of mutation, the disjointed time/space nature of their &quot;realm&quot; seems to perfectly fit with the True Fae.<br /> <br /> What about the C'tan?</div> </div> </div> </div> I am unsure. Perhaps Idigam that Coalesced in Irem?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T22:48:19-07:00","id":903969,"title":"","content":"Well, if you want to import canon wholesale, the Chaos Gods absolutely should have huge, cosmology shaking impacts for their presence/awakening. I'd actually make them Astral entities though, they're formed and empowered from the passions and emotions of humanity after all. Maybe Abyssal intruders in the Astral, warping the collective unconscious into massive snarls where hope is inextricably tied with betrayal and ambition, love with pestilence and entropy, pleasure with the obsessive pursuit of perfection and excess, and so on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11821-st-just","name":"St.Just","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T23:06:36-07:00","id":903976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>St.Just</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=903969#post903969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if you want to import canon wholesale, the Chaos Gods absolutely should have huge, cosmology shaking impacts for their presence/awakening. I'd actually make them Astral entities though, they're formed and empowered from the passions and emotions of humanity after all. Maybe Abyssal intruders in the Astral, warping the collective unconscious into massive snarls where hope is inextricably tied with betrayal and ambition, love with pestilence and entropy, pleasure with the obsessive pursuit of perfection and excess, and so on?</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd say they're closer to spirits than Goetia. The former can invade our realm, Possess and Claim more easily, while the latter usually can't Materialize on the rare occasions when they do invade. That being said, the Chaos Gods are definitely horrible and corrupting enough to count as Abyssals, whether they manifest in the Shadow or Astral.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 05-31-2016, 02:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T23:36:14-07:00","id":903985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>St.Just</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=894557#post894557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Root </b>is certainly an Integrator, though a somewhat radical one given she wants the God-Machine replaced wholesale by a more benevolent iteration. I'd probably put her as a Psychopmp, given her vast number of connections and excellence at arranging coincidences and moving people and things around in her past life. Messenger could also work though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I made her a Messenger who specifically transitions from being a Tempter to an Integrator. But yeah, Psychopomp makes sense too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T02:26:00-07:00","id":904053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=903976#post903976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'd say they're closer to spirits than Goetia. The former can invade our realm, Possess and Claim more easily, while the latter usually can't Materialize on the rare occasions when they do invade. That being said, the Chaos Gods are definitely horrible and corrupting enough to count as Abyssals, whether they manifest in the Shadow or Astral.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is worth noting that it is not, in fact, easy for the Ruinous Powers to invade our realm. The Materium and Immaterium are seperate and only the strongest manifestations of the Warp can pass through and survive without extenuating circumstances. Things like the Webway, the Eye of Terror, and, of course, legions upon legions of mortal cultists are required for the servants of the Chaos Gods to make their presence felt in this plane of reality.<br /> <br /> The Chaos Gods themselves don't seem to be willing or able to venture into our realm at all, in fact, preferring instead to act through agents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T13:49:49-07:00","id":904417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=865735#post865735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about <b><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ImxnwjBsUHU&#91;B\" target=\"_blank\">Danny Phantom</a></b> and <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XaXEo1CiCds\" target=\"_blank\"><b>XJ-9</b></a>? The former has no apparent Geist, so he's probably not a Sin-Eater. The latter is closer to an Automata Wonder in terms of powers, but she goes through the same sort of troubles that an Unfleshed Promethean would face in the Pilgrimage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see Danny Phantom as a straight Ghost, weirdly. Accidentally killed when his parents were studying an Avernian Gate, he Materialized (an Avernian Gate in your own house? That's some strong resonance) and has been sustained by the constant recognition of everyone around him ever since. The Materialize Manifestation protects from Essence bleed, and he's mostly surrounded by his friends and possessions, so he's basically golden - even a Rank 1 ghost can Strengthen and Anchor to create the Open condition, Materialize for X hours, and put on Mortal Guise for X hours in as many turns.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, I haven't seen the show in a while, and they did make a big deal over how he was &quot;half human&quot;, which screams Geist - but that <i>could </i>be his insane luck in starting with Materialize and Mortal Guise","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T15:04:49-07:00","id":904481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=904417#post904417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see Danny Phantom as a straight Ghost, weirdly. Accidentally killed when his parents were studying an Avernian Gate, he Materialized (an Avernian Gate in your own house? That's some strong resonance) and has been sustained by the constant recognition of everyone around him ever since. The Materialize Manifestation protects from Essence bleed, and he's mostly surrounded by his friends and possessions, so he's basically golden - even a Rank 1 ghost can Strengthen and Anchor to create the Open condition, Materialize for X hours, and put on Mortal Guise for X hours in as many turns.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, I haven't seen the show in a while, and they did make a big deal over how he was &quot;half human&quot;, which screams Geist - but that <i>could </i>be his insane luck in starting with Materialize and Mortal Guise</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd peg Danny as a one-off instance of a ghost possessing his biologically living but metaphysically dead &quot;corpse&quot;. Alternately, he might fit in under Deviant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T15:11:58-07:00","id":904487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\">