l Adept, Common Sense, Consilium Status 5, *Contacts (Executives, IT Professionals), Fast-Talking 3, High Speech, Hollow (Hidden Entry, Luxury Goods, Size Matters 2) 5, Language (English, Portuguese; native Spanish), Occultation 3, Order Status (Silver Ladder 5), Perfected Item (Brontium amalgam signet ring), Professional Training (Professional; Academics, Persuasion, Subterfuge) 4, Shadow Name 3, Spin Doctor, Striking Looks 2, Sympathetic, Takes One to Know One, Token (Book of Things Strange and Wondrous) 2, Tutelage, Vice-Ridden<br /> Wisdom: 8<br /> Willpower: 6<br /> Initiative: 6<br /> Defense: 5<br /> Armor: 0/0<br /> Size: 5<br /> Speed: 10<br /> Health: 8<br /> Gnosis: 6<br /> Mana/Per Turn: 20/6<br /> Nimbus Tilt: Grants +1 to Composure, Resolve, and Stamina rolls.<br /> Dedicated Magical Tool: Brontium amalgam signet ring.<br /> Arcana: Fate 5, Mind 5, Time 5<br /> Attainments: Conditional Duration; Counterspell (Fate, Mind, Time); Create Rote (Fate, Mind, Time); Intuitive Leap; Mage Armor (Fate, Mind, Time); Mind\u2019s Eye; Targeted Summoning (Fate, Mind, Time); Temporal Sympathy; Time in a Bottle; Unbound Fate; Gn\u014ds\u014dt\u0113s \u2014 Savantism; Multitasker; Extraordinary Defense; Inner Potential<br /> Praxes: Exceptional Luck (Fate 2); Serendipity (Fate 1)<br /> Rotes: None<br /> Rote Skills: Empathy, Persuasion, Subterfuge<br /> Conditions: Aponoia, Bonded (Cecilia, Salomon), Charmed, Driven, Embarrassing Secret (Hard Candy), Guilty, Informed (NPCs), Inspired, Resonant (<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1320203-the-pack-101-packs?p=1348517#post1348517\">Zia</a>), Steadfast<br /> Notes: The Gn\u014dst\u0113s give Kairos Mind as a third Ruling Arcanum and he has refunded most Praxes. Former merits: Allies (Family and Friends) 1, Resources 2, Retainer 2, Status (Condo Association) 2, Status (Holcim) 1, True Friend (Melissa).\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 11-06-2026, 10:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T08:22:47-07:00","id":920967,"title":"","content":"I decided to redo my sheet for Batman. This isn't any specific version, just what comes to my mind when I think of him (plus <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/784382-homebrew-idea-batman-in-the-wod?p=785124#post785124\"><b>some observations by Amechra</b></a>). In case you are wondering, this Batman is worth over 300 Experiences. And that's without going into Endowments.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Virtue: </b>Justice/Prudence<br /> <b>Vice: </b>Wrath<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 5, Wits 4, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 4, Dexterity 4, Stamina 5<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 4, Manipulation 3, Composure 5<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics (Criminology) 4, Crafts (Gadgets) 3, Computer 3, Medicine (Quick Patch Up) 2, Occult 2, Politics 3, Investigation (Deductive Reasoning, Crime Scenes) 5, Science (Forensics) 4<br /> <br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics (Gliding, Throwing) 4, Brawl (Neutralize) 4, Drive (Batmobile) 4, Firearms (Grappling Hook) 2, Larceny (Security Systems) 3, Stealth (Ambush, Shadowing) 5, Survival 2, Weaponry 4<br /> <br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken 1, Empathy (Motivations) 3, Expression 2, Intimidation (Interrogation, Appearing Out Of Nowhere) 4, Persuasion (Corporate) 3, Socialize (Formal Events) 2, Streetwise (Criminals) 3, Subterfuge (Protect Identity) 4<br /> <br /> <b>Skill Tricks:</b> Academics (Quick Cram), Investigation (Incisive Mind, Pattern Expert), Crafts (Improvised Tools), Computer (No Internet Footprint), Science (Applied Science, Occam's Razor), Firearms (Trick Shot), Brawl (Multiple Strike), Stealth (Know The Shadows, Still As A Statue), Intimidation (Fast Break), Streetwise (Network Of Eyes, Rumor Mill), Subterfuge (Perfect Disguise)<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area Of Expertise (Deductive Reasoning), At Any Cost, Common Sense, Danger Sense (Advanced), Encyclopedic Knowledge (Academics, Investigation, Science), Eye For The Strange, Fast Reflexes 3, Good Time Management, Indomitable (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration\"><b>Epic</b></a>), Interdisciplinary Specialty (Deductive Reasoning), Investigative Aide (Investigation), Investigative Prodigy 4, Language (Several), Professional Training 5 (Vigilante: Intimidation, Investigation, Stealth), Tolerance For Biology, Trained Observer 3, Virtuous, Automotive Genius, Crack Driver 3, Demolisher 2, Fleet Of Foot 3, Hardy 2, Iron Stamina 3, Parkour 4, Punch Drunk, Quick Draw (Gadgets, Grappling Hook), Stunt Driver 5, Allies (Police 3, Corporate 3), Air Of Menace, Alternate Identity 3, Closed Book 4, Contacts (Several), Fame 2, Fixer, Iron Will, Resources 5, Safe Place (Batcave), Status (Wayne Enterprises 5, Justice League 5), Table Turner, True Friend (Bat Family), Untouchable, Cursed, Fated Ferocity 4, Mind Of A Madman, Close Quarter Combat 5, Defensive Combat (Brawl), Grappling 3, Iron Chin 4, Martial Arts 4, Unarmed Defense 5<br /> <br /> <b>Health: </b>10<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10 [Risking Willpower]<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 10<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 12<br /> <b>Speed: </b>16<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 6<br /> <b>Conviction:</b> 7<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Obsessed (Fighting Crime)<br /> <br /> <b>Note:</b> If you want Batman to be truly amazing at what he does, you can give him Pendragon's Prodigy Merit for Investigation (see below), which could give him 1 Reversal Point as described on page 17 of Mage: The Awakening - Imperial Mysteries.<br /> <br /> New Merit: Prodigy \u2022\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> Prerequisites: Relevant Attribute or Skill at 5 dots<br /> <br /> The character is the best in the world at something. With the three dot version of this merit one of their Skills gains an additional dot, increasing it to 6. The five dot version does the same, but applies to an Attribute instead. The bonus dot comes along with the Merit, it needn\u2019t be purchased separately. The Prodigy Merit may be bought more than once, but Storytellers are strongly encouraged to restrict this only to skills and attributes in which a character has been proven to be unprecedentedly adroit.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 05-21-2019, 11:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T09:44:02-07:00","id":920996,"title":"","content":"I would be inclined to give him more Drive. After all, he doesn't only drive the Batmobile, but pilots the Batwing and Batboat and Batcycle, Batcopter, and has occasionally taken over space shuttles and alien vehicles, and usually all of these in the combative situations Drive is for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-25-2016, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T13:09:24-07:00","id":921112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=920996#post920996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would be inclined to give him more Drive. After all, he doesn't only drive the Batmobile, but pilots the Batwing and Batboat and Batcycle, Batcopter, and has occasionally taken over space shuttles and alien vehicles, and usually all of these in the combative situations Drive is for.</div> </div> </div> </div> Alright, I gave him one more dot in Drive. Is there anything else you think I missed?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T13:55:08-07:00","id":921140,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Shadows over Gotham</b><br /> <br /> Excellent Batman! This version feels very much like the street level Batman of the classic Detective Comics (which is my favorite interpretation). The only adjustments I would make is Athletics 4 (Throwing) and Weaponry 3.<br /> <br /> Using your Batman as a benchmark, here is the Joker. I went went something that is a blend of classic Detective Comics, with a bit of Batman:the Animated Series<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Joker</b></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; t