und-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar775_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"775\" data-vbnamecard=\"775\">Reighnhell</a>! I tried cutting back on his Skills and Merits so he's not a Bat God, as the joke goes. Big thanks to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1170_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1170\" data-vbnamecard=\"1170\">amechra</a> for helping me understand the nuances of the CoD rules better. I'll add your recommendations too, Reighnhell.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=921140#post921140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Re: Shadows over Gotham</b><br /> <br /> Excellent Batman! This version feels very much like the street level Batman of the classic Detective Comics (which is my favorite interpretation). The only adjustments I would make is Athletics 4 (Throwing) and Weaponry 3.<br /> <br /> Using your Batman as a benchmark, here is the Joker. I went went something that is a blend of classic Detective Comics, with a bit of Batman:the Animated Series<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Joker</b></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Humor <b>Vice:</b> Chaotic <b>Vice:</b> Cruel<br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Maniac<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 5, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 4, Manipulation 4, Composure 5<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Animal Ken 1 (Hyenas), Athletics 2, Brawl 3, Drive 3(Getaway), Computers 2, Crafts 3 (Explosives), Expression 2 (Comedy), Firearms 2(Pistols), Intimidation 4(Theatrics), Investigation 2, Larceny 3(Escape), Medicine 1(Poison), Persuasion 2 (Extortion), Science 2 (Chemistry), Stealth 3(Ambush), Streetwise 4 (Crime), Subterfuge 4 (Lies), Weaponry 2 (Blades, Improvised)<br /> <br /> <b>Skill Tricks: </b>Drive (Lose \u2019Em), Intimidation (Don\u2019t Mess with Me), Larceny (Light Fingers), Stealth (Backstab), Subterfuge (Cognitive Dissonance), Weaponry (Wearing Weapons)<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Allies 2 (Extortion Victims), Allies 4 (Harley Quinn), Area of Expertise (Chemistry, Comedy, Extortion, Theatrics), Closed Book 4, Contacts 4 (Criminals), Crack Driver, Danger Sense, Defensive Combat (Brawl), Fame 2 (Gotham Criminals), Encyclopedic Knowledge (Comedy), Fast Reflexes 2), Fleet of Foot 2, Hardy 2, Indomitable, Iron Will, Morbid Fascination, Quick Draw (Blades, Pistols), Seizing the Edge, Shiv 2, Sleight of Hand, Style: Fast Talking 4, Style: Improvised Weaponry 2, Style: Light Weapons 2, Murder Expert, Style: Street Fighting 3, Staff 4 (Henchmen), Striking Looks 1 (Frightening), Untouchable, Vice-Ridden<br /> <br /> <b>Conviction:</b> 7 [Mirrors, pg.32-33]<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 3<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 10<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 13<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <br /> <b>Condition: </b>Amnesia, Madness, Obsession (Batman, Crime), Notoriety<br /> <b>Talent: </b>Compelling Madness, Profiling<br /> <b>Frailty: </b>Intolerance for Chaos, Obvious Lunatic<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> First off, I really like those choices for Virtue and Vice. I'd lower his Composure to 4, seeing as how he is capable of losing his temper, such as when someone explains a joke or when he thought someone else had killed Batman. I'd add an Interdisciplinary Specialty for Lethal Joke Items, Mind Games and Chemistry, as well as +1 dot to Medicine, Persuasion, Science and Weaponry. I'd increase his Hardy to 3, seeing as how he's pretty much immune to poisons, especially those of his own making. He'd also have Iron Stamina 2, to laugh at injuries. Harley would be covered by Retainer. He definitely qualifies for Hurt Locker Merits like At Any Cost, Air Of Menace and Living With Death. He could have a Skill Trick or two in Streetwise. Those Conditions are spot on. I especially like your choices for the Fighting Merits, they really get across how he's a dirty fighter who will go for the kill as fast as possible. It's possible that he has <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/FanTheories/comments/230b06/the_joker_does_have_a_superpower/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>a specialized Omen Sensitivity he's not fully aware of.</b></a> Lastly, if we were to use <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/155637-slasher-gmc-port\"><b>Nightmare</b></a> instead of Conviction, I'd give him a rating of 2, maybe 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-25-2016, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T17:27:21-07:00","id":921242,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Lee Ping (From <i>Detentionaire</i>)</span></b><br /> <i>&quot;Huh, physics works in real life.</i>&quot;<br /> <b>Stigmatic <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/a/binghamton.edu/file/d/0B2K8R3qXyDyoY0lrSzZWSlN1SWc/view\" target=\"_blank\">Atariya</a><br /> Virtue:</b> Insightful; <b>Vice:</b> Driven<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Str</b> 2 / <b>Dex</b> 3 / <b>Sta</b> 2<br /> <b>Int</b> 3 / <b>Wit</b> 3 / <b>Res</b> 3<br /> <b>Pre</b> 2 / <b>Man</b> 2 / <b>Com</b> 2</span><br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics 2, Computer 1, Crafts 1, Investigation 3, Occult 1, Science 3<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 2, Firearms \u2022, Larceny 1, Stealth 2, Weaponry 1<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Empathy 1, Persuasion 1, Streetwise 1, Subterfuge 1<br /> <b>Specialities:</b> Cramped Spaces (Athletics), Never Left (Subterfuge), Oddly Practical Applications (Science)<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Allies (A. Nigma Student Body) \u2022, Damn Lucky \u2022\u2022, Indomitable \u2022\u2022, Interdisciplinary Speciality (Oddly Practical Applications) \u2022, Manifestum \u2022\u2022, Mr. Lucky \u2022, Parkour \u2022<br /> <b>Bonus Merits:</b> Omen Sensitivity (Uncontrolled), Unseen Senses (God-Machine)<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> <a href=\"http://princesswod.wikia.com/wiki/Conditions_and_Tilts#Legal_Minor_.28persistent.29\" target=\"_blank\">Legal Minor</a>, Notorious (&quot;Lee Ping the Prank King&quot;), Obsession (Mysteries)<br /> <br /> His Stigmata is the &quot;tattoo&quot; on his left arm. Manifestum is a version of Clear Sighted that immunizes you from mind control instead of mental illusions.<br /> <br /> He also has Legal Minor despite being a character in an Innocents game because there's no Grounded And In Detention For All My Free Time for The Foreseeable Future condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> Aw yiss, managed to fix him up so he's a legal starting character. Because having him be anything else wouldn't make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 06-25-2016, 08:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T17:18:11-07:00","id":922305,"title":"","content":"While somebody on the Beast boards had Elsa as a Beast (who'd have guessed.), I wanna say she's a Proximus-turned-Mage (hence her being born with her powers). Her Proximus curse isolates her at all times, and causes her to harm others when it flares up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T21:44:21-07:00","id":922456,"title":"","content":"Yuuko Ichihara from xxxHolic would be an <i>extremely</i> powerful Awakened sorceress, who may very well be eligible for Archmastery. She would be an Acanthus unaffiliated with any Order, who is a Master of her Ruling Arcana as well as Prime, Space, and Spirit. And at the very least a Disciple in the rest. Her inability to use her magic for another without it being a binding transaction could be the result of a Ban placed on her, or even an aspect of her Curse if she's a Proximus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 06-28-2016, 12:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T01:34:02-07:00","id":922501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=922305#post922305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While somebody on the Beast boards had Elsa as a Beast (who'd have guessed.), I wanna say she's a Proximus-turned-Mage (hence her being born with her powers). Her Proximus curse isolates her at all times, and causes her to harm others when it flares up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I made <i>Elsa</i> a queen from Silver Ladder tale - she started to be Guardian after 'accident' with Anna ( 'conceal, don't feel' ), but her life changing moment ( plot of <b>Frozen</b> 1 movie ) makes her understand she must live honest with her powers - and become sorceress-queen, not hiding from her magic. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T11:35:07-07:00","id":922754,"title":"","content":"I may have stated this earlier, but Seto Kaiba would be great as an Invictus Ventrue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T15:17:47-07:00","id":922872,"title":"","content":"I don't know if he's been brought up before, but Captain Jack Sparrow is the very image of an Acanthus mage. Pretty much always in the right place at the right time? His harebrained schemes always go according to plan? Capable of feats that break physics and make it cry in the corner? Has a compass that points him in the direction of his goal? Sounds pretty Acanthus to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T15:46:19-07:00","id":922889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=922872#post922872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if he's been brought up before, but Captain Jack Sparrow is the very image of an Acanthus mage. Pretty much always in the right place at the right time? His harebrained schemes always go according to plan? Capable of feats that break physics and make it cry in the corner? Has a compass that points him in the direction of his goal? Sounds pretty Acanthus to me.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's more like 1ED Acanthus. The 2ED version is closer to David Xanatos from Gargoyles, who is the trope namer for <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/XanatosGambit\" target=\"_blank\"><b>strategies where all paths lead to victory.</b></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-28-2016, 06:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0