s ?<br /> <br /> I was thinking a slasher<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HpfSmX-n9lk\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HpfSmX-n9lk\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HpfSmX-n9lk\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HpfSmX-n9lk </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> She is a complete Yandere. I mean her phone lets her know everything her love is doing. Also that same love makes her an almost unstoppable killing machine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since I've never seen Future Diary, I could be completely off base, but reading the plot synopsis, it sounds like it could be a game of Changeling in which a True Fae pits a bunch of changelings in a battle royale to take his spot. Alternatively, it's a G-M Chronicle game, with mortals fighting each other for the chance to become &quot;God&quot; (read: become a cover for an angel).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T16:22:43-07:00","id":942312,"title":"","content":"Is she a compulsive murderer? She just seems particularly dexterous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T19:51:57-07:00","id":942429,"title":"","content":"From <i>The Hobbit</i> and <i>The Lord of the Rings</i>:<br /> <b>Gandalf</b> is an Obrimos Mysterium mage.<br /> <b>Saruman</b> is a mage Tetrarch of the Seers of the Throne.<br /> <b>Sauron</b> is a lesser Exarch, whose Lustrum is in Stygia. Due to a <i>seriously</i> bad Paradox backlash, however, Sauron requires a very particular Soul Stone ring to send forth any Ochemata!<br /> <b>Smaug</b> is an Incarnate Ugallu Beast with a serious Hunger for collecting.<br /> <b>Treebeard</b> is a Wyrd 8 changeling Elemental with the dual kiths of Gargantuan and Woodblood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 08-02-2016, 10:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T20:09:26-07:00","id":942438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=942429#post942429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From <i>The Hobbit</i> and <i>The Lord of the Rings</i>:<br /> <b>Gandalf</b> is an Obrimos Mysterium mage.<br /> <b>Saruman</b> is a mage Tetrarch of the Seers of the Throne.<br /> <b>Sauron</b> is a lesser Exarch, whose Lustrum is in Stygia. Due to a <i>seriously</i> bad Paradox backlash, however, Sauron requires a very particular Soul Stone ring to send forth any Ochemata!<br /> <b>Smaug</b> is an Incarnate Ugallu Beast with a serious Hunger for collecting.<br /> <b>Treebeard</b> is a Wyrd 8 changeling Elemental with the dual kiths of Gargantuan and Woodblood.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue that Sauron's Lustrum is in Pandemonium. His great talent was in bending the minds of others to his will. That's Mind Arcana all the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":". 08-05-2016, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T22:07:38-07:00","id":942492,"title":"