ular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T12:23:31-07:00","id":963840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=963836#post963836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI've been thinking that the Gems are a lot like Prometheans; They come into being as fully formed adults, and much like Golems, are created with a specific purpose in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demons, tho.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T13:06:12-07:00","id":963867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=963840#post963840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons, tho.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't read D:tD. As I've mentioned elsewhere, I refuse to spend $20 that I can't get refunded on something without a chance to really look through it first. I hand out free samples for a living; Try before you buy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T13:28:13-07:00","id":963876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=963867#post963867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't read D:tD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which hasn't stopped you from murdering ancient leetspeak to speak ill of it.<br /> <br /> Ageless purpose-made characters with alien magic at their disposal and a prominent rebellion from a rigidly-defined society in their cultural history that has produced half-human hybrids with powers outside their parents' capabilities has significantly more resonance with the Unchained than the Created.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As I've mentioned elsewhere, I refuse to spend $20 that I can't get refunded on something without a chance to really look through it first. I hand out free samples for a living; Try before you buy. </div> </div> </div>The book was previewed for free in text-only form when its Prestige Edition was Kickstarted prior to its official release, just like Beast was; significantly less changed between drafts in Demon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T14:32:38-07:00","id":963912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=963840#post963840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons, tho.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, Rose achieved her Hell of pushing back the G-M/Homeworld? And Steven is some kind of weird Offspring?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T14:45:44-07:00","id":963919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=963867#post963867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I haven't read D:tD. As I've mentioned elsewhere, I refuse to spend $20 that I can't get refunded on something without a chance to really look through it first. I hand out free samples for a living; Try before you buy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well are you in the wrong niche hobby then. That closes off, like, 90% of most RPG's at the door, probably more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T15:46:00-07:00","id":963945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=963867#post963867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I haven't read D:tD. As I've mentioned elsewhere, I refuse to spend $20 that I can't get refunded on something without a chance to really look through it first. I hand out free samples for a living; Try before you buy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, question: If I bought you a PDF copy, would you actually read it, or would I be wasting my money?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T02:59:13-07:00","id":964170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=963945#post963945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, question: If I bought you a PDF copy, would you actually read it, or would I be wasting my money?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would read it. I actually find the espionage angle intriguing.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm not trying to speak ill of Descent when I call it D@3m0n, I just reject the &quot;God is a machine&quot; idea. Actual fallen angels that were made by the true Creator of the universe? Interesting. Agent Smith from <i>The Matrix</i>? Neat. Combining the two? Nope, now you lost me. Sometimes combining two things I like makes something I don't like. I like BBQ. I like potato chips. I don't like BBQ potato chips.<br /> <br /> As for the PDF vs. hardcopy thing, that's the publishing industries problem. Aside from the issue of not being able to browse through a book first, I also kind of hate reading from a computer screen for long periods of time; it's not good for my eyes, and I've found I don't retain the information as well as I do when I read it on paper. This is supported by scientific research; there's something about the combination of tactile sensation and the scent of the paper that helps people remember what they read.<br /> <br /> But that's getting off topic. The fact that Gems emerge from holes in the ground is another thing that reminds me of the Tammuz.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It occurs to me (and recently, to Cyclops) that humanty's reaction to mutants is a lot like Disquiet; irrational hatred, even after the X-Men save the world right alongside the Avengers. Defies all logic. Pagan gods and rock monsters? Respected heroes. A mutant who looks like an angel? KILL IT WITH FIRE!!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 09-14-2016, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T10:35:19-07:00","id":964378,"title":"","content":"As Satchel pointed out, there's a 99% complete text still available on the Kickstarter page for free, and it's been available there for almost three years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T11:46:18-07:00","id":964439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=964170#post964170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI'm not trying to speak ill of Descent when I call it D@3m0n, I just reject the &quot;God is a machine&quot; idea. Actual fallen angels that were made by the true Creator of the universe? Interesting. Agent Smith from <i>The Matrix</i>? Neat. Combining the two? Nope, now you lost me. Sometimes combining two things I like makes something I don't like. I like BBQ. I like potato chips. I don't like BBQ potato chips.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you have a bit of a misconception about Demon and the entire God-Machine thing. The God-Machine isn't God in the Abrahamic creator deity sense. It's an ancient machine of unknown origin and purpose that has vast knowledge and power (but is not omniscient or omnipotent), which is worshiped by some cults as a god. You were pretty on target when you compared demons to Agent Smith, with the God Machine being Deus Ex Machina, at least if the Matrix and Zion were part of the same world. The god of the Abrahamic religions may or may not exist in the CoD setting, but it's almost certainly not the God Machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12354-who-is-matt","name":"who.is.matt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T12:48:48-07:00","id":964477,"title":"","content":"I've been rewatching the MCU movies lately and have thoughts on thematic equivalents within CofD.<br /> <br /> SHIELD: SHIELD is Task Force Valkyrie. Semi-Secret quasi-government organization that deals with the unusual either by weaponizing or covering it up. The otherwise human SHIELD affiliated characters (Fury, Coulson, Hill, Hawkeye, Black Widow, etc) are Hunters.<br /> <br /> Iron Man: At first glance he'd appear to be a Wizard or Genius but after watching all of his movies in a month it's obvious that everything that makes Tony Stark Iron Man is the result of trauma. Making him a much better candidate for a Changeling (his name is a nice little bonus too). His obsessive tinkering (especially when under stress) and controlling tendencies suggest Wizened as his Seeming.<br /> <br /> Ten Rings: The unusually international but distinctly non-white terrorist organization is a collection of loyal Changelings under a True Fae with the title &quot;The Mandarin&quot; and &quot;The Iron Monger&quot;.<br /> <br /> Hulk: He'd be a textbook Deviant if there were any rules for it yet. So going back to his thematic aspects we have a radioactive monster that mostly wants to be left alone but is constantly hounded by those who hate and fear his very existence. Making him a good candidate to be Zeka Promethean, one with really good residual memories.<br /> <br /> Abomination: Was a horrifying monster made in response to the Hulk. Possibly another Promethean (made from the body of a soldier he killed in a torment induced rampage). Another possibility which fits with the gradual transformation set up he has in the movie is a Cheiron Group soldier hopped up on stolen Pyros that slowly make him just as monstrous.<br /> <br /> Whiplash: A huntsman preying on Tony's self doubt and fear in an approach.<br /> <br /> Warmachine: Fae-Touched best friend of Tony's wearing Token armour.<br /> <br /> Thor: The dynamic Thor has with the modern world, a world only vaguely resembling the world he knows is present in both Vampire and Mummy but Mummy caries the divine powers and worshipped as a God much better. So this Thor is a Mummy, part of a small sect of Arisen who's cults found their way to Nordic Europe and inspired Norse mythology.<br /> <br /> Loki: A Deceived, who manipulated Thor's cult into waking him into a berserk rage. He may or may not actually be Thor's brother, my knowledge of Mummy is spotty so I'm not even sure if that's possible.<br /> <br /> Jane: A Null Mysteries Hunter who had infiltrated Thor's cult with intent on studying it's slumbering benefactor.<br /> <br /> Captain America: Cap has a similar relationship with the modern world to Thor but to a lesser degree. A Deva Vampire super soldier allowed into the service of Taskforce Valkyrie in response to the actions of the Red Skull (See Below)<br /> <br /> Red Skull: Ordo Dracul Nosferatu who openly through his powers in with the Nazis. Red Skull begins an alternate approach to perfecting the Vampiric condition. He begins experimenting with the living and God Machine infrastructure to physically perfect them before they are even embraced.<br /> <br /> Chitari: Strange and unknowable with minimal context for their existence. These guys scream Idigam. Loki exploited some Infrastructure to release them into the world.<br /> <br /> Extremis: An unstable extract of Goblin Fruit that can physically restores and even enhances the human body. As with anything of the Wyrd it twists it's users turning them into Fae but most people can't withstand that strain and after a while turn into living bombs.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Mandarin&quot; and AIM: Aldrich Killian and Trevor Slattery are both Loyalist Changelings under the thrall of &quot;The Mandarin&quot;. Maya Hansen is in the process of escaping (probably going to become a Darkling).<br /> <br /> <br /> This post is already a bit on the TLDR side so I'll stop here at Iron Man 3 and see what people think thus far.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9065-darkblade","name":"Darkblade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T14:13:37-07:00","id":964511,"title":"","content":"Having been on a Star Wars kick for the better part of a year now, I would say that the Galaxy Far Far Away is a setting where the Lie has been lessened, and the Pentacle Orders operate openly (the Jedi Temple even has five spires!). The Sith are a Left-Handed Seer Legacy who got their butts handed to them by the Pentacle centuries ago, and have had to keep out of sight ever since. After Order 66, the Seers reinforced the Lie, which is why so many people think the Jedi are a myth or frauds less than 20 years after they're destroyed. The Knights of Ren are a Left-Handed Nameless Order who got their hands on Seer writings and propaganda.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T14:17:25-07:00","id":964517,"title":"","content":"Of course, the problem is that the show isn't &quot;We'll never be happy unless we become human, Steven! We are inherently inferior beings!&quot; or &quot;It isn't humanity's fault that they hate mutants! If they could just become human they'd be fine!&quot; But: HOLY SHIT DTD SU IS SUCH A GOOD IDEA. OFFSPRING STEVEN!<br /> <br /> Then again, that's the problem with adapting things to a horror setting. In a superhero comic, mutant =/= monster, but in a horror setting, an atomic mutant inevitably has to be inherently monstrous in some way. <br /> <br /> In other settings, the Noisy Tenant-verse (Burgrr, Awful Hospital) is totally a Changeling story. Dr. Phage is a True Fae, definitely. The whimsical dream-logic of the setting makes it Arcadian for me, as opposed to Abyssal, Idigam, or GM related. <br /> <br /> Speaking of Changeling, Dorohedoro probably works best there. It's about normals vs. magic users, but it's very hard to map it to Hunter or Mage, since the wizards in Dorohedoro aren't really like any kind of mages or sorcerers in ChroD, since they're people born with one specific power. And their whole deal with living in the Magic World and periodically popping into the human world to hunt/transmogrify random people is very Gentry-ish. I might make the Devils the Gentry and have some of the magic users be Loyalist Changelings, actually. Kaiman would be a Coldscale Beast (or possibly Ogre), Nikaido would be Kithless, Noi would be...what's that Ogre kith with a healing factor?, En would be some sort of custom fungus-Kith, and so on. <br /> <br /> I don't even have to change anything for What We Do In The Shadows, it's literally already a completely perfect Vampire: The Requiem story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 09-06-2016, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T17:28:06-07:00","id":964657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=964517#post964517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, the problem is that the show isn't &quot;We'll never be happy unless we become human, Steven! We are inherently inferior beings!&quot; or &quot;It isn't humanity's fault that they hate mutants! If they could just become human they'd be fine!&quot; But: HOLY SHIT DTD SU IS SUCH A GOOD IDEA. OFFSPRING STEVEN!</div> </div> </div> </div>...I think you misunderstood. I wasn't comparing SU to X-Men. Completely separate thought. The comparison was of how the general public of the Marvel universe respond to mutants seems similar to how people react to Prometheans; No matter how much good a mutant does, they will still be hated and feared. Thor is a pagan god, and makes no effort to conceal that fact, but people trust him. The Thing is a 600 pound rock monster, but he's a national hero. Angel rescues someone's kitten that's stuck in a tree, but because he's a mutant, someone will call the police. Sounds like Disquiet at work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6