As with anything of the Wyrd it twists it's users turning them into Fae but most people can't withstand that strain and after a while turn into living bombs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really seems like a Claimed, at least the movie. It's basically what the Seven Conflagarations did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-07-2016, 12:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T05:11:55-07:00","id":965611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=964666#post964666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obadiah Stane is the Iron Monger. There's a special feature on the Blu-Ray of Thor: the Dark World where the REAL Mandarin visits Trevor in prison.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes, but Fae Titles can take the form of completely different people. So You could have a Fae who is both the Iron Monger and the Mandarin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T13:27:20-07:00","id":965834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=965611#post965611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, yes, but Fae Titles can take the form of completely different people. So You could have a Fae who is both the Iron Monger and the Mandarin.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bPretty ballsy move, a Fae taking a name with IRON in it. Also, saying that trauma is what made Stark into Iron Man rings a little false; 95% of superheroes have some form of trauma in their past as motivation.<br /> <br /> Spider-Man: Uncle killed by burglar.<br /> Daredevil: Father killed by mafia/bookies; lost eyesight to chemical spill.<br /> Batman: Witnessed parent's death at the hands of a mugger.<br /> Hulk: Witnessed his mother's death at the hands of his abusive father.<br /> Flash: Father wrongly imprisoned for his mother's murder.<br /> Green Lantern: Witnessed his father's death in a plane crash.<br /> Wolverine: 100+ years of unimaginable hell, starting with seeing his biological father murder the man who raised him.<br /> Green Arrow: Shipwrecked, had to develop survival skills, had to evade drug runners using the island as a base.<br /> Punisher: Witnessed his wife and children murdered.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T14:04:16-07:00","id":965857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=965834#post965834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bPretty ballsy move, a Fae taking a name with IRON in it. Also, saying that trauma is what made Stark into Iron Man rings a little false; 95% of superheroes have some form of trauma in their past as motivation.<br /> <br /> Spider-Man: Uncle killed by burglar.<br /> Daredevil: Father killed by mafia/bookies; lost eyesight to chemical spill.<br /> Batman: Witnessed parent's death at the hands of a mugger.<br /> Hulk: Witnessed his mother's death at the hands of his abusive father.<br /> Flash: Father wrongly imprisoned for his mother's murder.<br /> Green Lantern: Witnessed his father's death in a plane crash.<br /> Wolverine: 100+ years of unimaginable hell, starting with seeing his biological father murder the man who raised him.<br /> Green Arrow: Shipwrecked, had to develop survival skills, had to evade drug runners using the island as a base.<br /> Punisher: Witnessed his wife and children murdered.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So...<br /> <br /> Spider-Man: Beast<br /> Daredevil: Darkling<br /> Batman: Darkling<br /> Hulk: Ogre<br /> Flash: Elemental (Levinquick)<br /> Green Lantern: ...Wizened?<br /> Wolverine: Ogre or Beast<br /> Green Arrow: Wizened?<br /> Punisher: Darkling?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T14:35:30-07:00","id":965875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=965857#post965857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So...<br /> <br /> Spider-Man: Beast<br /> Daredevil: Darkling<br /> Batman: Darkling<br /> Hulk: Ogre<br /> Flash: Elemental (Levinquick)<br /> Green Lantern: ...Wizened?<br /> Wolverine: Ogre or Beast<br /> Green Arrow: Wizened?<br /> Punisher: Darkling?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIf you wanted to shoehorn them all into Changelings, maybe. I'd say most of them fit better as Deviants:<br /> <br /> Spider-Man: Deviant, possible Beast<br /> Daredevil: Deviant, possible Hunter<br /> Batman: Hunter, head of his own Conspiracy<br /> Hulk: Deviant, or Extempore Zeka*<br /> Flash: Deviant*<br /> Green Lantern:*<br /> Wolverine: Deviant<br /> Green Arrow: Hunter, head of his own Compact<br /> Punisher: Slasher, of the Avenger(heh) Undertaking, with a very high Code/integrity rating<br /> <br /> *Power levels vastly exceed upper limits of all known Chronicles of Darkness splats, would fit better in Trinity Continuum.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T15:02:11-07:00","id":965890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=965875#post965875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bIf you wanted to shoehorn them all into Changelings, maybe. I'd say most of them fit better as Deviants:</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that was kinda the point. Other splats would fit them far more accurately. My post was an exercise in Changeling conversion.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T19:36:29-07:00","id":965992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=965857#post965857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So...<br /> <br /> Spider-Man: Beast<br /> Daredevil: Darkling<br /> Batman: Darkling<br /> Hulk: Ogre<br /> Flash: Elemental (Levinquick)<br /> Green Lantern: ...Wizened?<br /> Wolverine: Ogre or Beast<br /> Green Arrow: Wizened?<br /> Punisher: Darkling?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kiths, Assuming 1E:<br /> Spidey as Skitterskulk<br /> Daredevil would probably be a Darkling, but there's not a good Kith for him<br /> Batman would be Lurkglider<br /> Hulk is Gargantuan<br /> Flash: I'd agree on Levinquick, possibly dual-Kith Airtouched for some gross speed-boosting shenanigans.<br /> Green Lantern doesn't fit very well at all. I'd say an Elemental with a force- or light-based Kith, but that's not very good.<br /> Wolverine: I'd say a Hunterheart Beast.<br /> Green Arrow: I <i>guess</i> an Inventor Wizened, but that's a real difficult fit.<br /> Punisher: I'd actually go Bloodbrute Ogre.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T20:19:31-07:00","id":966013,"title":"","content":"Fangs Farnsworth from Wailing Heights is what happens when a Daeva who was super famous in life decides he needs to spend his Requiem being hated by everyone to make up for how easy he had it in life and thus spends his nights playing awful on purpose hipster music in a coffee shop so that he can be hated by all his new vampire hipster buddies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T00:30:45-07:00","id":969067,"title":"","content":"Gems from <b>Steven Universe</b> are totally Prometheans on their Pilgrimage to become humans! Just see this clip ( better whole episode! ):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lDtdH11yxWs\" data-code=\"lDtdH11yxWs\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/lDtdH11yxWs/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Pearl's 'My appearance is conscious manifestation of light' clearly indicate that Gems are made from Divine Fire! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T00:34:54-07:00","id":969069,"title":"","content":"I'd have to object to the &quot;become human&quot; part, though. And they do sort of work better as Demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T00:44:19-07:00","id":969073,"title":"","content":"Whole 'become human' thing comes from Gems rebellion - they wanted to become individuals, make 'their own personal way' ( like Pilgrimage ). And many times do not understand humanity ( like Pearl in this example ). so it's enough 'become human' in my book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T07:56:50-07:00","id":969232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=969073#post969073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whole 'become human' thing comes from Gems rebellion - they wanted to become individuals, make 'their own personal way' ( like Pilgrimage ). And many times do not understand humanity ( like Pearl in this example ). so it's enough 'become human' in my book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Making their own way sounds more Demon than Promethean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9065-darkblade","name":"Darkblade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T08:37:56-07:00","id":969241,"title":"","content":"I definitely think that they work better as Unchained, but the focus on change and understanding are definitely thematically Promethean. I'm with Wyrd, here, they could work as rogue Unfleshed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T22:54:01-07:00","id":969682,"title":"","content":"Eh. I can't really see them as anything but Unchained. Even if we switch Pilgrimage to Identity, they're still more Demon-y: the whole &quot;created by a mechanistic distant power to serve it&quot; is much more Demon than Promethean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T16:45:21-07:00","id":971574,"title":"","content":"The Animal Vendor blogs from tumblr give me a major Changeling vibe. I could totally see Elmer and Seymour as Hobgoblins. Though Seymour's claims of cosmic power make him seem more like an Exarch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T15:08:48-07:00","id":972148,"title":"","content":"Blade Runner is either Changeling or Demon set a few decades in the future.<br /> <br /> If Changeling: Roy Batty and his group of replicants are a motley of Changelings taken by a Keeper known as the Tyrell Corporation (because corporations are people now, right?). Roy's name was Rick Deckard before his abduction. After his escape, Roy saw that his fetch had done too good a job of taking over his old life, so took on the new identity of Batty. While the Deckard fetch doesn't know what he really is, he finds himself particularly skilled at hunting down &quot;replicants&quot; (i.e. changelings) at the behest of Gaff, a Loyalist changeling in service to Tyrell Corporation. While being hunted by Deckard, Roy confronts a manifestation of his Keeper in the form of Dr. Tyrell and manages to defeat him. When Roy and Deckard finally confront each other, Roy merges with his fetch. Roy/Deckard then helps the changeling Rachel escape from Tyrell Corporation. Gaff, impressed with Roy/Deckard, takes pity on the two by giving them time to run before taking up the chase.<br /> <br /> If Demon: The Tyrell Corporation is Infrastructure of the God-Machine. Replicants are demons, and Deckard is an angel tasked with hunting them down. Rachel is a demon that has been recaptured and is in the process of reconditioning. During his final confrontation with the demon Roy Batty, Deckard breaks free of the God-Machine's influence and escapes with Rachel. In this version, Gaff is a normal human who believes the &quot;replicant&quot; cover and allows his friend Deckard to escape once he realizes he's a &quot;replicant&quot;. Because the story is told from the perspective of angels and demons, Gaff's eccentricities (and those of the other characters, like J. F. Sebastian) are merely how they see humanity, which they don't quite understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12354,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12354-who-is-matt","user":"who.is.matt","date":". 09-18-2016, 06:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12354-who-is-matt","name":"who.is.matt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T15:35:04-07:00","id":972172,"title":"","content":"Ferris Beuller's Day Off: Ferris is a Beast, and the entire movie is a hunt with Cameron as the prey. Ferris is an Ugallu Ravager, and over the course of a single day strategically ruin's Cameron's sense of security (and Cameron's father's car) by exposing him to the world outside of Cameron's comfort zone, bringing Cameron the wisdom of acceptance. Principal Rooney is a Hero hunting Ferris, but badly. (Alternatively, Ferris' sister is also a Beast, and while hunting Ferris he made the mistake of encountering Jeannie in her lair.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12354,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12354-who-is-matt","user":"who.is.matt","date":". 09-20-2016, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12354-who-is-matt","name":"who.is.matt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T17:06:41-07:00","id":972218,"title":"","content":"On reflection, I have at last found something Mage can do better than any other splat: provide splats that match the four lead characters of Seinfeld. <br /> <br /> Jerry: Mastigos<br /> George: Moros<br /> Kramer: Acanthus<br /> Elaine: Thyrsus<br /> <br /> Also, I'm calling the above post as the best one in this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T00:22:58-07:00","id":980624,"title":"","content":"I think Birdman is the best accidental adaptation of Mage: The Awakening ever made, since the whole plot of the film works perfectly as a depiction of an Awakening, but I can't figure out what Path Riggan Thomson would end up with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T19:17:51-07:00","id":983682,"title":"","content":"Okay, I take it back - TV series <b>Lucifer</b> is Nemesis Beast, probably Anakim, with some Eshmaki mind powers. He has <i>literally</i> Dark Mother as parent! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( See season two for this plot. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X4bF_quwNtw\" data-code=\"X4bF_quwNtw\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/X4bF_quwNtw/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T19:37:10-07:00","id":983694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=983682#post983682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I take it back - TV series <b>Lucifer</b> is Nemesis Beast, probably Anakim, with some Eshmaki mind powers. He has <i>literally</i> Dark Mother as parent! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( See season two for this plot. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X4bF_quwNtw\" data-code=\"X4bF_quwNtw\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/X4bF_quwNtw/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I still think Lucifer is a demon but yea she is so the dark mother. Hmmmm Maybe the God-Machine when making Lucifer the Dark mother Corrupted him. Being too power to outright destroy currently without the correct things in place banished him into a containment reality till he could be destroyed. The Dark Mother used that moment to make it so he fell into the primordial dream where she made him. All of this as a part of a plan to free her from just a primordial dream into reality","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T14:24:56-07:00","id":984060,"title":"","content":"So Luke Cage is clearly a Deviant, with his thing being his tough skin providing Armor. His drawback is (spoiler ahead, whited out for your protection)<span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">that anything that can punch through his Armor rating can't be healed naturally. </span>Which kind of oversimplifies, but is close enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T01:08:48-07:00","id":986626,"title":"","content":"Has the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phantasm_(film)\" target=\"_blank\">Tall Man</a> been covered yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T01:15:04-07:00","id":986628,"title":"","content":"Pfff, low Wisdom Moros, clearly. Maybe even Silver Ladder Bokor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T01:51:02-07:00","id":986636,"title":"","content":"Double post, sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T14:49:48-07:00","id":987453,"title":"","content":"I'd like to hear your ideas for a few characters.<br /> What would be your take on the Grinch (Personally, I'd go with Anakim Ravager)?<br /> Popeye? Bugs Bunny? Adam Jensen? Letho of Gulet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T16:44:34-07:00","id":987490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=987453#post987453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to hear your ideas for a few characters.<br /> What would be your take on the Grinch (Personally, I'd go with Anakim Ravager)?<br /> Popeye? Bugs Bunny? Adam Jensen? Letho of Gulet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bugs Bunny, I'd put as a spirit or goetic associated with Rabbits and Trickery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T09:29:45-07:00","id":987794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=987453#post987453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to hear your ideas for a few characters.<br /> What would be your take on the Grinch (Personally, I'd go with Anakim Ravager)?<br /> Popeye? Bugs Bunny? Adam Jensen? Letho of Gulet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Grinch? Some sort of goetia or spirit of christmas and hate, maybe magath, but a Beast isn't that far off.<br /> Popeye... Probably some sort of Second Sight Mortal, though the Spinach might be related to the Ascending Ones' elixirs.<br /> Bugs, as Malonkey said, some sort of spirit or goetia too.<br /> Jensen, as a cyborg, just screams Deviant.<br /> And about Letho, every single Witcher, period, no matter who, where from, is a Deviant, full stop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T23:30:53-07:00","id":988154,"title":"","content":"I really like the Popeye - Ascending One idea o.o<br /> Thanks!<br /> What would you make of the Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles? Amalgalm Spirits made from Ninja movie tropes and turtles?<br /> I thought Summer Beasts (Changeling).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T01:27:09-07:00","id":988179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=988154#post988154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like the Popeye - Ascending One idea o.o<br /> Thanks!<br /> What would you make of the Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles? Amalgalm Spirits made from Ninja movie tropes and turtles?<br /> I thought Summer Beasts (Changeling).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe Turtles are probably Deviants.<br /> <br /> \u200bBTW, I started a new <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/986637-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-any-opp-ww-game\">thread</a>, to cover characters who don't fit very well in CofD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T13:12:44-07:00","id":988992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=988179#post988179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bThe Turtles are probably Deviants.</div> </div> </div> </div> Huh. Gotta admit I thought about that, but I don't see it. Unless you change the origin to human, like the tv Series did with splinter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T13:58:29-07:00","id":989009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=988992#post988992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. Gotta admit I thought about that, but I don't see it. Unless you change the origin to human, like the tv Series did with splinter.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWe don't know for sure animals becoming intelligent isn't an option for Deviants.<br /> <br /> Splinter being human first always made more sense to me; rats are smart, but not smart enough to learn Ninjitsu just by watching. For one thing, Ninjitsu is WAY more than a fighting style, it's a way of life; special diets, to build up immunity to various poisons, exercise regimens, stealth techniques... and how would a rat, even one with human intelligence and opposable thumbs, make their weapons? Don's staff is easy, but Leo's swords? And don't get me started on the new movies claim that Splinter could learn Ninjitsu from a <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lIMr7tOLdk0\" target=\"_blank\">book...</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T14:10:09-07:00","id":989012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=989009#post989009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bWe don't know for sure animals becoming intelligent isn't an option for Deviants.<br /> <br /> Splinter being human first always made more sense to me; rats are smart, but not smart enough to learn Ninjitsu just by watching. For one thing, Ninjitsu is WAY more than a fighting style, it's a way of life; special diets, to build up immunity to various poisons, exercise regimens, stealth techniques... and how would a rat, even one with human intelligence and opposable thumbs, make their weapons? Don's staff is easy, but Leo's swords? And don't get me started on the new movies claim that Splinter could learn Ninjitsu from a <a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lIMr7tOLdk0&quot;]book</a>...[/URL]</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I just liked the idea of Changeling Turtles (which would have the same Problem with their Origin I claimed Deviant would have ^^&quot; Talk about biased, huh?) If we simply go by the Alien-super Corp. Chemicals origin, deviant is a great fit, actually.<br /> <br /> OOC: Didn't see the New movie, but that sounds reaaaaally stupid. I actually like the new Comic's idea, having them be reincarnated as former Ninjas. Which got me thinking...<br /> OC again: Is there a way to Portray reincarnation like this in WoD?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":".  grammar 10-17-2016, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T17:11:35-07:00","id":990693,"title":"","content":"Metatton is sort of Promethean-y, in that he's a robot and his backstory involves identity and transition, but the whole &quot;ghost who permanently possesses a robot&quot; doesn't exactly map easily.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Promethean, here are some others. Aigis is clearly one, and for Refinement I would say she started as Argentum (being built to fight shadows) to possibly Aurum, though at least in P3 she comes to terms with not being human. <br /> <br /> I kinda like Raiden as one as well: the &quot;real&quot; Raiden died after MGS2, and cyborg ninja Raiden was made using his remains. If the Metal Gear lore wasn't such a nightmare, I'd say his story makes for an interesting Pilgrimage, in that he goes through a lot of stages regarding his relationship to humanity. He comes very close to becoming human, but in Revengeance he basically decides that being human won't give him the power he needs to protect people, so he ultimately rejects humanity to defend it. I'd say you could call him a sympathetic Stannum or Centimanus eventually, but Lumen or something similar would also work for him. I'd at least advise checking out Revengeance- at the very least, anyone who doesn't think non-humanoid Prometheans are workable needs to meet Bladewolf. <br /> <br /> Ennis fits well, especially since she was actually created by alchemy. She's a great example of a Promethean not on a Pilgrimage who's found peace with her condition. It helps that she has other immortals to hang out with. <br /> <br /> Young Frankenstein features an example of a successful Pilgrimage, in contrast to the original. I'd say that the Creature ends up as more of a Tempered, but you could spin it as him becoming fully human. <br /> <br /> Bender is obviously a Centimanus. <br /> <br /> (I'm trying to avoid being negative or starting up the old arguments, but it is very hard not to notice that none of these stories feature actually becoming human as a plot element, and while making the Pilgrimage more flexible makes me like the game more, I would definitely have rather that actually becoming human, if possible, was extremely rare and dangerous. Oh well, There Is No Canon, so I can just say that it is.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T06:36:42-07:00","id":995172,"title":"","content":"The Accountant<br /> <br /> So after watching the accountant I first thought it was a demon the decent movie but soon I got it that the accountant is not a demon but a <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Fractal</span> and his father was a demon . Any suggestions on the stats ?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://geeknation.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/the-accountant-trailer.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Name: </b>Christian Wolf</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>AKA</b>: The Accountant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Age:</b> 32</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Type:</b> Fractal</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Concept:</b> A highly skilled accountant with even deadlier military training who does accounting work for dangerous people.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Virtue: </b>Completionist - Driven to complete any task before him</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Vice: </b>Violent - Becomes Violent when given task can't be completed</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Mental Attributes: </b>Intelligence 4, Wits 2, Resolve 4</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Physical Attributes: </b>Strength 3, Dexterity 4, Stamina 3</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Social Attributes: </b>Presence 1, Manipulation 2, Composure 3</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Mental Skills: </b>Academics (Accounting, Forensic Accounting) 5, Computer 3, Investigation (Forensic Accounting) 5, Medicine, Occult, Politics, Science (Forensic Accounting) 5</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Physical Skills: </b>Athletics 4, Brawl (Martial Arts) 3, Drive 2, Firearms (Sniper Rifle, Match Grade, Barrett, Long distance, Handgun, Kimber Custom ) 4, Larceny (Money Laundering) 4, Stealth 2, Survival 2, Weaponry (Knife) 2</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Social Skills: </b>Empathy 1, Intimidation 1, Socialize 1, Streetwise (Accounting, Underworld) 3, Subterfuge 1</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Merits: </b>Area of Expertise (Accounting, Forensic Accounting, Sniping), Eidetic Memory, Encyclopedic Knowledge (Accounting), Good Time Management, Interdisciplinary Specialty(Accounting, Forensic Accounting) Investigative Aide (Forensic Accounting), Investigative Prodigy 3, Patient, Professional Training (Forensic Accountant, Solider) 5, Tolerance for Biology, Quick Draw, Allies (Treasury) 3, Alternate Identity 3, Fame (Accounting) 3, Iron Will, Resources 5, Safe Place 3, Striking Look 1, True Friend, Untouchable, Retainer 5 </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Fighting Merits:</b> Close Quarters Combat 2, Firefight 3, Grapple 2, Marksmanship 4, Martial Arts 5,</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Demon Merits: </b>Ambient Aether, Aether Pool, Instinctive Deflection, Sympathetic Demon, Bolthole (Arsenal 5)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Health: 8</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Embeds: </b>Merciless Gunman, Just Bruised, Ambush, Efficiency, Without a Trace, Bystander Effect, Strike First, Check Backdrop, Knockout Punch, Lucky Break</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Interlock: </b>(I could not think of a good interlock.) </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Willpower: </b>7</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Integrity: </b>7</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Conditions: </b>Cataloged</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Size: </b>5</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Speed: </b>12 </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Defense: </b>6</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family: