tps://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T18:00:09-08:00","id":1006488,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar134_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"134\" data-vbnamecard=\"134\">The Kings Raven</a> I haven't read Princess yet, so let me ask you this: would <a href=\"http://starvstheforcesofevil.wikia.com/wiki/Star_Butterfly\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Star Butterfly from Star VS The Forces Of Evil</b></a> work as a Princess? If so, what type would she be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T04:09:13-08:00","id":1006648,"title":"","content":"Danny, from &quot;The Shining&quot; by Stephen King. In the novel he is probably a very young Mastigos Mage with 1 dot in Death (he sees and talks to ghost but doesn't seem to be able to affect them), 1 dot in Fate (he can tell when something bad is about to happen), 1 dot in Space (he can find hidden things very easily) and maybe 1 or 2 dots in Mind (he manages at one point to &quot;persuade&quot; someone to do something).<br /> <br /> \u200bIn the film version, Danny is probably more like a very young and still not very adept Moros, with one dot in Death and Fate.<br /> <br /> \u200bIn &quot;Doctor Sleep&quot;, the sequel to The Shining, Abra Stone is probably an Acanthus or Obrimos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T21:01:09-08:00","id":1007016,"title":"","content":"Having been watching <i>Jojo's Bizarre Adventure</i> a lot recently, I can't help but imagine it as a particularly gonzo Chronicle that transitions from a Hunter game that focuses on hunting vampires to a Mage game. <br /> <br /> Basically, for the uninitiated, <i>Jojo </i>follows members of the Joestar family over the course of generations and the, well, bizarre adventures they have. Parts 1 and 2 revolved around their respective Joestars and their allies using solar-powered martial arts (it's anime, roll with it) to fight vampires, but Part 3 introduced Stands, which are basically (generally) anthropomorphic manifestations of a person's will that grant them supernatural powers. The best part is that Stands are invisible to all but people who possess them, which mirrors Nimbus and Sleepers' inability to process magic. Stands are also given names, which could easily translate to a Shadow Name. The abilities are pretty consistent and predictable, and probably correspond to Praxes. Alternatively, Stand-users could be Proximi, since their abilities often come with severe limitations of applicability. It would be way too long to try and list every Stand and its user, but to give people an idea, here's the first Stand and User we meet in the anime: <br /> <br /> <b><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Yd40iQjYXeM\" target=\"_blank\">Jotaro Kujo</a></b><br /> Shadow Name: Platinum Star<br /> Path: Thyrsus (Life 3, Time 5)<br /> Praxes: Body Control (Life 2), Heightened Senses (Life 2), Honing the Form (Life 3), Transform Life (Life 3), Acceleration (Time 3), Temporal Pocket (Time 5)<br /> <br /> Jotaro's Stand, Star Platinum, starts off with abilities that correspond well to Life magic: super-strength, super-speed, and heightened motor control and senses. His personality is dominant, but he is often cool under pressure and often displays surprising cunning, reflecting the bestial and unrelenting nature of some Thyrsus. Eventually, Jotaro discovers that Star Platinum also has the ability to stop time for the space of a few seconds, and eventually comes to rely on it as his main ability. At this point, Time magic can better represent the super-speed abilities that Star Platinum possesses. One could also make the argument that Star Platinum and all other Stands are actually Spirits, in which case Jotaro has Spirit 4, and Star Platinum is a Rank 2 Hope or Strength Spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T07:41:18-08:00","id":1008530,"title":"","content":"I know batman as a beast has probably been brought up before, but the telltale games version makes it fit even more, with the split between playing as batman and as Bruce Wayne and having to make hard choices that may help one and hurt the other perfectly capturing a beast that needs to balance it's life and legend.<br /> <br /> Also<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Harvey Dent's descent into madness and paranoia, and his blaming all Gotham's problems on Bruce (and Batman depending on what choices you made) after the events at the debate also makes a good example of what happens when a Beast's friend becomes a hero. Lady Arkham is probably a hero as well given what she is willing to do to bring down Gotham's powers that be, including Bruce.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T12:01:22-08:00","id":1009419,"title":"","content":"<b>Seth Brundle \u2013 the Fly</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Virtue: </b>Brilliant; <b>Vice: </b>Eccentric<br /> <b>Aspiration: </b>Find a Cure for his transformation<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 5, Wits 4, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 6, Dexterity 4, Stamina 4<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 2, Manipulation 2, Composure 2<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 2, Athletics 2, Computers 4(Programming), Crafts 4(Electronics), Expression 2, Persuasion 2, Science 4(Teleportation)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Fast Reflexes 2, Iron Stamina 1, Professional Training (Scientist) 4<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 4<br /> <b>Potency: </b>3<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 5<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 8<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 15<br /> <b>Health:</b> 9<br /> <b>Dread Powers: <i>Digestive Bile*</i></b>, Monstrous Resilience, Wall Climb<br /> <br /> <b>Digestive Bile: </b>At this stage of his transformation, Seth can no longer consume solid food. Instead, he must break down the food item beforehand with a digestive enzyme that he vomits forth. In combat, this is treated as a touch attack. Against organic tissue and materials, this is deals 2 points of lethal damage and continues to burn for [Potency] turns.<br /> <br /> <i>Notes</i><br /> For this write up, I am using the Horror rules to show the character of Seth Brundle from the 1986 film <i>The Fly</i>. The above depicts Seth in the later stages of his transformation, where he barely resembles a human anymore and is losing his mind as the primal impulses of the Fly begin to overwhelm him.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T11:46:39-08:00","id":1010283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1007016#post1007016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having been watching <i>Jojo's Bizarre Adventure</i> a lot recently, I can't help but imagine it as a particularly gonzo Chronicle that transitions from a Hunter game that focuses on hunting vampires to a Mage game. <br /> <br /> Basically, for the uninitiated, <i>Jojo </i>follows members of the Joestar family over the course of generations and the, well, bizarre adventures they have. Parts 1 and 2 revolved around their respective Joestars and their allies using solar-powered martial arts (it's anime, roll with it) to fight vampires, but Part 3 introduced Stands, which are basically (generally) anthropomorphic manifestations of a person's will that grant them supernatural powers. The best part is that Stands are invisible to all but people who possess them, which mirrors Nimbus and Sleepers' inability to process magic. Stands are also given names, which could easily translate to a Shadow Name. The abilities are pretty consistent and predictable, and probably correspond to Praxes. Alternatively, Stand-users could be Proximi, since their abilities often come with severe limitations of applicability. It would be way too long to try and list every Stand and its user, but to give people an idea, here's the first Stand and User we meet in the anime: <br /> <br /> <b><a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Yd40iQjYXeM&amp;quot;]Jotaro</a> Kujo[/URL]</b><br /> Shadow Name: Platinum Star<br /> Path: Thyrsus (Life 3, Time 5)<br /> Praxes: Body Control (Life 2), Heightened Senses (Life 2), Honing the Form (Life 3), Transform Life (Life 3), Acceleration (Time 3), Temporal Pocket (Time 5)<br /> <br /> Jotaro's Stand, Star Platinum, starts off with abilities that correspond well to Life magic: super-strength, super-speed, and heightened motor control and senses. His personality is dominant, but he is often cool under pressure and often displays surprising cunning, reflecting the bestial and unrelenting nature of some Thyrsus. Eventually, Jotaro discovers that Star Platinum also has the ability to stop time for the space of a few seconds, and eventually comes to rely on it as his main ability. At this point, Time magic can better represent the super-speed abilities that Star Platinum possesses. One could also make the argument that Star Platinum and all other Stands are actually Spirits, in which case Jotaro has Spirit 4, and Star Platinum is a Rank 2 Hope or Strength Spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div> Kira from Part 4: Diamond Is Unbreakable is definitely a Acanthus Banisher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","name":"Corax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T11:47:20-08:00","id":1010731,"title":"","content":"Santa Claus<br /> <br /> \u200bHe is a True Fae with his own snowy domain in Arcadia. He kidnaps humans en-masse to work as &quot;Little helpers&quot; making toys, for a purpose no one can even fathom. He sometimes travel around in a reindeer sleigh. The changelings who escape from his realm report a hellish landscape of false happiness and childish joy mixed in with horrible suffering as a Little helper (slave) in his Court. He is a rather strong fae and his visage and legend has travelled and taken root in the dreams of children everywhere and thereby rooted itself in western culture as well, but no one knows why he creates so many toys or why he is so fixated with children.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T14:34:53-08:00","id":1010823,"title":"","content":"El presidenti from tropico four is a relatively altruistic seer of the throne who makes dictatorship look good by routinely outwitting the cold war superpowers, while understanding that the best way for a tyrant to stay in power is to keep their people happy enough to not rebel, while using various brainwashing methods just to make sure.<br /> <br /> The Presidenti dynasty from Tropico 5, on the other hand, are an ivory claw bloodline that wound up in control of their own country, the rebels and pirates that they face off against are forsaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T18:43:49-08:00","id":1010893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1010283#post1010283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kira from Part 4: Diamond Is Unbreakable is definitely a Acanthus Banisher.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see him starting out as a Thyrsus. His &quot;make people explode&quot; ability is obviously a Life Unmaking spell, and it's probably a custom Praxis. &quot;Bites the Dust&quot; came after that ability, and it seems to be a combination of Fate and Time magic: the ability sends people back in time, which is the Time 5 Unmaking spell &quot;Corridors of Time,&quot; and the fact that there's a condition on when it take effect is the Fate 2 attainment &quot;Conditional Duration.&quot; So he's a second-degree Master of Life and Time, and has at least 2 dots in Fate. So not only is he a scary-powerful Stand-user, but he's also a scary-powerful mage. Of course, at least mage!Kira would be a little hampered by Paradox, but he's so clever and subtle that he would be smart about avoiding it. <br /> <br /> Banisher works well for him. But Mad also appeals to me, since he's got a very obvious obsession with murdering women.<br /> <br /> Long story short is: some of the Stand-users in Part 4 translate to stupid-powerful Awakened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T15:36:47-08:00","id":1011698,"title":"","content":"How about the Straw Hat Pirates from One Piece? They're a lot like a motley of changelings, with a few very skilled mortals and one hobgoblin (Chopper). The Going Merry could be a Mobile Hollow. Luffy himself would be tough to represent mechanically. I know his Contracts would include Might Of The Terrible Brute (for super strength), Red Rage Of Terrible Revenge (for his Gear techniques) and Chrysalis (for rubbery shapeshifting). He'd also have Epic Iron Skin, Advanced Danger Sense, Advanced Fast Reflexes and a lot of Fighting Styles. His Seeming would probably be Fairest, as he is a natural leader and excellent at making friends. His Kith is up for debate, but I can see it as an unique one tied to the Gum Gum Fruit. Its Blessing would be more powerful than most, at the cost of extra sea related Frailties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T16:29:19-08:00","id":1011729,"title":"","content":"why would chopper even have to be a Hobgoblin? He's humanoid enough to be a changeling<br /> <br /> I would totally peg Usopp as Wizened and Franky as Ogre (though Wizened is also possible)<br /> <br /> Nami might be a Mage though. or just using some sort of Token. And you cannot tell me that Brook is not a Sin-Eater. Zoro's either an Ogre or whatever that minor splat was that represented humans who are just inhumanly, improbably good at one thing for some reason.<br /> <br /> So, would you peg the Yonko as Changeling Monarchs or True Fae? I mean, even Whitebeard technically pressganged the Spade Pirates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T16:59:32-08:00","id":1011745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1011729#post1011729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">why would chopper even have to be a Hobgoblin? He's humanoid enough to be a changeling<br /> <br /> I would totally peg Usopp as Wizened and Franky as Ogre (though Wizened is also possible)<br /> <br /> Nami might be a Mage though. or just using some sort of Token. And you cannot tell me that Brook is not a Sin-Eater. Zoro's either an Ogre or whatever that minor splat was that represented humans who are just inhumanly, improbably good at one thing for some reason.<br /> <br /> So, would you peg the Yonko as Changeling Monarchs or True Fae? I mean, even Whitebeard technically pressganged the Spade Pirates.</div> </div> </div> </div> I am only superficially familiar with One Piece, so I don't know about the Yonko. But the rest of what you said makes sense. By the way, the minor template you're looking for are the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/830824-silly-fun-time-i-am-the-mastah\"><b>Cheaters</b></a>.<br /> <br /> By the way, I just sent you a private message.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T20:07:51-08:00","id":1011804,"title":"","content":"thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T07:02:13-08:00","id":1011999,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><i><b>Luffy</b></i></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Seeming:</b> Fairest<br /> <b>Kith:</b> <a href=\"https://1d4chan.org/wiki/Changeling_Homebrew_Kiths#Clayshapen\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Clayshapen</b></a><br /> <b>Mask:</b> Fool<br /> <b>Mien:</b> Adventurer<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 4, Resolve 6<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 6, Dexterity 5, Stamina 6<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 4, Manipulation 5, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics 1, Crafts 1, Computer 0, Medicine 1, Occult 2, Politics 0, Investigation (Strategy) 3, Science 1<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics (Running) 4, Brawl (Punches) 6, Drive 1, Firearms 0, Larceny 2, Stealth 3, Survival (Hedge) 3, Weaponry 3<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken 5, Empathy (Emotions) 4, Expression (Jokes) 4, Intimidation 3, Persuasion (Leadership, Befriend) 5, Streetwise (Bandits) 2, Subterfuge 0<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area Of Expertise (Strategy, Leadership, Hedge), Danger Sense (Advanced), Fast Reflexes 3 (Advanced), Indomitable (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration\"><b>Epic</b></a>), Interdisciplinary Specialty (Strategy, Leadership, Hedge), Professional Training 5 (Adventurer: Persuasion, Survival, Brawl), Tolerance For Biology, Trained Observer 3 (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration\"><b>Advanced</b></a>), Demolisher 3, Double Jointed (Advanced), Hardy 3, Iron Stamina 3, Parkour 4, Inspiring (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration?p=1088037#post1088037\"><b>Epic</b></a>), Iron Will, Resources 1, Pusher, Sympathetic, True Friend (Straw Hat Pirates), Cheap Shot, Defensive Combat (Brawl), Grappling 3, Iron Skin 2 (Advanced 2, Epic), Martial Arts 5, Unarmed Defense 5, Harvest 3 (Goblin Fruit), Potent Kith 2, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841832-homebrew-changeling-merits\"><b>Wyrd Evolution 2</b></a> (Earthbones, Gargantuan)<br /> <br /> <b>Health:</b> 11<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 9<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 10 (+3 With Unarmed Defense)<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 11<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 16<br /> <b>Wyrd:</b> 7<br /> <b>Clarity:</b> 8<br /> <br /> <b>Contracts: </b>Changeling Fate 2 (Wizened), Cloak Of The Elements 3 (Metal, Fire, Elemental), Dreamsteps (Fairest), Pipes Of The Beastcaller 3 (Beast), Pathfinder 1 (Beast), Might Of The Terrible Brute 2 (Ogre), Chrysalis 5 (Wizened), Red Rage Of Terrible Revenge 5 (Ogre)<br /> <br /> <b>Frailties:</b> Cannot swim (Major Taboo)</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-30-2017, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T16:33:42-08:00","id":1012249,"title":"","content":"How about Arthur Dent and his friends from the Hitchhiker's Guide To The Galaxy? The closest I can think of is that Arthur and Trillian are Fae-Touched (since they don't have Keepers), while Zaphod and Ford would be changelings from Arcadian Realms styled after alien worlds. Zaphod would be a Fairest who's not very good at leadership, while Ford would probably be a Wizened. Marvin would be a Hedgespun automaton. The various aliens are hobgoblins, the Heart Of Gold is a Mobile Hollow and the titular Guide is a Token. If I had to choose a Seeming for Arthur, it would be Elemental. After all, seeing the vastness and weirdness of the cosmos in the way he did really takes your ego down a notch. As for Kith, I'm unsure. Perhaps Airtouched to represent his talent for flying?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T17:20:22-08:00","id":1012274,"title":"","content":"I don't think any of them are more than a bit unusual mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T18:21:49-08:00","id":1012304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1012274#post1012274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think any of them are more than a bit unusual mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well you could argue that Arthur might be a Sleepwalker, considering his surprisingly blas\u00e9 reaction to weird shit. Hell, his entire story might be some kind of Awakening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T18:27:44-08:00","id":1012308,"title":"","content":"ok. I'm fairly unfamiliar with all the CoD Mage stuff, so I'll take your word for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T18:55:25-08:00","id":1012323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1012249#post1012249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about Arthur Dent and his friends from the Hitchhiker's Guide To The Galaxy? The closest I can think of is that Arthur and Trillian are Fae-Touched (since they don't have Keepers), while Zaphod and Ford would be changelings from Arcadian Realms styled after alien worlds. Zaphod would be a Fairest who's not very good at leadership, while Ford would probably be a Wizened. Marvin would be a Hedgespun automaton. The various aliens are hobgoblins, the Heart Of Gold is a Mobile Hollow and the titular Guide is a Token. If I had to choose a Seeming for Arthur, it would be Elemental. After all, seeing the vastness and weirdness of the cosmos in the way he did really takes your ego down a notch. As for Kith, I'm unsure. Perhaps Airtouched to represent his talent for flying?</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of Douglas Adams' work, Dirk Gently seems like a pretty good example of an Acanthus; one who trusts in Fate to much,(low Wisdom) but definitely an Acanthus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T19:10:11-08:00","id":1012333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1012304#post1012304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well you could argue that Arthur might be a Sleepwalker, considering his surprisingly blas\u00e9 reaction to weird shit. Hell, his entire story might be some kind of Awakening.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's an unusual interpretation, but it makes sense. Now I want to write a Mage character inspired by Arthur. I'm unsure of what their Path would be, though. My guess is Acanthus, to represent the unburdening that comes with realizing the absurdity of the world, and the resulting capacity to find humor in it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T19:26:31-08:00","id":1012342,"title":"","content":"Why is it that at least half the Mage suggestions I see in this thread are Acanthi?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T00:35:09-08:00","id":1012431,"title":"","content":"Protagonists tend towards luck and good fortune. They are arguably fated for greatness simply by existing, in more common stories.<br /> <br /> People seem to tend towards Mage for a lot because they have a big toolbox. One 'trick' a character pulls off, for instance Zack Morris' 'Time Out,' can be explained by a rote. Just ignore the rest of the toolbox, and assorted Mage Accessories like Wisdom, for purposes of making the character fit.<br /> <br /> As an added benefit, mages tend to be fairly human. Spider-man's physical abilities, drastically increased strength, agility and durability, could be explained by Vampire's physical disciplines. Mayor Hundred from Ex Machina speaks to machines, effectively using the Command Artifice Gift like a werewolf. But Spider-man goes out in the sun and doesn't usually drink blood, and Mayor Hundred doesn't turn into a hulking wolfman, and these things can't be ignored. However, both of them are fairly human aside from their special abilities, so you could just stick them under Mage, though again ignoring the rest of the game.<br /> <br /> If Deviant doesn't, I'm sure at some point there's going to be a book about having 'random' powers. We've already broached upon it with the Supernatural Merits and microtemplates, as well as Horrors and antagonist-building, but there's some sort of block for players when it comes to just hanging on a strange power to a character.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth, Mayor Hundred would be a Wolf-Blooded of Sagrim-Ur's Blood whose Tell would be their ancestor's markings and ability to command machine spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-05-2016, 03:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T10:38:31-08:00","id":1012663,"title":"","content":"Regarding the Yonko from One Piece<br /> . Big Mom is True Fae, given her fairy tale inspired kingdom and gaining power by forcing others into contracts.<br /> . I see Whitebeard as an extremely powerful Extempore on the refinement of Cuprum. His seeing his crew as his sons is indicative of a Promethean's need for a family.<br /> . Kaido is an Apex Beast from the Anakim family, his Hunger is Ravager. Everyone in the series is terrified at the mere mention of him, he is referred to as the &quot;world's strongest creature&quot; rather than &quot;world's strongest man&quot; and everywhere he goes ruin seems to follow.<br /> .Shanks is an Extraordinary Mortal if you're using Mirrors.<br /> . Blackbeard is the hardest to pin down. Besides his Dark-Dark and Tremor-Tremor powers something is off about him. Characters remark that there is something unique about his body's biology, he's always in the right place at the right time and he also seems to have almost a supernatural knowledge of what's going on. Maybe an Unchained? It would fit in his role as a defector from Whitebeard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11643,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","user":"Corax","date":". 12-05-2016, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","name":"Corax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T10:51:50-08:00","id":1012670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1012663#post1012663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the Yonko from One Piece<br /> . Big Mom is True Fae, given her fairy tale inspired kingdom and gaining power by forcing others into contracts.<br /> . I see Whitebeard as an extremely powerful Extempore on the refinement of Cuprum. His seeing his crew as his sons is indicative of a Promethean's need for a family.<br /> . Kaido is an Apex Beast from the Anakim family, his Hunger is Ravager. Everyone in the series is terrified at the mere mention of him, he is referred to as the &quot;world's strongest creature&quot; rather than &quot;world's strongest man&quot; and everywhere he goes ruin seems to follow.<br /> .Shanks is an Extraordinary Mortal if you're using Mirrors.<br /> . Blackbeard is the hardest to pin down. Besides his Dark-Dark and Tremor-Tremor powers something is off about him. Characters remark that there is something unique about his body's biology, he's always in the right place at the right time and he also seems to have almost a supernatural knowledge of what's going on. Maybe an Unchained? It would fit in his role as a defector from Whitebeard.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like it. question though: How does Whitebeard stop his Disquiet from turning his crew against him?<br /> <br /> And subtly different Covers could definitely explain the ability to contain different Devil Fruits","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T11:01:19-08:00","id":1012674,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Master Aquatosic;n1012670<br /> <br /> I like it. question though: How does Whitebeard stop his Disquiet from turning his crew against him?<br /> <br /> And subtly different Covers could definitely explain the ability to contain different Devil Fruits[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> He's just that badass.<br /> <br /> But seriously though I imagine he's just so inhumanly strong and charismatic he can quell any mutiny through words and strength alone. But yeah by 1st edition rules he should be a captain without a crew. <br /> <br /> I love the idea of Blackbeard assuming multiple Covers to use each of his fruits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","name":"Corax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T15:14:33-08:00","id":1017345,"title":"","content":"Is it just me, or would the Orkz from Warhammer 40000 make some really cool hobgoblins? They even have access to their own type of Hedgespinning, and their Wyrd would be proportional to their Status, to represent the system of &quot;I'm da biggest, I'm da boss!&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T17:58:20-08:00","id":1017412,"title":"","content":"I decided to rewrite my sheet for the Slender Man as an Incarnate Beast. <br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Anakim<br /> <b>Hunger: </b>Prey<br /> <b>Myth:</b> The Mysterious, Ever-Watching Boogeyman<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 5, Wits 6, Resolve 8<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 5, Dexterity 6, Stamina 8<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 8, Manipulation 6, Composure 8<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics 3, Computer 0, Crafts 1, Investigation (Searching) 4, Medicine 1, Occult 4, Politics 0, Science 0<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics (Chasing) 4, Brawl (Claws And Tentacles) 5, Drive 0, Firearms 0, Larceny 0, Stealth (Stalking) 8, Survival (Forests And Woodlands) 4, Weaponry 0<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken 0, Empathy (Fear) 3, Expression (Sound Mimicry) 3, Intimidation (Appearing Out Of Nowhere) 6, Persuasion (Taking People Away) 5, Socialize 0, Streetwise 0, Subterfuge (Evasive) 5<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area Of Expertise (Taking People Away), Danger Sense (Advanced), Direction Sense (Epic), Eidetic Memory (Advanced), Indomitable (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration\"><b>Epic</b></a>), Interdisciplinary Specialty (Taking People Away), Patient (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration\"><b>Advanced 3</b></a>), Trained Observer 3 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration\"><b>(Advanced)</b></a>, Demolisher 3, Double-Jointed (Advanced), Greyhound, Closed Book 5, Iron Will, Retainer (Proxies 3 To 5), Striking Looks 2 (Uncanny), Untouchable, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration/page2\"><b>Untouchable Style 4</b></a>, Hunger Management 3, Spoor 5, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1063048#post1063048\"><b>Wandering Soul 5</b></a><br /> <br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 10<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 14<br /> <b>Speed:</b> ST Fiat<br /> <b>Health:</b> 33 (Effective Size 25)<br /> <b>Lair:</b> 10<br /> <br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> Alien Allure, From The Shadows, Limb From Limb, Looming Presence, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=833241#post833241\"><b>In My Image</b></a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1067535#post1067535\"><b>Inescapable</b></a>, Mimir's Wisdom, Monster From The Deep, Needs Must, Relentless Hunter, Shadowed Soul, Siren\u2019s Treacherous Song, Unbreakable<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> Behold My True Form, Fear Is Contagious, They Are All Around You, Run Away, You Are Not Alone, You Cannot Run, You Can\u2019t Wake Up, You Will Never Rest, Tabula Rasa, You Are Lost, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1086900#post1086900\"><b>You Can't Trust Your Senses</b></a><br /> <br /> <b>Horror Traits: </b>Power 14, Finesse 14, Resistance 14, Size 25, Health 34, Defense 10, Initiative 14, Speed ST Fiat<br /> <br /> <b>Lair Traits:</b> Fog, Maze, Poor Light, Sealed Exits, Diseased (Grave), Disruption, Exposed, Mirages, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/649174-a-new-lair-trait\"><b>Wondrous</b></a><br /> <br /> <b>Beast-Shapes: </b>Legendary Size, One With The Shadows, <i><b>Superior Atavism*</b></i> (Alien Allure, From The Shadows, Inescapable, In My Image, Looming Presence, Needs Must, Siren's Treacherous Song), Unnatural Healing<br /> <br /> <b><i>*Superior Atavism (House Ruled): </i></b>It does not give a free Satiety Expenditure per chapter. Instead, when an Incarnate selects a Superior Atavism, they gain a pool of points equal to their [Lair] to spend on improvisational, narrative effects for that Atavism based on their Myth. Greater effects cost more points, and they may recharge once per chaper per Superior Atavism by spending 1 Willpower point and rolling [Highest Resistance Attribute + Occult + Lair] with Rote Quality. Each Success restores one point of Superior Atavism. The Incarnate restores 1 point even if they fail the roll. When a Superior Atavism faces against another supernatural power, roll for a Clash Of Wills against the Incarnate\u2019s [Highest Resistance Attribute + Lair].","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-02-2017, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence