/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=847701#post847701\"><b>Evolved Form 3</b></a> (Inhuman Strength, Directed Energy Weapon, Wings)<br /> <br /> <b>EMBEDS</b><br /> <br /> <b>Vocal:</b> Eavesdrop, Imagine, Voice Of The Machine<br /> <br /> <b>Instrumental:</b> Call Out, Check Backdrop, Efficiency, Fulcrum Point, Functional Identity, Miles Away, Open Sesame, Read Hostility, Right Tools Right Job, Tag &amp; Release, Turn Blade<br /> <br /> <b>Cacophony:</b> Cause And Effect, Combustion, Cool Heads Prevail, Just Bruised, Knockout Punch, On The Mend, Sabotage, Shatter, Special Someone<br /> <br /> <b>Mundane:</b> Alibi, Authorized, Clothes Make The Man, Deep Cover, Going Native, Homogeneous Memory, Idle Conversation, In My Pocket, Interference, Lost In The Crowd, Never Here, Occam\u2019s Razor, Persistent Legend, Quick Change, Without A Trace<br /> <br /> <b>EXPLOITS</b><br /> <br /> Break To Heal, Behind The Curtain, Context Matters, Devour Infrastructure, Disintegrate, Incendiary, Raze Infrastructure, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=839313#post839313\"><b>Demonic Might</b></a><br /> <br /> <b>DEMONIC FORM</b><br /> <br /> <b>Modifications:</b> Advanced Optics, Armored Plates, Sonic Acuity, Inhuman Strength, Tough As Stone<br /> <br /> <b>Technologies:</b> Blind Sense, Clairvoyant Sight, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=869395#post869395\"><b>Directed Energy Weapon</b></a>, Laser Cutter<br /> <br /> <b>Propulsions:</b> Plasma Drive, Wings<br /> <br /> <b>Processes:</b> Aegis Protocol, Amorphous, Wound Healing<br /> <br /> <b>Defense: </b>12<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 15<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 20<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Health:</b> 14<br /> <b>Primum:</b> 9<br /> <b>Cover: </b>8</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-11-2017, 10:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T18:17:24-08:00","id":1017886,"title":"","content":"Or, you could have Superman as a Beast:<br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Anakim<br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Power<br /> <br /> <b>Legend:</b> Unstoppable<br /> <b>Life:</b> Mild-Mannered<br /> <br /> <b>Lair:</b> His Fortress of Solitude, which has become quite massive over the 70-ish years he's spent as Superman. The central chamber holds the statues of his Kryptonian parents, and has the Exposed, Blazing Light, and Echoing Lair Traits.<br /> <br /> <b>Horror:</b> Clark's Horror, The Last Son of Krypton Kal-El, takes the form of a gleaming demigod with skin of gold (<a href=\"http://vignette3.wikia.nocookie.net/marvel_dc/images/8/8c/Superman_Prime.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20131230001603\" target=\"_blank\">By DC One Million, he's found his Inheritance either in Incarnation or Merger</a>).<br /> <br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> Cyclopean Strength, Dragonfire (manifested as laser eyes), Looming Presence, Needs Must, Titanic Blow, Unbreakable, and Wings of the Raptor<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> Run Away, You Are Alone, and You Deserve This, as well as a couple of Kinship Nightmares picked up from the other Justice League members.<br /> <br /> <b>Kin:</b> With Green Lantern (Obrimos Mage from the Matter and Space--focused Green Lantern Corps legacy), The Flash (Deviant), Aquaman (Wereshark), Cyborg (also Deviant), Batman (Whichever splat you want)<br /> <br /> Superman is a fairly benevolent Beast, who feeds his need for Power by asserting his dominance as protector of Truth, Justice and the American Way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T16:40:22-08:00","id":1018259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1017345#post1017345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it just me, or would the Orkz from Warhammer 40000 make some really cool hobgoblins? They even have access to their own type of Hedgespinning, and their Wyrd would be proportional to their Status, to represent the system of &quot;I'm da biggest, I'm da boss!&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could work, especially since 40K fluff is very explicit that Ork technology shouldn't hold together, let alone work, but it does because the Orks simply <i>believe that it should. </i><br /> <br /> Hm. In that case, the Imperium of Man is some unholy fusion of the Long Night, Knights of Saint Adrian, Knights of Saint George, and the Malleus Maleficarum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T09:07:50-08:00","id":1019276,"title":"","content":"I decided to rewrite my sheet for Jackie Estacado from The Darkness.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Legend: </b>Vicious<br /> <b>Life: </b>Loyal<br /> <b>Family:</b> Eshmaki<br /> <b>Hunger: </b>Prey<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 5, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 4, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 4, Manipulation 3, Composure 4<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics 2, Computer 1, Crafts 1, Investigation 3, Medicine 1, Occult 2, Politics 2, Science 1<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 3, Brawl 3, Drive 2, Firearms (Pistols) 4, Larceny 3, Stealth (Darkness) 4, Survival 1, Weaponry 2<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken 1, Empathy 2, Expression (Leadership, Wisecracking) 2, Intimidation (Physical Threats) 4, Persuasion (Trading Favors) 3, Socialize 3, Streetwise (Mafia) 4, Subterfuge (Hide Emotions) 3<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area Of Expertise (Mafia), Common Sense, Eye For The Strange, Fast Reflexes 3, Interdisciplinary Specialty (Mafia), Investigative Aide (Streetwise), Professional Training 5 (Mafioso: Streetwise, Intimidation, Firearms), Iron Stamina 3, Parkour 3, Quick Draw (Pistols), Barfly, Closed Book 3, Contacts (Hit Men, Drug Dealers, Arms Dealers), Fame 3 (Advanced 1: Frightened), Fixer, Inspiring, Iron Will, Resources 5, Status (Mafia 5), Striking Looks 1, Cheap Shot, Firefight 2, Gunslinger 5, Martial Arts 3, Street Fighting 4, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits\"><b>Dark Walker 3 (Advanced)</b></a>, Hunger Management 3, Legendary Horror 4<br /> <br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 8<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 7<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 11<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 12<br /> <b>Health:</b> 15<br /> <b>Lair:</b> 7<br /> <br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> Alien Mindset, Death Of Light, From The Shadows, Infestation, Limb From Limb, Needs Must, Looming Presence, Relentless Hunter, Shadowed Soul, Unbreakable, Monster Of The Deep<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> All Your Teeth Are Falling Out, Behold My True Form, Fear Is Contagious, Run Away, You Are Not Alone, You Cannot Kill It, You Deserve This<br /> <br /> <b>Horror Traits: </b>Power 10, Finesse 7, Resistance 10, Size 12, Corpus 17, Defense 7, Initiative 11, Speed 22, Influence (Darkness 3, Despair 1), Numina (Awe, Blast, Dement, Drain, Forge Servant, Omen Trance, Sign, Soul Snatch), Essence 25<br /> <br /> <b>Lair Traits:</b> Sealed Exits, Darkness, Engulfing, Exposed, Mirages<br /> <br /> <u><b>Gunslinger (\u2022\u2022\u2022 Or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></u><br /> Prerequisite: Wits \u2022\u2022\u2022, Dexterity \u2022\u2022\u2022, Firearms \u2022\u2022<br /> Your character can reliably hit any target within the short Range of his gun (the latter must be Size 1), but it requires a lot of concentration. By spending 1 Willpower point (which does not add dice) or sacrificing his Defense, he achieves 1 automatic Success on a Firearms roll this turn plus the actual results on the dice and Damage Bonus of the gun. With the 5 dot version, he can also hit targets within medium Range and may upgrade one point of damage into Aggravated, which causes permanent Tilts. He can use this Merit a number of times each chapter equal to Firearms rating. This Merit does not work if the target is behind full cover, unless the character also has Firefight 3, in which case he may combine Gunslinger with the third Maneuver of Firefight.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 05-29-2019, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T17:29:04-08:00","id":1019508,"title":"","content":"I know The Flash probably works better as a Deviant, but does anyone else think he might also work as Changeling? His is Kith is obviously Runnerswift, and with <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841832-homebrew-changeling-merits\"><b>Wyrd Evolution</b></a>, he could boost his Runnerswift Blessing and acquire those of Firetouched and Levinquick. I am unsure if his Seeming should be Wizened or Elemental, though.<br /> <br /> EDIT: He could also be an Obrimos with the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#heading=h.nu07hv65kt3i\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Gold And Silver Caul</b></a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-19-2016, 09:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T18:30:10-08:00","id":1019540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1019508#post1019508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know The Flash probably works better as a Deviant, but does anyone else think he might also work as Changeling? His is Kith is obviously Runnerswift, and with <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841832-homebrew-changeling-merits&amp;quot;]</a><b>Wyrd Evolution</b>[/URL], he could boost his Runnerswift Blessing and acquire those of Firetouched and Levinquick. I am unsure if his Seeming should be Wizened or Elemental, though.<br /> <br /> EDIT: He could also be an Obrimos with the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#heading=h.nu07hv65kt3i\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Gold And Silver Caul</b></a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Elemental - he's more powered by the Speed Force than self-made.<br /> <br /> He might also work as a Proximus or Mage Legacy.<br /> <br /> What about the rest og the current DC show characters?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T18:38:16-08:00","id":1019543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1019540#post1019540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elemental - he's more powered by the Speed Force than self-made.<br /> <br /> He might also work as a Proximus or Mage Legacy.<br /> <br /> What about the rest of the current DC show characters?</div> </div> </div> </div> That makes sense.<br /> <br /> As for other DC characters, I'd say that Wonder Woman is either a Galateid or an <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat\"><b>Empyrean</b></a>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T20:46:17-08:00","id":1020156,"title":"","content":"Here is the Batter from Mortis Ghost's &quot;OFF&quot;, as a Horror. The Gatecrash Dread Power and Occult Sight Numen are courtesy of Reighnhell.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Virtue: </b>Implacable<br /> <b>Vice: </b>Sanctimonious/Straightforward<br /> <b>Aspiration: </b>Purify The World<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 6, Resolve 9<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 5, Dexterity 4, Stamina 9<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 5, Manipulation 1, Composure 9<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 1, Medicine 1, Occult 3, Investigation 3, Athletics (Running) 4, Brawl 3, Survival 2, Weaponry (Baseball Bat) 5, Expression (Zealot) 2, Intimidation (Single-Minded) 5, Persuasion 2, Subterfuge (Hide Motivations) 4<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area Of Expertise 1 (Single-Minded), Direction Sense 1, Interdisciplinary Specialty 1 (Single-Minded), Trained Observer 3, Vice-Ridden 2, Greyhound 1, Iron Stamina 3, Parkour 4, Closed Book 3, Iron Will 2, Table Turner 1, Armed Defense 5, Defensive Combat 1 (Weaponry), Light Weapons 4, Killer Instinct 3 (Advanced 2)<br /> <br /> <b>Health:</b> 14 (Size 5)<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 26<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 9<br /> <b>Initiative: </b>13<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 30 (Species Factor 21)<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 8<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers: </b>Immortal, Gatecrash* (Anything Needed), Know Soul, Legion* (Add-Ons), Natural Weapon 1 (Baseball Bat), Nothing But The Mission*, Numen (Aggressive Meme, Occult Sight*, Pathfinder, Seek, Speed), Purification*, Reality Stutter, Regenerate 3, Surprise Entrance, Swift<br /> <br /> <b>*Gatecrash: </b>A Horror with this Dread Power can open a gateway to other planes of existence (such as the Hedge, Primordial Dream, Shadow, Underworld or Astral Realms). The Horror spends a point of Willpower and makes an appropriate dice pool roll; if successful a gateway into the destination realm opens. The creature can hold the gate open for a number of turns equal to its Potency. Gatecrash can only open a gate to a specific realm, but may be selected multiple times, each time applying to specific Realm.<br /> <br /> <b><i>*Legion:</i></b> The Horror is followed and served by Brief Nightmares of a similar nature. The amount and power of these Brief Nightmares is roughly proportional to the Horror\u2019s Potency. Use the following as a guideline: at Potency 1-3, a few Minions; at Potency 4-6, several Minions and a few Hordes, at Potency 7-9, several Hordes and a few Lone Terrors, at Potency 10, as many Lone Terrors as desired. If killed, replacements come within a few scenes at most. Most Horrors possess a weakness that prevents them from creating or commanding their Legions.<br /> <br /> <b><i>*Nothing But The Mission:</i></b> The Batter is to be treated as if he was a God-Machine Angel for the purposes of his Aspiration. In other words, any supernatural means of making him abandon it automatically fail, and he is immune to Tilts that would make it impossible for him to act (such as Insensate and Beaten Down). He is also treated as having Eidetic Memory, Natural Aptitude, Total Control, Liar\u2019s Tongue and Spoofing (use Composure + Subterfuge).<br /> <br /> <i><b>*Occult Sight:</b></i> The Batter is sensitive to supernatural phenomena. He notices the active use of supernatural abilities within the range of his senses and may make Perception rolls to approximate their distance and direction. In addition, by spending a point of Willpower, he can see through powers of concealment, illusion and deceit with a Clash Of Wills using his Wits + Potency as his dice pool. Lastly, he always knows when he is being targeted by a supernatural power and may mimic the Aura Reading Supernatural Merit using Wits + Potency, but without drawback.<br /> <br /> <b><i>*Purification:</i></b> The Batter has and his Add-Ons have Influence 5 (Purity). The effects of this Influence are up to the ST. However, the following effects are free:<ul><li>He can see and interact with all frequencies of Twilight.</li> <li>His attacks cause supernatural damage.</li> <li>Any Ephemeral Being of Rank 5 or less whose Corpus he fills with Aggravated damage immediately loses all Essence and is thus destroyed for real, and he restores a number of Willpower points equal to the Ephemeral Being's Rank.</li> <li>He could undo a pandemic by finding the patient zero and bludgeoning them to death. Or heal trauma by finding the people responsible and giving them his &quot;treatment&quot;. Perhaps you could add that using the Influence requires the Batter to kill someone.</li> <li>When he Purifies a place, there can be no Anchor, Infrastructure, Resonant or equivalent Conditions there (but may cause the Open Condition for certain Abyssals).</li> </ul><b>Ban:</b> The Batter must have the approval of a higher entity, force or group to progress with purification. Higher in this case does not necessarily mean supernatural or more ethical.<br /> <br /> <b>Ban:</b> The Batter cannot use his Influence on a place without first killing the most important creature representative of that place. If he does so, then the purification occurs without him either taking an action or spending any Willpower.<br /> <br /> <b>Ban:</b> The Batter cannot compromise or deal with problems indirectly; if the Batter gets into a fight, he <i>must</i> Go For Blood.<br /> <br /> <b>Add-Ons:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Best At: </b>10 (Assisting The Batter)<br /> <b>Worst At: </b>2 (Complex Tasks)<br /> <b>All Others Pools:</b> 5<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Assist The Batter<br /> <b>Willpower/Scene:</b> 15<br /> <b>Initiative: </b>8<br /> <b>Defense: </b>6<br /> <b>Speed: </b>35<br /> <b>Size: </b>4<br /> <b>Health: </b>12<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers: </b>Blast, Immortal, Influence (Faith 2, Light 5), Natural Weaponry 1, Numen (Speed), Reality Stutter, Regenerate 3, Twilight Entity</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-26-2017, 09:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T07:08:27-08:00","id":1022313,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Double post, sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 03-24-2017, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T07:21:45-08:00","id":1022321,"title":"","content":"I updated my sheet for Nyarlathotep. The Cipher is courtesy of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.th