Stealth (Plain Sight) 4, Survival 2, Weaponry 3<br /> <br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken 2, Empathy (Body Language) 3, Expression (Speeches) 4, Intimidation (Sudden Seriousness) 7, Persuasion 6, Socialize 2, Streetwise 3, Subterfuge (Propaganda) 6<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area Of Expertise (Psychology, Machines, Speeches), Common Sense, Encyclopedic Knowlegde (Crafts, Science, Occult), Indomitable (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration\"><b>Epic</b></a>), Interdisciplinary Specialty (Psychology, Machines), Professional Training 5 (Persuasion, Subterfuge, Occult), Tolerance For Biology, Trained Observer 3, Vice-Ridden (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration?p=847629#post847629\"><b>Advanced 3</b></a>), Ambidextrous, Iron Stamina 3, Sleight Of Hand, Allies (Anything Needed), Closed Book 5, Contacts (Anything Needed), Fixer, Inspiring, Iron Will, Resources 5, Pusher, Status (Anything Needed), Striking Looks 2 (Sinister), Table Turner, Untouchable, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration?p=848765#post848765\"><b>Untouchable Style 4</b></a>, Defensive Combat (Brawl), Killer Instinct 3 (Advanced 3), Light Weapons 4 (Natural Weaponry), Advanced Form, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=794814#post794814\"><b>Advanced Self-Repair System 5</b></a>, Bolthole (Anything Needed), Consummate Professional (Tempter, Inquisitor), Cultists 5, Efficient Dealer, Electromagnetic Linguistics, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=1022283#post1022283\"><b>Ephemeral Integration 5</b></a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=1074318#post1074318\"><b>Lambda Form 4 + Truly Unchained</b></a>, Living The Lie, Monkeywrencher, Multiple Agendas, Resonance Sensitivity, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=932094#post932094\"><b>Suborned Facility</b></a> (Anything Needed), Subborned Infrastructure 3, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=847701#post847701\"><b>Supernatural Integration 5</b></a>, Terrible Form 4, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=848219#post848219\"><b>Transcend Incarnation (Analyst)</b></a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=956486#post956486\"><b>Supernatural Infiltration 4</b></a>, Versatile Transformation<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Embeds</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Vocal:</b> All of them, maybe take out one or two<br /> <br /> <b>Instrumental:</b> Efficiency, Ellipses, Fungible Knowledge, High Of Birth, Open Sesame, Read Hostility, Right Tools Right Job, Wasted Time<br /> <br /> <b>Cacophony:</b> Cause And Effect, Cool Heads Prevail, Devil\u2019s Advocate, Lucky Break, Just Bruised, On The Mend, Raw Materials, Shatter, Shifty Eyes, Special Someone, Tag &amp; Release<br /> <br /> <b>Mundane:</b> Alibi, Associate And Integrate, Authorized, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=837729#post837729\"><b>Blink Of The Eye</b></a>, Deep Cover, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=855075#post855075\"><b>Face Off</b></a>, Going Native, Idle Conversation, Identity Theft, In My Pocket, Lost In The Crowd, Never Here, Persistent Legend, Quick Change, Without A Trace, You Can Tell Me<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Exploits</b></span><br /> <br /> Affliction, Behind The Curtain, Context Matters, Decoy, Deep Pockets, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=839313#post839313\"><b>Demonic Might</b></a>, Ephemeral Cover, <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=855075#post855075\">Form Of The Beast</a></b>, Hellfire, Hellhounds, Incendiary, Inflict Stigmata, Living Shadow, Rain Of Blood, Rip The Gates, Sermon, Show Of Power, Summon, Swarm, Terrible Avatar, Two Places At Once, Urban Legend, Visions Of Heaven And Hell<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Demonic Form</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Modifications:</b> Claws And Fangs, Huge Size, Sonic Acuity, Tough As Stone<br /> <br /> <b>Technologies:</b> Aura Sight, Clairvoyant Sight, Glory And Terror, Mind Reading<br /> <br /> <b>Propulsions:</b> Phasing, Teleportation<br /> <br /> <b>Processes:</b> Amorphous, Cavernous Maw, Nanobot Composition, Wound Healing,<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Lambda Form: </b>ST Fiat</span><br /> <br /> <b>Defense:</b> 9<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 13<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 16<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Health:</b> 13<br /> <b>Primum:</b> 10 <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Cipher</b></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><b>A Thousand Masks</b></div> <br /> The Crawling Chaos has many faces, and is not bound to only appear in one place at once. By not manifesting its true power through any of its Covers, Nyarlathotep\u2019s masks can act independently. Attacking one of its masks tends to draw its full, terrible attention<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> <i>Alibi</i> and <i>Persistent Legend</i><br /> <br /> <b>Dice pool:</b> Presence + Subterfuge<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Crawling Chaos\u2019s attempt to split its Covers apart draws the attention of the God-Machine. Take the Flagged Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> No effect. The demon may try again (suffering a cumulative -1 for each new attempt).<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> Nyarlathotep may manifest one of its Cover as separate entities. They can interact as normal. If the Crawling Chaos manifests Demonic Form abilities or any of its Covers switch into demonic form the waveform collapses and all the Covers fold back into the demon. By spending a point of Aether, another Cover can be manifested (no upper limit).<br /> These masks are advised to stay apart \u2013 in one another\u2019s presence each exhibits glitches.<br /> Any damage to the Cover rating of any mask ends this power \u2013 that mask is considered Nyarlathotep\u2019s true body, all other masks collapsing into it. The Wave Function Collapse Embed automatically deactivates this power in addition to any other effects, again collapsing all masks into the targeted body.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> All Aether costs are waived. <div align=\"center\"><br /> <b>Dreams Of What Is To Come</b></div> <br /> Sometimes, Nyarlathotep leaves its victims with dreams of the nightmare future that is to come. These visions gradually erode their sanity and open them to the Crawling Chaos\u2019 manipulation.<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> <i>Persistent Legend </i>and <i>Recurring Hallucinations</i><br /> <br /> <b>Dice pool:</b> Manipulation + Persuasion - Composure<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The target\u2019s dreams are protected, somehow, perhaps due to their strong will or some strange benefactor. They are immune to this Interlock for a lunar month.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> No effect. The demon may try again (suffering a cumulative -1 for each new attempt).<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> The power affects targets for a number of days equal to Crawling Chaos\u2019 Primum. The target no longer recovers Willpower when sleeping. The glimpses of madness each night cause a Breaking Point penalised by the number of successes on the demon\u2019s activation roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The target\u2019s will is bent to serve Nyarlathotep. The demon may impose the Obsession Condition on the target, setting whatever vile task it wishes as their Obsession. They must spend a point of Willpower each scene to resist their alien compulsions. <div align=\"center\"><br /> <b>Behind The Mask</b></div> <br /> The Crawling Chaos is merely the herald of incomprehensible forces. A glimpse of its true nature can shred a person\u2019s sanity. Simply looking upon any of its masks can, if Nyarlathotep wishes, shatter a mind.<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> <i>Recurring Hallucinations</i> and <i>Sum of all Fears</i><br /> <br /> <b>Dice pool:</b> Presence + Intimidation - Composure<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Crawling Chaos creates an imperfect vision of horror that only strengthens its target\u2019s will. They receive the Steadfast Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> No effect. The demon may try again (suffering a cumulative -1 for each new attempt).<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> The target takes the Broken Condition and rolls for a Breaking Point penalised by the number of successes on the demon\u2019s activation roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> In addition to the above, the target takes the Madness Condition.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-14-2017, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T07:32:46-08:00","id":1022323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1022321#post1022321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I updated my sheet for Nyarlathotep. The Cipher is courtesy of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar452_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"452\" data-vbnamecard=\"452\">Eremite</a>.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sweet Yog-Sothoth, that's terrifying.<br /> <br /> Then again, this has me wondering what the other Great Old Ones from the Lovecraft Mythos would be. Nyarathotep himself probably could be done as an idigam, along with a bunch of others. Or maybe they're all demons, Exiles, or even angels.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T08:10:39-08:00","id":1022343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1022323#post1022323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sweet Yog-Sothoth, that's terrifying.<br /> <br /> Then again, this has me wondering what the other Great Old Ones from the Lovecraft Mythos would be. Nyarathotep himself probably could be done as an idigam, along with a bunch of others. Or maybe they're all demons, Exiles, or even angels.</div> </div> </div> </div> The point of the entities of the Lovecraft Mythos is that they defy our reasoning. Trying to classify them takes away much of what makes them appealing.<br /> <br /> That being said, you can represent some of them with a combination of the Idigam and Abyssal templates. This was suggested by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1170_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1170\" data-vbnamecard=\"1170\">amechra</a> in a thread about the Yellow King. Take a look at the thread for <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/925972-2e-abyssal-aspects-and-numina\">homebrwed Abyssal powers</a></b> and you'll see what I mean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T08:17:31-08:00","id":1022347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1022343#post1022343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The point of the entities of the Lovecraft Mythos is that they defy our reasoning. Trying to classify them takes away much of what makes them appealing.<br /> <br /> That being said, you can represent some of them with a combination of the Idigam and Abyssal templates. This was suggested by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1170_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1170\" data-vbnamecard=\"1170\">amechra</a> in a thread about the Yellow King. Take a look at the thread for <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/925972-2e-abyssal-aspects-and-numina\">homebrwed Abyssal powers</a></b> and you'll see what I mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>That I agree, on cosmic horror depending on defying our reasoning. But that never stopped the human race, did it? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And thanks for the links.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T11:18:36-08:00","id":1022401,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a> Here's my attempt at writing Nyarlathotep as an Idigam + Abyssal. I chose this Rank because he is essentially a Royal Avatar of Yog-Sothoth and Azathoth.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank:</b> 5<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 14, Finesse 14, Resistance 14<br /> <br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 19<br /> <br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <br /> <b>Defense:</b> 10<br /> <br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 14<br /> <br /> <b>Speed:</b> 33<br /> <br /> <b>Max Essence/Per Turn:</b> 100/15<br /> <br /> <b>Influence:</b> Paradox 5, Technology 5<br /> <br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Twilight Form, Materialize, Discorporate, Realm Gateway (All Realms)<br /> <br /> <b>Numina:</b> Absence Of Life/Mind/Prime/Space, Aggressive Meme, Essence Thief, Implant Delusion, Implant Mission, Mortal Mask, Seek, Terrify, Versatile Energies<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Beastmaster, Call Void Spirit, Colossus, Gauntlet Cloak, Interface, Madness And Terror, Monstrous Resilience, Natural Weaponry 2, Nightmare Plague, Pierce Mind, Reality Stutter, Shifting, Surprise Entrance<br /> <br /> <b>Essence Shaping:</b> Essence Void, Locus Manipulation, One Million Eyes<br /> <br /> <b>Forge Servant:</b> Forge Claimed, Forge Herald, Forge Spawn<br /> <br /> <b>Abyssal Aspects: </b>Affront To Possibility, Deny The Supernal","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-26-2016, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T16:59:54-08:00","id":1022530,"title":"","content":"Been a while since I have done one of these. <hr /><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Blade</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Virtue:</b> Justice; Blade is driven to stop the undead so they can no longer harm mortal society.<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Aloof; Blade is a chronic loner, and is frequently cold, surly and distrusting \u2013 even to proven allies. <br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 4, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 5[8], Dexterity 4, Stamina 4[6]<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 4, Manipulation 2, Composure 4<br /> <b>Skills: </b>Academics 2, Athletics 4, Brawl 5, Crafts 2(Weaponry), Drive 2, Empathy 2 (Detect Lies), Firearms 3, Investigation 3 (Vampires), Intimidation 4, Larceny 3, Medicine 2 (Blood), Occult 2, Science 2, Stealth 4, Streetwise 4 (Black Markets), Survival 2 (Urban), Weaponry 5 (Blades)<br /> <b>Skill Tricks: </b>Athletics (Deadly Accuracy, Size Up), Stealth (Know the Shadows), Weaponry (Cripple, Wearing Weapons)<br /> <br /> <b>Merits: </b>Air of Menace*,Allies 3 (Nightstalkers), Ambidextrous, Anonymity 2,Area of Expertise (blades, detect lies, vampires), Contacts 2 (Medical, Hunters), Danger Sense, Defensive Combat (Weaponry), Encyclopedic Knowledge (vampires), Esoteric Armory 3, Fast Reflexes 2, Fixer, Hardy 2, Indomitable, Interdisciplinary Specialty (vampires), Iron Skin 2, Iron Stamina 2, Iron Will, Language (English; French, Spanish, Russian, likely others), Meditative Mind 2, Quick Draw (Blades), Resources 2, Safe Place 2, Scarred*, Striking Looks 1 (Bad Ass), Style: Armed Defense 5, Style: Close Quarters Combat 4, Style: Heavy Weapons 5, Style: Light Weapons 3, Style: Martial Arts 4, Style: Thrown Weapons 2*, Style: Unarmed Defense 4, Supernatural Resistance 3*, Trained Observer 3, Unseen Sense (Vampires)<br /> <i>*From Hurt Locker</i><br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 5<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 8<br /> <b>Blood Potency: </b>0<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 10<br /> <b>Armor:</b> Kevlar Vest (1/3), Iron Skin (1bashing)<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 9 [11 Celerity]<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 17 [51 Celerity]<br /> <b>Health:</b> 9 [11 Resilience]<br /> <b>Disciplines: </b>Auspex 1, Celerity 2, Resilience 2, Vigor 3<br /> <br /> <b>Special Template \u2013 Daywalker</b><br /> Blade is a \u201cDaywalker\u201d \u2013 exposed to the Vampire\u2019s curse at birth, he has many of the strengths of the undead without suffering their flaws. Like a member of a Ghoul Family, Daywalkers age slower than a normal human, gain the Unseen Sense (Vampires) Merit, and retain the use of their supernatural powers even without any vitae in his body (and may activate Disciplines using Willpower if they so choose).Daywalkers naturally generate vitae at a rate of 1point every 3 days. In addition, a Daywalker can ingest human blood and turn it into Vitae (every 3 points ingested become one point of Vitae). Despite retaining their powers Daywalkers still gain the <i>Deprived</i> Condition when their Vitae pool is empty and gain the <i>Bestial</i> Condition as well. In all other respects a Daywalker is treated mechanically as a Ghoul. A Daywalker\u2019s vitae is sterile, and cannot be used to embrace, ghoul, form vinculum or cause blood addiction.<br /> <br /> <b>Equipment:</b> Blade employs an arsenal of weapons in his hunt. His standard gear consists of a sword (Daywalker\u2019s Sword), 2 heavy pistols, and assorted knives, throwing blades and wooden stakes. He also carries any number of unique and specialized weapons as the situation may demand. For protection he sports a Kevlar vest that protects the chest, back, abdomen and groin as well as a long leather trench coat. <br /> <br /> <b>Daywalkers Sword </b>\u25cf\u25cf<br /> The Daywalkers Sword is an acid etched titanium ninjato style sword. It is laced with silver and has been consecrated to deal deadly wounds to supernatural creatures.<br /> <b>Damage</b>: +3 <b>Initiative:</b> -3 <b>Strength:</b> 2 <b>Size:</b> 3 <b>Durability: </b>4(6) <b>Availability: </b>5<br /> <b>Powers</b><br /> Damage dealt by the Daywalkers Sword is considered supernatural damage.<br /> <b><i>Trapped Grip: </i></b> The grip of the sword is set with a trap designed to maul the unwary. The trap may be armed or deactivated with a simple switch. While the weapon is armed, anyone that grips the hilt makes a Wit+ Larceny roll at a -2 penalty. If successful they can disarm the trap or discard the sword. Failing the roll inflicts 2 points of lethal damage and the <i>Arm Wrack</i> tilt.</span> <hr /><br /> <b><i>Notes:</i></b><i> This version of Blade is a blend of the character as depicted in the films, with some of the comic\u2019s version and VtR style vampire mechanics.</i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T17:11:35-08:00","id":1022535,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4443_5.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4443\" data-vbnamecard=\"4443\">GibberingEloquence</a> What Lambdas did Nyarlathotep incorporate for his/its Evolved Form abilities?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T17:41:09-08:00","id":1022550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1022535#post1022535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4443_5.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4443\" data-vbnamecard=\"4443\">GibberingEloquence</a> What Lambdas did Nyarlathotep incorporate for his/its Evolved Form abilities?</div> </div> </div> </div> For Claws And Fangs, he used Demonic Might + Shatter + Hellfire. This allows him to mimic the Claws Of The Unholy Merit from Vampire 2ED for one turn by spending 1 Aether.<br /> <br /> For Glory And Terror, he used Visions Of Hell + Sum Of All Fears + Affliction. It gives him 8 Again on all Intimidate rolls using that Technology.<br /> <br /> For Teleportation, he used Behind The Curtain + Two Places At Once. It allows him to Teleport outside of his line of sight within a radius of Priimum x 2 miles by spending 1 Willpower point.<br /> <br /> For Amorphous, he used Quick Change + Face Off + Form Of The Beast. This allows him to use that Process without assuming Full Demonic Form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-26-2016, 08:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T18:29:26-08:00","id":1022565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1019540#post1019540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Elemental - he's more powered by the Speed Force than self-made.<br /> <br /> He might also work as a Proximus or Mage Legacy.<br /> <br /> What about the rest og the current DC show characters?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Oliver Queen/Green Arrow is a pretty standard Hunter.<br /> <br /> Ra's Al Ghul <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">(and White Canary)</span> is probably a Deviant, with immortality as his main power and his Scars making him violently insane. Slade could fit there, too.<br /> <br /> All the metahumans fit as Deviants, for that matter.<br /> <br /> Damien Darhk is a Left-Handed Moros Mage, while Alchemy is probably an Obrimos, with some Life and Fate peppered in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T03:24:42-08:00","id":1022675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1022565#post1022565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, Oliver Queen/Green Arrow is a pretty standard Hunter.<br /> <br /> Ra's Al Ghul <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">(and White Canary)</span> is probably a Deviant, with immortality as his main power and his Scars making him violently insane. Slade could fit there, too.<br /> <br /> All the metahumans fit as Deviants, for that matter.<br /> <br /> Damien Darhk is a Left-Handed Moros Mage, while Alchemy is probably an Obrimos, with some Life and Fate peppered in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Darhk seems more limited than a full Mage - Proximus, or maybe a Relic Adept seems more fitting (based solely on the show's version, of course).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T03:32:10-08:00","id":1022677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1022550#post1022550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> For Claws And Fangs, he used Demonic Might + Shatter + Hellfire. This allows him to mimic the Claws Of The Unholy Merit from Vampire 2ED for one turn by spending 1 Aether.<br /> <br /> For Glory And Terror, he used Visions Of Hell + Sum Of All Fears + Affliction. It gives him 8 Again on all Intimidate rolls using that Technology.<br /> <br /> For Teleportation, he used Behind The Curtain + Two Places At Once. It allows him to Teleport outside of his line of sight within a radius of Priimum x 2 miles by spending 1 Willpower point.<br /> <br /> For Amorphous, he used Quick Change + Face Off + Form Of The Beast. This allows him to use that Process without assuming Full Demonic Form.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, if he's using Demonic Might, he barely needs Shatter (unless ignoring 4-5 Durability <i>and</i> adding Primum to the attack roll just isn't enough). Since, unless it is a 3rd Order Lambda, Claw And Fangs should be included in there somewhere, you could drop one or the other.<br /> <br /> The Glory And Terror mod is just mean.<br /> <br /> For Amorphous, does he really care about clothes (Quick Change) at this point?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T00:35:30-08:00","id":1023614,"title":"","content":"How about Marvel's Thor? The closest fit I can think of is an <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat\"><b>Empyrean</b></a>, but I'd like to know if there is a canon splat that works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T01:32:53-08:00","id":1023626,"title":"","content":"Claimed by the Thunderer. Except more PG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T01:41:49-08:00","id":1023629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1023626#post1023626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Claimed by the Thunderer. Except more PG.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's the Royal Avatar from page 28 of Summoners, right? That makes a lot of sense. If Thor is a benevolent Claimed, what would Loki be? My hunch is a Mastigos, but his nature as a Frost Giant suggests he is something more. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T01:57:49-08:00","id":1023633,"title":"","content":"Mage is the go to, so sure.<br /> <br /> You could also play on Red Wolf's link to Loki and have him be a royal avatar of a powerful being, something that's been done in the Ultimates universe the movies are based on. Or you could have him be one of the L'Enfant Diabolique. It fits his powers and background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T03:02:17-08:00","id":1023643,"title":"","content":"What about Spawn and The Mask?<br /> Spawn made me think Sin-Eater, with the Suit being his Geist. Beast could work, too, to a degree.<br /> The Mask could be a very powerful item, like a 9-dot Token or something. Other ideas?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T03:11:16-08:00","id":1023645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1023643#post1023643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about Spawn and The Mask? Spawn made me think Sin-Eater, with the Suit being his Geist. Beast could work, too, to a degree. The Mask could be a very powerful item, like a 9-dot Token or something. Other ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div> Dave Brookshaw said that Spawn could be a Deviant in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=946593#post946593\"><b>this post.</b></a><br /> <br /> Loki's Mask could be a Relic containing a Rank 5 spirit of mischief that is the Royal Avatar of Rank 6+ entity. Whoever wears the Mask is Claimed by said spirit. It could also be a Title of a True Fae in Prop form that turns you into a pseudo True Fae.<br /> <br /> I made stats for the Claimed version. What do you think? I just couldn't think of a Bane. Perhaps an item blessed by a powerful Helion, since that type of spirit tends to be steadfast and unchanging, as opposed to mercurial and deceitful?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Attribute Bonuses:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> +5 Strength, +3 Presence, +2 Intelligence, +3 Dexterity, +7 Manipulation, +5 Wits, +5 Stamina, +2 Composure, +3 Resolve. These increase derived traits and may bring the Attributes beyond 10 dots.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Maximum Essence/Per Turn:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> 50/15</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Influences:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Mischief 5 (May Be Used To Create Equipment, Weapons, Firearms And Temporary Skill Dots)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Armored Hide 3, Leap, Monstrous Resilience, Numen (Drain, Essence Thief, Hallucination, Mortal Mask, Speed), Reality Stutter, Regenerate 5, Swift, Unbreakable</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Indomitable (</span></span></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration\"><b>Advanced</b></a><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">), Vice-Ridden (Mischievous), Ambidextrous, Crack Driver 3, Demolisher 3, Double Jointed (Advanced), Fleet Of Foot 3, Iron Stamina 3, Parkour 4, Sleight Of Hand, Stunt Driver 3, Barfly, Closed Book 4, Fast-Talking 5, Iron Will, Pusher, Striking Looks 2 (Cartoonish), Table Turner, Cheap Shot, Heavy Weapons 5, Martial Arts 4</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <i>Liar's Tongue</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> - Same as the one of the Unchained (Demon: The Descent, Pages 182-183)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <i>Fiendish Deceit</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> - Gain an Interdisciplinary Specialty with Area Of Expertise for Mischief. Anytime this Specialty might apply to a roll, you may spend 1 Essence to give it 8 Again. You suffer no untrained penalties for Skills you do not have, as long as you use them for mischief.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <i>Tazmanian Whirlwind</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> - Spend 1 Essence and roll Stamina + Athletics. You inflict the Heavy Winds Environmental Tilt around yourself with an intensity equal to Successes for one turn, capping at intensity 5. The Essence cost may be paid again on subsequent turns to keep this power activate.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <i>Incite Bedlam</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> - Same as the one of the Lost, spending Essence instead of Glamour and using Rank instead of Wyrd.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Ban:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Can only be used at night.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-30-2016, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T03:16:47-08:00","id":1023649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1023645#post1023645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Dave Brookshaw said that Spawn could be a Deviant in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=946593#post946593\"><b>this post.</b></a><br /> <br /> Loki's Mask could be a Relic containing a Rank 5 spirit of mischief that is the Royal Avatar of Rank 6+ entity. Whoever wears the Mask is Claimed by said spirit. It could also be a Title of a True Fae in Prop form that turns you into a pseudo True Fae.<br /> <br /> I made stats for the Claimed version. What do you think?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Attribute Bonuses:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> +5 Strength, +3 Presence, +2 Intelligence, +3 Dexterity, +7 Manipulation, +5 Wits, +5 Stamina, +2 Composure, +3 Resolve. These increase derived traits and may bring the Attributes beyond 10 dots.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Maximum Essence/Per Turn:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> 50/15</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Influences:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Mischief 5 (May Be Used To Create Equipment, Weapons, Firearms And Temporary Skill Dots)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Armored Hide 3, Leap, Monstrous Resilience, Numen (Drain, Essence Thief, Hallucination, Mortal Mask, Speed), Reality Stutter, Regenerate 5, Swift, Unbreakable</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Indomitable (</span></span></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration\"><b>Advanced</b></a><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">), Vice-Ridden (Mischievous), Ambidextrous, Crack Driver 3, Demolisher 3, Double Jointed (Advanced), Fleet Of Foot 3, Iron Stamina 3, Parkour 4, Sleight Of Hand, Stunt Driver 3, Barfly, Closed Book 4, Fast-Talking 5, Iron Will, Pusher, Striking Looks 2 (Cartoonish), Table Turner, Cheap Shot, Martial Arts 4</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <i>Liar's Tongue</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> - Same as the one of the Unchained (Demon: The Descent, Pages 182-183)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <i>Fiendish Deceit</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> - Gain an Interdisciplinary Specialty with Area Of Expertise for Mischief. Anytime this Specialty might apply to a roll, you may spend 1 Essence to give it 8 Again. You suffer no untrained penalties for Skills you do not have, as long as you use them for mischief.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <i>Tazmanian Whirlwind</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> - Spend 1 Essence and roll Stamina + Athletics. You inflict the Heavy Winds Environmental Tilt around yourself with an intensity equal to Successes for one turn, capping at intensity 5. The Essence cost may be paid again on subsequent turns to keep this power activate.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <i>Incite Bedlam</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> - Same as the one of the Lost, spending Essence instead of Glamour and using Rank instead of Wyrd.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Ban:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Can only be used at night.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I like it a lot! I'd bump it up a bit in regards to Rank since the Comic version of the Mask was more powerful than the one in the movie, but I feel like your writeup reflects the movie version perfectly!<br /> <br /> Thanks, haden't seen Dave's post on that. At first I was &quot;Naaaah, Spawn is really really powerful!&quot; but thinking back on the story, considering the limitations and the price of using them... Scars really sounds like the perfect mechanism for that!<br /> So, what about the Violator? Read: &quot;The Evil Fat Clown Demon&quot; ^^ Inferno Demon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T03:33:45-08:00","id":1023651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1023649#post1023649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like it a lot! I'd bump it up a bit in regards to Rank since the Comic version of the Mask was more powerful than the one in the movie, but I feel like your writeup reflects the movie version perfectly!<br /> <br /> Thanks, haden't seen Dave's post on that. At first I was &quot;Naaaah, Spawn is really really powerful!&quot; but thinking back on the story, considering the limitations and the price of using them... Scars really sounds like the perfect mechanism for that!<br /> So, what about the Violator? Read: &quot;The Evil Fat Clown Demon&quot; ^^ Inferno Demon?</div> </div> </div> </div> The problem with raising the Rank of the spirit within Loki's Mask is that it is already Rank 5. Entities of Rank 6+ are too powerful and distant to bother with Claiming people personally. They create Royal Avatars precisely for that sort of task.<br /> <br /> The Violator could be a Deviant as well. His clown form is just a disguise, after all. Dave said that Deviants will have access to a Variation that lets them appear human at the cost of turning off most of their powers. To quote him: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The way we're currently handling it is not to have a supermode like Demon and Changeling2e; rather, there will be a variation that supresses other variations while active, along with their scars. When that power turns off, your true form reppears. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Or, put another way, Bruce Banner does not have a Variation of &quot;grow big and green when angry&quot;. Hulk has a Variation of &quot;turn off size increase and strength increase, with their associated beserk rage and inhuman appearance scars, as long as you remain calm.&quot;</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-29-2016, 06:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T06:33:22-08:00","id":1023723,"title":"","content":"I think Deadpool might work as a Deviant, but while we wait for that book, would it make sense to write him up as an Ashwood Abbey Hunter with low Integrity who signed up for a Cheiron experiment? He's a hero in name only more often than not. It seems like he'd be the type who would hunt monsters for fun and money first and foremost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T06:56:39-08:00","id":1023736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1023723#post1023723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Deadpool might work as a Deviant, but while we wait for that book, would it make sense to write him up as an Ashwood Abbey Hunter with low Integrity who signed up for a Cheiron experiment? He's a hero in name only more often than not. It seems like he'd be the type who would hunt monsters for fun and money first and foremost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Experimental Thaumatech that gives him insane (heh) regeneration? Side effects, limited supply, or followup &quot;incident&quot; means Cheiron can't replicate it easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T08:07:35-08:00","id":1023766,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i><b>Deadpool</b></i></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Virtue: </b>Cunning<br /> <b>Vice: </b>Loudmouthed/Hedonistic<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 4, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 4, Dexterity 5, Stamina 6<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics 2, Crafts (Arsenal Maintenance, Explosives) 3, Computer 2, Medicine 2, Occult 1, Politics 1, Investigation (Marks) 3, Science 2<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 4, Brawl 4, Drive 2, Firearms (Pistols) 5, Larceny 2, Stealth (Shadowing) 4, Survival 2, Weaponry (Swords) 5<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken 1, Empathy 1, Expression (Humor) 3, Intimidation (Batshit Crazy) 3, Persuasion 3, Socialize 0, Streetwise 3, Subterfuge (Fast Talking) 3<br /> <br /> <b>Skill Tricks:</b> Computer (No Internet Footprint), Firearms (Trick Shot), Stealth (Backstab), Weaponry (Butcher), Streetwise (Dark Underbelly Of The City)<br /> <br /> <b>Merits: </b>Area Of Expertise (Humor, Batshit Crazy), At Any Cost, Danger Sense, Fast Reflexes 3 (Advanced), Indomitable, Interdisciplinary Specialty (Batshit Crazy), Language (Japanese, German, Spanish, Among Others), Living With Death 4, Patient, Professional Training 5 (Hit Man: Stealth, Weaponry, Firearms), Tolerance For Biology, Trained Observer, Vice-Ridden, Ambidextrous, Demolisher 2, Fleet Of Foot 2, Hardy 3, Iron Stamina 3, Parkour 4, Quick Draw (Pistols, Swords), Allies (X-Men 3), Alternate Identity 3, Anonymity 4, Closed Book 3, Contacts (Hunters, Black Market), Fixer, Iron Will, Resources 4, Retainer 3 (BOB, Agent Of Hydra), Safe Place 3, Status (Ashwood Abbey 3), Striking Looks 2 (Testicle With Teeth), Table Turner, Untouchable, Healing Factor*, Cheap Shot, Close Quarter Combat 3, Defensive Combat (Weaponry), Fighting Finesse (Swords), Firefight 2, Iron Skin 2 (Advanced 2), Light Weapons 4, Marksmanship 4, Martial Arts 4, Shiv 2, Two Weapons Fighting 4<br /> <br /> *Deadpool heals one bashing damage each turn, one lethal each minute and one aggravated each hour. Whatever Tilts he receives go away once the damage is healed, including lost limbs and organs. His Stamina goes beyond normal limits, which gives him 1 Reversal Point as described on page 17 of Mage: The Awakening \u2013 Imperial Mysteries. He receives 8 Again when rolling to resist the effects of drugs, diseases and poisons, and their Toxicity rating is halved round down. He can live for centuries without suffering any infirmity. <br /> <br /> <b>Defense:</b> 8 (9 With Swords)<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 11<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 16<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 8 [Risking Willpower]<br /> <b>Health:</b> 11<br /> <b>Conviction:</b> 6<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 4</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 01-06-2017, 01:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T08:28:16-08:00","id":1023775,"title":"","content":"Shouldn't he get the Immortal Dread Power as well? He's pretty hard to kill, really. And maybe &quot;Common Sense&quot; to represent his 4th-Wall-Breaking knowledge.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T09:40:03-08:00","id":1023824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1023775#post1023775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shouldn't he get the Immortal Dread Power as well? He's pretty hard to kill, really. And maybe &quot;Common Sense&quot; to represent his 4th-Wall-Breaking knowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div>His immortality was a curse placed upon him by Thanos when he found that Deadpool was Death's love interest. You would need a similarly powerful entity in the COD to make him truly immortal, probably an Archmage. As for his Fourth Wall Awareness, that's not a Merit, just a roleplay consideration. I assume his other traits are fitting?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T22:48:03-08:00","id":1024124,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i><b>Conan</b></i></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Life:</b> Honor<br /> <b>Legend: </b>Barbarian<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 4, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 6, Dexterity 4, Stamina 5<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 4, Manipulation 3, Composure 4<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics (Tactics And Strategy) 3, Crafts 2, Enigmas 2, Medicine 2, Occult 2, Politics 0, Investigation (Beasts) 3, Science 1<br /> <br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 5, Brawl 4, Ride 3, Archery 4 (Long Bow), Larceny 4, Stealth (Shadowing) 3, Survival (Hunting) 3, Weaponry (Great Sword) 5<br /> <br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken 2, Empathy 2, Expression (Leadership) 4, Intimidation (Violence) 4, Persuasion 3, Socialize (Taverns) 3, Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 3<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Epic Potential (Strength), Area Of Expertise (Tactics And Strategy), At Any Cost, Common Sense, Danger Sense (Advanced), Direction Sense, Eye For The Strange, Fast Reflexes 3, Indomitable (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration\"><b>Epic</b></a>), Interdisciplinary Specialty (Tactics And Strategy), Language (Several), Professional Training 5 (Mercenary: Weaponry, Intimidation, Larceny), Tolerance For Biology, Trained Observer 3, Demolisher 3, Fleet Of Foot 3, Giant, Hardy 3, Greyhound, Iron Stamina 3, Parkour 4, Punch Drunk, Quick Draw (Great Sword, Bow), Relentless, Seizing The Edge, Allies (Pirates 5), Barfly, Closed Book 3, Cohesive Unit 5, Contacts (Merchants, Mercenaries), Inspiring, Iron Will, Resources 3, Striking Looks 2 (Strong), Bowmanship 4, Brute Force 1, Combat Archery 5, Heavy Weapons 5, Iron Chin 4, Iron Skin 2 (Advanced 2), Martial Arts 4, Relentless Assault 5, Strength Performance 4<br /> <br /> <b>Health: </b>15<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 9<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 12<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 11<br /> <b>Speed: </b>33<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 6<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1300357-homebrew-playable-heroes-as-a-hurt-locker-style-micro-template\"><b>Destiny:</b></a> 4<br /> <b>Gifts:</b> Champion\u2019s Endurance 4, Chosen Blade x 2 (Great Sword, Long Bow), Kinslayer, Legendary Hunter, Open Gate 3, Vanquisher\u2019s Strength 4, Warrior\u2019s Speed 3, Beowulf's Fury, Dragon Slayer 4</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 05-24-2019, 12:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T23:06:12-08:00","id":1024128,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4443_5.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4443\" data-vbnamecard=\"4443\">GibberingEloquence</a>, okay, Conan is the Beast - but what's his Horror?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T23:10:54-08:00","id":1024132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1024128#post1024128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4443_5.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4443\" data-vbnamecard=\"4443\">GibberingEloquence</a>, okay, Conan is the Beast - but what's his Horror?</div> </div> </div> </div> What? No, he's a Hero. Take another look at his sheet. See that he has Gifts but no Atavisms, Nightmares or Lair? I got the idea of making him a Hero from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/595179-beast-inspiration?p=595881#post595881\"><b>this post</b></a>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T23:12:20-08:00","id":1024133,"title":"","content":"I believe in this Conan is the Hero, though I'm not sure which source material we're going off of. He's more of a wandering rogue, which could be a Collector Beast. He doesn't really have any irrational hatred of monsters or evil sorcerers. He tends to go after them when they've screwed him over, or bump into them while he's trying to steal their treasure.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Having read the reasoning, I'd still have to disagree, though it's sort of understandable because they're mixing various media, most of which depict him differently. Thulsa Doom, in that movie, would probably be a Seer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-30-2016, 02:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T23:21:19-08:00","id":1024136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1024133#post1024133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe in this Conan is the Hero, though I'm not sure which source material we're going off of. He's more of a wandering rogue, which could be a Collector Beast. He doesn't really have any irrational hatred of monsters or evil sorcerers. He tends to go after them when they've screwed him over, or bump into them while he's trying to steal their treasure.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, I admit my research wasn't very deep. I just read some Dark Horse Comics featuring him.<br /> <br /> You are right that he doesn't have an irrational hatred of monsters. That's a characteristic of the typical Heroes, who have Integrity 4 or less. I gave him Integrity 6 to represent how he is more stable than the rest.<br /> <br /> Would you change any of his traits?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-30-2016, 02:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T23:25:31-08:00","id":1024137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1024136#post1024136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you change any of his traits?</div> </div> </div> </div>Athletics 5 is a given. Probably one less Occult, one more Larceny, another Subterfuge. I don't always agree with the game lines but you're very good at statting out fictional characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T23:30:46-08:00","id":1024138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1024137#post1024137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Athletics 5 is a given. Probably one less Occult, one more Larceny, another Subterfuge. I don't always agree with the game lines but you're very good at statting out fictional characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the compliment. I'll add those changes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T15:15:43-08:00","id":1024514,"title":"","content":"What type of splat would characters from the metal gear solid series fall under ?<br /> <br /> So far I feel like Quiet from the new MGS V is a fractal with demonic parts installed into her. Well I guess you could say that all the Skull Units are like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T15:31:54-08:00","id":1024521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1024514#post1024514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What type of splat would characters from the metal gear solid series fall under ?<br /> <br /> So far I feel like Quiet from the new MGS V is a fractal with demonic parts installed into her. Well I guess you could say that all the Skull Units are like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Deviant?<br /> <br /> Speaking of MGS, Reighnhell wrote stats for <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=633927#post633927\"><b>Solid Snake</b></a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=635456#post635456\"><b>Psycho Mantis</b></a>.<br /> <br /> Since we're discussing video games, how about Dante from Devil May Cry? Really skilled Lucifuge Hunter with Dread Powers and Relic weapons, or a Deviant?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T16:10:13-08:00","id":1024534,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Metal Gear</b><br /> <br /> The first group are the characters that are Mortal (or mostly Mortal). For these I would recommend using the Extraordinary Mortals and Conviction Rules from WoD: Mirrors. Depending on character they may have access to certain &quot;Endowment&quot; merits.<br /> Big Boss, Solid Snake (as well as Liquid and Solidus), as well as any character that are shown to be extraordinarily talented, but lacking in superhuman/supernatural abilities.<br /> <br /> The next group demonstrates some degree of supernatural ability (such as Vulcan Ravens reputed shamanic abilities, or the psychic powers of Colonel Volgin or Psycho Mantis). These characters would have access to more Supernatural Merits or more blatantly supernatural Endowments. Depending on characters, minor templates such as &quot;Slasher&quot; could also be appropriate.<br /> <br /> The last group are the blatantly superhuman characters. Cyborgs (Raiden, Grey Fox, and the cyborg warriors shown in MGR) as well as the Nanomachine enhanced Vamp and Senator Armstrong would likely be Deviants (hard to say since we know little about Deviant at this point). This characters could also be represented by the more extreme minor templates and Endowments.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T17:47:51-08:00","id":1024585,"title":"","content":"I'm current working on Stating out Quiet. I will post when I'm done","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T05:48:22-08:00","id":1024730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1024521#post1024521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since we're discussing video games, how about Dante from Devil May Cry? Really skilled Lucifuge Hunter with Dread Powers and Relic weapons, or a Deviant?</div> </div> </div> </div>Due to his backstory and lack of drawbacks In Regards To His powers, I'd agree more with a powerful lucifuge than a deviant.<br /> What would he be like, stat-wise, though? High Weaponry, Fire arms and athleticism, obviously, and some occult and investigation. I Could not place any social skills apart from intimidation, maybe. High regeneration, strength, Speed and hp too, are a must. Definitely Ambidextrous and Gunslinger.<br /> Also, which Version, since DMC, 2 and 3 are very very different from each other?<br /> <br /> No books at Hand atm sadly, so cannot look up fitting abilities/merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 12-31-2016, 08:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T11:13:27-08:00","id":1024841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1024730#post1024730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Due to his backstory and lack of drawbacks In Regards To His powers, I'd agree more with a powerful lucifuge than a deviant.<br /> What would he be like, stat-wise, though? High Weaponry, Fire arms and athleticism, obviously, and some occult and investigation. I Could not place any social skills apart from intimidation, maybe. High regeneration, strength, Speed and hp too, are a must. Definitely Ambidextrous and Gunslinger.<br /> Also, which Version, since DMC, 2 and 3 are very very different from each other?<br /> <br /> No books at Hand atm sadly, so cannot look up fitting abilities/merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with those traits, except Gunslinger. 2ED has removed the idea of multiple attacks per turn. However, Ebony &amp; Ivory are capable of autofire, so it's not a big deal.<br /> <br /> Do you mind explaining the differences between DMC 2 and 3? I am only superficially familiar with the series.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T14:01:48-08:00","id":1024892,"title":"","content":"<i><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Bayonetta</span></b></i><br /> <br /> Her relationship between Angels and Demons would have to be changed. I'd say that the Angels would be powerful and arrogant spirits operating as Balder's personal Choir that takes advantage of human beliefs. The Demons would be powerful spirits as well, but they'd be the purer, no-bullshit sort that can make deals but aren't anyone's slaves, which is why Bayonetta likes them more. Her Wicked Weaves and Witch Time are part of her Legacy Attainments, so there is no danger of Dissonance/Paradox/Quiescence. Otherwise, she'd get torn apart by Paradox for pulling off all those over the top stunts. The Physical Attributes between parentheses were acquired through Honing The Form.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Virtue:</b> Loyal<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Aloof<br /> <br /> <b>Path:</b> Thyrsus<br /> <b>Order:</b> Adamantine Arrow<br /> <b>Legacy:</b> Umbran Witches<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 4, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 4(7), Dexterity 6(9), Stamina 4(7)<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 4, Manipulation 3, Composure 4<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics 2, Crafts 2, Computer 1, Medicine 2, Occult (Spirits) 3, Politics 1, Investigation 2, Science 1<br /> <br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics (Acrobatics) 6, Brawl 4, Drive (Motorcycle) 4, Firearms (Pistols) 4, Larceny 1, Stealth 3, Survival 2, Weaponry 4<br /> <br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken 2, Empathy 2, Expression (Wisecracking, Dancing) 3, Intimidation (Violence) 3, Persuasion (Seduction, Taunting) 3, Socialize 3, Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 3<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area Of Expertise (Spirits), Common Sense, Danger Sense, Indomitable, Interdisciplinary Specialty (Spirits), Professional Training 5 (Umbran Witch: Athletics, Firearms, Occult), Tolerance For Biology, Trained Observer 3, Ambidextrous, Crack Driver 3, Demolisher 3, Iron Stamina 3, Parkour 3, Stunt Driver 3, Allies (Enzo, Rodin, Luka), Barfly, Closed Book 2, Iron Will, Resources 3, Pusher, Order Status (Adamantine Arrow 3), Striking Looks 2 (Slender And Curvy), Table Turner, True Friend (Jeanne), Heavy Weapons 5, Martial Arts 5, Enhanced + Imbued Item (Scarborough Fair*), High Speech, Potent Nimbus 2, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#heading=h.bmyv6hvea7jw\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Rote Mastery</b></a> (Shapechanging 3, Acceleration 3, Spirit Summons 3, World Walker 3), Shadow Name 2<br /> <br /> *The Scarborough Fair is treated as a single item modeled after Heavy Pistols. It contains the following benefits: Find The Balance, Ex Nihilo (Conjures Ammunition Only), Ephemeral Enchantment, Auto Fire, +2 Damage Bonus, +2 Durability, +10 Mana.<br /> <br /> <b>Health:</b> 12<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 8<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 10<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 13<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 21<br /> <b>Wisdom:</b> 4<br /> <b>Gnosis:</b> 7<br /> <b>Arcana:</b> Life 4, Spirit 4, Time 3, Forces 2, Matter 4<br /> <br /> <b>Rotes:</b> Life (Honing The Form, Shapechanging), Time (Acceleration), Spirit (Know Spirit, Command Spirit, Bolster Spirit, Reaching, Spirit Summons, Twilit Body, World Walker), Matter (Shaping)<br /> <br /> <b>Praxes:</b> Life (Shapechanging), Time (Acceleration), Forces (Control Gravity), Spirit (Ephemeral Shield, Reaching, Spirit Summons, World Walker), Matter (Shaping)<br /> <br /> <b>Dedicated Magical Tool:</b> Umbran Watch</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-08-2017, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T14:52:12-08:00","id":1024908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1024841#post1024841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with those traits, except Gunslinger. 2ED has removed the idea of multiple attacks per turn. However, Ebony &amp; Ivory are capable of autofire, so it's not a big deal.<br /> <br /> Do you mind explaining the differences between DMC 2 and 3? I am only superficially familiar with the series.</div> </div> </div> </div>DMC 3 is a young Dante, a lot more reckless and cocky in comparison to 2.<br /> IIRC, Dante in 2 was also more stoic, wasn't impaled, was more mature.<br /> In regards to skills/abilities, there wasn't too much of a difference, I think, though 2 was chronologically older/Stronger.<br /> <br /> Abilities I remember: trickster: moving around quickly, shunpo, moving in air.<br /> royal guard: block incomming attacks, charge up to retribute with a powerful attack.<br /> gunslinger: more effective/creative use of firearms/ special skills like e.g. riccocheting (spelling?) Rockets.<br /> Swordmaster: like gunslinger for weaponry.<br /> Quicksilver: stopping time for a while<br /> Doppelganger: invincible shadow-you helping you out<br /> Devilform: stronger, faster, more resilient","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T15:14:58-08:00","id":1024917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1024908#post1024908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DMC 3 is a young Dante, a lot more reckless and cocky in comparison to 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=W-nEtnQYSlo\" data-code=\"W-nEtnQYSlo\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/W-nEtnQYSlo/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T15:47:12-08:00","id":1024930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1024908#post1024908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DMC 3 is a young Dante, a lot more reckless and cocky in comparison to 2.<br /> IIRC, Dante in 2 was also more stoic, wasn't impaled, was more mature.<br /> In regards to skills/abilities, there wasn't too much of a difference, I think, though 2 was chronologically older/Stronger.<br /> <br /> Abilities I remember: trickster: moving around quickly, shunpo, moving in air.<br /> royal guard: block incomming attacks, charge up to retribute with a powerful attack.<br /> gunslinger: more effective/creative use of firearms/ special skills like e.g. riccocheting (spelling?) Rockets.<br /> Swordmaster: like gunslinger for weaponry.<br /> Quicksilver: stopping time for a while<br /> Doppelganger: invincible shadow-you helping you out<br /> Devilform: stronger, faster, more resilient</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'll go with the DMC 3 version. I might also use Deionscribe's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/848133-minor-template-hellspawn\"><b>Hellspawn</b></a> rules.<br /> <br /> What did you think of my write up for Bayonetta?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T03:16:42-08:00","id":1025043,"title":"","content":"Not really familiar with bayonetta, sry. Seems to fit what little I know about her well, however.<br /> Hellspawn look decent, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T05:50:00-08:00","id":1025058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1024930#post1024930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I'll go with the DMC 3 version. I might also use Deionscribe's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/848133-minor-template-hellspawn\"><b>Hellspawn</b></a> rules.<br /> <br /> What did you think of my write up for Bayonetta?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been a while since I last revisited those ideas. Nice to know they're still having some use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T09:34:03-08:00","id":1025479,"title":"","content":"A thing in tv in Quebec during christmas time is that they show the old animated movies of asterix and obelix (as well as some lucky luke).<br /> So that got me thinking.<br /> <br /> Asterix would be a hunter with access to an Elixir that the Ascending Ones would give everything to possess. And Obelix would be a Deviant based on said Elixir i guess.<br /> Actually the whole village could be a hunter compact with access to the magic potion as their endowments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T15:55:16-08:00","id":1025602,"title":"","content":"I just thought of another possibility, although it is unconventionnal i think.<br /> <br /> Obelix could be a Beast, an Anakim with a hunger for ruin more specifically. Especially in the eyes of the roman and the pirates.<br /> With Obelix and the village the horror has pretty much a near endless supply of roman (troups and camps) to crush and destroy. It must also like destroying roman troup formations and legionnaires morale. <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">&quot;Engagez-vous, engagez-vous, ils disaient... Vous verrez du pays, ils disaient...&quot;</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T11:59:10-08:00","id":1026093,"title":"","content":"So, I've been reading Natsume's Book of Friends...<br /> <br /> Exorcist clans IMHO work best as Proximi dynaties with Spirit. Natsume line in particular translates to Fox-blooded Proximi with Fate (note the serial usage of Sworn Oaths by Reiko) and the Piercing Eyes Tell (I tie them to Kitsune and not Uratha because of slit pupils).<br /> <br /> The interesting thing is potential Orders.<br /> <br /> Takashi strikes me as a Libertine, insofar his attitude towards spirits is concerned.<br /> Matoba seems Thearch-y.<br /> Where would you place Natori, though? My gut tells Arrow, but it could well be wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T12:04:36-08:00","id":1026095,"title":"","content":"Anime made me remember Princess Mononoke. Ashitaka a Deviant? Or some sort of Spirit ridden?<br /> I'd say the titular heroine is wolf-blooded, her pack being powerful Wolf spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T15:55:23-08:00","id":1026194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1026095#post1026095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anime made me remember Princess Mononoke. Ashitaka a Deviant? Or some sort of Spirit ridden?<br /> I'd say the titular heroine is wolf-blooded, her pack being powerful Wolf spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Deviant is more fitting, personally. His Scar is his crazy gross arm trying to murder people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a 