tyle=\"font-family:Calibri\">Transparent Flesh: When using phasing you can see under her skin and flesh</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Description:</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Bio:</b></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","user":"Basic","date":". 01-10-2017, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T03:39:15-08:00","id":1029989,"title":"","content":"<b>Geralt of Rivia</b> from the The Witcher videogames seems to me an Adamantine Arrow Mage. I have searched in the forums and many classify him as an Exalted. I haven't played the Exalted game, so by my experience it seems a Mage to me. He could be an Obrimos for his sense of justice) or a Thyrsus (for that primal aura that surrounds Geralt), His abilities could be represented by:<br /> <br /> <b>Abilities</b>:<ul><li><b>Witcher senses</b>: Life arcanum. <b>Suggested rotes</b>: Heightened senses (Life 2), Eyes of the dead (Death 2 attainment),</li> <li><b>Witcher life span</b>: Life 4 or 5, self only <b>Suggested rotes</b>: none come to my mind, any ideas?</li> <li><b>Witcher meditation</b>: Mind arcanum. <b>Suggested rotes</b>: Sleep of the just (Mind 3, self only)</li> <li><b>Witcher regeneration</b>: Life arcanum. <b>Suggested rotes</b>: Cleanse the body (Life 1, self only), Body control (Life 2), Purge illness (Life 2, self only), Knit (Life 3, self only), Mend (Life 4, self only)</li> <li><b>Witcher reflexes</b>: Time, Life or Forces <b>Suggested rotes</b>: Armor attainment (Life and Time, Time because remember, witchers can avoid crossbow bolts... well, noobs perhaps not too much, remember Witcher 1 final scene on the siege of Kaer Morhem...)</li> <li><b>Witcher combat abilities</b>: Forces and Life arcanum, perhaps Time too. <b>Suggested rotes</b>: Kinetic Blow (Forces 2)</li> </ul><b>Potions</b>:<ul><li><b>Cat potion</b>: Forces arcanum. <b>Suggested rotes</b>: Nightvision (Forces 1) rote into a delicious and toxic potion.</li> </ul><b>Signs</b>:<ul><li><b>Aard</b>: Forces arcanum. <b>Suggested rotes</b>: Telekinetic strike (Forces 3)</li> <li><b>Axii</b>: Mind arcanum. <b>Suggested rotes</b>: Emotional urging (Mind 2), Psychic domination (Mind 2)</li> <li><b>Igni</b>: Forces arcanum. <b>Suggested rotes</b>: Control fire (Forces 2), Thunderbolt (Forces 3, but with fire instead of electricity)</li> <li><b>Quen</b>: Forces arcanum. <b>Suggested rotes</b>: Turn momentum (Forces 3)</li> <li><b>Yrden</b>: Forces arcanum. <b>Suggested rotes</b>: Gravitic supremacy (Forces 3, only to increase gravity, and combined with spirit and death to affect etereal entities)</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","user":"dourden","date":". 01-11-2017, 06:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","name":"dourden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T04:54:25-08:00","id":1030003,"title":"","content":"Well, as a guy who read all Witcher's Saga in Polish in his younger years ( <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) I would say that Witchers, generally, would work as Proximus Dynasties, probably 3-4 based on Schools character was changed from. They have limited magical powers, they work in direct versions and most of their inner powers are 'mutations'. <br /> <br /> P.S. Interesting trivia - in <b>Left Hand Path</b> there is implication that Witchers were previous Soul Stealing Legacy in Poland, but Tremere hunt them and convert them all in to their ranks as new House. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T06:43:28-08:00","id":1030025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1030003#post1030003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, as a guy who read all Witcher's Saga in Polish in his younger years ( <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) I would say that Witchers, generally, would work as Proximus Dynasties, probably 3-4 based on Schools character was changed from. They have limited magical powers, they work in direct versions and most of their inner powers are 'mutations'.<br /> <br /> P.S. Interesting trivia - in <b>Left Hand Path</b> there is implication that Witchers were previous Soul Stealing Legacy in Poland, but Tremere hunt them and convert them all in to their ranks as new House. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Proximus could work... at least until Deviant comes out. Because they seem to <i>really</i> fit that mold (Mutations? Variations. Limited magic use? Variations. Needing to activate certain powers with potions? Scars, maybe? The other side-effects are obviously Scars, of course).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T06:48:06-08:00","id":1030028,"title":"","content":"As was already mentioned somewhere, the upcoming deviant probably fits witcher best, what with the Trial of the Grasses on young and possibly 'abducted' young boys. Fits the 'changed against my will/without my consent&quot;-narrative. Abilities would be accordingly working Scars.<br /> I also feel Mage is too powerful (not to mention Exalted) to represent Geralt or other witchers. If not Deviants, then I propose them to be Hedge Mages with access to Potions the Ascending Ones would dream of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":".  correcting autocorrect 01-11-2017, 11:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T07:40:47-08:00","id":1030048,"title":"","content":"As I have said before, Anthony Fremont from <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Literature/ItsAGoodLife\" target=\"_blank\"><b>It's A Good Life</b></a> and Kilgrave from <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Series/JessicaJones2015\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Jessica Jones</b></a> are perfect examples of why Mages most definitely count as monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T07:59:47-08:00","id":1030056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1030048#post1030048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\