> Ehhhh, Kilgrave really more fits as a <b>(BIG-ASS SPOILER ALERT HERE, SERIOUSLY TURN BACK IF YOU HAVEN'T WATCHED JESSICA JONES)</b> Deviant, given the source of his power is an specially-engineered brain-repair virus. (I think? I may not have been paying full attention at that moment.)</div> </div> </div> </div> In terms of power level and origins, sure. I meant the way Kilgrave abuses his powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T09:19:45-08:00","id":1030087,"title":"","content":"SPOILER people, SPOILER for <i>Jessica Jones</i> series! For me, Kilgrave is <b>archetypical </b>low Wisdom Mastigos, His abilities works 'like magic', and he can only by stopped by putting him to sleep. Mage like no other. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T10:01:27-08:00","id":1030104,"title":"","content":"Or a ghoul with Majesty and Domination. Or a Claimed or Ridden by a spirit of control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-11-2017, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T11:40:52-08:00","id":1030161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1030104#post1030104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or a ghoul with Majesty and Domination. Or a Claimed or Ridden by a spirit of control.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would disagree on the level of his power - he just do not make 'Command' things Majesty can do. He makes everyone, just passingly, totally worship him and make everything for him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T11:40:52-08:00","id":1030162,"title":"","content":"Double post, sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T12:13:14-08:00","id":1030170,"title":"","content":"Specifically, people have to do what Kilgrave says, which makes me think of the Bearers of the Eternal Voice...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T12:44:51-08:00","id":1030191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1030161#post1030161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would disagree on the level of his power - he just do not make 'Command' things Majesty can do. He makes everyone, just passingly, totally worship him and make everything for him.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is what Majesty does.<br /> <br /> 'The vampire inspires burning loyalty in the victim. She\u2019d do anything for him, giving up her blood or organs \u2014 or taking a bullet for him. The victim gains the Enthralled Condition.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T14:31:29-08:00","id":1030252,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://comicvine.gamespot.com/purple-man/4005-3227/\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Kilgrave/Purple Man </span></a>is a Deviant; his origin, his power level, and it's limitations, all add up to a Deviant. While I will concede that Kilgrave's abuse of his power is an excellent cautionary tale, and proof that mind control powers are an easy path to becoming a monster; he's just not powerful or versatile enough to be a Mage. A Mastigos can control people from a great distance with a sympathetic connection via the Space Arcanum; Kilgrave can only effect people who are breathing the same air as him. A Mastigos can plant ideas in someone's head without any giving any outward sign that he's doing anything at all; Kilgrave must speak his commands aloud.<br /> <br /> Also, Kilgrave even has a Scar:<br /> <img src=\"http://static3.comicvine.com/uploads/scale_small/4/47635/2149417-purple.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><img src=\"http://static4.comicvine.com/uploads/original/11/117763/2880972-new_thunderbolts__12___page_14.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 01-11-2017, 07:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T15:48:44-08:00","id":1030289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=501774#post501774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1+1 may not necessarily equal 2</div> </div> </div> </div>As a mathematician, that's... actually quite easy to construct. It depends on what group you're working with, granted, but that's not <i>unheard</i> of.<br /> <br /> Sorry, I just have to be a pedant when I see that as an example of &quot;impossibility&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T18:40:09-08:00","id":1030374,"title":"","content":"OK, tax paying time.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Dimitri Ravinoff (A.K.A. The Raven)</span></b><br /> <img src=\"http://orig03.deviantart.net/9a55/f/2011/120/9/9/snow_crash__raven_by_huxtable-d3f8mrr.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <b>Scary As Fuck (But Still Mortal)</b><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Religious<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Poor Impulse Control<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Str</b> 5 / <b>Dex</b> 3 / <b>Sta</b> 4<br /> <b>Int</b> 2 / <b>Wit</b> 3 / <b>Res</b> 3<br /> <b>Pre</b> 2 / <b>Man</b> 2 / <b>Com</b> 2</span><br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Crafts 1, Investigation 1, Medicine 1, Politics 1<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 4, Brawl 5, Drive 2, Stealth 1, Survival 3, Weaponry 4<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Empathy 2, Intimidation 5, Persuasion 1, Socialize 1, Streetwise 3<br /> <b>Specialities:</b> Glass Knives and Harpoons (Weaponry), Kayaking (Athletics), One Man Nuclear Power (Intimidation), Murderous Sociopath (Intimidation)<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area of Expertise (Glass Knives and Harpoons) \u2022, Area of Expertise (One Man Nuclear Power) \u2022, Aura of Menace \u2022\u2022, Boxing \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Encyclopedic Knowledge (Imperialist History) \u2022\u2022, Giant \u2022\u2022\u2022, Improvised Weapons \u2022\u2022\u2022\u00b9, Killer Instinct \u2022\u2022\u2022, Killer Instinct (Advanced) \u2022, Fame \u2022\u2022, Language (Russian), Light Weapons \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Quick Draw (Glass Knives) \u2022, Shiv \u2022\u2022, Strength Training \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Tolerant of Biology \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Dead Man's Switch [Persistent], Notorious [Persistent]<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Dead Man's Switch [Persistent]</span><br /> You have a bomb linked to your brain. A <i>nuclear weapon</i>, to be more precise. If you die, everyone within a few miles gets experience a mushroom cloud first-hand. In other words, killing you is the equivalent of committing both mass-murder <i>and</i> suicide - even <i>attempting</i> to do so is a Breaking Point at -5. Also, the cops tend to let you get away with things because the side effects of you resisting arrest could mean that the city is <i>fucked</i>.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> Whenever someone else goes out of their way to get out of your way.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Someone disables that nuke. You die (and take everyone else with you).<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> He <i>also</i> needs something that prevents him from taking Breaking Points for killing people. He's no Slasher, he's just... indifferent to the copious amounts of murder he inflicts.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">\u00b9 Substitutes for Street Fighting for the purposes of taking Shiv.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T09:52:48-08:00","id":1030630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1030161#post1030161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would disagree on the level of his power - he just do not make 'Command' things Majesty can do. He makes everyone, just passingly, totally worship him and make everything for him.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1030252#post1030252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I will concede that Kilgrave's abuse of his power is an excellent cautionary tale, and proof that mind control powers are an easy path to becoming a monster; he's just not powerful or versatile enough to be a Mage. A Mastigos can control people from a great distance with a sympathetic connection via the Space Arcanum; Kilgrave can only effect people who are breathing the same air as him. A Mastigos can plant ideas in someone's head without any giving any outward sign that he's doing anything at all; Kilgrave must speak his commands aloud. Also, Kilgrave even has a Scar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think both of you are right. He is not as versatile as a Mage. In terms of Mage power, he can only use Mind spells, and only command spells and trigger orders under certain conditions (nor dreams, nor boost intelligence, nor boost skills, nor doing diferent mental tasks at the same time...), and is limited also in having to use his voice as a necessary Yantra. He can't event <b>***SPOILER ALERT, BEEP BEEP ***</b> use his power if confined.<br /> <br /> But how he use his &quot;psychic domination&quot; and the power and influence of it... whoa!... I find he is at a Mage Tier.<br /> <br /> Also the megalonamiacal use of his power and his attittude makes an excelent Wisdom 1 Mage example.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","user":"dourden","date":". 01-12-2017, 01:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","name":"dourden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T21:19:06-08:00","id":1040404,"title":"","content":"Would a <a href=\"https://zoink.ch/torrent/Justice.League.Action.S01E03.Nuclear.Family.Values.HDTV.x264-DEADPOOL&#91;eztv].mkv.torrent\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Family&quot;</a> of automatons given &quot;life&quot; by an atomic bomb test count as Zeka, Extempore, Unfleshed, or all of the above?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T03:41:39-08:00","id":1040536,"title":"","content":"Looking at computer games, I am curious as to what you'd make the League of Legends Champion Vladimir.<br /> Because I am stumped if I'd try to apply major templates, and am not as familiar with the minor ones.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6138_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6138\" data-vbnamecard=\"6138\">Mangle77</a> Well, we don't know about 2ed Zeka yet iirc, so I'd go for Extempore or Unfleshed, I guess. Tending towards Unfleshed, actually, if that is a more defining characteristic of the event than the act of creation (the test) itself.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T06:30:07-08:00","id":1041227,"title":"","content":"I posted this a while back <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/470005-gotham-city-of-secrets\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ity-of-secrets</a> and as it seems on topic I'll give my take on the Clan and Bloodline of Batmans cast.<br /> Joker is part of The Carnival (Daeva) from Bloodlines the Legendary, this explains how he gets people to follow him (Magisty) and all round theme.<br /> Most of the Bat family are Khaibit (Meket) from Bloodlines the Hidden (or the V:tR sticky) due to Batman being so fond of his shadowport.<br /> Two Face is a Nahualli (again from Bloodlines the Hidden) due to theme.<br /> Killer Crock is a Noctuku (Nosferatu) (he's a sewer dwelling monster who might eat you) and Penguin is a Rotgrafen (Ventrue) (both from Bloodlines the Chosen) as he has a thing for boats and telling birds what to do (Animalism)<br /> Poison Ivy is portrayed more like a Deava with Animalism than a Gangrel (or Ventrue) with Majesty but you could make a case for either one (especially if her Bloodline boon let's her treat plants like animals for Disipline use).<br /> Scarecrow is a Nightmare user and therefore a Nosferatu and Ridler is likely a Meket.<br /> Ras is most likely a Ventrue from the way he carries himself but I'm open to other interpretations.<br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4714,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","user":"Live Bait","date":". 01-31-2017, 09:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T17:57:54-08:00","id":1041596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1041227#post1041227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I posted this a while back <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/470005-gotham-city-of-secrets\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ity-of-secrets</a> and as it seems on topic I'll give my take on the Clan and Bloodline of Batmans cast.<br /> Joker is part of The Carnival (Daeva) from Bloodlines the Legendary, this explains how he gets people to follow him (Magisty) and all round theme.<br /> Most of the Bat family are Khaibit (Meket) from Bloodlines the Hidden (or the V:tR sticky) due to Batman being so fond of his shadowport.<br /> Two Face is a Nahualli (again from Bloodlines the Hidden) due to theme.<br /> Killer Crock is a Noctuku (Nosferatu) (he's a sewer dwelling monster who might eat you) and Penguin is a Rotgrafen (Ventrue) (both from Bloodlines the Chosen) as he has a thing for boats and telling birds what to do (Animalism)<br /> Poison Ivy is portrayed more like a Deava with Animalism than a Gangrel (or Ventrue) with Majesty but you could make a case for either one (especially if her Bloodline boon let's her treat plants like animals for Disipline use).<br /> Scarecrow is a Nightmare user and therefore a Nosferatu and Ridler is likely a Meket.<br /> Ras is most likely a Ventrue from the way he carries himself but I'm open to other interpretations.<br /> Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Joker depends on whether you think the skin and hair is makeup (Ventrue Malkavian) or if it's bleached that and/or has facial scarring (Nosferatu Malkavian). Harley is probably just his ghoul, whom he has infected with his madness to keep him company. <br /> <br /> Two-Face could work as a Nahuali, though I also like the idea of him originally being a handsome man who got Embraced by a Nosferatu out of spite. Though if you want to be zany, he could be a member of the Brethren of the Hundred Faces. <br /> <br /> Killer Crock as Noctuku is perfect. Penguin as Rotgrafen is perfect, too. <br /> <br /> Just by powers, Ivy is an Androazi Nosferatu who just happens to be gorgeous, but has a very inhuman attitude. The episodes I remember where she employs pheromones or perfume remind me of a Gullikan Daeva. If you're willing to put in the work, she could be a Daeva with a custom bloodline that lets her use Animalism, but only in the case of plants. <br /> <br /> Scarecrow as Nosferatu is perfect, and the Morotrophian bloodline works nicely in a thematic sense. Riddler as a Mekhet is fine. Ra's as a Ventrue... sure, makes sense to me. Him trying to get Batman to lead the League of Shadows sounds like trying to convince him to join a bloodline or something. Catwoman is a Gangrel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T01:20:35-08:00","id":1041736,"title":"","content":"I'm mostly with you (the post I linked to was less definite about stuff but the above is my preferred call) but Catwoman relies on speed, the ability to jump very far and is free with the sex appeal, she's Daeva. The Carnival was due to his charisma and those times he's shown as able to evade Batman trying to land a punch or successfully run away, by now Harrly has been Embraced as she's done her own thing far too often plus having a Bloodline backing the Joker should scare the players out of trying to down him, claiming the rep for the task, and calling it a day.<br /> I'm assuming Talli is one of Ras' mortal descendants who he might Embrace or give to Batman to gain an alliance and the League of Assassins is a Ghoul Family.<br /> That just leaves The Court of Owls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T05:22:20-08:00","id":1041768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1041736#post1041736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm mostly with you (the post I linked to was less definite about stuff but the above is my preferred call) but Catwoman relies on speed, the ability to jump very far and is free with the sex appeal, she's Daeva. The Carnival was due to his charisma and those times he's shown as able to evade Batman trying to land a punch or successfully run away, by now Harrly has been Embraced as she's done her own thing far too often plus having a Bloodline backing the Joker should scare the players out of trying to down him, claiming the rep for the task, and calling it a day.<br /> I'm assuming Talli is one of Ras' mortal descendants who he might Embrace or give to Batman to gain an alliance and the League of Assassins is a Ghoul Family.<br /> That just leaves The Court of Owls.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the name screams Striges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T00:20:50-08:00","id":1043406,"title":"","content":"I know that the Doctor and the TARDIS have both been discussed quite often in the group, but I've found that the two can really be made absurdly easy through the Horrors system.<br /> <br /> The Doctor I've not statted out definitively outside of the Immortal merit (regeneration ahoi). The/A TARDIS (if the Doctor isn't part of the game, another TARDIS can be had) on the other hand, is a Horror with Chameleon Horror, Home Ground (its interiors), Immortal, Influence (Time), Know Soul, Maze (its interiors, again), Reality Stutter, Surprise Entrance and or Unbreakable, and that's just from CofD alone. You can easily kit it with any number of Dread Powers, and with all of movement abilities that allow for teleportation, and with a bit of reskinning, you could easily make them how it dematerializes/materializes in a scene, provided you worked out a system for how an immobile object doesn't really &quot;move&quot; outside of these jumps. That said, a Horror TARDIS would likely use Surprise Entrance, since it doesn't appear to have a distance limit; it would thus be warded off by a large number of clocks, under the principle that observing/measuring something changes it, and thus by observing/measuring time so overtly you're disrupting it enough that a TARDIS can't land easily.<br /> <br /> Really, the only limitation I can find to making a TARDIS is the number of Dread Powers that you could logically have on it without making it overpowered, either as an antagonist or as an ally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T01:51:01-08:00","id":1043419,"title":"","content":"Out of curiousity:<br /> What would Lucifer from, well, Lucifer, be when translated into CofD?<br /> Which Supernatural Splat fits Cale Lightman from Lie to Me best?<br /> What kind of Hunter would the Grimm's from Grimm be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T01:58:05-08:00","id":1043422,"title":"","content":"I think the first two were called out as Demons. At least Lucifer was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T03:17:59-08:00","id":1043442,"title":"","content":"Lucifer from TV show is totally Ankim Nemesis , uncovering people secret desires and punishing wicked. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T19:48:44-08:00","id":1044834,"title":"","content":"So I've been thinking some more about the Gems from Steven Universe; and I while the Unchained are <u><i><b>A</b></i></u> viable interpretation, it is <b><i><u>NOT</u></i></b> the only one:<br /> <br /> \u200bRose's opinion of humans really does fit with Promethean's &quot;Humans are SOO awesome!&quot; themes, and the Gem mutants/corrupted Gems remind me of Pandorans/Created who have fallen prey to Flux.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Diamonds could fit the Gentry just about as well as they do the GM; and the Human Zoo from recent episodes is a good example of &quot;even their kindness is cruel&quot;. Yes, the Zoo could also work as a GM &quot;Eden/Heaven&quot;.<br /> <br /> So yes, D:tD fits best for the Gems, but isn't a perfect fit for everyone on the show.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct