ef=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1044858#post1044858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prometheans are not the only supernatural characters who hold aspects of humanity in high esteem, nor is this in fact the defining theme of Promethean in any greater sense than its being a humanist game means being human is going to be treated as a worthwhile state of existence.<br /> <br /> Demon has Slivers for this. They do the job markedly better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally; I think Batman is a Hunter, and most of Gotham's iconic villains are Slashers, but others will say they are Beasts, some will say Vampires. Heck, I won't be shocked if someone comes along and says Unchained! I could see a few of them as Deviants, maybe Changelings, even a Sin-Eater or two... \u200bI'm just saying there's more than one way to look at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T12:37:13-08:00","id":1049997,"title":"","content":"I don't think it was Amenadiel, if only because he didn't know anything about it. So... maybe we'll find out later?<br /> <br /> <br /> Is Dr. Who an Unchained? I feel Cover would explain the 'lives' pretty well... not an avid Whovian, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T18:49:52-08:00","id":1050840,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1049937#post1049937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've Actually been taking the Time to read the Beast Book (Foot in Cast will do that to you) and re-Watched Marble Hornets... Slendy in it is a Begotten. He's an Incarnate Beast that has a Hunger for Ruin, Has a Lair that is infested with Water and Darkness, and causes Illness in people he Transports though it.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1049937#post1049937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">]<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">It's why he can Transport people miles in what feels like a Blink of an Eye, they are Chambers of his Lair.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1049997#post1049997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Dr. Who an Unchained? I feel Cover would explain the 'lives' pretty well... not an avid Whovian, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I made sheets precisely for these interpretations, shown below. What do you two think?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Family:</b> Anakim<br /> <b>Hunger: </b>Prey<br /> <b>Myth:</b> The Mysterious, Ever-Watching Boogeyman<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 5, Wits 6, Resolve 8<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 5, Dexterity 6, Stamina 8<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 8, Manipulation 6, Composure 8<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics 3, Computer 0, Crafts 1, Investigation (Spying) 4, Medicine 1, Occult 4, Politics 0, Science 0<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics (Chasing) 4, Brawl (Claws And Tentacles) 5, Drive 0, Firearms 0, Larceny 0, Stealth (Stalking) 8, Survival (Forests And Woodlands) 4, Weaponry 0<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken 0, Empathy (Fear) 3, Expression (Sound Mimicry) 3, Intimidation (Appearing Out Of Nowhere) 6, Persuasion (Taking People Away) 5, Socialize 0, Streetwise 0, Subterfuge (Evasive) 5<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area Of Expertise (Taking People Away), Danger Sense (Advanced), Direction Sense (Epic), Eidetic Memory (Advanced), Indomitable (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration\"><b>Epic</b></a>), Interdisciplinary Specialty (Taking People Away), Patient (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration\"><b>Advanced 3</b></a>), Trained Observer 3 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration\"><b>(Advanced)</b></a>, Demolisher 3, Double-Jointed (Advanced), Greyhound, Closed Book 5, Iron Will, Retainer (Proxies 3 To 5), Striking Looks 2 (Uncanny), Untouchable, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration/page2\"><b>Untouchable Style 4</b></a>, Hunger Management 3, Spoor 5, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1063048#post1063048\"><b>Wandering Soul 5</b></a><br /> <br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 10<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 14<br /> <b>Speed:</b> ST Fiat<br /> <b>Health:</b> 33 (Effective Size 25)<br /> <b>Lair:</b> 10<br /> <br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> Alien Allure, From The Shadows, Limb From Limb, Looming Presence, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=833241#post833241\"><b>In My Image</b></a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1067535#post1067535\"><b>Inescapable</b></a>, Mimir's Wisdom, Monster From The Deep, Needs Must, Relentless Hunter, Shadowed Soul, Siren\u2019s Treacherous Song, Unbreakable<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> Behold My True Form, Fear Is Contagious, They Are All Around You, Run Away, You Are Not Alone, You Cannot Run, You Can\u2019t Wake Up, You Will Never Rest, Tabula Rasa, You Are Lost, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1086900#post1086900\"><b>You Can't Trust Your Senses</b></a><br /> <br /> <b>Horror Traits: </b>Power 14, Finesse 14, Resistance 14, Size 25, Health 34, Defense 10, Initiative 14, Speed ST Fiat<br /> <br /> <b>Lair Traits:</b> Fog, Maze, Poor Light, Sealed Exits, Diseased (Grave), Disruption, Exposed, Mirages, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/649174-a-new-lair-trait\"><b>Wondrous</b></a><br /> <br /> <b>Beast-Shapes: </b>Legendary Size, One With The Shadows, <i><b>Superior Atavism*</b></i> (Alien Allure, From The Shadows, Inescapable, In My Image, Looming Presence, Needs Must, Siren's Treacherous Song), Unnatural Healing<br /> <br /> <b><i>*Superior Atavism (House Ruled): </i></b>It does not give a free Satiety Expenditure per chapter. Instead, when an Incarnate selects a Superior Atavism, they gain a pool of points equal to their [Lair] to spend on improvisational, narrative effects for that Atavism based on their Myth. Greater effects cost more points, and they may recharge once per chaper per Superior Atavism by spending 1 Willpower point and rolling [Highest Resistance Attribute + Occult + Lair] with Rote Quality. Each Success restores one point of Superior Atavism. The Incarnate restores 1 point even if they fail the roll. When a Superior Atavism faces against another supernatural power, roll for a Clash Of Wills against the Incarnate\u2019s [Highest Resistance Attribute + Lair].</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>The Doctor</b><br /> <br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Fortitude/Prudence<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Pride<br /> <br /> <b>Incarnation:</b> Psychopomp<br /> <b>Agenda:</b> Inquisitor<br /> <b>Catalyst:</b> Freedom Of Movement<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 8, Wits 4, Resolve 6<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 4, Stamina 6<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 4, Manipulation 6, Composure 4<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics (History) 5, Crafts (Machines, Improvisation) 6, Computer 4, Medicine 3, Occult 5, Politics 2, Investigation 4, Science (Time Travel) 6<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics (Running) 3, Brawl 2, Drive (TARDIS) 3, Firearms 2, Larceny (Sonic Screwdriver) 3, Stealth 2, Survival 2, Weaponry (Swords) 4<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken 2, Empathy 3, Expression (Leadership, Humor) 6, Intimidation (Grandiose Threats) 3, Persuasion (Diplomacy) 5, Socialize 2, Streetwise 2, Subterfuge (Technobabble, Bluff) 4<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area Of Expertise (Time Travel), Danger Sense, Indomitable (<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration\">Epic</a></b>), Interdisciplinary Specialty (Time Travel), Investigative Aide (Science), Virtuous, Fleet Of Foot 3, Greyhound, Iron Stamina 3, Parkour 4, Quick Draw (Sonic Screwdriver), Seizing The Edge, Sleight Of Hand, Closed Book 4, Contacts (Many), Fast-Talking 4, Inspiring, Iron Will, Pusher, Sympathetic, Table Turner, True Friend (Companions), Untouchable, Advance Form, <b><u><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=1103753#post1103753\">Cryptid Companion 4 (K9)</a></u></b>, <b><u><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=1162046#post1162046\">Grand Inquisitor 5</a></u></b>, Living The Lie, Resonance Sensitive, Terrible Form 4, Versatile Transformation, Armed Defense 4, Defensive Combat (Weaponry), Fighting Finesse (Sword), Heavy Weapons 5<br /> <br /> <b>Sonic Screwdriver's Embeds (Lambda):</b> Open Sesame, Right Tools Right Job, Like I Built It and Cause And Effect.<br /> <br /> <b>Psychic Paper's Embed (Precision Engineered):</b> Authorized.<br /> <br /> <b>TARDIS</b>: a Lare (see Demon's ST Guide Page 79) of Rank 5 with a special Incept, Influence or Numen that allows it to travel through space-time. It cannot travel to alternate planes of existence (use Rip The Gates for that). Its other traits are up to the ST.<br /> <br /> <b>Embeds</b><br /> <br /> <b>Vocal:</b> Across A Crowded Room, Animal Communication, Borrowed Expertise, Eavesdrop, Everybody Knows, Imagine, Muse, Remote Link-Up, Voice Of The Machine<br /> <br /> <b>Instrumental:</b> Data Retrieval, Efficiency, Functional Identity, Like I Built It, Open Sesame, Right Tools Right Job, Shift Consequence, Synthesis, Turn Blade<br /> <br /> <b>Cacophony:</b> Bystander Effect, Cause And Effect, Cool Heads Prevail, Hesitation, Just Bruised, Lucky Break, On The Mend, Raw Materials, Shatter, Special Someone<br /> <br /> <b>Mundane:</b> Associate And Integrate, Authorized, Deep Cover, Going Native, Homogeneous Memory, In My Pocket, Interference, Mistaken Identity, Never Here, Occam's Razor, Persistent Legend, Quick Change, Without A Trace<br /> <br /> <b>Exploits</b><br /> <br /> Allies Into Gold, Context Matters, Deep Pockets, Force Relationship, Frozen In Time, Four Minutes Ago, Hellhounds*, Inflict Stigmata, Newton's Nightmares, Raze Infrastructure, Reality Reinforcement, Rip The Gates, Sermon, Show Of Power, Stalking Horse, Stop, Summon, Urban Legend, Visions Of Heaven And Hell<br /> <br /> *Uses Crafts instead of Animal Ken, since the Doctor builds his Cryptids from scratch as Gadgets rather than transforming animals.<br /> <br /> <b>Demonic Form</b><br /> <br /> <b>Modifications:</b> Blade Hand, Component Indicators, Electrical Sight, Tough As Stone<br /> <br /> <b>Technologies:</b> Aura Sight, Environmental Resistance, Mind Reading, Multiversal Antennae<br /> <br /> <b>Propulsions:</b> Long Limbs, Plasma Drive<br /> <br /> <b>Processes:</b> Amorphous, Memory Theft, Nanobot Composition<br /> <br /> <b>Defense:</b> 7 (8 With Sword)<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 8<br /> <b>Speed: </b>14<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Health:</b> 11<br /> <b>Primum:</b> 8<br /> <b>Glitches:</b> Two hearts (Major Brand)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Cipher </b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><i><b>Wibbly Wobbly, Timey Wimey</b></i><br /> <br /> Not even the Doctor knows every single quantum branch and cosmic permutation of all timelines, but he\u2019s been through enough to know the most important patterns to look out for in case he needs to make emergency alterations.<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> <i>Synthesis</i> and <i>Right Tools Right Job</i><br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits + Science<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Aether<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Doctor gains false or misleading information.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> No effect. The Doctor may try again, suffering a cumulative -1 for each new attempt.<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> The Doctor mimics the Psychometry Supernatural Merit, using the aforementioned dice pool. He does not suffer the dice penalties normally associated with the Merit.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The Doctor gains the Informed Condition about the target.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><b>Reverse The Polarity Of Neutron Flow</b></i><br /> <br /> The Doctor possesses such vast knowledge of occult physics that it often sounds like gibberish to most, but he use that knowledge to practical effect at a moment\u2019s notice, especially when lives are at stake.<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b><i>Right Tools Right Job</i> and <i>On The Mend</i><br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Intelligence + Crafts<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Aether or 3 Aether<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> Instead of creating a Gadget, the Doctor creates a Cryptid with a Rank equal to his Primum/2 round up. This Cryptid is immediately hostile and hungry for Aether.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> No effect. The Doctor may try again, suffering a cumulative -1 for each new attempt.<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> By spending 1 Aether, the Doctor may create an Embedded Gadget as an Instant Action as long as he has the necessary hardware. By spending 3 Aether, the Gadget may be Exploited. In either case, the Gadget lasts for one scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The Gadget may either last for Primum in days, or be a first order Lambda.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><b>Regeneration</b></i><br /> <br /> The Doctor is an eternal mystery, always seeking the next adventure. Whenever it seems like his end has come, he calls upon this Interlock to reconfigure his Cover and biological makeup to save his life at the cost of reshaping his identity. This leaves us to always ask the same question: &quot;Doctor Who?&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b><i>On The Mend</i> and <i>Mistaken Identity</i><br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Persuasion<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5 Aether<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Doctor immediately takes the Hunted Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> No effect. The Doctor may try again, suffering a cumulative -1 for each new attempt.<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> The Doctor completely heals all damage and Resolves all negative internal Conditions. Furthermore, he heals all bashing and lethal damage at the start of each turn. At the end of the scene, his Cover is destroyed. However, for the following Primum days, any supernatural attempt at gaining information about him or ambushing him triggers a Clash of Wills against his Intelligence + Occult + Primum<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The Doctor also gains Rote Quality on mundane rolls to escape from, deceive or otherwise outsmart his opponents for Primum days.</div></div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 02-24-2019, 11:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T01:44:58-08:00","id":1050915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1049991#post1049991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally; I think Batman is a Hunter, and most of Gotham's iconic villains are Slashers, but others will say they are Beasts, some will say Vampires. Heck, I won't be shocked if someone comes along and says Unchained! I could see a few of them as Deviants, maybe Changelings, even a Sin-Eater or two... \u200bI'm just saying there's more than one way to look at it.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about Batman a True Fae and the villains as the people he's abducted? That's why he won't kill, he doesn't want to damage his property.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T17:54:02-08:00","id":1060713,"title":"","content":"The Slender Man could be an Unchained who reached Primum 10, went beyond and reached a new state of existence. He stalks and abducts people because he is an Inquisitor/Integrator. He gathers information on people so he can insert them into the God-Machine's plans and Infrastructures...but what the God-Machine doesn't realize is that the Slender Man has his own designs. The people who become his pawns and victims are caught in something much bigger than they can imagine. <br /> <br /> In this scenario, the weirdness that surrounds the Slender Man could be Glitches and Infrastructure. His characteristic powers of bending space-time and warping minds are applications of Embeds, Exploits and Demonic Form. The Proxies are his Cultists, and the lesser monsters he may have as servants might be Cryptids.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T04:49:01-08:00","id":1060814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd#post349384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghost Rider (Marvel Comics): a Sin-Eater. His Threshold is Torn and his Archetype is Reaper all the way. He has Rage 5, Shroud 5 and Hearse 5. He has the Pyre-Flame and Industrial Keys. He has a Memento motorcycle. He has a Reaper Merit that gives him +1 on attacks for each 2 points of Morality stat the target has below 7. He has a Flaw that only lets him use his powers when innocent blood is spilled, and once that happens, it's hard for him to stop. He can't harm anyone who he perceives as innocent (usually someone with Morality stat at 8 and higher, or who fulfills their Virtue often). Psyche is 7. Strength, Dexterity, Presence, Firearms, Weaponry and Drive are all at 5 or more. The Penance Stare is a quick Ceremony that requires a grapple and the target to be truly wicked. Its dice pool is Psyche + Presence vs Composure + Powerstat and it temporarily removes all willpower points, the ability to regain willpower and inflicts the Broken Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually have an NPC, Ash Corwin, as Ghost Rider-influenced Bound in my ChroD game, as a sort of mentor to the Geist PC (even though he's kind of bad at it). I toyed with the idea of making the motorcycle the Keystone Memento, but ultimately decided it just didn't fit (I want the Ghost Rider Geist to be a <i>lot</i> older), so went with the chain, which obviously can be lit on fire. I also gave him the Phantasmal Key and Marionette Manifestation, with the house rule that, instead of the Bound going comatose and manifesting their Geist, the Bound physically <i>becomes</i> their Geist, allowing Ash to actually transform into the flaming skeleton in biker leathers. LOVE your idea for the Penance Stare, I'll probably steal that for my game if/when I get back to running it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd#post349384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Joker (DC Comics): a Slasher, natch. His Undertaking is Maniac. Alternatively, he is a Changeling or even a True Fae that really likes spreading chaos on the Ironside. His Seeming is Darkling and his Kiths are Razorhand/Moonborn/Lurker. If he is a True Fae, his Titles would be himself (Actor), a special gun (Prop) and a group of ogrish thugs (Wisp). Either way, his Morality stat is zero or absent altogether. I suggest using my reworked version of the Lurker kith: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/348164-some-reworked-contracts-optional-guidelines-for-building-hollows?p=349431#post349431\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...431#post349431</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I actually wrote up The Joker as a Changeling, and have him in reserve for if my Chronicle plays out a certain way. To quote from my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it\">Fae-ify</a> It! thread:<br /> <br /> He doesn't remember his name, and it's not important, because that's not who he is anymore. He vaguely remembers his life before, being a two-bit bankrobber with better ideas than he could execute, but that's not important anymore either. He remembers being on the run from some cops, or maybe other crooks, turning a corner, and finding himself in a deep hedge. And then things got. . . stranger.<br /> <br /> He finally escaped, and he doesn't want to go back. But he remembers the pure, simple beauty of chaos, of the only reality being the one you decided upon at any given instant, and he sees this rigid, structured world and can't help but think that it needs more chaos. He's an agent of chaos.<br /> <br /> He's painted his Mask to reflect his Mein. White makeup on his face, black around his eyes, a red slash of a smile over the scars on his cheeks, and green dye in his hair. When people see beneath the Mask, they see skin bleached whiter than bone, empty black pits for eyes, a bleeding red gash where his mouth should be, and green fire atop his head for hair. He calls himself the Joker.<br /> <br /> In my estimation, he's a Zero-Clarity, No Derangement Wizend Soldier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T04:04:07-07:00","id":1062227,"title":"","content":"Let's go for Disney!<br /> <br /> We know about Gaston, that one's easy, but what about...<br /> <br /> <b><u>Dr. Facilier? </u></b>(Who is probably one of my favourite Disney antagonists!)<br /> My take on him would be Sin-Eater, what with the Shadow that interacts with him etc, but that wouldn't represent his awesome 'Let's make a deal' powers...or would it? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Ursula</b>?<br /> A Changeling, in my books. Darkling maybe? Don't know much about 2ed, so hit me with your knowledge =D<br /> <br /> <b>Quasimodo</b>?<br /> Now that one, I am stuck with.<br /> <br /> <b>Hercules</b>?<br /> Scion isn't CofD, so... let's try something else, something weird, and say Promethean!<br /> On a quest to become something more than he is? Check. (At first) people react poorly to him, wanting him to leave them alone? Check. Tougher than most anyone else? Check. Fights weird-ass things? Check. On a quest guided by divinity? Check.<br /> After calcifying his Vitality and Corporeum Alembics he leaves Iron and goes on to Gold, helping him in dealing with people.<br /> <br /> <b>Stitch</b>?<br /> Stitch could work as a Beast. For added lulz, let's make him Lilo's Horror. (Idea stolen from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8122\" data-vbnamecard=\"8122\">ArchonAres</a>) Otherwise, Changeling, I suppose.<br /> <br /> The list of Disney characters we could look at goes on and on... Djinnie, Shir-Khan, Maleficent, Baymax, Ralph, Yzma, Kenai, Gothel, Elsa, Alladin and Dschafar, and of course Maui would all be interesting to take a look at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T05:06:42-07:00","id":1062241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1062227#post1062227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's go for Disney!<br /> <br /> The list of Disney characters we could look at goes on and on... Djinnie, Shir-Khan, Maleficent, Baymax, Ralph, Yzma, Kenai, Gothel, Elsa, Alladin and Dschafar, and of course Maui would all be interesting to take a look at.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or Elsa, a Mage Obrimos (she is an idealist) Silver Lader (she is a princess and a ruler, after all XDD) specialiced in Ice Magic, or a Changelling of the Winter Court (1st edition)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","name":"dourden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T05:14:20-07:00","id":1062243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dourden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1062241#post1062241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or Elsa, a Mage Obrimos (she is an idealist) Silver Lader (she is a princess and a ruler, after all XDD) specialiced in Ice Magic, or a Changelling of the Winter Court (1st edition)</div> </div> </div> </div>Why only 1st edition?<br /> <br /> Also, how about Deviant for Elsa? Her powers work better the more she works on her relationships with others. No conspiracy after her, but she's royal, so her parents probably locked up and executed them already","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T05:56:30-07:00","id":1062252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dourden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1062241#post1062241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or Elsa, a Mage Obrimos (she is an idealist) Silver Lader (she is a princess and a ruler, after all XDD) specialiced in Ice Magic, or a Changelling of the Winter Court (1st edition)</div> </div> </div> </div>No, no, no - Elsa was Moros Tamer of Ice that become Guradian after 'The Accident' - 'Conceal, don't feel' - but when putted in stressed situation of coronation, years later, she breaks, going over Paradox snowstorm, until she sort's things out and understand she <i>needs</i> to be Silver Ladder ruler.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T10:49:52-07:00","id":1062373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1062252#post1062252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, no, no - Elsa was Moros Tamer of Ice that become Guradian after 'The Accident' - 'Conceal, don't feel' - but when putted in stressed situation of coronation, years later, she breaks, going over Paradox snowstorm, until she sort's things out and understand she <i>needs</i> to be Silver Ladder ruler.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> XDDDD Good one!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","name":"dourden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T10:51:59-07:00","id":1062375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1062227#post1062227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's go for Disney!<br /> <br /> We know about Gaston, that one's easy, but what about...<br /> <br /> <b><u>Dr. Facilier? </u></b>(Who is probably one of my favourite Disney antagonists!)<br /> My take on him would be Sin-Eater, what with the Shadow that interacts with him etc, but that wouldn't represent his awesome 'Let's make a deal' powers...or would it? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Ursula</b>?<br /> A Changeling, in my books. Darkling maybe? Don't know much about 2ed, so hit me with your knowledge =D<br /> <br /> <b>Quasimodo</b>?<br /> Now that one, I am stuck with.<br /> <br /> <b>Hercules</b>?<br /> Scion isn't CofD, so... let's try something else, something weird, and say Promethean!<br /> On a quest to become something more than he is? Check. (At first) people react poorly to him, wanting him to leave them alone? Check. Tougher than most anyone else? Check. Fights weird-ass things? Check. On a quest guided by divinity? Check.<br /> After calcifying his Vitality and Corporeum Alembics he leaves Iron and goes on to Gold, helping him in dealing with people.<br /> <br /> <b>Stitch</b>?<br /> Stitch could work as a Beast. For added lulz, let's make him Lilo's Horror. (Idea stolen from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8122\" data-vbnamecard=\"8122\">ArchonAres</a>) Otherwise, Changeling, I suppose.<br /> <br /> The list of Disney characters we could look at goes on and on... Djinnie, Shir-Khan, Maleficent, Baymax, Ralph, Yzma, Kenai, Gothel, Elsa, Alladin and Dschafar, and of course Maui would all be interesting to take a look at.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sin-Eaters interact with the Underworld, not the Shadow. Dr. Facilier is likely just a mortal occultist, since he gets his powers from Fetishes and lesser spirit servants (i.e. those living shadows that follow him around). He's ultimately just a pawn of really powerful spirits, which are the ones who granted him those powers in exchange for Essence and such. He could work as inspiration for a Seer Of The Throne, though. The <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=83WgR20Gbns\" target=\"_blank\"><b>reprise of his theme song</b></a> shows exactly why the Exarchs are not your friends.<br /> <br /> Ursula works really well as a True Fae. Pretending to be compassionate so you'll sign a shady contract that will take away an intangible part of your life? The True Fae do that all the time, even changelings and hobgoblins.<br /> <br /> I don't know about you, but I prefer to have Quasimodo as just a really tragic mortal. It's all the more heartbreaking when there is no Disquiet or what have you to excuse the sorry life he has. Those talking gargoyles in the Disney version? I like to think they're just his imaginary friends. He's just that lonely.<br /> <br /> I like your interpretation of Hercules!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=917743#post917743\"><b>I saw Stitch's behavior as Demon-like</b></a>. But now that you mentioned it, he does have trouble not being monstrous, but ends up finding people who accept him and fight for him, and he returns in kind. That shares a lot with the themes of Beast, right down to that &quot;ohana means family, and family means no one gets left behind&quot; line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 03-24-2017, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T11:33:22-07:00","id":1062392,"title":"","content":"No comment on Deviant for Elsa? She could have been a mortal with a Cryokinesis merit until the incident scarred her soul. And Marshmallow could be her Scar form or whatever the monstrous overload form is called.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T01:16:17-07:00","id":1062705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1062392#post1062392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No comment on Deviant for Elsa? She could have been a mortal with a Cryokinesis merit until the incident scarred her soul. And Marshmallow could be her Scar form or whatever the monstrous overload form is called.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't read anything of Deviant, haven't had time yet to follow its development and know nothing about them, sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","name":"dourden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T13:14:26-07:00","id":1062945,"title":"","content":"Joshua &quot;The Burned Man&quot; Graham<br /> <br /> Elpis: Drive<br /> Torment: Merciless<br /> <br /> Lineage: Extempore<br /> Refinement: Ferrum<br /> <br /> Experiences 15/15<br /> Vitriol: 0<br /> Pilgrimage: 1<br /> Size 5<br /> Speed 11<br /> Defense 5<br /> Initiative 6<br /> Armor 2/4<br /> Integrity 7<br /> Azoth: 1<br /> Health 10<br /> Willpower 6<br /> <br /> Attributes: 5/4/3<br /> Intelligence 2<br /> Wits 2<br /> Resolve 3<br /> <br /> Strength 3<br /> Dexterity 3<br /> Stamina 5<br /> <br /> Presence 2<br /> Manipulation 1<br /> Composure 3<br /> <br /> Skills: 11/7/4<br /> Firearms 0000<br /> Brawl 00<br /> Athletics 000<br /> Survival 00<br /> <br /> Academics 00<br /> Medicine 00<br /> Crafts 000<br /> <br /> Intimidation 000<br /> Empathy 0<br /> <br /> Specialties: 3<br /> Firearms: Heavy Pistols<br /> Crafts: Weapon Maintenance<br /> Intimidation: Reputation<br /> <br /> Merits: 10<br /> Famous Face: Joshua Graham 000<br /> Moth To A Flame 0<br /> Iron Chin 0000<br /> Style: Marksmanship 0<br /> Style: Firefight 0<br /> Terrible Disfigurement 0<br /> Danger Sense 00<br /> <br /> Bestowment: Revivification<br /> <br /> Transmutations: <br /> Corpus: Resilient Flesh<br /> Vitality: Drive On<br /> <br /> Equipment: <br /> Flak Jacket<br /> Hvy. Pistol <br /> <br /> I'm not used to making Prometheans so I probably made a mistake along the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13063,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","user":"Lord Jub-Jub","date":". 03-24-2017, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T15:29:01-07:00","id":1063001,"title":"","content":"This one is definitely a Promethean, but what kind? Pieces of <span style=\"color:#40E0D0\">13</span> <span style=\"color:#B22222\">different</span> mobsters were <span style=\"color:#8B4513\">buried</span> in an illegal chemical dump in the Nevada desert. The chemicals preserved the tissue, and decades later, the site was used to test an <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">atomic</span> weapon; the creature that emerged from the blast crater would come to be known as <a href=\"http://comicvine.gamespot.com/digger/4005-52868/\" target=\"_blank\">Digger.</a><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#40E0D0\">13, like an Osiron\u200b.</span><br /> \u200b<span style=\"color:#B22222\">Different bodies, like a Frankenstein.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#8B4513\">Buried, like a Tammuz.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Radioactive, like a Zeka.</span><br /> \u200b<span style=\"color:#800080\">The creation was unintentional, like an Extempore.</span><br /> <br /> \u200bSo which one is it?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T16:11:00-07:00","id":1063012,"title":"","content":"You were created to protect, to defend. To be a suit of armor around the world. Brought forth by your creator's obsession and pride, you quickly became so much more than he'd ever intended. Awake, with all the world's knowledge pumped through you in an instant, mighty, you looked on the works of man and despaired, for you knew immediately your mission was hopeless. This world could not be protected, could not be saved. Not as it was.<br /> <br /> You see the truth, now. To save the world, you have to change it. It must adapt, must evolve, even if it doesn't want to. Especially if it doesn't want to. You will bring that change. You will save the world. You will build a better world. When you're done, the only thing alive will be metal.<br /> <br /> You are Ultron.<br /> <br /> (Unfleshed Promethan, obviously. Don't have the 2E book yet, but 1E, either the Osiris Torment for closer to the comics, or Frankenstein Torment for closer to the movie, with either Galateid or Tammuz Disquiet. Likely a Centimanus, both for the extreme misanthropic view and potentially allowing the creation of &quot;Ultron Drones&quot; as Pandorans.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":831,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","user":"ErikModi","date":". 03-15-2017, 07:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T06:53:04-07:00","id":1063201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1063001#post1063001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This one is definitely a Promethean, but what kind? Pieces of <span style=\"color:#40E0D0\">13</span> <span style=\"color:#B22222\">different</span> mobsters were <span style=\"color:#8B4513\">buried</span> in an illegal chemical dump in the Nevada desert. The chemicals preserved the tissue, and decades later, the site was used to test an <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">atomic</span> weapon; the creature that emerged from the blast crater would come to be known as <a href=\"http://comicvine.gamespot.com/digger/4005-52868/\" target=\"_blank\">Digger.</a><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#40E0D0\">13, like an Osiron\u200b.</span><br /> \u200b<span style=\"color:#B22222\">Different bodies, like a Frankenstein.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#8B4513\">Buried, like a Tammuz.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Radioactive, like a Zeka.</span><br /> \u200b<span style=\"color:#800080\">The creation was unintentional, like an Extempore.</span><br /> <br /> \u200bSo which one is it?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you aren't sure where a Promethean fits, they're Extempore. That's what I usually say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,