take seems like either mage or hunter to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T23:30:23-07:00","id":1069905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1069214#post1069214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heh. I like that. Explains the unhealthy obsession people have about her while isolating her.<br /> And Beast is a Changeling Beast? Or is he a literal Beast, and the Castle is his Lair? The Latter might work better for romance purposes, and I think you could fluff the Devouring as a sort of curse.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bChangeling, most likely Hunterheart. The Enchantress was a Gentry, and the rest of the castle staff are Wizened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 03-31-2017, 12:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T23:40:40-07:00","id":1069910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1069662#post1069662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering Azathoth is the universe itself?<br /> ...yep!</div> </div> </div> </div>Better yet -&gt; Azathoth = Azoth !!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T23:48:12-07:00","id":1069913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1069910#post1069910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Better yet -&gt; Azathoth = Azoth !!!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say Azatoth is closer to the God-Machine. Both are Blind Idiot Gods who create and destroy without a clear purpose, are responsible for maintaining reality as we know it, are associated with cosmic forces, and nobody knows what would happen if they woke up/were fixed. And Azathoth has at least one named agent who takes on human form. Who's to say it doesn't create many Nyarlathoteps like the God-Machine creates many Angels?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T01:43:39-07:00","id":1069928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1069913#post1069913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say Azatoth is closer to the God-Machine. Both are Blind Idiot Gods who create and destroy without a clear purpose, are responsible for maintaining reality as we know it, are associated with cosmic forces, and nobody knows what would happen if they woke up/were fixed. And Azathoth has at least one named agent who takes on human form. Who's to say it doesn't create many Nyarlathoteps like the God-Machine creates many Angels?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>OMG, Nyarlathothep is a Demon! His many faces are Covers, and despite being a Messenger for the Outer Gods, he is kind of different, and there are interpretations about him hating them and trying to become more important. Also the only eldritch horro that really meets humans at face-to-face, on a personal level.<br /> So... Demon with one Angel-hijacked Cover plus a thousand additional ones? I'd peck him as a Messenger Tempter-Integrator.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T12:45:30-07:00","id":1070245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1069928#post1069928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OMG, Nyarlathothep is a Demon! His many faces are Covers, and despite being a Messenger for the Outer Gods, he is kind of different, and there are interpretations about him hating them and trying to become more important. Also the only eldritch horro that really meets humans at face-to-face, on a personal level. So... Demon with one Angel-hijacked Cover plus a thousand additional ones? I'd peck him as a Messenger Tempter-Integrator.</div> </div> </div> </div> He definitely works as a godlike Messenger Demon. Not only does he have many faces, he is served by cultists, crosses vast distances in moments, visits other realms, and creates wondrous devices. Both Demons and Angels can do all of that. He'd be a Tempter-Integrator if he's still loyal to Azathoth/the God-Machine. It's also possible that he despises servitude so much that he decided to become his own God, which would make him a Tempter-Inquisitor. I wrote <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1022321#post1022321\"><b>a character sheet for him.</b></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T07:14:44-07:00","id":1071234,"title":"","content":"Would Doctor Doom be a Hoffnung Genius with a lot of mystical knowledge, or a Moros Mage that complements his magic with scientific knowledge? I'm inclined to think he's the latter.<br /> <br /> As a side note, here's Aku from Samurai Jack, cross-posted from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1068101-foolish-samurai-warrior-aku-idigam?p=1068176#post1068176\"><b>here</b></a>.<br /> <br /> <b>Type:</b> Idigam (Or An Idigam-Like Maeljin)<br /> <b>Rank:</b> 6<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 15, Finesse 15, Resistance 15<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 240<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 15<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 11<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 40<br /> <b>Size:</b> Varies<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 15 + [Size x 2] + [Rank x 10]<br /> <b>Armour: </b>15<br /> <b>Manifestations: </b>Twilight Form, Discorporate, Gauntlet Breach, Materialize, Reaching, Royal Avatar, Shadow Gateway<br /> <b>Influences: </b>Darkness 6, Tyranny 3<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Awe, Blast, Dement, Essence Thief, Hallucination, Mortal Mask, Omen Trance, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\"><b>Phantom Arsenal</b></a>, Seek,Telekinesis<br /> <b>Dread Powers: </b>Call Void Spirit, Colossus, Devourer, Elemental Fury, Crazed Evolution, Regenerate 3, Shifting, Spirit Dominion, Spirit Interrogation<br /> <b>Essence Shaping: </b>Gauntlet Manipulation, Ghost Manipulation, Locus Manipulation, One Million Eyes, Spirit Manipulation<br /> <b>Forge Servant:</b> Claimed, Herald, Spawn<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Must show a trait of his true form no matter what disguise he takes<br /> <b>Bane: </b>Jack's Magic Sword","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 07-17-2017, 10:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T08:37:02-07:00","id":1071272,"title":"","content":"Doom has always seemed slightly more Mad Scientist-y than Mad Mage. I don't think his tricks are vulnerable to Dissonance-like effects, so I think that is the deciding factor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T08:40:56-07:00","id":1071275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1071272#post1071272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doom has always seemed slightly more Mad Scientist-y than Mad Mage. I don't think his tricks are vulnerable to Dissonance-like effects, so I think that is the deciding factor.</div> </div> </div> </div>not to mention that there is that group of Genii who try to test the limits of Inspiration by building Wonders with theories that involve magical trappings like ritual circles and such","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T18:47:42-07:00","id":1082865,"title":"","content":"What do you think desert punk would be ?<br /> <br /> I was thinking a demon blooded. Anyone got a better idea ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","user":"Basic","date":". 04-25-2017, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T21:33:48-07:00","id":1082897,"title":"","content":"So I watched Smurfs 2 last week, and I realized it's a Promethean story. Some liberties must be taken, of course:<br /> <br /> Smurfs are stable, natural creatures,(like humans) but they contain magical &quot;essence&quot;(Azoth/Pyros) that Gargamel seeks.(that makes them like Prometheans)<br /> <br /> The Naughties are unstable, artificial creatures, that require &quot;essence&quot; on a regular basis to survive,(like Pandorans) but have the potential to become Smurfs.(like Prometheans can become human)<br /> <br /> Gargamel is obviously an Insatiate Alchemist, (&quot;I want MORE than enough!&quot;)<br /> <br /> \u200bHere's the kicker; part of the formula for turning a Naughty into a Smurf is &quot;a hopeful thought&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 04-24-2017, 12:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T19:50:03-07:00","id":1083279,"title":"","content":"I got one.<br /> <br /> Shazam (formerly Captain Marvel) as a Noble, from Princess: the Hopeful.<br /> <br /> Alternate form with superior attributes? Check.<br /> <br /> Supernatural gifts that only work when transformed? Check.<br /> <br /> Supernatural powers treat either form as a separate person from the other? <a href=\"http://youngjustice.wikia.com/wiki/Misplaced\" target=\"_blank\">If <i>Young Justice</i> is anything to go by, yes.</a><br /> <br /> Hopeful child fighting against evil? Check.<br /> <br /> He doesn't really have regalia, but he still fits pretty well. Not sure off the top of my head what court he'd be, though.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T05:06:42-07:00","id":1083408,"title":"","content":"The Joker? An Angel of the Godmachine.<br /> <br /> Massively elaborate but seemingly pointless plans? Incredibly advanced technology from no clear source? No clear motivation? A total lack of identity? Almost but not quite human looking? Unavoidable bans he must follow? The world conspires to keep him alive and free?<br /> <br /> All the killings and destruction are part of an an occult matrix. However, he's getting more and more obsessed with a local ungulla nemesis, and is close to falling. Which would probably be really bad for everyone.<br /> <br /> Also, various horror games:<br /> <br /> The Path is a depiction of a Fae abduction of an entire family. The wolves are different appearances of the same fae (with, presumably, The Big Bad Wolf as its title), grandma's house was a series of distorted memories of a durance, and the forest was an unusual area of the Hedge. the girl in white is a rival releasing her enemies captives. The six sisters are presumably now changelings.<br /> <br /> The animatronics of FNAF are, arguably, bound- a series of geists who have found a way to merge with machines rather then people. It didn't go quite as well as they planned, and now they are lashing out at the living.<br /> <br /> Amnesia is the after-effects of a mortal's examinations of an abyssal artefact. The Darkness and Alexander are both intruders drawn to it.<br /> <br /> Bendy, from bendy and the ink machine, is a geotia summoned to earth. Someone rolled a dramatic failure when doing that.<br /> <br /> Limbo is some poor kid being dragged into a beast (the spider's) lair. Surprisingly, he is able to overpower and defeat the horror, at which point the chambers start to break down a bit. We've probably got either a powerful beast or a powerful hero in the making here.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T06:13:33-07:00","id":1083427,"title":"","content":"Or just an awesome Human","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T06:19:36-07:00","id":1083435,"title":"","content":"Can a Deviant be made by a Slasher? If so, I think <a href=\"https://comicvine.gamespot.com/abuse/4005-68114/\" target=\"_blank\">this kid</a> qualifies:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://static5.comicvine.com/uploads/square_medium/6/64770/1268980-abuze.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> \u200bAnd yes, I mean kid. His pre-pubesant body chemistry reacted rather strangely to performance-enhancing super-drugs. This is what he looks like powered down:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://static4.comicvine.com/uploads/square_medium/5/59958/1390088-colin2.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T08:16:41-07:00","id":1083463,"title":"","content":"Mechanically, Abuse is more of a Skinchanger. A Were-Man. With Venom-based stuff I suggest using the Lost Boys microtemplate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T11:36:26-07:00","id":1088397,"title":"","content":"I was just rewatching the fight scene from the Samurai Jack episode Jack vs. the Guardian when I realized that he is a perfect Anakim. The foe you cannot beat because you are not the one. He either hungers for Power or Punishment. If the former, his fights serve to demonstrate how small and powerless you are before destiny. If the latter, he punishes people for the hubris of believing that they are &quot;the one&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T20:25:11-07:00","id":1088609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1083463#post1083463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mechanically, Abuse is more of a Skinchanger. A Were-Man. With Venom-based stuff I suggest using the Lost Boys microtemplate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Were means man, so that would make him a Man-Man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T03:44:02-07:00","id":1088686,"title":"","content":"More horror things!<br /> <br /> Little Nightmares is a straight up changeling durance- the main character becomes either a gristlegrinder or leechfinger at the end.<br /> <br /> House of Leaves is what happens when an incarnate gets corrupted by the Abyss. The weird meta things are the beast hunting through the dream- read it, and it can find you.<br /> <br /> The videotape from the Ring <i>isn't</i> haunted, at least not in the conventional sense. Samara was a particularly powerful Arcanthus, and in her dying moments laid one hell of a curse on the world.<br /> <br /> Freddy Kruger is a vampire, with dream-based powers letting him feed on dreams. He keeps coming back because no-one's found his toporic body to destroy.<br /> <br /> Heavy Rain includes VASCU's attempt to create a technological version of Teleinformatics, field tested by tracking down a Maniac called the Origami Killer. You can decide for yourself how well it went.<br /> <br /> Cloverfield is an important warning to werewolves as to what can happen when an Idigam goes unchecked for too long.<br /> <br /> The tabletop game Chronicles of Darkness contains kindred, I think, although I'm unsure, they're quite subtle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","user":"Urbenmyth","date":". 05-06-2017, 07:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T06:24:55-07:00","id":1088727,"title":"","content":"The kinden from <i>Shadows of the Apt</i> are insectile Beasts. Or, if you'd prefer, Nahual feral wereinsects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 05-08-2017, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T09:06:27-07:00","id":1088771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1083463#post1083463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mechanically, Abuse is more of a Skinchanger. A Were-Man. With Venom-based stuff I suggest using the Lost Boys microtemplate.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/879911-ichorous-symbiote-homebrew-mini-template\">Oh! Oh! I have something intended precisely for this!</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T11:37:37-07:00","id":1088807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1088771#post1088771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/879911-ichorous-symbiote-homebrew-mini-template\">Oh! Oh! I have something intended precisely for this!</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Venom the drug, not the symbiote. That said, I love your work on this and could even see it expanded to a Sin-eater-esque full fan Template with the theme of &quot;humans bonded to amorphous monstrosities&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T20:30:08-07:00","id":1088983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1088807#post1088807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Venom the drug, not the symbiote. That said, I love your work on this and could even see it expanded to a Sin-eater-esque full fan Template with the theme of &quot;humans bonded to amorphous monstrosities&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, my bad. Thanks, though!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T17:18:38-07:00","id":1091342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/-TqfBEX6QtE\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/-TqfBEX6QtE\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/-TqfBEX6QtE\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/-TqfBEX6QtE </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The guy's name is Maestro Leopold and he literally came back from the dead as the necromancer with a daemonic familiar due to a supernatural touch on his mother's side. He is such a Bound that I wonder if it was intentional. Given his backstory said he was killed by his fiance (who didn't want to marry a mestizo), he would probably be a Torn Advocate, though he doesn't seem to fit personality-wise. He might fit powers-wise, but I'm not familiar enough with the game to tell. Same goes for what exactly to call the monstrous ghost he fought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 05-12-2017, 09:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T20:04:27-07:00","id":1093510,"title":"","content":"How about Jack Skellington from a Nightmare Before Christmas as a Namtaru Predator who has Kinship with Changelings, Sin-Eaters and likely more? He is probably the Apex of whatever game he is in. Halloween Town is his Lair, with Chambers being shared with other Beasts of his Brood. He would impose the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/649174-a-new-lair-trait\"><b>Wondrous (Halloween Decorations And Monsters)</b></a> Lair Trait on the Hive. His plan to kidnap Santa Claus was due to his identity crisis over being a monster that has to spread fear over and over, but he eventually embraced who he was and defeated a much worse Beast (Oogie Boogie), possibly earning his Incarnate Inheritance in the process. Santa might have been a high level Changeling who was kidnapped through the use of cold iron and his Frailties. I'm thinking of making Jack's mortal identity be a party organizer and wise aristocrat, as a reference to how much he loves holidays and books, as well as that classy look he has. I'll rewatch the movie and write a character sheet for him. Anybody interested?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T00:20:30-07:00","id":1093560,"title":"","content":"So from the stuff I've watched recently:<br /> Into the Badlands: Quinn as a Lance Sanctum Archbishop that was cast down and had to go into hiding. Bonus points for Ventrue as he is quite insane <br /> American Gods: Technical Boy as a Acanthus mage from Free Council. Man-child on a power trip <br /> John Wick 1/2: Winston as an Ordo Dracul prince. Does not take sides in fights between the covenants, knows all the secrets, makes sure everyone plays by the rules. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12924-orzhov","name":"Orzhov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T06:37:50-07:00","id":1093641,"title":"","content":"I just read through all the compiled Changeling playtest, and the first thing I thought of with the Huntsmen, was &quot;Terminator.&quot;<br /> <br /> Skynet as a True Fae, with the &quot;apocalyptic future&quot; actually being its Arcadian Realm, with the various time travellers being Changelings escaped to before they were taken in order to try and prevent Sarah from being taken, and prevent the Wizened (from a more modern, computer-themed Kith) Changeling that becomes Skynet from hitting zero Clarity.<br /> <br /> The eponymous Terminator is a Huntsman made from metal scrap (the T-1000 is made from a pool of quicksilver), right down to killing somebody upon showing up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T12:39:16-07:00","id":1093746,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i><b>Jack Skellington</b></i></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Family:</b> Eshmaki<br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Prey<br /> <b>Life:</b> Shy<br /> <b>Legend:</b> Unexpected<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 3, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 5, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 5, Manipulation 3, Composure 4<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics (Literature) 3, Computer 1, Crafts 2, Investigation 3, Medicine 2, Occult (Beasts, Changelings) 4, Politics 3, Science 2, Athletics 4, Larceny (Breaking And Entering) 3, Stealth (In Plain Sight) 5, Survival 2, Animal Ken (Canines) 2, Empathy (Fear) 3, Expression (Oratory, Singing) 4, Intimidation (Shock) 5, Persuasion 4, Socialize (High Class) 4, Streetwise 1, Subterfuge 2<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area Of Expertise (Fear), Encyclopedic Knowledge (Academics, Occult), Interdisciplinary Specialty (Fear), Professional Training 5 (Socialite: Expression, Socialize, Academics), Double Jointed (Advanced), Iron Stamina 3, Parkour 3, Allies (Autumn Courtiers 3), Barfly, Contacts (Several), Fame 1, Fixer, Inspiring, Iron Will, Resources 4, Retainer (Zero 3), Status (High Class 4), Striking Looks 2 (Spooky), True Friend (Sally), Iron Skin 2 (Advanced 2), Hunger Management 3, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits\"><b>Dark Walker 3 (Advanced)</b></a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits\"><b>Find A Vein (Glamour 5)</b></a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1063048#post1063048\"><b>Wandering Soul 4</b></a><br /> <br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 9<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 7<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 9<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 12<br /> <b>Health:</b> 14<br /> <b>Lair:</b> 6<br /> <br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> Alien Allure, Death Of Light, Dragonfire, From The Shadows, Illusion Of Safety, Infestation (Shadowy Bats), Looming Presence, Needs Must, Relentless Hunter, Shadowed Soul, Siren\u2019s Treacherous Song, Unbreakable, Wings Of The Raptor<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> Behold My True Form, Bugs Everywhere, Run Away, You Are Not Alone, Fear Is Contagious<br /> <br /> <b>Horror Traits:</b> Power 11, Finesse 9, Resistance 7, Size 11, Corpus 14, Defense 9, Initiative 9, Speed 25<br /> <br /> <b>Lair Traits:</b> Crosswinds, Fog, Poor Light, Sealed Exits, Thunderous, Mirages, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/649174-a-new-lair-trait\"><b>Wondrous</b></a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 05-29-2019, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T12:46:22-07:00","id":1093751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1069214#post1069214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heh. I like that. Explains the unhealthy obsession people have about her while isolating her.<br /> And Beast is a Changeling Beast? Or is he a literal Beast, and the Castle is his Lair? The Latter might work better for romance purposes, and I think you could fluff the Devouring as a sort of curse.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Something I regret that we didn't put in the <b>Beast </b>core, as an inspirational media example, was Jean Cocteau's <i>La Belle et la Bete</i>. It's an amazing example of a Beast with a Lair, as well as the power of dreams and nightmares.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T09:22:16-07:00","id":1094175,"title":"","content":"How about Invader Zim as a God-Machine Angel who was Exiled for being supremely incompetent and destructive but too loyal to Fall? GIR would be either a minor Angel or a Cryptid. Dib and Gaz are Stigmatics, which is why they are the only ones who ever bother to investigate Zim. Professor Membrane is a rare example of a successful Genius (possibly the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1062191-homebrew-the-genius-supernatural-merit-template-and-a-new-exploit-fill-position\"><b>Stigmatic version</b></a> rather than the Major Template one). Miss Bitters could be a Charlatan Gentry or some weird Spirit of Despair and Discipline that is Fettered to the Skool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T13:04:08-07:00","id":1096835,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i><b>Koro Sensei (Assassination Classroom)</b></i></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Virtue:</b> Compassionate/Cunning<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Petty<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b> Bring Out The Best In Others, Foil Attempts At Assassinating Him<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 8, Wits 10, Resolve 8<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 7, Dexterity 10, Stamina 7<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 5, Manipulation 6, Composure 8<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics (Strategy) 5, Computer 4, Crafts 5, Investigation (Assassination) 6, Medicine 4, Occult 3, Politics 3, Science 5, Athletics 8, Brawl 4, Firearms 4, Larceny 4, Survival 3, Weaponry 4, Empathy (Individual Needs) 6, Expression (Teaching) 4, Intimidation (Sudden Seriousness) 4, Persuasion (Bringing Out The Best In Others) 5, Socialize (Jovial) 3, Subterfuge 3<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area Of Expertise (Assassination, Bringing Out The Best In Others), Common Sense, Danger Sense (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1107057#post1107057\"><b>Epic</b></a>), Encyclopedic Knowledge (Academics, Investigation, Science), Fast Reflexes 3 (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1107057#post1107057\"><b>Epic</b></a>), Indomitable (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration\"><b>Epic</b></a>), Interdisciplinary Specialty (Assassination, Bringing Out The Best In Others), Professional Training 5 (Assassination Teacher: Investigation, Empathy, Expression), Trained Observer 3 (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration\"><b>Advanced</b></a>), Virtuous (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration?p=847629#post847629\"><b>Advanced 3</b></a>), Ambidextrous, Demolisher 3, Double Jointed (Advanced), Iron Stamina 3, Sleight Of Hand, Inspiring (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration?p=1088037#post1088037\"><b>Epic</b></a>), Iron Will, Pusher, Sympathetic, Table Turner, Untouchable, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration?p=848765#post848765\"><b>Untouchable Style 4</b></a>, Close Quarters Combat 1, Defensive Combat (Brawl), Unarmed Defense 5<br /> <br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 26<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 30<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 22<br /> <b>Speed:</b> Special (See Absurd Agility)<br /> <b>Health:</b> 14 (Size 7)<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 10<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Absurd Agility*, Influence 3 (Assassination), Know Soul, Mimir\u2019s Wisdom*, Numen (Blast, Occult Sight*, Omen Trance), Reality Stutter, Shifting*, Surprise Entrance, Unnatural Healing*<br /> <br /> <i><b>*Absurd Agility:</b></i> Koro Sensei adds his Potency to Perception rolls and his Defense. His Defense is applied against ranged attacks, and his Dodging rolls receive the Rote Quality and are done reflexively. His Speed is considered to be enough to win any Chase against mundane opponents, and he can fly up to his full Speed. In the case of supernatural opponents with powers that significantly enhance their Speed, roll a Clash Of Wills against Koro Sensei\u2019s Dexterity + Potency. Furthermore, Koro Sensei may spend 1 Willpower point to reduce the time taken by most Mental and Physical Extended Actions into 1 turn per roll. Spending 3 Willpower points makes each roll reflexive, allowing Koro Sensei to multitask to extreme levels.<br /> <br /> <b><i>*Occult Sight:</i></b> Koro Sensei is sensitive to supernatural phenomena. He notices the active use of supernatural abilities within the range of his senses and may make Perception rolls to approximate their distance and direction. In addition, by spending a point of Willpower, he can see through powers of concealment, illusion and deceit with a Clash Of Wills using his Wits + Potency as his dice pool. Lastly, he always knows when he is being targeted by a supernatural power and may mimic the Aura Reading Supernatural Merit, but without drawback.<br /> <br /> <i><b>*Mimir\u2019s Wisdom:</b></i> As per the Atavism (Beast: The Primordial, page 127). Koro Sensei is considered to always be at Low Satiety, and can mimic the Satiety Expenditure effect by spending 2 Willpower points.<br /> <br /> <i><b>*Shifting:</b></i> As per Idigam version (Werewolf: The Forsaken 2ED, page 222). This Dread Power can be used to mimic his miscellaneous powers like Molting and Absolute Defense.<br /> <br /> <i><b>*Unnatural Healing:</b></i> Koro Sensei can only receive aggravated damage from weapons specifically designed to be his Bane (any other potential source of aggravated damage is downgraded into lethal). He also heals all lethal and bashing damage reflexively each turn. Should he be attacked with his Bane, he downgrades a number of aggravated damage equal to Potency/2 into lethal at the end of the turn.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-27-2017, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T09:58:00-07:00","id":1098461,"title":"","content":"Mr.World from American Gods takes it as an ochemata of Mamon for me<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5tfjJcLmyfY\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5tfjJcLmyfY\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5tfjJcLmyfY\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5tfjJcLmyfY </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12924-orzhov","name":"Orzhov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T16:14:55-07:00","id":1098932,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://comicvine.gamespot.com/drax-the-destroyer/4005-6807/\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\"><i>Drax the Destroyer</i></span> </a>is a Promethean. Forget what you saw in the movies, comicbook Drax was born as a human on Earth. After he and his family were killed by Thanos, Arthur Douglas was recreated as an Eternal known as Drax the Destroyer by Mentor and Kronos with the sole purpose of destroying Thanos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T18:05:03-07:00","id":1098951,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Chihiro Ogino (from Spirited Away) would have been transformed into a wizened drudge changeling by her experience in Yubaba's bathhouse, while her parents would be beasts of </span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">some kind.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13297-josiah","name":"Josiah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T19:33:13-07:00","id":1098991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1098932#post1098932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://comicvine.gamespot.com/drax-the-destroyer/4005-6807/\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\"><i>Drax the Destroyer</i></span> </a>is a Promethean. Forget what you saw in the movies, comicbook Drax was born as a human on Earth. After he and his family were killed by Thanos, Arthur Douglas was recreated as an Eternal known as Drax the Destroyer by Mentor and Kronos with the sole purpose of destroying Thanos.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Interesting, since I thought that comic book background better fit in as a Deviant. Gamora and Nebula, and maybe Rocket too, would also be such Deviants. No idea what Star-Lord and Groot would be. Maybe the latter is a plant-based Promethean?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T20:01:07-07:00","id":1098999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1098991#post1098991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting, since I thought that comic book background better fit in as a Deviant. Gamora and Nebula, and maybe Rocket too, would also be such Deviants. No idea what Star-Lord and Groot would be. Maybe the latter is a plant-based Promethean?</div> </div> </div> </div>From my limited understanding of Guardians Of The Galaxy, Star Lord might be a very skilled Offspring with access to some Embeds and Implanted Gadgets. In one origin, Groot was exiled from his planet for rebelling against the the cruel experiments the other members of his species were performing through the galaxy, and he even risked his life to save a human woman he met again decades later. He also has a profound knowledge of science and technology in general. Maybe he's an unusual Unchained with high Primum, a faulty Cover and Catastrophic Glitches?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T02:07:33-07:00","id":1099082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Josiah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1098951#post1098951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Chihiro Ogino (from Spirited Away) would have been transformed into a wizened drudge changeling by her experience in Yubaba's bathhouse, while her parents would be beasts of </span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">some kind.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Though if it was 2e, she'd be a Grim and her parents would be seemingless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T14:46:15-07:00","id":1099296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1098999#post1098999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From my limited understanding of Guardians Of The Galaxy, Star Lord might be a very skilled Offspring with access to some Embeds and Implanted Gadgets. In one origin, Groot was exiled from his planet for rebelling against the the cruel experiments the other members of his species were performing through the galaxy, and he even risked his life to save a human woman he met again decades later. He also has a profound knowledge of science and technology in general. Maybe he's an unusual Unchained with high Primum, a faulty Cover and Catastrophic Glitches?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Alternatively, Groot could simply be an Elemental Changeling (Woodblood dual-kithed with Gargantuan?). Or even a Fae Exile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T15:49:30-07:00","id":1099314,"title":"","content":"Of topic, but now I want to see a TV interview between Hodor and Groot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T06:37:30-07:00","id":1099489,"title":"","content":"I know he probably fits better as a Deviant, but he is supposed to be &quot;half-ghost&quot;, so how would one build Danny Phantom as a Sin-Eater. I don't know much about G: tS, but his powers include energy beams, forcefields, flight, intangibility, invisibility, cryobeams, a sonic attack, super-strength, and what's basically an Unseen Sense (Ghosts) power called the Ghostly Chill","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T07:29:44-07:00","id":1099508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1099489#post1099489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know he probably fits better as a Deviant, but he is supposed to be &quot;half-ghost&quot;, so how would one build Danny Phantom as a Sin-Eater. I don't know much about G: tS, but his powers include energy beams, forcefields, flight, intangibility, invisibility, cryobeams, a sonic attack, super-strength, and what's basically an Unseen Sense (Ghosts) power called the Ghostly Chill</div> </div> </div> </div>Energy Beams: Rage?, or Blast (from a Fetter)<br /> Force-fields: Phantasmal Shroud<br /> Flight: Cold-Wind Caul<br /> Intangibility: Phantasmal Caul? Something from a Fetter?<br /> Invisibility: Stillness Caul<br /> Cryobeam: Cold-Wind Rage<br /> Sonic Attack: Cold-Wind Rage? or a Numina from a Fetter?<br /> Super-Strength: high Psyche<br /> See Ghosts: template ability<br /> <br /> Bear in mind, Sin-Eaters also have access to Fetters, so they can use Ghost Numina.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-02-2017, 06:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T14:40:39-07:00","id":1099647,"title":"","content":"I headcanon Johnson &quot;The Metaphysical Goalie&quot; (a very minor side character in <a href=\"http://www.checkpleasecomic.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Check Please!</a>) as an Acanthus who has projected himself into the creator's oneiros <i>for reasons</i>.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://68.media.tumblr.com/2832f02780a2f1c4c3a2d2b0ff0b8365/tumblr_inline_msselwrOkQ1qz4rgp.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T22:32:47-07:00","id":1100016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1099508#post1099508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Energy Beams: Rage?, or Blast (from a Fetter)<br /> Force-fields: Phantasmal Shroud<br /> Flight: Cold-Wind Caul<br /> Intangibility: Phantasmal Caul? Something from a Fetter?<br /> Invisibility: Stillness Caul<br /> Cryobeam: Cold-Wind Rage<br /> Sonic Attack: Cold-Wind Rage? or a Numina from a Fetter?<br /> Super-Strength: high Psyche<br /> See Ghosts: template ability<br /> <br /> Bear in mind, Sin-Eaters also have access to Fetters, so they can use Ghost Numina.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forgotten Gatekeeper is my basic knee-jerk assessment. It fits both the manner of his transformation/death and the role he takes where ghosts are concerned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T00:46:42-07:00","id":1100037,"title":"","content":"<b>Wonder Women</b> from movie is totally Galateid on Stannum from<b> Promethean</b>! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> She is 'made from clay and Zeus thunder', have some strange powers, and now want to save world by slaying Ultimate Evil. She takes the Role of Soldier and go on the Great War front lines. Only, to become true human being, she need to learn that Evil is in all humans, all at once, not some mythological being. She even toss Divine Fire in movie! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T22:15:05-07:00","id":1100341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1098991#post1098991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Interesting, since I thought that comic book background better fit in as a Deviant. Gamora and Nebula, and maybe Rocket too, would also be such Deviants. No idea what Star-Lord and Groot would be. Maybe the latter is a plant-based Promethean?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bComicbook Gamora? Regeneration is a natural ability for her, and that's really her only &quot;power&quot;.<br /> Nebula has a LOT of cybernetic implants, so sure, deviant.<br /> Rocket is a Deviant, assuming that animal uplifts are an option for Deviant concepts.<br /> \u200bStarlord doesn't really have any powers at all in the comics. And Ego is NOT his father.<br /> \u200bGroot is an alien tree... probably Changeling related?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T06:25:03-07:00","id":1100802,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i><b>Saitama (One Punch Man)</b></i></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Virtue: </b>Determined/Humble<br /> <b>Vice: </b>Ennui<br /> <b>Aspirations: </b>Be A Hero For Fun, Do The Right Thing, Find Challenges In Everyday Life<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 8, Resolve 10<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Special (See Unsurpassable Might)<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 1, Manipulation 2, Composure 8<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 1, Crafts 1, Investigation 2, Occult 1, Athletics (Absurd Agility) 10, Brawl (Punching) 10, Empathy (Personalities) 3, Expression (Heroic) 1, Intimidation (Unsurpassable Might) 3, Persuasion 2, Subterfuge 1<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area Of Expertise (Punching), Common Sense, Danger Sense (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1107057#post1107057\"><b>Epic</b></a>), Fast Reflexes 3 (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1107057#post1107057\"><b>Epic</b></a>), Indomitable (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration\"><b>Epic</b></a>), Interdisciplinary Specialty (Punching), Tolerance For Biology, Trained Observer 3 (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration\"><b>Advanced</b></a>), Virtuous (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration?p=847629#post847629\"><b>Advanced 3</b></a>), Ambidextrous, Iron Stamina 3, Iron Will, Resources 1, Status (Hero Association 1), True Friend (Genos)<br /> <br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 28<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 32<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 22<br /> <b>Speed:</b> Special (See Absurd Agility)<br /> <b>Health:</b> Special (See Not Hurt At All)<br /> <b>Potency: </b>10<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 9<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers: </b>Absurd Agility*, Not Hurt At All*, Numen (Occult Sight*), Surprise Entrance, Unsurpassable Might*,<i> <b><u>Serious Series</u></b></i><br /> <br /> <b><i>*Absurd Agility:</i></b> Saitama uses the highest between Dexterity and Wits to determine Defense, adds his Potency to Defense and applies it to ranged attacks. His Dodging rolls receive bonus Successes equal to Potency and are done reflexively. His Speed is considered to be enough to win any Chase against mundane opponents. In the case of supernatural opponents with powers that significantly enhance their Speed, roll a Clash Of Wills against Saitama\u2019s effective Stamina + Athletics of 20, and give him bonus Successes equal to Potency.<br /> <br /> <b><i>*Not Hurt At All: </i></b>Saitama is considered to have an immunity to harm equivalent to that granted by an Imperial spell of Excision for all Gross Arcana (see Mage The Awakening - Imperial Mysteries). For any source of harm that does not come from the purviews of those Arcana, he still rolls Resolve + Potency to contest, and gains bonus Successes equal to Potency.<br /> <br /> <b><i>*Occult Sight:</i></b> Saitama is sensitive to supernatural phenomena. He notices the active use of supernatural abilities within the range of his senses and may make Perception rolls to approximate their distance and direction. In addition, by spending a point of Willpower, he can see through powers of concealment, illusion and deceit with a Clash Of Wills using his Wits + Potency as his dice pool, with bonus Successes equal to Potency. Lastly, he always knows when he is being targeted by a supernatural power and may mimic the Aura Reading Supernatural Merit, but without drawback.<br /> <br /> *<b><i>Unsurpassable Might: </i></b>Saitama receives an automatic Exceptional Success on all Physical rolls which benefit from his Punching Specialty. If the action has nothing to do with Punching but is still mostly Physical in nature, he may spend 1 Willpower point to apply the Specialty anyway. He forces any opponent that is not godlike into Down And Dirty Combat. Should he face a godlike opponent, he uses Serious Series.<br /> <br /> <b><i><u>Serious Series:</u></i></b> The stats above are for when Saitama isn't making any effort. When he does, he can spend 3 Willpower points to perform an equivalent of an Imperial spell of Transfiguration for Forces (see Mage The Awakening - Imperial Mysteries). That is, he has omnipotence within the purview of that Arcanum, but cannot give that omnipotence to others and needs to perceive his target directly. Only godlike beings may contest this by rolling their Stamina + Supernatural Tolerance with bonus godlike Successes vs Saitama's effective &quot;Rote&quot; of Strength + Brawl + Potency (30 dice) and bonus Successes equal to his Potency.. He he may use techniques other than Punching, does not need Quintessence and does not suffer Paradox.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 09-29-2017, 07:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T11:29:20-07:00","id":1100893,"title":"","content":"Stats for Saitama are pointless. He's so powerful even an Exarch would only last a few moments against him. It's a comedy series, really. He's yet to run into <i>anything</i> that can <i>remotely</i> hurt him. He hits you; fight's over. (Even Boros remarked Saitama was half-assing his way throughout their fight and was really putting extremely little effort into it.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T12:38:50-07:00","id":1100922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1100893#post1100893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stats for Saitama are pointless. He's so powerful even an Exarch would only last a few moments against him. It's a comedy series, really. He's yet to run into <i>anything</i> that can <i>remotely</i> hurt him. He hits you; fight's over. (Even Boros remarked Saitama was half-assing his way throughout their fight and was really putting extremely little effort into it.)</div> </div> </div> </div>My sheet isn't serious either. I'm well aware that Saitama should be handled through ST fiat. This is simply an exercise in theorycrafting. And I did take into account that the fight is over when he hits you (see the &quot;Unsurpassable Might&quot; and &quot;Serious Series&quot; Dread Powers). He also has Unbreakable, Armor 30/30, Unnatural Healing and Immortal. Seems pretty close to me.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T22:42:29-07:00","id":1101506,"title":"","content":"From what we have heard of Deviant thus far, it seems like Skullgirls would work really well as inspirational material for it. But in the meantime, I think the characters could also be interpreted as follows:<br /> <br /> Filia: a Sin-Eater, probably a Forgotten Pilgrim.<br /> <br /> Cerebella: a Mortal, with her Vice-Versa being a Relic containing a powerful Spirit of Violence. Alternatively, a Fairest Dancer, with Vice-Versa being a hobgoblin.<br /> <br /> Peacock: a mortal who has been augmented with many Wonders or Gadgets. Alternatively, her traumatic backstory and cybernetic reconstruction caused her to Awaken as a Mastigos. Her cartoonish nature would be her Nimbus, and her cartoon cronies are Goetia from her Oneiros she Materializes through Spirit. Her arsenal is mostly pre-existing, and stored and summoned through Space. High Gnosis and low Wisdom.<br /> <br /> Parasoul: a Hunter, with her umbrella Krieg being a powerful Relic, a Lambda Gadget or a Cryptid with the Variable Form Adaptation.<br /> <br /> Ms. Fortune: my first thought was Promethean, but she is beloved by the people of Little Innsmouth and doesn't seem to cause Disquiet/Wastelands. She could be a Gangrel with Protean 4 and a special Protean + Resilience Devotion<br /> <br /> Painwheel: an actual Promethean, the poor girl. Probably an Extempore.<br /> <br /> Valentine: an Unchained Demon, which explains her superhuman abilities, individualism and talent for deception.<br /> <br /> Double: a God-Machine Angel tied to the Occult Matrix centered around the Skullheart.<br /> <br /> Marie: a mortal altered by the Skullheart into an Angel with access to Infrastructure that gives her godlike power.<br /> <br /> Squigly: a Sin-Eater, likely a Torn Bonepicker.<br /> <br /> Big Band: a mortal augmented by several Wonders or Gadgets. Alternatively, being betrayed and cybernetically rebuilt might have Awakened him as a Thyrsus. His musicality would be his Nimbus, and he would improve his already high tech arsenal with Life, Matter, Mind and Forces. High Gnosis and decent Wisdom.<br /> <br /> Beowulf: a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/849630-minor-template-supernatural-wrestlers\"><b>Supernatural Wrestler</b></a>.<br /> <br /> Eliza: an Elder Daeva of the Invictus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-30-2017, 08:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T03:30:01-07:00","id":1103066,"title":"","content":"Incidentally after watching John Wick 2.... I came to the realisation that John is a Beast.<br /> <br /> Reputation to the Degree that People Blanch out of fear upon hearing His Name? Check.<br /> Skills to overcome anyone in combat like an Anakim? Check<br /> Relationship with everyone based on mutual Respect? Check.<br /> Going on a rampage because someone Stole his property and Killed something he cared for? Check (Lesson Taught: Never mess with peoples stuff if you don't know about them.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T06:09:32-07:00","id":1103457,"title":"","content":"The Music Meister from Batman: The Brave and the Bold is a Nameless Mastigos with songs as his yantra and hidden speakers as his magical tool and his various costume switches coming from a Space-arcana-made hammerspace pocket. The only thing I can't figure out is what Mystery he is obsessed with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T06:20:29-07:00","id":1103459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1103457#post1103457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Music Meister from Batman: The Brave and the Bold is a Nameless Mastigos with songs as his yantra and hidden speakers as his magical tool and his various costume switches coming from a Space-arcana-made hammerspace pocket. The only thing I can't figure out is what Mystery he is obsessed with.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Song of the Universe? What Frequencies could allow for Ascenscion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T07:11:38-07:00","id":1103473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1103459#post1103459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Song of the Universe? What Frequencies could allow for Ascenscion?</div> </div> </div> </div>But why try to hypnotize everyone in the world just to make them steal stuff and do a huge musical number?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T07:41:40-07:00","id":1103480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1103473#post1103473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But why try to hypnotize everyone in the world just to make them steal stuff and do a huge musical number?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe he needs the whole world singing? And he's a greedy asshole?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T07:53:39-07:00","id":1103489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1103473#post1103473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But why try to hypnotize everyone in the world just to make them steal stuff and do a huge musical number?</div> </div> </div> </div>If everyone is singing the Same Song maybe... that is how he can Ascend. Maybe he's found a song that will allow him to &quot;Unmake&quot; something, and he's doing it to see if it works. If it does then Surely he's right.. and a song of Creation is real aswell. Maybe it's just a case of finding the right place to sing it so the whole city can hear it... if they can all hear it they all think it. Maybe its a form of Immortality he's after he needs supplies and he can perform multiple tasks at the same time by stealing stuff while also getting people to sing for him.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's the only way for him to Remain himself... a Deal with a Demon is not a good thing. And one doesn't want to fail their terms of the contract.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":3981,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","user":"RickmanUK","date":". 06-14-2017, 10:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T08:27:04-07:00","id":1103504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1103489#post1103489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe it's the only way for him to Remain himself... a Deal with a Demon is not a good thing. And one doesn't want to fail their terms of the contract.</div> </div> </div> </div>Inferno, God-machine or Fae?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T08:43:02-07:00","id":1103507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1103504#post1103504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Inferno, God-machine or Fae?</div> </div> </div> </div>What difference does it make?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T20:21:58-07:00","id":1104598,"title":"","content":"On second thought, Aku probably works better as a Maeljin who happens to have a few Idigam-like powers instead of an actual Idigam.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T20:30:37-07:00","id":1104602,"title":"","content":"Whats a maeljin","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T20:39:51-07:00","id":1104607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ameraaaaaa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1104602#post1104602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whats a maeljin</div> </div> </div> </div> See <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Maeljin_(CofD)\" target=\"_blank\"><b>here</b></a> for more information. Basically, Aku does not behave like an Idigam is supposed to. The Idigam are more alien, while Maeljin are more classicaly evil demon overlords.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T21:03:40-07:00","id":1104613,"title":"","content":"It could be an idigam trying to become a maeljin. Some of the ones that have more of an interest in social aspects of the world seem to adapt to that. The angel who runs a church, the one that makes werewolves reproduce, and so forth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T08:05:18-07:00","id":1107015,"title":"","content":"<br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i><b>Alex Mercer (Prototype)</b></i></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Virtue:</b> Cunning/Implacable<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Cruel<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b> Wreak Havoc And Destruction, Spread The Blacklight Virus, Devour And Evolve, Infiltrate And Subvert<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 8, Wits 6, Resolve 8<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 7, Dexterity 5, Stamina 10<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 4, Manipulation 6, Composure 8<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics (Strategy) 3, Computer (Hacking) 4, Crafts 3, Investigation (Espionage) 4, Medicine 3, Occult 2, Politics 3, Science (Genetics) 5, Athletics (Parkour) 6, Brawl (Natural Weapons) 6, Drive 5, Firearms 4, Larceny (Security Systems) 3, Stealth (Blending In) 4, Survival (Tracking) 4, Weaponry 6, Empathy (Secrets) 3, Intimidation 4, Persuasion 4, Subterfuge (Disguise) 4<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area Of Expertise (Espionage), Direction Sense, Eidetic Memory, Indomitable (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration\"><b>Epic</b></a>), Interdisciplinary Specialty (Espionage), Virtuous, Crack Driver 3, Demolisher 3, Double Jointed (Advanced), Greyhound, Iron Stamina 3, Parkour 4, Seizing The Edge, Stunt Driver 5, Closed Book 4, Fast Talking 5, Iron Will, Table Turner, Untouchable, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration?p=848765#post848765\"><b>Untouchable Style 4</b></a>, Heavy Weapons 4, Iron Skin 2 (Advanced 2), Killer Instinct 3 (Advanced 3), Relentless Assault 5<br /> <br /> <b>Willpower: </b>26<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 11<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 13<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 37 (Species Factor 25)<br /> <b>Health:</b> 15 (Size 5)<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 6/5<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 10<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Contagious*, Cyclopean Strength*, Mimir\u2019s Wisdom*, Monstrous Resilience, Natural Weapons 3, Needs Must*, Numen (Seek, Speed), Psychic Talent x 2* (Psychokinesis: Flesh And Bones 5/<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/842864-advanced-supernatural-merits-and-styled-supernatural-merits\"><b>Advanced 5/Epic 2</b></a>, Aura Reading 3, Telepathy 5), Reality Stutter, Relentless Hunter*, Snare, Skin-Taker, Unbreakable*, Wall Climb<br /> <br /> <b><i>*Contagious:</i></b> The Horror carries a virulent disease that turns the infected into a creature of the same (or similar) type as the Contagious Horror. To infect a target, the horror must typically injure the victim (a bite or claw is most common, but other methods can be defined depending on the horror) and inflict one level of lethal damage. The victim must make a reflexive Stamina +Resolve roll (with a penalty equal to the Horrors Potency (maximum 5)) Success means that the victim doesn't contract the contagion. an exceptional success renders them immune to further uses of this Dread Power from that particular creature. If the roll fails, then the victim gains the Sick (grave) tilt and becomes a Horror themselves after (9-Potency) hours. At the Storytellers discretion, certain supernatural creatures may be immune to this Dread Power.<br /> <br /> <b><i>*Cyclopean Strength, Mimir\u2019s Wisdom, Needs Must, Relentless Hunter and Unbreakable: </i></b>As per the Atavisms from Beast: The Primordial. Alex Mercer is considered to always be at Low Satiety and can mimic the Satiety Expenditure effect by spending 2 Willpower points.<br /> <br /> <b><i>*Psychic Talent: </i></b>Creatures with this dread power are endowed with great powers of the Mind. Each dot in this Dread Power grants a creature a number of Merit dots equal to its Potency. These Merit dots may be used to purchase Supernatural Merits. Alex Mercer rolls Stamina + Science + Genetics Specialty instead of Resolve + Occult to use his Psychokinesis.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-23-2017, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T14:48:20-07:00","id":1107419,"title":"","content":"The version of Tony Montana that exists in the Payday 2 universe is a Promethean made from Tony's body, he is acting as if he is a continuation of his body's original owner because he feels that the famous drug lord's identity and well documented life story offers a means of exploring multiple refinements. after following Aurum, Ferrum and Phosphorum, Tony is now following Aes, using the fact that the feds recognize his face to protect his new friends in the pack of iron masters known as the Payday gang by drawing some serious agro from the FBI during heists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T12:22:25-07:00","id":1108101,"title":"","content":"<b>Note:</b> This is meant to be a version of the Slender Man that follows the recommended limits of the Potency chart for building Horrors in Chronicles Of Darkness (but with a few extra Merits), rather than a version that has all the powers from all the stories featuring him. I turned Skill dots into Dread Power dots on a 5 for 1 basis.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Virtue:</b> Mysterious/Fearsome<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Observant<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b> Take People Away, Remain Just Out Of Sight, Spread Fear And Madness, + ST Fiat<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 5, Wits 6, Resolve 8<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 5, Dexterity 6, Stamina 8<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 8, Manipulation 6, Composure 8<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Investigation (Spying) 4, Occult 3, Medicine 1, Athletics 3, Brawl 4, Stealth (Stalking) 8, Survival 3, Empathy 1, Intimidation (Appearing Out Of Nowhere) 5, Persuasion (Taking People Away) 4, Subterfuge (Evasive) 4<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area Of Expertise 1 (Taking People Away), Direction Sense 1 (Advanced 2, Epic 2), Eidetic Memory 2, Interdisciplinary Specialty 1 (Taking People Away), Trained Observer 3, Virtuous 2, Greyhound 1, Seizing The Edge 2, Iron Will 2, Striking Looks 2, Untouchable 1, Killer Instinct 3 (Advanced 2)<br /> <br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 26<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 9<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 14<br /> <b>Speed:</b> ST Fiat<br /> <b>Health:</b> 17 (Size 9)<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 10<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Claws And Tentacles [+1L melee; 9 dice]<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Chameleon Horror, Elusive*, Hypnotic Gaze, Immortal, Madness And Terror, Maze, Numen (Hallucination), Reality Stutter, Shifting*, Surprise Entrance, Vanish*<br /> <br /> <b>*Elusive: </b>Creatures with this Dread Power only ever appear on camera as a blurred silhouette of their actual shape. Humanoid monsters can easily be mistaken for humans or upright bears, while unusually large creatures blend into the scenery. Humans have a hard time remembering exact detail about creatures they encounter. Rolls to accurately describe or recall such events are made at a \u20133 modifier.<br /> <br /> <b>*Shifting</b>: The Horror can reform its shape in accordance to its needs. Once per turn, as a reflexive action, it may change itself in a significant manner. The Horror can only sustain one such alteration at a time. The possibilities include:<br /> \u2022 Developing Armor equal to its Potency.<br /> \u2022 Growing limbs or means of locomotion that add +10 to its Speed (and possibly allow it to fly, swim, climb, or tunnel with ease).<br /> \u2022 Changing appearance to perfectly copy a person or animal.<br /> \u2022 Dissolve into a liquid, allowing it to escape a grapple and move through tiny gaps, grilles and channels.<br /> \u2022 Form Natural Weapons with a +1 weapon modifier.<br /> \u2022 Shift dots from one Physical Attribute to another on a one-for-one basis, up to its Potency in dots per round.<br /> <br /> <b>*Vanish: </b>The Horror with this Dread Power can disappear in a flash, a puff of smoke, or the blink of an eye. Once per scene, by spending 1 Willpower, the creature may instantly exit the scene. The Slender Man may also bring other people with him, but must first establish a Grapple or open all the Doors of the target.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-30-2017, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T20:55:23-07:00","id":1109096,"title":"","content":"<i><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Bill Cipher (Gravity Falls)</b></span></i><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Rank:</b> 5 (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=1061536#post1061536\"><b>Deceptor</b></a>)<br /> <b>Vices:</b> Pride, Greed<br /> <b>Keys:</b> Conspiracies, Cults<br /> <b>Malapraxis:</b> Overseer Of Ruinous Secrecy<br /> <b>Attributes: </b>Power 12, Finesse 14, Resistance 12<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Maximum Essence/Per Turn:</b> 50/15<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 13<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 10<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 36<br /> <b>Size:</b> 4<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 16<br /> <b>Influences: </b>Secrecy 3, Ambition 2<br /> <b>Ban 1: </b>Can only use Influences or Numina as part of a bargain.<br /> <b>Ban 2:</b> Can only use Manifestations other than Twilight Form if Summoned.<br /> <b>Ban 3:</b> Must perform at least one act of bizarre or cruel humor whenever he appears.<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Unicorn Hair<br /> <b>Demonic Powers:</b> Corruption, Dragon\u2019s Tongue, Lord Of Lies, Keeper Of Secrets, Soul Of Sin<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Twilight Form, Dreamwalker*, Image, Possess, Fetter, Unfetter, Claim, Reaching<br /> <b>Numina</b>: Create Pact*, Far Sight*, Dream Shaping*, Hallucination, Host Jump, Implant Mission, Occult Sight*, Omen Trance, Perfect Lie*, Sign, Soul Snatch*, Telepathy*, Price Of Power x 2*<br /> <br /> <b>*Create Pact:</b> See Inferno page 52.<br /> <br /> <b>*Dream Shaping:</b> This Numen requires the Dreamwalker Manifestation. The entity may mimic all powers covered by the Oneiromancy of Changelings, but spends Essence instead of Glamour.<br /> <br /> *<b>Dreamwalker:</b> This Manifestation requires the Open Condition. By spending 2 Essence, the entity shifts from Twilight into the Dream Space of an individual or location. Once there, it can interact with the Dream Space in the same way it interacts with the real world (including other entities also active in the Dream Space), and may use Influence and Numina.<br /> <br /> <b>*Far Sight:</b> The entity may project its senses to other locations as if it had the Clairvoyance Supernatural Merit, but does not suffer dice penalties. It spends 1 Essence as an instant action and rolls Finesse + Rank. This may be combined with other Numina or Manifestations that enhance its senses or communication, such as Occult Sight, Gauntlet Vision, Seek, Telepathy or Reaching. If the location has the Open Condition, the entity may combine this with any Numina and Influences by spending 1 willpower point. Locations that have been Warded with the entity's Bane are immune to this Numen.<br /> <br /> <b>*Occult Sight</b>: The entity is sensitive to supernatural phenomena. The entity notices the active use of supernatural abilities within the range of its senses and may make a Finesse roll to approximate its distance and direction. In addition, by spending a point of Essence, it can see through powers of concealment, illusion and deceit with a Clash of Wills using its Finesse + Rank as its die pool. Lastly, it may mimic the Aura Reading Supernatural Merit using Finesse + Rank, but without drawback.<br /> <br /> *<b>Perfect Lie: </b>When this Numen is used successfully, its victim will believe anything it says, no matter how unlikely, as long as it isn\u2019t utter fantasy or contradicted by anything the target knows to be true. The Numen costs one Essence to activate and is contested by Composure + Supernatural Tolerance. If the entity succeeds, the victim believes the lie for the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>*Soul Snatch:</b> This rare but terrifying Numen - possessed only by ephemeral beings of at least Rank 3 - requires 3 Essence to spend, and a successful Power + Rank roll penalized by the target's Composure + Supernatural Tolerance. If it succeeds, its victim immediately suffers Soul Loss as his soul comes to its possession. An ephemeral being can then do with the soul what it will. Most slowly devour it for Essence, regaining a point of Essence per hour spent feasting. For every amount harvested equal to the victim's Willpower dots, though, the soul's Integrity drops by one dot. Should it reach 0, it is destroyed. Most supernaturals may also be targeted by this Numen. And the effects of Soul Loss may vary depending on what type of supernatural they are. Mages, for example, drop in both Willpower and Gnosis without their souls, and lose their ability to cast spells upon being reduced to Wisdom 0.<br /> <br /> *<b>Telepathy</b>: Entities with this Numen can reach out and link their minds with others, allowing instantaneous and reliable communication. This Numen costs one Essence. If the target chooses to resist, the roll is contested by the target\u2019s Resolve + Supernatural Advantage. Success allows the entity to freely communicate with the target and to read their thoughts until the end of the scene. If the target is mortal, they gain the <i>Shaken</i> Condition - being that intimate with an alien mind is profoundly disturbing.<br /> <br /> <b>*Price of Power:</b> By taking on an additional Ban or Bane, an ephemeral entity can increase its repertoire of abilities. Each additional Ban or Bane can give it one of the following.<br /> <br /> * Two Numina, Influence dots, or Manifestations.<br /> * An increase of its maximum Essence pool by 5.<br /> * A Dread Power.<br /> <br /> An entity may take this Numen a number of times equal to its Rank.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 07-02-2017, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.c