e.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">\u200b<b>Virtue:</b> Justice<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Foolish<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b> Fight Crime, Inspire People, Have Fun<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 1, Wits 2, Resolve 8<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 10, Dexterity 5, Stamina 10<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 4, Manipulation 2, Composure 6<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 1, Crafts 1, Investigation (Crime Fighting) 3, Athletics (Jumping) 6, Brawl 6, Stealth 2, Survival 2, Weaponry 3, Empathy 2, Expression (Heroic) 1, Intimidation (Craziness) 3, Persuasion (Friendly) 2, Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 1<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area Of Expertise 1 (Crime Fighting, Craziness), Direction Sense 1, Indomitable 2, Interdisciplinary Specialty 1 (Crime Fighting, Craziness), Trained Observer 3, Greyhound 1, Iron Stamina 3, Parkour 4, Seizing The Edge 2, Allies (Superheroes 3), Inspiring 3, Iron Will 2, Striking Looks 2, True Friend 3 (Arthur), Iron Skin 2 (Advanced 2)<br /> <br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 21<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 8<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 11<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 30 (Species Factor 15)<br /> <b>Health:</b> 16 (Size 6)<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 2/2<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 7<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Bare Fists [+0L Melee; 16 dice]<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Hideous Strength*, Juggernaut, Prodigious Leap*, Regenerate 1, Unbreakable, Wall Climb<br /> <br /> <b><i>*Hideous Strength:</i></b> The Tick\u2019s might is truly formidable; by spending a point of Willpower, he can increase his Strength by his Potency until the end of the scene. Furthermore, he adds his Potency as automatic successes on Strength + Stamina rolls made to perform a feat of strength, such as lifting a massive object, jumping or breaking free of restraints.<br /> <br /> <b>*Prodigious Leap:</b> The Tick does not have to spend Willpower to use this Dread Power.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 07-29-2017, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T15:28:14-07:00","id":1122518,"title":"","content":"Spoooooon!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T16:16:26-07:00","id":1122830,"title":"","content":"Obviously, in terms of theme and power level, Naruto Uzumaki fits best as some kind of Exalt; but for CofD, I would say a Beast, with the Nine-Tails as his Horror. Not sure what family, I still haven't had a chance to look at the book. Eshmaki? Hunger for Ruin?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T18:59:49-07:00","id":1122872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1122830#post1122830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously, in terms of theme and power level, Naruto Uzumaki fits best as some kind of Exalt; but for CofD, I would say a Beast, with the Nine-Tails as his Horror. Not sure what family, I still haven't had a chance to look at the book. Eshmaki? Hunger for Ruin?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pre-shippuden Naruto certainly is feasible, I think. Though with their Mudra-like hand signs, lack of horror hungers etc I think mage would be the best fit. Nine-Tails being his Spirit Familiar?<br /> <br /> Eshmaki would fit the general concept of Ninjas but not those from Naruto, since they are not very stealthy nor is hunting much of a thing for them except for a few occasions. I'd say if he'd be a Beast, Naruto would be a Namtaru (everyone hates him) Tyrant (wants to be Boss, and force people to acknowledge him). Anakim might be fitting, too, considering he does a lot through simple brute force/ridiculous stamina.<br /> Ravager doesn't fit in my opinion, because he is not out to destroy or upset society, nor does he do that. In contrast, Sasuke would be far more easy to peck as a Beast imo: Ugallu Nemesis. Sharingan are a very Ugallu-like ability, exposing the enemies movements on a temporal scale so to speak, and all throughout the series, he is motivated by the desire to punish (take revenge on his brother, take revenge on Madara, take revenge on Konoha, take revenge on the world etc.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 07-30-2017, 10:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T20:29:33-07:00","id":1125468,"title":"","content":"Kuroo Hazama, aka <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Jack_(character)\" target=\"_blank\">Black Jack</a>, is probably some sort of Remade, and his youthful ward Pinoco is best represented as a Promethean to whom he is demiurge. (Coppelia, from &quot;Sir Night Compiles <b>Night Horrors: Conquering Heroes</b>&quot;, and her maker the Ace of Spades started out as riffs on Pinoco and Jack, but soon acquired elements of the Beautiful Daughters and Mad Scientists I mentioned <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1031943-new-let-s-read-of-conquering-heroes-by-a-sour-unchained-other-rpers-appreciated?p=1110680#post1110680\">here</a>. In particular, there are three Coppelia models because there were seven Nemuri Project units and three Madaraki sisters, so Mark III wound up less like Fran [whom I consider closest to Pinoco] than Veronica.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1426-aberranteyes","name":"AberrantEyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T21:10:35-07:00","id":1125475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1122872#post1122872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pre-shippuden Naruto certainly is feasible, I think. Though with their Mudra-like hand signs, lack of horror hungers etc I think mage would be the best fit. Nine-Tails being his Spirit Familiar?<br /> <br /> Eshmaki would fit the general concept of Ninjas but not those from Naruto, since they are not very stealthy nor is hunting much of a thing for them except for a few occasions. I'd say if he'd be a Beast, Naruto would be a Namtaru (everyone hates him) Tyrant (wants to be Boss, and force people to acknowledge him). Anakim might be fitting, too, considering he does a lot through simple brute force/ridiculous stamina.<br /> Ravager doesn't fit in my opinion, because he is not out to destroy or upset society, nor does he do that. In contrast, Sasuke would be far more easy to peck as a Beast imo: Ugallu Nemesis. Sharingan are a very Ugallu-like ability, exposing the enemies movements on a temporal scale so to speak, and all throughout the series, he is motivated by the desire to punish (take revenge on his brother, take revenge on Madara, take revenge on Konoha, take revenge on the world etc.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Naruto himself may not be interested in destruction for destruction's sake, but the Nine-Tails seems to revel in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T09:12:47-07:00","id":1127679,"title":"","content":"Scrooge McDuck: Anakim Collector just one famous adventure from going Incarnate<br /> <br /> Writing up a sheet for him in the DuckTales Era, which I will post in an edit","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T10:50:21-07:00","id":1127709,"title":"","content":"Hm... Iron Man could have a few different possible answers.<br /> <br /> First, we could have an Obrimos Mage (depending on the characterization, he could be Libertine, Silver Ladder, or possibly a Seer)<br /> <br /> I could also see a Hunter with a custom Endowment making up his armor.<br /> <br /> He could also be a Wizened Changeling, with the Metalflesh and/or Smith Kith. His Keeper, The Ten Rings (also known as The Mandarin, Killian, and sundry other Titles), took him while he was in Afghanistan to build weapons to arm his soldiers and Huntsmen.<br /> <br /> Finally, he could be a Klagen Navigator Genius, with his armors being distinct Wonders.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to get a little silly, we could also use Princess for Magical Girl Iron Man, as a Champion of Diamonds, possibly dipping into Storms or Tears territory at times. Iron Man's done some stuff, so his Belief would probably be pretty low. In that case, Rhodey could reasonably be Sworn with a War Machine Bequest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 08-11-2017, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T11:12:47-07:00","id":1127713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1127679#post1127679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scrooge McDuck: Anakim Collector just one famous adventure from going Incarnate<br /> <br /> Writing up a sheet for him in the DuckTales Era, which I will post in an edit</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, he seems more like a Sleepwalker or <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023190-homebrew-proximi-dynasties?p=1123222#post1123222\"><b>Master Of Coin</b></a> with Status in the Mysterium (those adventures in Duck Tales where he and his family hunt relics in ancient ruins and such is very similar to what the Mysterium does). His first coin has turned into a really powerful Artifact for Mysterious reasons, which is why so many people try to steal it. Alternatively, he is a Hunter of the Aegis Kai Doru.<br /> <br /> But go ahead. Just be sure to write his Resources rating as simply &quot;Yes&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-11-2017, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"h