ll of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T12:02:24-07:00","id":1127728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1127726#post1127726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no idea how to stat that, so I'll stop at like, 7, or something. The rest He's too miserly to spend on stufc</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a joke. I meant that his Resources rating is so high that if you ask &quot;can he buy this?&quot;, the answer is not &quot;only if it's Availability X&quot;. The answer is always just &quot;Yes&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T12:14:23-07:00","id":1127735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1125475#post1125475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Naruto himself may not be interested in destruction for destruction's sake, but the Nine-Tails seems to revel in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are absolutely correct, I confused Beast and Horror for a second there.<br /> However, 9Tails is practically decent/docile later on, his Rampages Being retConned into having been mindcontrolled. So arguably, he does not hunger for ruin.<br /> <br /> <br /> I prefer your Interpretation though, honestly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T12:14:52-07:00","id":1127736,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4443_5.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4443\" data-vbnamecard=\"4443\">GibberingEloquence</a> I know, but I'm too anal to just give him a free resources merit","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T16:43:54-07:00","id":1127826,"title":"","content":"I know people have attempted to stat Superman before (Beast, Princess, or Mage, was it?), but what about as a simple Horror? Obviously, he has the Blast Numen, Unbreakable, Flight, Speed (Numen?), and ludicrously high Strength (not even factoring into his other Attributes). Bane is obviously Kryptonite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T19:49:12-07:00","id":1127891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1127826#post1127826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know people have attempted to stat Superman before (Beast, Princess, or Mage, was it?), but what about as a simple Horror? Obviously, he has the Blast Numen, Unbreakable, Flight, Speed (Numen?), and ludicrously high Strength (not even factoring into his other Attributes). Bane is obviously Kryptonite.</div> </div> </div> </div> I wrote him as <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1017869#post1017869\">an epic Demon</a>.</b> But he also works as a Horror:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Virtue:</b> Justice/Kindness<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Pride<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b> Inspire People, Be A Superhero, Do The Right Thing<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 5, Wits 8, Resolve 10<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 10, Dexterity 8, Stamina 10<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 6, Manipulation 4, Composure 8<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics (Journalism) 3, Crafts 2, Computer 1, Medicine 1, Occult 2, Politics 1, Investigation (People In Trouble) 4, Science 2<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics (Flight, Laser Vision) 6, Brawl 5, Stealth (Plain Sight) 2, Survival 2, Weaponry 3<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Empathy 3, Expression (Heroic) 5, Intimidation (Overwhelming Power) 3, Persuasion (Leadership) 4, Socialize 3, Streetwise 1, Subterfuge (Protect Identity) 2<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area Of Expertise 1 (People In Trouble, Heroic), Common Sense 3, Danger Sense 2 (Advanced 2), Direction Sense 1 (Advanced 2), Eidetic Memory 2, Indomitable (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration\"><b>Epic</b></a>), Interdisciplinary Specialty 1 (People In Trouble, Heroic), Professional Training 5 (Journalist: Academics, Investigation, Expression), Trained Observer 3 (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration\"><b>Advanced 2</b></a>), Virtuous (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration\"><b>Advanced 3</b></a>), Greyhound 3, Iron Stamina 3, Seizing The Edge 2, Allies (Superheroes 5), Alternate Identity 3, Closed Book 3, Contacts (Journalists, Law Enforcers), Fame 3, Inspiring 3, Iron Will 2, Resources 2, Safe Place 5 (Fortress Of Solitude), Status (Justice League 5), Striking Looks 1, Sympathetic 2, Table Turner 1, True Friend 3 (Lois Lane), Iron Skin 2 (Advanced 2), Defensive Combat (Brawl), Martial Arts 5, Unarmed Defense 5,<br /> <br /> <b>Defense:</b> 14<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 16<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 50 (Flight 150)<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 28<br /> <b>Health:</b> 15<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 10<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 5/5<br /> <br /> <b>Bane:</b> Kryptonite<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers: </b>Armored Hide 3, Eye Spy, Breath Weapon*, Hideous Strength*, Juggernaut, Natural Weapons 3 (Bare Fists), Numen (Awe, Blast, Speed, Occult Sight*), Reality Stutter, Swift, Regenerate 3, Surprise Entrance, Unbreakable, Vanish*<br /> <br /> <b><i>*Breath Weapon: </i></b>Horrors with this Dread Power can command the elements to destroy their enemies, often literally breathing gouts of fire or hurling bolts of lightning. Choose the type of attack when this Dread Power is selected; this is typically an element such as acid, fire, lighting or cold, but other, more exotic elements might be used depending on the nature of the creature. By spending 1 point of Willpower, the Horror can blast individual targets in range (5/10/15) that counts as a ranged attack with a thrown weapon and requires a roll of an appropriate dice pool \u2013 the opponent\u2019s Defense. This attack has a weapon bonus of +0L. By expending 3 Willpower, the weapon bonus increases to +2L and inflicts the Burning Tilt. In Superman's case, the breath is made of ice, the Tilt inflicted is Immobilized and the Range is 100/200/400.<br /> <br /> <b><i>*Hideous Strength:</i></b> Superman\u2019s might is truly formidable; by spending a point of Willpower, he can increase his Strength by his Potency until the end of the scene. Furthermore, he adds his Potency as automatic successes on Strength + Stamina rolls made to perform a feat of strength, such as lifting a massive object, jumping or breaking free of restraints.<br /> <br /> <b><i>*Occult Sight:</i></b> Superman is sensitive to supernatural phenomena. He notices the active use of supernatural abilities within the range of his senses and may make Perception rolls to approximate their distance and direction. In addition, by spending a point of Willpower, he can see through powers of concealment, illusion and deceit with a Clash Of Wills using his Wits + Potency as his dice pool. Lastly, he always knows when he is being targeted by a supernatural power and may mimic the Aura Reading Supernatural Merit, but without drawback.<br /> <br /> <b>*Vanish: </b>The Horror with this Dread Power can disappear in the flash, a puff of smoke, or the blink of an eye. Once per scene, by spending 1 Willpower, the creature may instantly exit the scene. The Horrors must have an established location (at least a dot in the Safe Place Merit or equivalent) that they retreat to when using this ability.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T19:58:45-07:00","id":1127896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1127891#post1127891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I wrote him as <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1017869#post1017869\">an epic Demon</a>.</b> But he also works as a Horror:</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice. But shouldn't have the/an Alternate Identity (Clark Kent) merit?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Nevermind. I saw it later (wasn't alphabetical)/","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T21:22:34-07:00","id":1127906,"title":"","content":"I might as well post the Doctor as a Horror.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Virtue:</b> Brave/Curious<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Proud<br /> <b>Aspirations: </b>Explore And Have Adventures, Protect And Teach Those In Need, Solve Mysteries And Crises<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 9, Wits 8, Resolve 9<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 5, Stamina 5<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 6, Manipulation 9, Composure 6<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics (History) 4, Crafts (Machines) 6, Computer 2, Medicine 2, Occult 3, Investigation 3, Science (Time Travel) 6<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 3, Drive (TARDIS) 1, Larceny (Sonic Screwdriver) 3, Stealth 2, Survival 2, Weaponry (Swords) 3<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Empathy 2, Expression (Humor) 4, Intimidation 2, Persuasion (Leadership) 5, Subterfuge 3<br /> <br /> <b>Merits: </b>Area Of Expertise 1 (Time Travel, Sonic Screwdriver), Common Sense 3, Direction Sense 1, Indomitable 2, Interdisciplinary Specialty 1 (Time Travel, Sonic Screwdriver), Investigative Aide 1 (Academics, Science), Professional Training 5 (Time Lord: Science, Expression, Persuasion), Trained Observer 3, Virtuous 2, Greyhound 1, Sleight Of Hand 2, Allies (People He Has Helped 3), Contacts (Historical Figures, Earth\u2019s Governments), Inspiring 3, Iron Will 2, Safe Place 5 (TARDIS), Table Turner 1, Untouchable 1, Armed Defense 4, Defensive Combat 1 (Weaponry), Fighting Finesse (Sword), Light Weapons 4<br /> <br /> <b>Defense:</b> 8<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 11<br /> <b>Speed: </b>13<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 25<br /> <b>Health:</b> 10<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 10<br /> <br /> <b>Ban 1:</b> Can only use Hypnotic Gaze with Psychic Paper.<br /> <br /> <b>Ban 2:</b> Can only use Gremlin, Laying On Hands, Telekinesis and Technopathy with Sonic Screwdriver.<br /> <br /> <b>Ban 3:</b> Can only use Maze, Surprise Entrance and Vanish with TARDIS.<br /> <br /> <b>Ban 4:</b> Can only use Regeneration once per story.<br /> <br /> <b>Ban 5:</b> Cannot harm his Companions.<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Gremlin, Hypnotic Gaze, Influence 1 (Exploration), Know Soul, Maze, Mimir\u2019s Wisdom*, Numen (Occult Sight*), Psychic Talent x 3* (Clairvoyance 3, Laying On Hands 3 [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/842864-advanced-supernatural-merits-and-styled-supernatural-merits\"><b>Advanced 3</b></a>], Omen Sensitivity 3, Telekinesis 3 [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/842864-advanced-supernatural-merits-and-styled-supernatural-merits\"><b>Advanced 2, Epic 2</b></a>], Technopathy 3, Telepathy 5, Psychometry 3), Regeneration*, Surprise Entrance, Vanish, Price Of Power x 5<br /> <br /> <b>*Mimir\u2019s Wisdom: </b>As per the Atavism (see Beast: The Primordial). The Doctor is considered to always be at Low Satiety and can mimic the Satiety Expenditure effect by spending 2 Willpower points.<br /> <br /> <b>*Occult Sight:</b> The Doctor is sensitive to supernatural phenomena. He notices the active use of supernatural abilities within the range of his senses and may make Perception rolls to approximate their distance and direction. In addition, by spending a point of Willpower, he can see through powers of concealment, illusion and deceit with a Clash Of Wills using his Wits + Potency as his dice pool. Lastly, he always knows when he is being targeted by a supernatural power and may mimic the Aura Reading Supernatural Merit, but without drawback.<br /> <br /> <b>*Psychic Talent:</b> Creatures with this dread power are endowed with great powers of the mind. Each dot in this Dread Power grants a creature a number of Merit dots equal to its Potency. These Merit dots may be used to purchase Supernatural Merits.<br /> <br /> <b>*Regeneration:</b> The Doctor may heal all damage and Resolve all negative Conditions as an instant action without spending Willpower points. He changes appearance and often Virtue/Vice as well.<br /> <br /> <b>*Vanish: </b>The Horror with this Dread Power can disappear in the flash, a puff of smoke, or the blink of an eye. Once per scene, by spending 1 Willpower, the creature may instantly exit the scene. The Horrors must have an established location (at least a dot in the Safe Place Merit or equivalent) that they retreat to when using this ability.<br /> <br /> <b>*Price Of Power:</b> By taking on an additional Ban or Bane, an entity can increase its repertoire of abilities. Each additional Ban or Bane can give it one of the following.<br /> <br /> * Two Numina, Influence dots, or Manifestations.<br /> * An increase of its maximum Essence pool by 5.<br /> * A Dread Power.<br /> <br /> An entity may take this Numina a number of times equal to its Rank.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-12-2017, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T22:43:37-07:00","id":1127928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1127891#post1127891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I wrote him as <b><a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1017869#post1017869&amp;quot;]an</a> epic Demon[/URL].</b> But he also works as a Horror:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Virtue:</b> Justice/Kindness<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Pride<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b> Inspire People, Be A Superhero, Do The Right Thing<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 5, Wits 8, Resolve 10<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 10, Dexterity 8, Stamina 10<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 6, Manipulation 4, Composure 8<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics (Journalism) 3, Crafts 2, Computer 1, Medicine 1, Occult 2, Politics 1, Investigation (People In Trouble) 4, Science 2<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics (Flight, Laser Vision) 6, Brawl 5, Stealth (Plain Sight) 2, Survival 2, Weaponry 3<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Empathy 3, Expression (Heroic) 5, Intimidation (Overwhelming Power) 3, Persuasion (Leadership) 4, Socialize 3, Streetwise 1, Subterfuge (Protect Identity) 2<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area Of Expertise 1 (People In Trouble, Heroic), Common Sense 3, Danger Sense 2 (Advanced 2), Direction Sense 1 (Advanced 2), Eidetic Memory 2, Indomitable (<a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration&amp;quot;]</a><b>Epic</b>[/URL]), Interdisciplinary Specialty 1 (People In Trouble, Heroic), Professional Training 5 (Journalist: Academics, Investigation, Expression), Trained Observer 3 (<a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration&amp;quot;]</a><b>Advanced 2</b>[/URL]), Virtuous (<a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration&amp;quot;]</a><b>Advanced 3</b>[/URL]), Greyhound 3, Iron Stamina 3, Seizing The Edge 2, Allies (Superheroes 5), Alternate Identity 3, Closed Book 3, Contacts (Journalists, Law Enforcers), Fame 3, Inspiring 3, Iron Will 2, Resources 2, Safe Place 5 (Fortress Of Solitude), Status (Justice League 5), Striking Looks 1, Sympathetic 2, Table Turner 1, True Friend 3 (Lois Lane), Iron Skin 2 (Advanced 2), Defensive Combat (Brawl), Martial Arts 5, Unarmed Defense 5,<br /> <br /> <b>Defense:</b> 14<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 16<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 50 (Flight 150)<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 28<br /> <b>Health:</b> 15<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 10<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 5/5<br /> <br /> <b>Bane:</b> Kryptonite<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers: </b>Armored Hide 3, Eye Spy, Breath Weapon*, Hideous Strength*, Juggernaut, Natural Weapons 3 (Bare Fists), Numen (Awe, Blast, Speed, Occult Sight*), Reality Stutter, Swift, Regenerate 3, Surprise Entrance, Unbreakable, Vanish*<br /> <br /> <b><i>*Breath Weapon: </i></b>Horrors with this Dread Power can command the elements to destroy their enemies, often literally breathing gouts of fire or hurling bolts of lightning. Choose the type of attack when this Dread Power is selected; this is typically an element such as acid, fire, lighting or cold, but other, more exotic elements might be used depending on the nature of the creature. By spending 1 point of Willpower, the Horror can blast individual targets in range (5/10/15) that counts as a ranged attack with a thrown weapon and requires a roll of an appropriate dice pool \u2013 the opponent\u2019s Defense. This attack has a weapon bonus of +0L. By expending 3 Willpower, the weapon bonus increases to +2L and inflicts the Burning Tilt. In Superman's case, the breath is made of ice, the Tilt inflicted is Immobilized and the Range is 100/200/400.<br /> <br /> <b><i>*Hideous Strength:</i></b> Superman\u2019s might is truly formidable; by spending a point of Willpower, he can increase his Strength by his Potency until the end of the scene. Furthermore, he adds his Potency as automatic successes on Strength + Stamina rolls made to perform a feat of strength, such as lifting a massive object, jumping or breaking free of restraints.<br /> <br /> <b><i>*Occult Sight:</i></b> Superman is sensitive to supernatural phenomena. He notices the active use of supernatural abilities within the range of his senses and may make Perception rolls to approximate their distance and direction. In addition, by spending a point of Willpower, he can see through powers of concealment, illusion and deceit with a Clash Of Wills using his Wits + Potency as his dice pool. Lastly, he always knows when he is being targeted by a supernatural power and may mimic the Aura Reading Supernatural Merit, but without drawback.<br /> <br /> <b>*Vanish: </b>The Horror with this Dread Power can disappear in the flash, a puff of smoke, or the blink of an eye. Once per scene, by spending 1 Willpower, the creature may instantly exit the scene. The Horrors must have an established location (at least a dot in the Safe Place Merit or equivalent) that they retreat to when using this ability.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>One problem with the Occult Sight merit; Superman's powers are specifically described as being ineffective against the supernatural. That is to say that he is just as vulnerable to hostile magic as any mortal; a fireball from an Obrimos might not do anything, because it's still just fire, but Balefire, Hellfire, or other types of fire-like supernatural attacks that don't obey the laws of physics are a different story. Likewise, seeing through a wall is one thing; seeing through a cloaking spell is another. Vampires have successfully pierced his skin with their fangs on at least two occasions that I can think of; one spat out the blood, saying that it tastes foul,(alien blood) the other promptly burst into flames.(his blood is charged with solar energy)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T12:59:56-07:00","id":1128134,"title":"","content":"Hey, how would you guys stat up Dresden Files's &quot;Gentleman&quot; Tony Marcone, or Marvel's Kingpin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T14:13:14-07:00","id":1128179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1128134#post1128134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, how would you guys stat up Dresden Files's &quot;Gentleman&quot; Tony Marcone, or Marvel's Kingpin?</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren't they both just really smart and well-trained humans though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T15:25:06-07:00","id":1128222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1128179#post1128179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aren't they both just really smart and well-trained humans though?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kingpin can crush bones and kind of keep up with spider man in hand to hand combat.<br /> Marcone managed to get valkyrie retainers, And Is The Sole human With territory respected by the accords. Also, enough mental willpower to win out battles of will even against nicodemus and co. I'd pecked him as some sort of criminal-based Hunter who has decided on some sort of cease-fire? After all, protecting His Own And Those Under His Care Against Supernatural Threats Is a common theme.<br /> <br /> Sorry for uppercase, written from mobile<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Edit :<br /> Overlord's Ainz Ool Gown is an (Arch)Mage, with Mastery of Death, Prime, Matter and Life. Much of his superiority over his own people is due to planning and using powerful artifacts.<br /> The only other characters we have seen going all out are Shalltear and some of the Battle Maidens.<br /> Shalltear is a Vampire, I'd say Gangrel, with some nasty equipment. The worship of Ainz and acceptance of her monstrous nature places her in... the Circle of the Crone?<br /> &quot;Nobu&quot; is an Obrimos Arrow, with high Forces and supposedly some Life. Also, likely part of a battle-focused Legacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":".  to avoid double-posting 08-17-2017, 03:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avata