ef=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1gfFNSeOv-xvhM1cC6h9Zfpyt11XcmIUvtCjbgSmYWgg/edit#heading=h.4sijm5g3prcx\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Sanguine Crafting</b></a>) 6, Politics 1, Investigation (Riddles) 4, Science 2<br /> <br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics (Flight) 4, Brawl (Claws And Fangs) 5, Drive 0, Firearms 0, Larceny (Sleight Of Hand) 3, Stealth (Darkness) 5, Survival (Forests And Woodlands) 6, Weaponry (Dagger) 4<br /> <br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken 4, Empathy (Wickedness) 3, Expression (Evil Laugh) 3, Intimidation (Terrible Punishments) 6, Persuasion (Bargaining) 4, Socialize 0, Streetwise 2, Subterfuge (Hide Motivations) 6<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Epic Potential (Stamina), Area Of Expertise 1 (Wickedness), Common Sense 3, Eye For The Strange 2, Indomitable 2 (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration\"><b>Advanced 3, Epic 4</b></a>), Interdisciplinary Specialty 1 (Wickedness), Professional Training 5 (Witch: Medicine, Crafts, Occult), Trained Observer 3, Double Jointed 2, Greyhound 1, Iron Stamina 3, Seizing The Edge 2, Sleight Of Hand 2, Air Of Menace 2, Closed Book 5, Iron Will 2, Resources 3, Retainer (Day, Dawn And Night 5, Ghoul Animals 4), Status (Circle Of The Crone 5), Striking Looks (Frightening) 2, Table Turner 1, Killer Instinct 3 (Advanced 3), Acute Senses 1,Altar 3, Atrocious 1, Bloodhound 2, Claws Of The Unholy 1, Feeding Grounds (Iron Forest 5), Haven (Chicken Legged Hut 5), Riding The Wave 5, Swarm Form 2, Unsettling Gaze 1<br /> <br /> <b>Health: </b>20<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 11<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 10<br /> <b>Speed: </b>20 (80 With Celerity)<br /> <b>Humanity:</b> 3<br /> <b>Blood Potency:</b> 9<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Animalism 5, Auspex 5, Celerity 3, Nightmare 5, Obfuscate 5, Protean 5, Resilience 5, Vigor 5<br /> <br /> <b>Devotions:</b> ST Fiat<br /> <br /> <b>Blood Sorcery:</b> Cruac 5 (ST Fiat)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OyVs-12emmgTK6XSu6dgmACqv7B8TpZuJv2z-9A7yxw/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Elder Transmutations:</b></a> ST Fiat</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T20:51:49-07:00","id":1133654,"title":"","content":"The Black Chamber from the Laundry Files books works pretty well as a group of Seers of the Throne from Panopticon that got a job reading people's mail and then metasticized into basically taking over the US intelligence apparatus. If you ever wanted to fight an NSA run by Sauron.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T16:05:35-07:00","id":1135630,"title":"","content":"Dracula from Castlevania could be a powerful Beast? The Castle would be his Lair, and he'd have a very extensive Brood with tons of powerful Horrors (not the Beast-kind), and lesser ones that listen to them.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, a Daeva?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T16:18:52-07:00","id":1135636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1135630#post1135630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dracula from Castlevania could be a powerful Beast? The Castle would be his Lair, and he'd have a very extensive Brood with tons of powerful Horrors (not the Beast-kind), and lesser ones that listen to them.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, a Daeva?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't remember who posited it, but someone else posited that the Dracula who founded the Ordo Dracul was actually a Beast even in-universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T13:10:03-07:00","id":1135894,"title":"","content":"Interesting. That would make sense, in some ways. I prefer him to be a very weird Vampire though.<br /> <br /> What about Dracula Untold's Dracula ? High Protean, little Auspex, Nightmare's Dread Presence, Resilience, and Vigor. In addition, permanent Hydra's Vitae seems apporpriate, as well as Surmounting the Daysleep, The Warm Face, Oh, and the Mass Embrace Scale, of course.<br /> Could be made into a Beast with Sunlight as an Anathema, I guess, but this would be more topical imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T13:35:51-07:00","id":1135909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1135636#post1135636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't remember who posited it, but someone else posited that the Dracula who founded the Ordo Dracul was actually a Beast even in-universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems unlikely, especially given his embraces and having the banes of a vampire. Also his blood bonding and Protean use.<br /> <br /> He's certainly a weird vampire but those are hardly uncommon.<br /> <br /> I think Baba Yaga is more fitting for a True Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-31-2017, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T06:45:49-07:00","id":1149908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1122872#post1122872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pre-shippuden Naruto certainly is feasible, I think. Though with their Mudra-like hand signs, lack of horror hungers etc I think mage would be the best fit. Nine-Tails being his Spirit Familiar?<br /> <br /> Eshmaki would fit the general concept of Ninjas but not those from Naruto, since they are not very stealthy nor is hunting much of a thing for them except for a few occasions. I'd say if he'd be a Beast, Naruto would be a Namtaru (everyone hates him) Tyrant (wants to be Boss, and force people to acknowledge him). Anakim might be fitting, too, considering he does a lot through simple brute force/ridiculous stamina.<br /> Ravager doesn't fit in my opinion, because he is not out to destroy or upset society, nor does he do that. In contrast, Sasuke would be far more easy to peck as a Beast imo: Ugallu Nemesis. Sharingan are a very Ugallu-like ability, exposing the enemies movements on a temporal scale so to speak, and all throughout the series, he is motivated by the desire to punish (take revenge on his brother, take revenge on Madara, take revenge on Konoha, take revenge on the world etc.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Orochimaru is easily a Namtaru Tyrant / Collector<br /> <br /> First of all, one look at this guy and you instantly know <i>&quot;VILLAIN, VILLAIN, HE IS THE VILLAIN!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Second of all, his obsession with conquering death itself and mastering genetics shows that he has a hunger for Power.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, his desire to learn every jutsu in the world displays a hunger for Hoard. In this case, he hoards supernatural abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-15-2017, 09:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T10:04:59-07:00","id":1149943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1149908#post1149908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Orochimaru is easily a Namtaru Tyrant / Collector<br /> <br /> First of all, one look at this guy and you instantly know <i>&quot;VILLAIN, VILLAIN, HE IS THE VILLAIN!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Second of all, his obsession with conquering death itself and mastering genetics shows that he has a hunger for Power.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, his desire to learn every jutsu in the world displays a hunger for Hoard. In this case, he hoards supernatural abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How do you steal knowledge of a technique or ability though? I mean, I guess you could spy on them or torture them for it but that still sounds like a stretch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T12:19:00-07:00","id":1149974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1149943#post1149943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> How do you steal knowledge of a technique or ability though? I mean, I guess you could spy on them or torture them for it but that still sounds like a stretch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oneiros (or Beast-equivalent) jacking? Kinship Nightmares (not really stealing the abilities, but still...)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T12:42:45-07:00","id":1149983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1149943#post1149943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> How do you steal knowledge of a technique or ability though? I mean, I guess you could spy on them or torture them for it but that still sounds like a stretch.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, aside from the obvious method of just stealing whatever instructions happen to be recorded down, he is a master of genetic modification. His usual method of stealing exclusive abilities involves harvesting a sample of genetic tissue and finding a way to transplant it into other people. There's like a 9 out of 10 chance that his test subjects end up rejecting the transplant. But for those successful 1 out of 10, they gain access to powers they would otherwise not be able to use.<br /> <br /> Plus, he can transfer his essence into another body once every 3 years, retaining his original knowledge, but gaining access to any powers his new body might have possessed as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-15-2017, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T12:58:03-07:00","id":1149987,"title":"","content":"Ok, taking flesh samples could work I guess. Hunger for Power does seem more accurate, though","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T14:49:47-07:00","id":1150016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1149987#post1149987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, taking flesh samples could work I guess. Hunger for Power does seem more accurate, though</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah. Like I said, the guy is obsessed with conquering death itself. His body snatching technique (commonly known as the 'Immortality' Jutsu) has allowed him to prolong his life span by jumping into younger, healthier bodies when his current one becomes too old, or weak to be of any more use. The drawback is he can only use it once every 3 years. So he has to be careful about how and when he uses it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-15-2017, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T23:08:09-07:00","id":1150087,"title":"","content":"Let's do some league of legends &quot;conversions&quot;.<br /> Vladimir could be part of a bloodline whose signiture discipline would allow feeding at a distance and turning into a Pool of blood (modified Protean?). Resilience modified to scale with blood potency, and vice versa would reflect him well, but also be too op. Would be definitly an elder.<br /> <br /> Voidborn are Abyssals, which would make Malzahar A Scelestus (Mind/Fate/Space ?) And Kassadin an Arrow (Space and Prime focused?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T14:05:17-07:00","id":1152019,"title":"","content":"Life is Strange: Max Caulfield is an Acanthus mage and Chloe Price is her sleepwalker friend","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T14:09:26-07:00","id":1152022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=840447#post840447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok yesterday i finished Life is Strange and was quite amazed how the whole thing could be seen as an Acanthus Awakening. So here's Maxine Caulfield, as a mage after the events of the game.<br /> <br /> Name: Maxine Caulfield<br /> Shadowname: Supermax<br /> Order: Orderless, as she hasn't come in contact with the Orders yet, if she does, she'll propably join the Free Council<br /> Legacy: None<br /> Virtue: Charity<br /> Vice: Nosyness<br /> Obsessions: Though Max has largely gone over what happened with Arcadia, there's a thought in her head that it might be possible to change the past without making the necessary sacrifice. There has to be something she missed.<br /> <br /> Gnosis: 2<br /> Wisdom: 7<br /> Dedicated magical tool: Camera<br /> <br /> <br /> Attributes:<br /> Physical: Strenght 2, Dextrerity 3, Stamina 1<br /> Mental: Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 4<br /> Social: Presence 2, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <br /> Skills:<br /> Physical: Stealth 2, Drive 2, Firearms 1 Athletics 1 Larcery 1<br /> Mental: Investigation 2, Crafts 1, Computer 1,<br /> Social: Empathy 2, Persuassion 2, Socialize 1, Subtefuge 2, Expression (Photographs) 3, Animal Ken 1<br /> <br /> Merits:<br /> Sleepwalker Retainer (Chloe Price)<br /> True friend (Chloe Price)<br /> Taste<br /> <br /> Arcana:<br /> Time 3<br /> Fate 2<br /> Space 1<br /> <br /> Rotes:<br /> None as she yet has to come in contact with the Orders.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's already been done? That's hella cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12561,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","user":"Shawarbaaz","date":". 10-23-2017, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T16:40:21-08:00","id":1159252,"title":"","content":"I just watched <i>Jeepers Creepers 3</i> the other night, and I noticed some similarities to Pennywise from <i>IT</i>: They're both only active for short periods of time, with decades-long periods of dormancy; and they both REQUIRE that their prey be afraid in order to feed. That dormancy part makes me think of cicadas, also known as the 17 year locust. Anyone have any idea what these two might be in CofD?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 11-15-2017, 08:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T05:44:26-08:00","id":1162442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1159252#post1159252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just watched <i>Jeepers Creepers 3</i> the other night, and I noticed some similarities to Pennywise from <i>IT</i>: They're both only active for short periods of time, with decades-long periods of dormancy; and they both REQUIRE that their prey be afraid in order to feed. That dormancy part makes me think of cicadas, also known as the 17 year locust. Anyone have any idea what these two might be in CofD?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I haven't seen the Jeepers series, but two possibilities come to mind: spirits and True Fae. I lean towards the second in the case of It, or at least the Actor of one. Their sleep cycle is a ban/frailty in any case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T00:52:21-08:00","id":1167238,"title":"","content":"How would you mechanically represent the setting of Corpse Party game? For those who haven't played the game, it's an elementary school that was torn down after a series of murders but still exists in spiritual dimension and you can access it by performing a harmless-looking ritual. The school is full of ghosts of previous victims who relive the pain of their deaths and can be actively malevolent, corpses of previous victims, various cursed objects, there's no food and water and it can drive people and non-malevolent ghosts mad. The architecture and time is also not consistent. There's more to it, but it will spoil the plot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23530-dante-ru","name":"Dante[RU]","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T01:25:13-08:00","id":1167241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante[RU]</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1167238#post1167238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you mechanically represent the setting of Corpse Party game? For those who haven't played the game, it's an elementary school that was torn down after a series of murders but still exists in spiritual dimension and you can access it by performing a harmless-looking ritual. The school is full of ghosts of previous victims who relive the pain of their deaths and can be actively malevolent, corpses of previous victims, various cursed objects, there's no food and water and it can drive people and non-malevolent ghosts mad. The architecture and time is also not consistent. There's more to it, but it will spoil the plot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds as Twilight or Underworld Domain to me...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T09:44:26-08:00","id":1167941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1167241#post1167241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds as Twilight or Underworld Domain to me...</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really know much about both, but Twilight doesn't seem fitting to me. Why do you think it's in Twilight?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23530-dante-ru","name":"Dante[RU]","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T12:56:50-08:00","id":1167998,"title":"","content":"I\u00b4m doubting if classify Willy Wonka as True Fae or hobgoblin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T13:01:25-08:00","id":1168000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante[RU</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">]<br /> <br /> I don't really know much about both, but Twilight doesn't seem fitting to me. Why do you think it's in Twilight?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Your own words - bolded what's important<br /> <br /> '<b>it's an elementary school that was torn down after a series of murders</b> but still <b>exists in spiritual dimension</b> and <b>you can access it by performing a harmless-looking ritual</b>. <u><b>The school is full of ghosts</b></u> of previous victims who relive the pain of their deaths and can be actively malevolent, corpses of previous victims, various cursed objects,<b> there's no food and water and it can drive people and non-malevolent ghosts mad</b>. The architecture and time is also not consistent. There's more to it, but it will spoil the plot.'<br /> <br /> While Twilight is mostly contastant - this made for ghosts have weird left-overs, like destroyed buildings, etc. Opening it with ritual is still consistant with setting lore about Twilight. And it's full of ghosts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Ghosts Twillight ALSO do not have food or water. But changing geography sounds much more as Underworld Domain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-15-2017, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T19:46:35-08:00","id":1179062,"title":"","content":"Hmm... <b>Franken Fran</b>, a horror manga of somewhat lighter tone than you might expect, is something I would take as a good example of extremely low wisdom, if not actually zero.<br /> <br /> Fran herself, I'm not sure what I'd call her in the CofD. An automaton constructed by a mad Professor, who took after him as a surgeon of such quality she can bend the laws of physics, but at terrible consequences for everyone involved (except herself, always ending up spared of harm by the fallout of messing with things they probably shouldn't). She also doesn't have the same sense of right and wrong as normal beings, such as placing the value of life so high that she'll keep people living in an immortal nightmare state, or mutated into barely recognizable, questionably sentient things, if it ensures survival.<br /> <br /> Mad science is easy to compare to magic, but there's something different than most cases of either when she manages to teach other people her methods, and have them work, or gives lectures and generally be found to be correct, except for the whole 'lack of human values' thing.<br /> <br /> And, while I'm on the topic of horror manga, what would <b>The Enigma of Amigara Fault</b> be? Just an abyssal manifestation of some sort?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T17:40:55-08:00","id":1180297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryphon's Feather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1179062#post1179062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... <b>Franken Fran</b>, a horror manga of somewhat lighter tone than you might expect, is something I would take as a good example of extremely low wisdom, if not actually zero.<br /> <br /> Fran herself, I'm not sure what I'd call her in the CofD. An automaton constructed by a mad Professor, who took after him as a surgeon of such quality she can bend the laws of physics, but at terrible consequences for everyone involved (except herself, always ending up spared of harm by the fallout of messing with things they probably shouldn't). She also doesn't have the same sense of right and wrong as normal beings, such as placing the value of life so high that she'll keep people living in an immortal nightmare state, or mutated into barely recognizable, questionably sentient things, if it ensures survival.<br /> <br /> Mad science is easy to compare to magic, but there's something different than most cases of either when she manages to teach other people her methods, and have them work, or gives lectures and generally be found to be correct, except for the whole 'lack of human values' thing.<br /> <br /> And, while I'm on the topic of horror manga, what would <b>The Enigma of Amigara Fault</b> be? Just an abyssal manifestation of some sort?</div> </div> </div> </div>The most obvious answer to the question of &quot;What is Fran&quot; is that she's a Promethean. About 90% of what you described there sounds like one of the Created; probably an Unfleshed. <br /> Artificial being? \u2713<br /> Unnatural abilities? \u2713<br /> Weird moral compass? \u2713<br /> Doesn't understand why humans might choose death over transformation? \u2713","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T21:46:38-08:00","id":1180344,"title":"","content":"Ah, was so absorbed into the low wisdom view I missed an obvious one. I never think of Prometheans as having strange morals, for some reason. That would make her and her 'sisters' Frankenstein lineage, flesh and metal stitched together to create life, it's the classic. The attempts at immortality and curing disease can fit into classical alchemy pretty easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T23:31:06-08:00","id":1182826,"title":"","content":"I can see Venom being done as a Changeling, or any of the symbiotes really, specifically a Beast Mirrorskin. Mirrorskins are able to change their features and don't take penalties for not having proper kit for disguises, just as the symbiote can become clothing and basically disguise its host's features, and among the Beast's affinity contracts is Boon of the Scuttling Spider, allowing a Changeling to move on any surface that could support them, with both Seeming bonuses working for it. Add in other contracts for shapeshifting, increased strength and the weapon creation and bang, symbiote.<br /> <br /> Only problem is finding an effect for the webbing - there is no contract that would allow for webslinging as far as I know. (incidentally, working from the kickstarter materials here)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T22:42:18-07:00","id":1200717,"title":"","content":"Anyone here seen Tientsin Mystic/He Shen? It's a Chinese drama I recently watched on Netflix, and it seems like a really good basis for a mortals campaign.<br /> <br /> Ding Mao -- son of a corporate executive, educated in Europe in forensic medicine. He'd get Resources, Staff and Retainer merits, plus Library (Medicine).<br /> Guo Deyou -- a salvage diver and the titular mystic. He has visions that would probably qualify as a reskinned Omen Sense, but most of his dots seem to be in social skills/merits otherwise (Definitely more dots in Wits than Intelligence, unlike Ding Mao). Also a persistent condition reflecting his &quot;weak body,&quot; since that's a recurring plot point.<br /> Gu Ying -- a &quot;sorceress&quot; who mostly seems to interact with ghosts and spirits, so, Medium? And also the bruiser of the troupe, with multiple dots in Martial Arts.<br /> Xiao Lanlan -- an heiress and a journalist. Definitely has to deal with the Fame merit, but I'm not quite sure how else to model her.<br /> <br /> And the Mo Gu Dao (I cannot take the Netflix subtitles seriously when they call it &quot;Ancient Evil Gang&quot;) is pretty much already a mystery cult in the show, but I'd have to think more about how to model it. Aside from the obvious Diseased and Addicted conditions, since they're canonically all infected with a mysterious virus and use opium to manage their symptoms....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T06:47:49-07:00","id":1201238,"title":"","content":"Persona 5 is in my opinion one of the best examples of Beasts in nonCoD works.<br /> <br /> Showing some love to the protag, Ren Amamiya (or Akira Kurusu if you're still attached to the manga name).<br /> <br /> He's definitely an Ugallu, Arsene has enough bird thematics to make it work, plus the entire MO of a phantom thief involves exposing a victim's weakness. One would be forgiven for assuming right off the bat that Ren's a Collector, stealing the treasures his targets are obsessed with. The Brood's primary Collector is actually Morgana, an Inaguma.<br /> <br /> Ren's actually a Nemesis, punishing those in power for their transgressions by forcing them to confess their crimes. It's not the fear of being punished that Ren feeds off of, but rather the victim's horror of their actions. And given the rather public nature of these confessions, all Ren has to do is watch the news to feed. It kind of scares the rest of the Brood how easily he can feed. And with Family Dinner, everyone gets in on the feast.<br /> <br /> <b>The following contains spoilers for Persona 5's endgame!</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The final boss is definitely where Ren Incarnates. Hard not to when your latest victim is what amounts to a god.<br /> <br /> But what is Arsene Lupin without his Inspector Ganimard?<br /> <br /> Goro Akechi looks the picture of a Hero. He's a people person, he fights for justice, and his threat to the Phantom Brood certainly paints him as one. The truth is a lot worse. Goro Akechi is actually an Insatiable, a Void Ravager. Truth? Justice? Friendship? None of that matters, nothing fucking matters beyond bringing chaos to Japan and turning the country on its' head. All the murders he committed as the Black Mask did their service in making sure he could keep going. But the true feast will be Ren's terror as Goro personally kills his Brood right before his eyes.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23824-adorablechou","name":"AdorableChou","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T10:41:22-07:00","id":1212354,"title":"","content":"Phantom Brood<br /> <br /> Apologies for the double post, but given the anime of Persona 5 is now out, I couldn't help but give the rest of Ren's Brood their moment in the spotlight.<br /> <br /> Ryuji - Anakim Nemesis. Ryuji himself isn't all that big, but his personality is larger than life. Plus his primary motivation as a Phantom Thief is getting back at those in power. Definitely a Nemesis alongside Ren.<br /> <br /> Ann - Inaguma Predator. Ann is ostracized for being biracial, if that doesn't scream Inaguma I don't know what does. As for her hunger, she outright names herself Panther because it sounds more ferocious than a simple cat. Plus her interaction with Kamoshida's shadow after the PT defeat him just screams Predator to me.<br /> <br /> Yusuke - Ugallu Collector. Yusuke was hard to place in a Family. But as his ult persona is a god of storms, I felt Ugallu suited him. While his primary collection is the Treasures he shares with Morgana, Yusuke also collects anything that catches his eye. Such as the lobsters during the beach trip.<br /> <br /> Makoto - Talassii Predator. Talassii might be an odd fit, until you remember she's a budding police officer. An officer's end goal usually involves locking up those who break the law. As the Brood's second Predator, Makoto feeds at the end of the chase, when the prey has nowhere to escape from justice.<br /> <br /> Futaba - Inaguma Whisper. Her Persona is literally a ufo, how could Futaba not be an Inaguma? Futaba originally began her hacking while trying to ferret out the secrets behind her mother's death. It's almost too easy to turn that into cracking into lairs and airing out the dirty secrets of the Brood's latest target.<br /> <br /> Haru - Namtaru Tyrant. Haru's ultimate persona is a woman's torso coming from a skull, is that Namtaru enough for you? Besides, one of her favored types of coffee is brewed from beans that came from elephant dung. As for her Hunger, just listen to her Mementos conversations and the almost twisted glee she takes in beating down shadows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23824-adorablechou","name":"AdorableChou","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T23:14:56-07:00","id":1218420,"title":"","content":"Funnily enough, I actually started a fanfic with a friend of mine on AO3 where the Phantom Thieves are a motley of changelings. [/obvious plug]<br /> <br /> The working model I have is:<br /> <br /> Ren (Shinobu in the fic, kind of an author's signature of my co-writer): Spring Court Fairest Mirrorskin, he literally has multiple masks, and also the primary oneriomancer. He's also always been more of the emotional support to his team, the raw planning power goes to...<br /> <br /> Futaba: Autumn Court Wizened Gameplayer, the mental heavy lifter of the motley, and the Hollow-keeper. A master of combining computer coding with sorcery to entice the Hedge into doing exactly what she wants it to.<br /> <br /> Ryuji: Summer Court Ogre Bloodbrute, because he's goddamned Ryuji.<br /> <br /> Ann: Summer Court Elemental Bright One, the fire giantess who manages to be the face because of sheer force of distraction despite not having one clue as to how to act.<br /> <br /> Morgana: Spring Court Beast Lurker, a street child turned actual alley cat bagman. He actually was human here, but by the time he escaped he was more fae than human; he literally can't make sense of his own memories.<br /> <br /> Yusuke: Winter Court Wizened Artist, honestly joined up with the Silent Arrow because they're better about giving him actual pay for his paintings, and they help him with his dream of being able to paint in peace. That, and he wasn't in a particularly great mood after he escaped from the Hedge having realized Madarame was a privateer who sold him to an art-obsessed Keeper.<br /> <br /> Makoto: Winter Court Beast Gravewright, and prime example of how going through a Durance can outright break you. Any more is a spoiler, but let's say she's based on an<a href=\"http://yokai.com/inugami/\" target=\"_blank\"> inugami</a> and leave it at that.<br /> <br /> Haru: Autumn Court Ogre Witchtooth. Ryuji's the sword, she's the wizard's stave, and is probably the only one who outright focuses on discovering new Contracts and ways to craft new tokens.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 05-14-2018, 02:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T11:33:00-07:00","id":1218626,"title":"","content":"Also, while we're on the subject:<br /> <br /> The Murderer of P4: Namtaru Ravager, reveling in the fact that he and his nihilism makes him abhorrent to all the sheep-like mortals who surround him. He's likely a Dominae, viewing it as natural and right that he greedily devours all he can and leaves his territory a wreck for being unable to resist him. Really, his feeding strategy is quite brilliant; he uses the Primordial Dream to, in effect, get victims to kill themselves. He's no Enabler though, and in fact they are disgusted by him; he doesn't show you your worst side to embrace or overcome it, he shows you it so that you kill each other over it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T12:33:47-07:00","id":1218646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1218626#post1218626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, while we're on the subject:<br /> <br /> The Murderer of P4: Namtaru Ravager, reveling in the fact that he and his nihilism makes him abhorrent to all the sheep-like mortals who surround him. He's likely a Dominae, viewing it as natural and right that he greedily devours all he can and leaves his territory a wreck for being unable to resist him. Really, his feeding strategy is quite brilliant; he uses the Primordial Dream to, in effect, get victims to kill themselves. He's no Enabler though, and in fact they are disgusted by him; he doesn't show you your worst side to embrace or overcome it, he shows you it so that you kill each other over it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Namtaru because his Horror is Magatsu Izanagi, the god after he became ritually impure due to his time in the Underworld? I like it.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T12:45:30-07:00","id":1218654,"title":"","content":"Kelsier from Mistborn sounds like he'd be a Deviant from the sounds of it, with his hatred against the Final Empire and his loyalty to his crew.<br /> <br /> I can also see him being a Geist as well, especially how Geist are now made in 2e","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T12:47:21-07:00","id":1218655,"title":"","content":"Why Deviant? Is there something about how he got his abilities that I am misremembering?<br /> <br /> Also, question for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar180_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"180\" data-vbnamecard=\"180\">Leliel</a>. Do their miens look like their Phantom Thief outfits, their Personae or something else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 05-14-2018, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T14:42:41-07:00","id":1218692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1218655#post1218655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why Deviant? Is there something about how he got his abilities that I am misremembering?<br /> <br /> Also, question for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar180_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"180\" data-vbnamecard=\"180\">Leliel</a>. Do their miens look like their Phantom Thief outfits, their Personae or something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kelsier got his power in the pits of hathsin, working as if in hell and only got his powers when his wife was beaten to death. And that broke him. For someone to gain allomancy you must first be broken in some way. Which going for what was teased by Deviants that's what they are, people with broken souls by the hands of others, the only difference in Kelsiers case what was done to him was no type of experiment or how it's gonna be for Deviants. The other stuff the Lord Ruler and Nobilty all fit for Kelsiers organization backstory and he already acted like a Deviant in trying to tear the whole empire down. It just seems to fit to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T14:43:42-07:00","id":1218693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1218692#post1218692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kelsier got his power in the pits of hathsin, working as if in hell and only got his powers when his wife was beaten to death. And that broke him. For someone to gain allomancy you must first be broken in some way. Which going for what was teased by Deviants that's what they are, people with broken souls. The other stuff the Lord Ruler and Nobilty all fit for Kelsiers organization backstory and he already acted like a Deviant in trying to tear the whole empire down. It just seems to fit to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, I forgot the part about having to be &quot;broken&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T15:21:01-07:00","id":1218706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1218655#post1218655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, question for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar180_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"180\" data-vbnamecard=\"180\">Leliel</a>. Do their miens look like their Phantom Thief outfits, their Personae or something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, no. They look like something else due to [spoilers]. Japanese species of yokai, to be precise, except for a couple of special cases.<br /> <br /> Ren/Shinobu looks like a menreiki (living collection of masks), Futaba a mujina (badger spirit), Yusuke a mokumokuren (living paper wall with a lot of eyes), Makoto inugami (ghost dog), Ryuji and Haru red and blue oni. Ann and Morgana are exceptions, being a Norse fire giant (Ann) and a cat sith (Morgana).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T15:58:52-07:00","id":1225109,"title":"","content":"Actually, speaking of, I just got done with the third chapter of that <a href=\"https://archiveofourown.org/works/14446794/chapters/33371001\" target=\"_blank\">same fic</a>.<br 