 that third chapter. That required the most thought yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Persona and CofD (Changeling)? Why, oh why? I need to study! Must... keep... off... internet...<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll read that on the weekend. In the meantime, wouldn\u2019t the Murderer of Persona 4 also fit as Inguma? I mean, considering their identity...<br /> <br /> EDIT: Now that I think of it... The Persona Users in 3 would be Bound. They all had a brush with death as the trigger for awakening their powers. Here, they all really died at those moments. The guys in 4 sound a lot like changelings. While they didn\u2019t lose their lives, they nonetheless rebuilt it and themselves. (This would also mean that their Shadow Selves really were their \u201ctrue self\u201d; they were the changelings, and the humans who \u201caccepted\u201d them were fetches who merged with them.) The crew in Persona 5, along with most of the major villains they beat up are Beasts, hands down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 06-07-2018, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T10:54:01-07:00","id":1225625,"title":"","content":"Headless Horseman and Jack - The Miserable?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T11:28:46-07:00","id":1225637,"title":"","content":"People seem to like Changelings for the headless horseman, but spirits and ghosts fit well too. Oh and Beast.<br /> <br /> Beast is a pretty easy catch all for anything scary, just like Changeling is for anything bordering fantasy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-07-2018, 03:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T12:40:31-07:00","id":1225665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1225585#post1225585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Persona and CofD (Changeling)? Why, oh why? I need to study! Must... keep... off... internet...<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll read that on the weekend. In the meantime, wouldn\u2019t the Murderer of Persona 4 also fit as Inguma? I mean, considering their identity...<br /> <br /> EDIT: Now that I think of it... The Persona Users in 3 would be Bound. They all had a brush with death as the trigger for awakening their powers. Here, they all really died at those moments. The guys in 4 sound a lot like changelings. While they didn\u2019t lose their lives, they nonetheless rebuilt it and themselves. (This would also mean that their Shadow Selves really were their \u201ctrue self\u201d; they were the changelings, and the humans who \u201caccepted\u201d them were fetches who merged with them.) The crew in Persona 5, along with most of the major villains they beat up are Beasts, hands down.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To be honest, I can see that, but A), changeling was the first thing we came up with, and B), my co-author dislikes Beast, so...<br /> <br /> I suppose the Murderer could fit that as well, except they revel too much in the destruction of humanity and bringing out the internal ugliness of everyone, making them something inhuman. That's a fear of disease, which is more of a Namtaru thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T12:35:56-07:00","id":1249508,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m thinking of Rose Lalonde as a junior occult invistgator","si