 lesson be that luck doesn't really matter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T12:57:01-07:00","id":1251474,"title":"","content":"Probably, but it couldn't be Vriska's lesson because she relied on luck almost as much as her own ruthlessness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T14:06:29-07:00","id":1251487,"title":"","content":"I think Vriska could actually be a changling","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T14:10:02-07:00","id":1251490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>[Insert Original Name]</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1251178#post1251178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That does sound like her, or maybe a Mysterium mage<br /> <br /> Kanaya: probably an Unaligned Daeva.<br /> <br /> Vriska: A Beast I Imagine her lesson would be something like &amp;quot;Life is brutal and only the strong survive, if you want a better life WORK FOR IT!&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Rose as a 13 year old snarky mystrium mage would be awesome","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-20T10:37:22-07:00","id":1255803,"title":"","content":"Abridged!Kirito (seriously, check it out, it is far superior to the Anime it parodies) would make for a very, very good Beast. Snarky as all hell, with an ingrained need to prove himself superior to everyone else, usually by putting other people down, verbally, socially, intellectually, physically.<br /> Relentless Hunter for sure, and most likely both Lightning Strike and Weakness Exposed. Maybe even Mimir's Wisdom and/or Eye of Heaven.<br /> For Nightmares, I'd say You Deserve This and Run Away, at least.<br /> Lair Trait wise, he seems immune to a number of things, mostly Poor Light, Extreme Heat and Extreme Cold.<br /> Stumped for a Horror, however - maybe Abridged!Asuna?<br /> That would make them an Inguma Tyrant - quite fitting imo!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-20T15:59:45-07:00","id":1255934,"title":"","content":"The Monster from The Ritual (will be referring to said monster as a she, as the director confirmed it was a she) screams Beast the Primordial to me.<br /> <br /> She's a Namtaru Predator who's likely earned her Inheritance, seeing as she never leaves her Horror form, I'm assuming the one she took was the Merger. The forest is her Lair and the pagans in the film are her Cultists, the mummies in the attic her Heralds that earned eternal life in service to their master.<br /> <br /> The Monster relies more on Nightmares than anything, Her kit includes Soldier's Heart, The Walls Have Eyes and You Deserve This and she uses them to break her prey before the kill. Her most prominant Atavisms are Unbreakable and Enemy Within.<br /> <br /> Spoilers for the end of the movie below<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> There are multiple ways to view the ending and why Luke was able to leave the Monster's Lair and she remained inside. Perhaps she willingly let Luke go, he had tried multiple times to kill her and she may have been impressed with his perseverance. The fact she'd feasted on both his fears and that of his friends would certainly leave her in a better mood.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps the Monster can't actually leave her Lair anymore and Luke simply got lucky.<br /> <br /> Or...Luke may very well be a budding Beast himself, and the Monster recognized an infant family member. Would explain why she marked him in the first place, she knew he resonated with the Primordial Dream. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23824-adorablechou","name":"AdorableChou","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T21:37:54-07:00","id":1261479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1255803#post1255803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abridged!Kirito (seriously, check it out, it is far superior to the Anime it parodies) would make for a very, very good Beast. Snarky as all hell, with an ingrained need to prove himself superior to everyone else, usually by putting other people down, verbally, socially, intellectually, physically.<br /> Relentless Hunter for sure, and most likely both Lightning Strike and Weakness Exposed. Maybe even Mimir's Wisdom and/or Eye of Heaven.<br /> For Nightmares, I'd say You Deserve This and Run Away, at least.<br /> Lair Trait wise, he seems immune to a number of things, mostly Poor Light, Extreme Heat and Extreme Cold.<br /> Stumped for a Horror, however - maybe Abridged!Asuna?<br /> That would make them an Inguma Tyrant - quite fitting imo!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My guess is that Abriged Kirito's Horror is the Black Swordsman; the legendary, borderline sociopathic berserk he wants people to see him as, when in reality he's a scared, lonely kid who exists at the mercy of his jackass sister.<br /> <br /> Asuna strikes me as an Urathra who is hiding her predatory instincts out of shame, and it's unbalancing her severely towards Flesh and the more id-driven possessive rages that come with it. She gets notably saner the more she lets down her guard around Kirito when she realizes he's fine with that part of her, though even an Asuna at peace with herself is still kind of a jackass.<br /> <br /> Given her well-meaning fumbling around other ethnicities and her <i>lovely </i>parentage, she's probably an Ivory Claw who's realized how toxic they are as a culture and is desperately trying to escape to the Storm Lords, and her father hates her for calling them out on their bullshit.<br /> <br /> Kayaba, naturally, is a mage dealing with the most horrible Paradox of his life in the worst, least Wise way possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T04:52:12-07:00","id":1261527,"title":"","content":"I mean, what kind of horrible Beast is his sister, if he feels powerless in real life? I thought a big part of his character is that he's (at least at the start) a total Internet Tough Guy who just got lucky enough to get stuck inside a game he'd already been level-grinding in. If he has these powers irl, he would have totally abused them. Probably even killed some people who annoyed him and dumped them in his Lair<br /> <br /> Ok, so maybe it's not 1:1, but maybe he's just in an area full of entrenched and magically powerful supernaturals and he feels weak in comparison<br /> <br /> Oh and the Black Swordsman is totally an Anakim Tyrant who looks like Guts' Berserker Armor with hints of a twisted ogre-like being under all the metal","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 10-25-2018, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-25T14:47:46-07:00","id":1262740,"title":"","content":"Kirei Kotomine as a Beast, it fits so well","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-25T15:48:17-07:00","id":1262757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1262740#post1262740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kirei Kotomine as a Beast, it fits so well</div> </div> </div> </div>The creepy priest from the Fate series, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-25T16:01:12-07:00","id":1262761,"title":"","content":"Yep, he is a person who feels pleasure from others sufferings but he was raised with a moral compass so he wishes to know why if there is a God why he is the way that he is even when that contradicts everything he grew up to believe.<br /> <br /> I can see that working quite well with Beasts themed as one the begotten confused his place in the world and seeking to know why, though generally through world destroying results","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T15:12:49-07:00","id":1298199,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><b>Shigeo &quot;Mob&quot; Kageyama (Mob Psycho 100)</b></i></span><br /> <br /> Virtue: Humble<br /> Vice: Stoic<br /> Path: Obrimos<br /> Order: None<br /> <br /> Mental Attributes: Intelligence 2, Wits 2, Resolve 4<br /> Physical Attributes: Strength 2, Dexterity 2, Stamina 2<br /> Social Attributes: Presence 1, Manipulation 2, Composure 5<br /> <br /> Skills: Academics 1, Investigation 2, Occult 4, Athletics 2, Stealth 2, Empathy (Good Listener) 4, Persuasion (Kindness) 3, Subterfuge (Hide Emotions) 4<br /> <br /> Merits: Common Sense 3, Danger Sense 2, Eye For The Strange 2, Investigative Aide 1 (Occult), Trained Observer 3, Allies (Body Improvement Club 3), Iron Will 2, Sympathetic 2, True Friend 3 (Reigen, Dimple), Potent Nimbus 2<br /> <br /> Willpower: 9<br /> Defense: 4<br /> Initiative: 7<br /> Speed: 9<br /> Health: 6 (Size 4)<br /> Gnosis: 6<br /> Wisdom: 9<br /> Arcana: Death 2, Forces 5, Mind 4, Prime 5, Spirit 2<br /> Rotes: None<br /> Praxes: Kinetic Shield, Levitation, Telekinesis, Telekinetic Strike, Thunderbolt, Know Nature, Psychic Projection, Supernal Dispellation, Ephemeral Shield, Exorcist's Eye, Channel Essence<br /> Conditions: Psychic Overflow (see below)<br /> <br /> Psychic Overflow (Persistent Arcane Condition)<br /> Whenever Mob regains 1 Willpower from his Vice or uses Patter Scouring to remove an emotion-based Condition from his Pattern, the ST places a token on his character sheet. Once per Chapter, the ST can make a roll of Mob's Resolve + Composure - 1 for each such token. On a Failure, Mob becomes completely overwhelmed by his current emotional state, which shapes his every Imago and removes his usual inhibitions regarding the harmful use of magic. He is considered to suffer from the Rampant and Fugue Conditions for the rest of the scene. He retains enough awareness to distinguish friend from foe and can contain Paradox, but otherwise acts in accordance with what whatever emotion is taking control of him. Any rolls for Wisdom Degeneration are postponed to the end of the scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-02-2020, 08:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-26T19:11:47-07:00","id":1314623,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i><u><b>Guts (Berserk)</b></u></i></span><br /> <br /> <b>Life:</b> Parental<br /> <b>Legend:</b> Relentless<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 4, Resolve 6<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 5, Dexterity 4, Stamina 5<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 2, Manipulation 3, Composure 4<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 1, Crafts 2, Enigmas 2, Investigation 3, Medicine 1, Occult (Beasts) 2, Athletics (Chases) 4, Brawl 5, Ride 3, Stealth 2, Survival 3, Weaponry (Dragonslayer) 5, Empathy 1, Intimidation (Violence) 5, Streetwise (Mercenaries) 3, Subterfuge (Hide Emotions) 3<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Epic Potential (Resolve), Common Sense, Danger Sense (Advanced), Direction Sense, Eye For The Strange, Fast Reflexes 3, Indomitable (Epic), Professional Training 5 (Mercenary: Weaponry, Intimidation, Streetwise), Trained Observer 3, Demolisher 3, Greyhound, Iron Stamina 3, Parkour 4, Quick Draw (Dragonslayer), Relentless, Seizing The Edge, Air Of Menace, Closed Book 4, Contacts (Mercenaries, Fencers), Iron Will, Striking Looks 1 (Vicious), Brute Force 1, Defensive Combat (Weaponry), Heavy Weapons 5, Martial Arts 4, Killer Instinct 3 (Advanced 2), Unseen Sense (Beasts)<br /> <br /> <b>Health:</b> 14<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 13<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 15<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 30<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 4<br /> <b>Destiny:</b> 5<br /> <b>Gifts:</b> Champion\u2019s Endurance 4, Champion's Trophy x 2 (Dragonfire, Unbreakable), Chosen Blade x 1 (Dragonslayer), Heroic Leap 4, Kinslayer, Legendary Hunter, Open Gate 3, Vanquisher\u2019s Strength 5, Warrior\u2019s Speed 4, Beowulf's Fury, Dragon Slayer Style 5<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Blind (One Eye), Stoic, Vendetta, Violent<br /> <br /> <b>Notes:</b> This version of Guts uses my homebrew rules for Heroes, which can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1300357-homebrew-playable-heroes-as-a-hurt-locker-style-micro-template\"><b>here</b></a>. For his Champion's Trophies, Dragonfire represents the Arm Cannon and Unbreakable represents the Berserker Armor. As a modification, the Low Satiety effect of the Arm Cannon does not allow Automatic Fire, and instead ignores Defense due to the overwhelming size of the blast. The Berserker Armor's Satiety Expenditure effect causes the Berserk Condition, obviously (see Werewolf The Forsaken 2ed, page 306). The Stoic, Vendetta and Violent Conditions are from the Hunter The Vigil 2ed Playtest. His Chosen Blade has a Damage Bonus of +5L, Durability 10, Size 6 and Armor Piercing 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 05-30-2019, 10:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-27T20:21:55-07:00","id":1314875,"title":"","content":"And now, from the obscure property folder:<br /> <br /> <b><i><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><u>Purge (HERO System)</u> </span></i></b><br /> <br /> Rather than a single individual, the vicious vigilante known as Purge is actually a series of people that have bonded with the symbiotic armor of the original Purge, Nigel Coburn. A powerful Remade with relatively potent psychic powers, Coburn realized his time would soon be up, and during his last battle, he controlled his final Blowout to burn a mental pattern of his ideology into his suit, along with the ability to learn, repair itself, find bearers, and a canny tactical mind. From there, the suit regularly finds its way into the hands of people across the chronicle's urban area, seeking out individuals with a profound, overwhelming grudge to chose as its temporary master; it was Coburn's belief that only genuine hurt from cruel actions produces the level of hate that the suit is attracted to, so it doesn't judge the morality of the feeling, only that the person is willing to kill to see justice done. It is for this reason that Purge is a nightmare of police departments; because &quot;he&quot; can just as easily be an Iraq vet punishing the murder of his family by a serial killer protected by the Mob, a wife finally boiling over for her physical and emotional abuse, or a murderer who had his ego punctured by the police actually pinning his crimes on him, it's impossible to build a psychological profile apart from &quot;deeply hates singular targets, willing to kill others who attack him to an unpredictable degree.&quot; The suit does not care; all it knows is that its wielder has a mission, and it seeks to assist them.<br /> <br /> The current Purge is treated as a normal human with an Aspiration based around avenging a personal wrong, with some Supernatural Merits at most - the suit doesn't bond with supernatural beings for fear of damaging its internal psionic circuitry. Upon binding with the suit, gains the ability to dematerialize and materialize it at will for as long as they own it. In fact, if Purge is enraged, they must succeed at a Resolve + Composure roll to not instinctively summon the distinct red and black cloth of the face-covering armor. While wearing it, the current Purge has the general physical profile of Coburn, a 6'7'' muscular man with relatively feminine hips; the armor deliberately configures itself to hide Purge's current real identity. While bonded, Purge must succeed at a Resolve + Composure roll to pursue any action apart from furthering their Aspiration, protecting their identity, or survival. They do not suffer breaking points based around actions pursuing that goal while, although they will have to roll one with a -3 penalty when the suit unbinds itself for the sudden jolt of their original self snapping back and no longer having the haze block the cost of what they're doing. They also instinctively grow angry at the idea of innocents (in their view) being hurt, and if they fail or chose not to resist the urge to suit up, Purge will instinctively intervene to protect them and punish the oppressors if possible in the same scene - failure to do so successfully results in a breaking point. Once the vengeful Aspiration is resolved, the suit pressures the wearer to transport it nearby a new host, which it can sense from miles away; once a new master is found or the current Purge is dead, the suit reverts to an unclaimed state and calls to the vengeful to accept its service; to assist, it can teleport once per week with a range of about two city blocks, including as soon as it thinks nobody is looking should its master be killed.<br /> <br /> The current Purge is treated as a Horror; because the psionic circuitry interacts differently with each host to give the armor new capabilities, there is also a &quot;free pool&quot; of two Dread Powers to add, and its Attributes are distributed by the GM among their respective categories (the veteran may be a brute with highly boosted Strength and Dexterity with Dread Powers based around endurance and direct combat, while an actor may be a stealthy planner with higher Wits and Composure, for whom the armor serves as a Chameleon Horror and can use a Hypnotic Gaze even in civilian form).<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes: </b>Power 10, Finesse 7, Resistance 12<br /> <br /> <b>Skills: </b>Same as the wearer, but raise Athletics, Brawl, Firearms, Survival, and Streetwise to 5, and chose three from that list to add Specialties to; the armor learns from its bearers and offers specialized skills needed to complete its master's missions.<br /> <br /> <b>Merits: </b>Add Ambidextrous, Gunslinger, Quick Draw, Disarm, Danger Sense, Fast Reflexes 3, Fleet of Foot 3, Iron Stamina 3, Heavy Weapons 5, Tolerance for Biology to the character sheet of the master for as long as they remain the master, even in civilian form (and in fact this is one of the clues to discover Purge's current identity; people notice).<br /> <br /> <b>Potency: </b>6<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers: </b>Hunter's Senses (target of Aspiration), Surprise Entrance, two others depending on current identity.<br /> <br /> <b>Armor: </b>2/3, while suit is materialized.<br /> <br /> <b>Vice: </b>Changes to Ruthless for duration of being Purge<br /> <br /> <b>Ban: </b>Besides the obsessive nature of Purge as outlined above, the armor's enhanced Attributes and Skills do not apply while dematerialized, as they are traits of the suit itself, and the armor's master can only use one of their custom Dread Powers while in civilian form. In addition, being mentally fused with a wearable psychic killbot made by a violent fanatic isn't good for rational thought; each master has a unique Ban based on their personal psychological problems representing an aggravated mental problem for as long as they are bond to the suit (the veteran may need to roll Resolve + Composure to avoid being fascinated by wounded soldiers being cared for by their family, while the angered wife may need to follow any reports of domestic abuse she personally is told about, no matter how credible they are).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-28T13:28:11-07:00","id":1315006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_c