s very limited, I only got that it was mage because I google searched. I bet if you asked in the simple questions threads in the mage subforum they could help you there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-28T22:13:19-07:00","id":1521578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bernese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1521575#post1521575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">can you explain what they are?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are not a consistent place. &quot;From Stranger Spheres&quot; is the title of the chapter in <i><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/60624/Summoners\" target=\"_blank\">Summoners</a></i> where things from outside of the conventional cosmology are detailed \u2014 the presence of a unified &quot;Outer Channel&quot; spell for summoning some of them notwithstanding, they're a disconnected set of alien phenomena that don't have a consistent place in the setting's metaphysics, seeing as they're not Abyssal and the Lower Depths are discussed in an earlier part of the book (though this book was one of the weird points in Mage 1e's development timeline such that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/185173-ammut-the-devourer-theories?p=1200323#post1200323\">the Hellminth might be considered as coming from the Depths in 2e's presentation of the cosmology</a>).<br /> <br /> tl;dr It doesn't mean anything more sophisticated than &quot;alien being from a weird part of the cosmos.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T01:04:50-07:00","id":1521580,"title":"","content":"40k <b>Imperium Ascendant </b>Primarch as mages<br /> Eddard Fendragon (<b>Acanthus</b>\u200b)<br /> Moric Thane(<b>Sophros</b>\u200b)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27472-phoenix853457","name":"Phoenix853457","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27472_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T07:36:53-07:00","id":1521589,"title":"","content":"Not that I have a statblock to back this up but Soma Cruz from Castlevania: Aria / Dawn of Sorrow and his whole arc strikes me as a Beast pursuing an Inheritance, with my initial gut reaction leaning towards a theme of Anakim Tyrant given that his Horror embodies the nightmare of Dracula as the Dark Lord, creates Horrorspawn fashioned after other monsters that he has defeated and can bend the will of others, and his Lair would be Dracula's Castle that has merged with reality of its own accord under special circumstances allowed by a solar eclipse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23800-the-firebrand","name":"The Firebrand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23800_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-30T19:18:28-07:00","id":1523385,"title":"","content":"The (unnamed) protagonist of <i>The Third Policeman </i>is either a changeling still in durance or someone experiencing an very unpleasant Mystery Play. Possibly while dead. The God-Machine also seems to be involved, judging by one of the titular Policemen's appearance in the God-Machine Chronicles.<br /> <br /> Mr. Crow and Mr. Owl from the Rusty Lake games are Pentangle mages who have figured out how to <i>force </i>people to go through Mystery Plays, using a mental health facility as a front. Some of their 'clients' are <i>also </i>dead but that's probably one of the less concerning aspects of their operation.<br /> <br /> <i>The Nightmare Network </i>by Thomas Ligotti depicts the evolution of a near future society into the True Fae, though the story ends before they fully come into their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27692,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27692-alexanderalaska","user":"alexanderalaska","date":".  Added author's name to the last example to make it easier to google. 09-30-2023, 10:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27692-alexanderalaska","name":"alexanderalaska","avatar"